ab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2749,"created":1789063730000,"updated":1791812529000,"title":"Products and applications of weather satellites","titleNative":"Productos y aplicaciones de los satélites meteorológicos","startDate":1794819600000,"endDate":1795183200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Montevideo","host":"AECID","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This classroom course is the second phase of a training programme structured in two stages: a three-week online component followed by a one-week face-to-face session.\n\nThe course provides participants with an applied introduction to the use of meteorological satellite data and products for environmental monitoring and early warning activities. Through a combination of trainer-led demonstrations, practical exercises, and collaborative activities, participants will strengthen their ability to access and interpret satellite-derived information for a range of environmental applications.\n\nThroughout the week, participants will apply the knowledge and methods introduced during the thematic sessions to a collaborative group project. On the final day, each group will present its results, discuss the applied methodology, and exchange feedback with trainers and fellow participants.\n\nThe classroom format encourages active participation, interaction with trainers, peer learning, and the exchange of operational experiences among participants.\n\nThe course follows a participant-centred and application-oriented methodology that includes:\n\n* Trainer-led demonstrations\n* Practical data-access and visualisation activities\n* Thematic exercises\n* Daily briefings and discussions\n* Collaborative group project work\n* Student project presentations and feedback","country":{"id":"UY","name":"URUGUAY","region":"RA-III","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"* Recognise the role of satellite information in early warning services, including its contribution to the Early Warnings for All initiative. \n* Access, visualise, and download selected satellite datasets using the data access approaches introduced during the course.\n* Identify and interpret selected satellite products, and describe their potential applications.\n* Combine information from different satellite products to investigate a practical case study.","summary":"Classroom course on satellite products and applications for environmental monitoring and early warning, featuring practical exercises, discussions and group work.","content":null,"targetAudience":"Personnel from the Meteorological and Hydrological Services of the Ibero-American countries participating in CIMHET (Conferencia de los Servicios Meteorológicos e Hidrológicos Nacionales Iberoamericanos), with professional expertise in agrometeorology.","registrationHowto":"Participants are selected from the online phase, after successfuly completing the mandatory course activities.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"web