iption":"The Regional Focus Group Meeting of the Indonesia VLab Center of Excellence will be held on 28 October 2026, from 02:00–04:00 UTC, with a dedicated session on “Satellite Analysis for Volcanic Ash Dispersion and Distribution.” This session will bring together participants to explore the role of satellite observations in detecting and monitoring volcanic ash, as well as understanding its dispersion patterns and distribution. Through the sharing of knowledge, experiences, and analysis techniques, the session aims to strengthen the use of satellite data for volcanic ash monitoring and support more effective hazard assessment, early warning, and mitigation efforts.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Please register here: [https://link.bmkg.go.id/rfgvlaboct26](https://)","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":12861,"name":"Khafid Pratama","email":"khafid.pratama@bmkg.go.id","agency":"","country":"ID","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":32,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Indonesia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":274,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Indonesia ","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":2,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Observer"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":1,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Forecaster"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2692,"created":1774345113000,"updated":1774358815000,"title":"TREVOR–SAFARI Symposium 2026","titleNative":"TREVOR–SAFARI Symposium 2026","startDate":1793088000000,"endDate":1793984400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Kochi","host":null,"contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":null,"contactUrl":"https://trevorfoundation.org/symposium/","description":"The Trevor Platt Science Foundation (TPSF) and its partners are proud to announce **TREVOR-SAFARI 2026**.\n\nThis landmark event merges two major community-building initiatives inspired by the legacy of Prof Trevor Platt, FRS, FRSC. This symposium marks the second instalment of the TREVOR symposium, following its 2023 debut at the Plymouth Marine Laboratory, UK, and the third SAFARI symposium. The previous two SAFARI symposia were organised by ICAR-CIFT (2010) and ICAR-CMFRI (2018).\n\nThe symposium is being jointly organised by **TPSF, COD-CUSAT, MBAI, ICAR-CMFRI** and will be held on 4–6 November 2026, at the Central Marine Fisheries Research Institute (ICAR-CMFRI) in Kochi, India.\n\nThe symposium will be preceded by a training course organised by the Indian National Centre for Ocean Information Services (INCOIS, Hyderabad) and the Department of Chemical Oceanography at Cochin University of Science and Technology (CUSAT, Kochi).\n\nThe training course will be run in two segments. The initial segment consists of a series of online lectures, followed by in-person classroom sessions and computer work, from 27–31 October 2026 at INCOIS, Hyderabad, India. The second segment, held in Kochi, India from 1-3 November 2026, consists of a field trip to Vembanad Lake in Kerala, India, and laboratory analyses of the samples collected during the field trip at CUSAT, Kochi, India.\n\nAll participants in the training course are expected to submit an abstract to the symposium and actively participate in it.","country":{"id":"IN","name":"INDIA","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"For more information on how to apply, please visit the [Trevor Foundation 2026 Symposium](https://trevorfoundation.org/symposium) course page.","registrationEndDate":1777075140000,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2748,"created":1789027981000,"updated":1789039222000,"title":"Emissions Monitoring from Space and Ground Conference 2026","titleNative":"Emissions Monitoring from Space and Ground Conference 2026","startDate":1792972800000,"endDate":1793318400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Frascati","host":"ESA","contactPerson":"Antony Delavois","contactEmail":"EO4Society.Conf@esa.int","contactUrl":"https://emissionsmonitoring2026.esa.int/","description":"This conference, co-organised by ESA, EEA, CAMS and EUMETSAT, will bring together several European and international stakeholders involved in the monitoring, reporting, and verification of greenhouse gases and air pollutants emissions. The event will span the observations, modelling, national inventory and reporting, operational service, and policy communities. \n\nParticipants will be able to attend state-of-the-art presentations about emission estimations based on spaceborne and ground-based observations, atmospheric modelling, and integrated monitoring systems, covering applications ranging from national emission inventories to sector specific sources. The event will serve as a platform for collaboration and knowledge exchange, helping to bridge scientific advances, operational implementation, and policy needs.\n\nThe workshop will be structured around the following thematic sessions:\n* Top-Down inventories supporting national inventories: from R&D to operational systems.\n* Training/workshop on understanding the inversion methodologies and underlying observations (aimed at inventory compilers and anyone interested in using inversion-based emissions).\n* Link between inversions and LULUCF communities.\n* Space missions and ground networks: status and products.\n* Methane from local and diffuse sources.\n* CO2 monitoring at facility scale — EU-ETS and CBAM perspective.\n* Sectoral Deep Dives.\n* Ancillary data for improving emission estimates.","country":{"id":"IT","name":"ITALY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"The core objective of the conference is to showcase and discuss scientific, operational, and policy-relevant advances supporting the monitoring, reporting, and verification (MRV) of greenhouse gas and air pollutant emissions.\n\nAttendees will engage in discussions on the latest advancement on European and international policy frameworks, advances in observation- and model-based emission monitoring approaches, and the integration of these approaches into operational MRV systems. Specific focus will be given to national inventories, and how these methodologies can support the compilation, verification, and quality assurance and quality control (QA/QC) processes, enhancing consistency across reporting and monitoring frameworks. ","summary":"The event brings together science, operations, inventory and policy communities to advance greenhouse gas and air pollutant emissions monitoring, reporting, and verification.","content":null,"targetAudience":"The Emissions Monitoring from Space and Ground is a free conference, open to all the interdisciplinary and cross-sectoral communities of experts working on GHG and air pollutants emissions detection, quantification, and reporting.\nOral presentations will be invitation-only from the Programme Committee.\nAcceptance to present in the poster session is determined by the Programme Committee, following review of submitted abstracts.\n\nWe strongly encourage in-person participation. A broadcast of the event is foreseen; details will follow soon.\n\nAlthough there is no participation/registration fee, participants are expected to finance their own travel and accommodation expenses.","registrationHowto":"There is an [abstract submission portal](https://www.conftool.pro/emissionsmonotoring2026/index.php?page=submissions), and we invite you to submit your contribution, along with your selection of the conference thematic sessions and the poster presentation format. The submission deadline has been extended to 7 September 2027.\n\nAbstracts should be between 200 and 400 words. As a reference, one A4 page with single spacing typically contains 400–500 words.\nPlease ensure that you provide complete co‑author information (including first name, last name, affiliation, and contact email).","registrationEndDate":1788825540000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9984,"name":"Dominika Leskow-Czyzewska ","email":"Dominika.Leskow-Czyzewska@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"HYBRID","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":223,"value":"ESA","visible":true},{"id":250,"value":"CAMS","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":24,"title":"Greenhouse gases and ozone","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":22,"title":"Air quality","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataG