sat.int","contactUrl":"https://cwg.eumetsat.int/2026/02/convection-working-group-and-3t-forum-meetings-19-23-october-2026-in-alcara-de-henares-spain/","description":"The next CWG meeting, jointly organised with the Expert Forum for Preparing Meteorological Applications and Training (3T Forum), will be held 19-23 October 2026, in Alcalá de Henares, Spain. The meeting venue is at Colegio de San Ildefonso of the University of Alcalá, near Madrid.\n\nIn recent years, convection monitoring through satellites has taken big steps, through the capabilities the new satellites and instruments provide. The meeting in Spain will be an opportunity for the expert community to gather and exchange the latest progress in research and operations for convection monitoring.\n\nWe are expecting a week with engaging presentations, discussions, and application demonstrations. ","country":{"id":"ES","name":"SPAIN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"* Discussions on coordinating development and enhancement of techniques for early detection and prediction of convective storms.\n* Stimulating research activities for better understanding and description of processes in the convective environment and their footprints on satellite data.\n* Exchanging information at an international level for leading scientist and experts in satellite meteorology.\n* Planning and reporting of the progress. ","summary":"The next joint CWG/ 3T Forum expert community meeting is an exchange on the latest progress in research and operations for convection monitoring.","content":null,"targetAudience":"CWG and 3T Forum networks of convection researchers, developers, forecasters, and other operational users. ","registrationHowto":"The meeting is for CWG and 3T Forum members only. Contact EUMETSAT Training for further details. ","registrationEndDate":1788566340000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","coun