ques for atmospheric composition monitoring and chemical transport modelling in a global context. The course builds on nearly a decade of rich heritage. Past examples of training, including pre-training webinars, can be found at the link below.","country":{"id":"GR","name":"GREECE","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"This year the course is focused on the remote sensing of air quality. Key topics will include:\n\n- The recently launched Sentinel-4 and Sentinel-5 missions\ntools and techniques for retrieving concentrations of pollutant gases from satellites.\n- Principles of atmospheric chemistry/dynamics and relevance on climate and air quality.\n- Combining data from different satellite instruments.\n- Methods underlying how high-quality satellite retrievals can improve the reliability of air quality models and forecasts.\n- Science communication.\n\nAdditional aims include fostering collaboration among participants and encouraging the development of individual and team projects using the data, resources, and methodologies present","summary":"The training will introduce the participants to state-of-the-art satellite remote sensing, ground-based and in-situ measurement techniques for atmospheric composition monitoring an","content":null,"targetAudience":"The training is of interest for PhD students, early-career scientists, researchers from academia and research institutes, industry, and anyone interested in atmospheric composition monitoring and modelling. On-site training participation is limited, and selection is competitive.\n\nWe are pleased to announce that the webinars prior to the in-person training will be accessible to all. Basic knowledge in the concept of remote sensing and working knowledge of python is expected.\n\nParticipants from ESA, EUMETSAT and ECMWF member states are given preference for the in-person training; however, participants from all other countries are also welcome to apply, subject to availability of space.","registrationHowto":"Submit your application on the official [website](https://atmostraining2026.esa.int/).","registrationEndDate":1779235140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":11762,"name":"Noemi Marsico","email":"noemi.marsico@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":223,"value":"ESA","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":221,"value":"ECMWF","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":20,"name":"WEkEO"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2743,"created":1787566453000,"updated":1787566748000,"title":"NWC SAF MTG-I Lightning Imager Prototype Products Workshop","titleNative":"NWC SAF MTG-I Lightning Imager Prototype Products Workshop","startDate":1792054800000,"endDate":1792058400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Ana Fazinić","contactEmail":"eumetrain@gmail.com","contactUrl":"https://www.eumetrain.org/","description":"Join this event to learn about the upcoming NWC SAF GEO-LI software package and the new generation of products based on data from the MTG Lightning Imager. The workshop will offer participants useful guidance on how to interpret and exploit LI-based products and their use in combination with other satellite products available in the NWC SAF EWC Viewer based on ADAGUC.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn how to interpret and effectively use the new LI-based products.","summary":"An online workshop to learn about the upcoming NWC SAF GEO-LI software package and the new generation of products based on data from the MTG Lightning Imager.","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, researchers and anyone interested in LI-based satellite products.","registrationHowto":"Registration is free to everyone.\nTo receive the meeting link, register for the workshop [here](https://forms.gle/EgkDU8PA8GoRf2TY6).\n\nTo find out more, check out the [agenda](https://resources.eumetrain.org/events/NWCSAF_MTGLI_workshop.pdf).","registrationEndDate":1792195140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":12935,"name":"Ana Fazinic","email":"ana.fazinic@dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true},{"id":244,"value":"NWC SAF","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2756,"created":1790349525000,"updated":1790349565000,"title":"Geostationary Remote Sensing of Aerosols for Air Quality Applications in North America","titleNative":"Geostationary Remote Sensing of Aerosols for Air Quality Applications in North America","startDate":1791903600000,"endDate":1792081800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/geostationary-remote-sensing-aerosols-air-quality-applications-north-america","description":"The Tropospheric Emissions: Monitoring of Pollution (TEMPO) mission is the first NASA instrument to continuously measure daytime air pollution over North America, from the Atlantic Ocean to the Pacific and from Central Canada to Mexico City, using hyperspectral imagery. Together with the Advanced Baseline Imager (ABI) on the Geostationary Operational Environmental Satellite–R Series (GOES-R)—which provides visible to infrared multispectral information every 1-10 minutes—these geostationary sensors form a powerful constellation for understanding diurnal changes in aerosols, their sources, their movement over North America, and their impacts on air quality. \n\nTEMPO’s UV-visible observations make possible new geostationary aerosol products, including Aerosol Layer Height (ALH), UV Absorbing Aerosol Index (AAI), and hourly surface estimated PM2.5 concentration. In addition, the synergy between TEMPO and ABI enhances the existing geostationary Aerosol Optical Depth (AOD) and Aerosol Detection Smoke/Dust mask products.\n\nThis training will provide an overview of TEMPO capabilities and available NOAA aerosol products generated using synergistic TEMPO and ABI observations. Instructors will demonstrate how to access near real-time and archived TEMPO aerosol products imagery on the NOAA AerosolWatch website. \n\nThis training includes hands-on exercises that walk participants through accessing TEMPO aerosol products imagery on AerosolWatch, while also demonstrating how to interpret these observations to assess the scope of smoke and blowing dust aerosol hazards and their potential impacts on air quality.","country":null,"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\nDescribe the capabilities of the TEMPO instrument and its advantages and disadvantages compared to ABI on the GOES-R satellites.\n\nIdentify available TEMPO aerosol data products and recognize their characteristics, benefits, and limitations.\n\nUse the AerosolWatch website to visualize near real-time and archived hourly TEMPO aerosol product imagery.\n\nInterpret TEMPO aerosol imagery on AerosolWatch to analyze smoke and blowing dust events and anticipate their air quality impacts.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"North American air quality managers & forecasters within the TEMPO field of regard\n\nAerosol, atmospheric composition, and air quality research scientists","registrationHowto":"Please register here: https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/geostationary-remote-sensing-aerosols-air-quality-applications-north-america\n\nCourse Format\nThe complete course consists of two 90-minute parts, with part 1 offered on October 13, and part 2 on October 15, 2026.\n\nOn each day, there are two opportunities to take the course (identical offerings):\nSession A: 11:00 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. EDT (UTC-4)\nSession B: 3:00 p.m. to 4:30 p.m. EDT (UTC-4)\n\nEach part will include a 30-minute live Q&A.\n\nThose who attend parts 1 and 2 and complete the homework by the due date will receive a certificate of attendance.","registrationEndDate":1792076400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"title":"Aerosols","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":22,"title":"Air quality","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2752,"created":1789545330000,"updated":1789625014000,"title":"Online International Training on RGB Analysis Technique for Himawari Satellite Data","titleNative":"Online International Training on RGB Analysis Technique for Himawari Satellite Data","startDate":1791770400000,"endDate":1792126800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"BMKG, Indonesia","contactPerson":"Khafid Rizki Pratama","contactEmail":"khafid.pratama@bmkg.go.id","contactUrl":"link.bmkg.go.id/trainingvlab2026bmkg","description":"The program introduces the scientific foundations of satellite remote sensing, particularly focusing on how multispectral observations from the Advanced Himawari Imager (AHI) can be transformed into meaningful RGB (Red-Green-Blue) composite products. RGB techniques combine information from multiple spectral channels such as visible, near-infrared, and infrared wavelengths into a single color image, where each color component (red, green, and blue) represents specific physical properties of the atmosphere or Earth's surface. By integrating these channels, RGB composites enhance the visual differentiation of atmospheric phenomena that may not be easily distinguished in single-channel imagery, allowing users to quickly identify cloud types, cloud phase, cloud top temperature, moisture distribution, dust and volcanic ash plumes, smoke, fog, and various surface characteristics. The training also emphasizes interpretation skills — understanding how color signatures correspond to meteorological processes such as deep convection, tropical cyclone development, frontal systems, severe storms, and heavy rainfall potential. In addition, the course highlights the operational application of RGB imagery in weather forecasting and nowcasting, supporting early warning systems, aviation safety, maritime operations, disaster risk reduction, and environmental monitoring.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"1. Identify official data sources and platforms, download Himawari AHI data in appropriate formats, and\nunderstand data availability, latency, and file structures for operational use.\n2. Apply proper data management practices, including file organization, metadata understanding, data storage\nstrategies, and basic data quality control to ensure reliable analysis.\n3. Process multispectral Himawari data to create standard RGB products using appropriate software tools such\nas SATAID, including correct channel selection, band combinations, and enhancement techniques.\n4. Analyze RGB composites to identify cloud characteristics, convective activity, moisture patterns, dust,\nvolcanic ash, fog, and other significant atmospheric phenomena.\n5. Integrate RGB products into real-time forecasting workflows to support weather monitoring, early warning\nsystems, aviation safety, and disaster risk reduction.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"The training is open to meteorological, climate, hydrological, and related technical personnel from relevant national institutions, agencies and universities involved in weather monitoring, forecasting, satellite meteorology, disaster risk reduction, aviation meteorology, and environmental monitoring, with priority given to participants from National Meteorological and Hydrological Services (NMHSs)","registrationHowto":"Please register here: [link.bmkg.go.id/trainingvlab2026bmkg](https://)","registrationEndDate":1791331140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":12861,"name":"Khafid Pratama","email":"khafid.pratama@bmkg.go.id","agency":"","country":"ID","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":32,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Indonesia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":274,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Indonesia ","visible":true},{"id":254,"value":"JMA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":8,"value":"PWS: Weather Broadcasters and Communicators"},{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "},{"id":10,"value":"PWS: Advisors Supporting Disaster Prevention and Mitigation and Other User Activities"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2624,"created":1759915390000,"updated":1759926459000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1791194400000,"endDate":1791550800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"The testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. \n\nAt these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.","summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the are operational forecasters with a strong background in severe storms forecasting.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. Nominated candidates can apply at: \nhttps://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158.\n","registrationEndDate":1774483140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":15,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":235,"value":"ESSL","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":137,"name":"SEVIRI","uniqueName":"SEVIRI (MSG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":140,"name":"LI","uniqueName":"LI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2744,"created":1788784739000,"updated":null,"title":"The edge of tomorrow: Collaborative operational multi-hazard multi-impact forecasting","titleNative":"The edge of tomorrow: Collaborative operational multi-hazard multi-impact forecasting","startDate":1790679600000,"endDate":1790683200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem93","description":"Weather conditions have a significant impact on public demand for First Response Services. In a changing climate, we do not only see an increased frequency of extreme weather and corresponding risks for society; in addition, we see a concerning increase, over multiple decades, of 'risk correlation'. In practical terms, this means that we see an increasing number of days on which multiple branches of the First Response Services experience a risk of high service demand, at the same time.\n\nAs such, climate change and associated risk correlation have the potential to erode diversification of First Response Services: Instead of responding to one type of impact on one day, and another type of impact the next day, First Response Services will more often experience multi-impact scenarios, where they will have to respond to multiple impacts simultaneously. The ultimate effect would be an overload of combined First Response services, to the extend of First Response service-denial to citizens in need of help.\n\nAt KNMI, in a daily cycle, we run 14-day quantitative impact forecasts for six types of First Response impact. Over the past years, getting here was not only a technical AI/ML challenge. Mostly, this journey was about collaboration: We have built this operational impact forecast in a collaborative process of co-design with First Responders; and we have done so in an internal research-to-operations (R2O) process that was tailored to zero-to-one R2O, instead of the usual incremental R2O process.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/6bc9ef47-c170-41d4-88fa-bbdf3e2938e8@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2755,"created":1790158458000,"updated":1791306097000,"title":"Quarter 3 African Weather Briefing","titleNative":"Quarter 3 African Weather Briefing","startDate":1790586000000,"endDate":1790589600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"ASMET","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.tools.eumetsat.int/videos/AfricaWeatherBriefing/Weather_Briefing_28Sep2026_SAWS.mp4","description":"El Niño 2026/27: From Climate Signal to Satellite Observations\n\nThe South African Weather Service, in collaboration with EUMETSAT, organises a weather briefing, which is open to everyone, to discuss the current weather situation, using various satellite products, plus NWP models. In this briefing, we are going to discuss how a strong climate signal translates into what we actually see in the atmosphere.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"https://training.tools.eumetsat.int/videos/AfricaWeatherBriefing/saws_briefing_mogale_engelbrecht.pdf","summary":"An online weather briefing, open to everyone, to discuss the current weather situation, using various satellite products, plus NWP models in Africa.","content":null,"targetAudience":"African meteorologists.","registrationHowto":"To participate in the briefing, please [register](https://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/9Gj58sbzTC6HDwKXESjNVg#/registration).\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":454,"name":"Jannie Stander","email":"jannie.stander@weathersa.co.za","agency":" South African Weather Service","country":"ZA","programme":" ","trainingPartner":{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":258,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2764,"created":1792077133000,"updated":1792490641000,"title":"Products and applications of weather satellites","titleNative":"Productos y aplicaciones de los satélites meteorológicos","startDate":1790586000000,"endDate":1792537200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"AECID","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This three-week online course is the first phase of a two-stage training programme. It aims to prepare participants for the subsequent one-week face-to-face session.\n\nThe course comprises a total of 20 hours. Each week includes a one-hour synchronous session for questions and clarification.\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"* Select and interpret appropriate satellite products for real-world meteorological situations.\n* Apply and share the acquired knowledge in the operational environment.\n* Use satellite products to derive information for operational forecasting and decision-making.","summary":"Online training for Latin American and Caribbean meteorological professionals on the use of satellite data, instruments and products for meteorological applications.","content":null,"targetAudience":"Personnel from the National Meteorological and Hydrological Services of Latin American and Caribbean countries participating in CIMHET (Conference of Ibero-American National Meteorological and Hydrological Services), with professional expertise in agrometeorology.","registrationHowto":"Participation is managed through direct invitations to the member institutions of the Conference of Directors of Ibero-American Meteorological and Hydrological Services (CIMHET).","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":257,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":31,"title":"Surface features","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":39,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Terrestrial","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":36,"title":"Fires","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":15,"name":"EUMETCast Terrestrial"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":15,"name":"AVHRR","uniqueName":"AVHRR (Metop)"}]},{"id":2738,"created":1787151519000,"updated":1787151573000,"title":"Agricultural Flash Drought Detection using Solar-Induced Fluorescence (SIF) and Soil Moisture Data","titleNative":"Agricultural Flash Drought Detection using Solar-Induced Fluorescence (SIF) and Soil Moisture Data","startDate":1790265600000,"endDate":1790715600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/agricultural-flash-drought-detection-using-solar-induced-fluorescence-sif-soil","description":"Flash droughts are rapidly developing drought events that severely affect vegetation health, resulting in reduced crop yields and increased wildfire risk. Unlike long-term droughts, which develop gradually and can persist for multiple years, flash droughts emerge over a period of weeks and occur on subseasonal to seasonal timescale. Timely detection is essential for effective monitoring and response.\n\nThis intermediate training focuses on the use of solar-induced fluorescence (SIF) observations from satellites to detect the early vegetation stress associated with flash droughts and to assess their impacts on natural and managed ecosystems. Participants will learn how SIF measurements from the Orbiting Carbon Observatory-2 (OCO-2) provide insights on changes in photosynthetic activity, enabling the early detection of vegetation stress before visible changes occur.\n\nBecause vegetation responses are closely linked to water availability, the training also incorporates soil moisture observations from the Soil Moisture Active Passive (SMAP) mission. This additional dataset helps characterize land surface moisture conditions to improve flash drought detection.\n\nTogether, SIF and soil moisture observations provide a powerful framework for monitoring the onset and evolution of flash droughts, and they can offer skillful predictions of flash drought with multiple weeks of lead time compared to conventional meteorological and hydrological drought indicators.\n\nThe methodology will be demonstrated through recent historic examples of flash droughts, while highlighting how the methodology can be adapted for flash drought monitoring across global regions.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\nIdentify the causes, risks, and consequences of flash droughts as compared to slowly-evolving droughts.\n\nRecognize how SIF data can be used for the detection and prediction of flash drought events.\n\nCompare the advantages and limitations of SIF, soil moisture, and meteorological data to detect the onset of flash drought.\n\nSynthesize Solar-Induced Fluorescence Rapid Change Index (SIF-RCI) time series data for a selected region using a provided Jupyter Notebook.\n\nRetrieve and manipulate SMAP Soil Moisture (SM) and land process model-based Soil Water Deficit Index (SWDI) time series, and compare with SIF-RCI time series data using a provided Jupyter Notebook.\n\nCompare the implications of different methods for flagging and identifying flash droughts in real-world scenarios.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"National and international water resources managers at local, state, and federal levels. \n\nPublic and private water utilities, natural resources conservation organizations, and fisheries and aquaculture organizations.\n\nAcademic faculty and students.","registrationHowto":"Please register here: \nhttps://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/agricultural-flash-drought-detection-using-solar-induced-fluorescence-sif-soil\n\nThe complete course consists of two 2-hour parts, with Part 1 offered on September 24, 2026 and Part 2 on September 29, 2026.\nOn each day, there are two opportunities to take the course (identical offerings):\nSession A: 12:00 p.m. to 2:00 p.m. EDT (UTC-4)\nSession B: 3:00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. EDT (UTC-4)\nEach part will include a 30-minute live Q&A.\nThose who attend Parts 1 and 2 and complete the homework by the due date will receive a certificate of attendance.","registrationEndDate":1790697600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":58,"name":"SMAP"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":17,"name":"Aqua/Terra"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":46,"name":"MODIS","uniqueName":"MODIS (Aqua/Terra)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":168,"name":"SMAP","uniqueName":"SMAP (SMAP)"}]},{"id":2713,"created":1780596404000,"updated":1780638742000,"title":"Regional Focus Group of the Americas and the Caribbean - September 2026 Weather and Climate Discussion","titleNative":"Regional Focus Group of the Americas and the Caribbean - September 2026 Weather and Climate Discussion","startDate":1790175600000,"endDate":1790181000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Erin Sanders","contactEmail":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"https://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup/","description":"The monthly weather and climate discussions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and focus on WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean). The sessions highlight the use and interpretation of satellite imagery and products for meteorological applications, using SLIDER (http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu) for imagery. Anyone with an interest is welcome to attend.\n\nGoToWebinar is the software platform used. The session will begin at 15:00 UTC, with the webinar opening 10 minutes earlier (14:50 UTC) for those who wish to check their microphone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/3154437743270280030\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5874,"name":"Erin Sanders","email":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":30,"value":"CIRA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true},{"id":257,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":true},{"id":267,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":true},{"id":265,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":true},{"id":266,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2742,"created":1787559871000,"updated":1787563597000,"title":"EUMeTrain Monthly Weather Briefing","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Monthly Weather Briefing","startDate":1790164800000,"endDate":1790167500000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMetrain","contactPerson":"Ana Fazinić","contactEmail":"eumetrain@gmail.com","contactUrl":"https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Once a month, EUMeTrain organises an open to all Weather Briefing to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussion are today's satellite images and the corresponding numerical weather prediction data. A basic knowledge on conceptual models used in satellite meteorology is of advantage to follow the presentations.\n\nThis session will be conducted via Webex.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn which RGB products to use in a particular weather situation, as well as how to interpret the products and single channels.","summary":"An open weather briefing to discuss the present weather situation using satellite images and corresponding numerical weather prediction data. ","content":null,"targetAudience":"The open event could be of interest to forecasters, students and researchers.","registrationHowto":"To join, go to: [https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html](https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html) and follow the instructions.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":12935,"name":"Ana Fazinic","email":"ana.fazinic@dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2733,"created":1785328319000,"updated":1789458498000,"title":"Hands-on workshop on the analysis of active Fire Events during the 2026 EUMETSAT Conference","titleNative":"Hands-on workshop on the analysis of active Fire Events during the 2026 EUMETSAT Conference","startDate":1790080200000,"endDate":1790085600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"trainings@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The Short Course on EUMETSAT Active Fire products will take place on Tuesday, 22 September 2026, from 12:30 to 14:00 CEST, during the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference 2026 in Darmstadt, Germany.\n\nThis hands-on session will introduce participants to active fire monitoring, using Jupyter notebooks to analyse Sentinel-3 NRT FRP, as well as MTG FCI FRP and MTG FCI Fire Temperature products. Attendees will learn how to access, process, and visualise these datasets in order to reproduce the workflow independently after the training session.\n\nParticipants must bring their own laptops, and a basic understanding of Python is required.","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"A hand-on short course on EUMETSAT Active Fire Products during the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference.","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is intended for:\n* Researchers working on wildfire detection and monitoring\n* Data providers and users of satellite-based fire products\n* Developers and analysts interested in integrating active fire datasets into applications","registrationHowto":"To express interest, please select the 'Hands-on analysis of active fire events' workshop option when completing your [conference registration form](https://kuonicongress.eventsair.com/eumetsat-2026/registration/Site/Register)  for the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference 2026.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":11805,"name":"Noemi Fazzini","email":"noemi.fazzini@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":16,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":36,"title":"Fires","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":20,"name":"WEkEO"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":163,"name":"SLSTR","uniqueName":"SLSTR (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2698,"created":1776262425000,"updated":1776941161000,"title":"9th European Weather Cloud (EWC) User Workshop","titleNative":"9th European Weather Cloud (EWC) User Workshop","startDate":1790058600000,"endDate":1790091000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"support@europeanweather.cloud","contactUrl":"","description":"A hybrid event hosted at EUMETSAT, as part of its 40th anniversary, bringing the European Weather Cloud (EWC) user community together to discuss the latest developments, use cases, and future possibilities of the EWC. \n\nJointly organised by EUMETSAT and ECMWF, the workshop provides an opportunity for users to engage directly with the teams behind the EWC, and with peers who are leveraging this platform for various applications in meteorology, climate, and environmental science. Users from diverse backgrounds, ranging from fisheries and environmental monitoring to weather prediction and AI-driven modelling, will share their experiences, challenges, and innovative solutions developed using EWC. This segment highlights the real-world applications of the cloud.\n\nThe full agenda is coming soon.\n\nAttendees can join on-site at EUMETSAT, Darmstadt, Germany, or online.\nThe workshop is open to participants from ECMWF and EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating States.\n\nIf you’re interested in presenting your own example of using the EWC, during the next workshops, get in touch with us through our [support portal](http://support.europeanweather.cloud).","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"**Stay informed**: Users will get the latest updates on EWC, including new features, capabilities, and plans for the future.\n\n**Learn from real-world use cases**: users will discover how other users are making the most of the EWC for their unique applications and gain inspiration for your own projects.\n\n**Engage with the community**: Users will have the chance to connect with other EWC users, share insights, and find potential collaborators.\n\n**Provide feedback**: Users will be able to share their thoughts with the EWC team to help shape future improvements.","summary":"A hybrid event hosted at EUMETSAT, as part of its 40th anniversary, bringing the European Weather Cloud (EWC) user community together to discuss the latest developments, use cases,","content":null,"targetAudience":"Participants from EUMETSAT and ECMWF Member and Co-operating States. ","registrationHowto":"Register [on the event page](https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_cQlDBMfJRTGbJilDPpKzWA#/registration).","registrationEndDate":1785517200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":7912,"name":"Niklas Jordan","email":"niklas.jordan@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"HYBRID","attendeeCount":85,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":224,"value":"ECMWF","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2724,"created":1781779704000,"updated":1784638838000,"title":"Innovation Café - Celebrating 40 years of innovation at EUMETSAT ","titleNative":"Innovation Café - Celebrating 40 years of innovation at EUMETSAT ","startDate":1790013600000,"endDate":1790024400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"TU Darmstadt","contactPerson":"Daniel Lee; Sahar Dehnavi","contactEmail":"Daniel.Lee@eumetsat.int; Sahar.Dehnavi@external.eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=OeVNzEKNvEqNINJWuR836m4dh4mOfl5CgzjBsEf2li1URUdCODdRQzhHWDU5T1I1SkpWR0hORklWNi4u&route=shorturl","description":"Join us as we celebrate 40 years of innovation at EUMETSAT by reviewing our legacy, examining how our environment has changed, and looking forward to what the next 40 years might hold. Expect an evening filled with insights, interaction, as well as a bit of the unexpected.\n\nThe Innovation Café is a joint event organised by EUMETSAT and ESOC. This edition is unique as it zooms in on this important milestone in EUMETSAT's history. Come for the ideas, stay for the conversations, and leave with inspiration for what we can achieve with the next 40 years.\n\nThe event is taking place after the first day of the EUMETSAT Conference — so if you’re attending, simply continue the conversation with us at the Innovation Café. If you are not attending the conference, we'd still love to see you!\n\nThe location of the event is Franziska-Braun-Straße 10, 64287 Darmstadt-Ost L4|02 Hörsaal- und Medienzentrum (HMZ). ","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Here is a rough agenda:\n\n* 18:00 – Doors open\n* 18:30 – Welcome and refreshments \n* 18:45 – Icebreaker\n* 19:05 – Talk: 40 years of innovation and impact\n* 19:15 – Interactive session\n* 19:35 – Talk: The changing landscape — new users, use cases & capabilities\n* 19:45 – Interactive session\n* 20:05 – Talk: The next 40 years — where do we go from here?\n* 20:15 – Interactive session\n* 20:30 – Networking\n* 21:00 – Close.","summary":"Join us as we celebrate 40 years of innovation at EUMETSAT by reviewing our legacy, examining how our environment has changed, and looking forward to what the next 40 years might h","content":null,"targetAudience":"Everyone interested in innovation.","registrationHowto":"Sign up [here](https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=OeVNzEKNvEqNINJWuR836m4dh4mOfl5CgzjBsEf2li1URUdCODdRQzhHWDU5T1I1SkpWR0hORklWNi4u&route=shorturlhttps://).\n\nJoin our [mailing list](https://forms.office.com/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=OeVNzEKNvEqNINJWuR836m4dh4mOfl5CgzjBsEf2li1UNU1NUkNVQjJHR0hFMU1IRFpTVlhNVU5UUi4u&route=shorturl) to hear about other upcoming activities.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":108,"value":"Meeting"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2754,"created":1789737636000,"updated":1789978856000,"title":"EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference 2026","titleNative":"EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference 2026","startDate":1789980300000,"endDate":1790343000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"","contactUrl":"https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-meteorological-satellite-conference-2026","description":"The EUMETSAT user conference is a key annual event for the meteorological and scientific communities, where participants from around the world can meet to share their experience and knowledge during plenary, poster, and workshop sessions.\n\nThe main theme of the conference this year is '40th Anniversary of EUMETSAT – Advancing Earth System Satellites for Europe and Beyond'.\n\nThe year 2026 marks the 40th anniversary of the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), established in 1986 to deliver operational satellite data for weather, climate, and environmental monitoring. Over the past four decades, EUMETSAT has grown into a key pillar of the global operational Earth observation system. The organisation operates an advanced fleet of polar-orbiting and geostationary satellites, which play a prominent role in today’s global weather and air-quality forecasting, and it contributes actively to international partnerships.\n","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"EUMETSAT conference is a key annual event for the meteorological and science communities where participants can share their experience and knowledge on satellites and applications.","content":null,"targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Register at the [official event page](https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-meteorological-satellite-conference-2026).","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"Yes","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2736,"created":1786008764000,"updated":1789042790000,"title":"EUMETSAT altimetry: Why measure water surface level? Applications and uses of altimetry","titleNative":"EUMETSAT altimetry: Why measure water surface level? Applications and uses of altimetry","startDate":1789560000000,"endDate":1789567200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT marine training team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=621","description":"Radar altimetry has evolved from a technique developed primarily for geodesy and oceanographic research into a fundamental Earth observation capability, supporting an increasingly wide range of scientific and operational applications. Measurements of water surface height provide essential information for monitoring sea level, ocean circulation, mesoscale dynamics, and long-term climate variability, while also supporting coastal applications, wave forecasting, marine ecosystem studies, inland hydrology, cryosphere research, and geodesy.\n\nThis two-hour online event provides an overview of the current applications of satellite altimetry, and the latest EUMETSAT and Copernicus products available to support them. Participants will explore how altimetry measurements are used across different domains, with practical examples illustrating the information that can be derived from satellite observations of water surface height and related parameters.\n\nThe session will also provide guidance on selecting appropriate altimetry datasets, processing levels, and data latencies according to user needs. Particular attention will be given to the range of products and data access services available through the EUMETSAT and Copernicus ecosystems, helping users identify the most suitable data for their applications.\n\nThe course will include a practical demonstration using Jupyter Notebooks, providing participants with an opportunity to explore altimetry data and tools in a hands-on environment. The latest user support resources, including documentation, training materials, and practical examples, will also be highlighted.\n\nThis event is intended for existing and prospective users of satellite altimetry who would like to broaden their understanding of its applications, and learn how to make better use of available data and tools. It will be particularly valuable for participants planning to attend the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference, providing an opportunity to become familiar with current altimetry products, applications, and services in advance of the meeting. Attendees will, therefore, be well prepared to engage with EUMETSAT experts and take full advantage of technical discussions throughout the conference.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this event, participants will be able to:\n\n* Describe the main scientific and operational applications of satellite radar altimetry.\n* Understand how altimetry measurements can be used across ocean and coastal applications.\n* Identify appropriate altimetry datasets and processing levels for different user requirements.\n* Understand the importance of data latency and product characteristics when selecting datasets.\n* Access and explore altimetry data using EUMETSAT and Copernicus tools and services.\n* Make use of available documentation, training materials, Jupyter Notebooks, and other user support resources.","summary":"A two-hour overview of satellite altimetry applications, products, and tools, with practical examples and Jupyter Notebooks.","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is open to all, but is primarily designed for:\n\n* Established and early career remote sensing researchers with an interest in altimetry.\n* Private and public sector specialists engaged in marine and coastal monitoring activities.\n* Marine forecasters.\n* Those attending the coming EUMETSAT conference, who wish to discuss marine applications.","registrationHowto":"Please [register](https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_jvApfkWZRJ-cZTTO0G_JqQ) to attend the webinar.","registrationEndDate":1789560000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":9,"name":"Sentinel-6"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"name":"Jason"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":164,"name":"SRAL","uniqueName":"SRAL (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":103,"name":"Poseidon-3B","uniqueName":"Poseidon-3B (Jason)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":167,"name":"Poseidon-4","uniqueName":"Poseidon-4 (Sentinel-6)"}]},{"id":2623,"created":1759915368000,"updated":1788959958000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1789380000000,"endDate":1789736400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"The testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. \n\nAt these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.","summary":"A series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists/forecasters to use Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) data.","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the are operational forecasters with a strong background in severe storms forecasting.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. Nominated candidates can apply at: \nhttps://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158.\n","registrationEndDate":1774483140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":12,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":235,"value":"ESSL","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":137,"name":"SEVIRI","uniqueName":"SEVIRI (MSG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":140,"name":"LI","uniqueName":"LI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2735,"created":1785928276000,"updated":1788875726000,"title":"EUMETSAT Ocean Colour: Recent Updates to Sentinel-3 OLCI Marine Products, Tools and User Support","titleNative":"EUMETSAT Ocean Colour: Recent Updates to Sentinel-3 OLCI Marine Products, Tools and User Support","startDate":1788955200000,"endDate":1788962400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT marine training team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=620","description":"Ocean colour observations from Copernicus Sentinel-3 OLCI provide essential information for monitoring marine ecosystems, water quality, biogeochemical processes, and the health of the global ocean. Recent months have seen significant developments to EUMETSAT's Sentinel-3 OLCI marine product portfolio, including updates to processing, new product formats and variables, and an expanding range of tools and user support resources.\n\nThis two-hour online event provides a concise update on the latest developments to EUMETSAT's Sentinel-3 OLCI marine products. Participants will gain an overview of recent changes to the operational product suite, including updates to product processing, data formats, marine geophysical products, and access services.\n\nThe session will also showcase the latest user support resources available through EUMETSAT, including documentation, software tools, training materials, and practical examples, designed to help users transition to the latest products.\n\nThis event is intended for existing and prospective users of EUMETSAT Sentinel-3 OLCI marine products who wish to stay up to date with the latest developments. It will be particularly valuable for participants planning to attend the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference, providing an opportunity to become familiar with recent product and service developments in advance of the meeting. Attendees will, therefore, be well prepared to engage with EUMETSAT product experts and take full advantage of technical discussions throughout the conference.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this event, participants will be able to:\n\n* Describe the recent developments across EUMETSAT's Sentinel-3 OLCI marine product portfolio.\n* Understand the latest updates to Sentinel-3 OLCI processing, products, and services.\n* Identify the most appropriate EUMETSAT products and supporting resources for their applications.\n* Access and make use of the latest documentation, software tools, and training materials.\n* Engage with EUMETSAT experts and the wider user community on current and forthcoming developments.","summary":"A two-hour update on recent developments to EUMETSAT ocean colour products, tools and user support.","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is open to all, but is primarily designed for:\n\n* Established and early career remote s