on Winter Weather","titleNative":"EUMETCAL Hackathon on Winter Weather","startDate":1788739200000,"endDate":1789084800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Norrköping","host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1wgY6vEngV9K2thAW4mNxNRLdLW68gGxH/view","description":"We’re excited to invite you to the 2026 EUMETCAL Hackathon on Winter Weather, where we’ll collaborate to build online training materials—for new forecasters or as pre-winter refreshers.\n\nWho should join?\nMeteorological forecasters, instructional designers, and researchers with winter weather expertise. Your skills can make a real impact.\n\nWhy participate?\n- Shape the future of meteorological training in Europe\n- Work alongside experts from across the field\n- Develop practical resources in a hands-on, creative environment\n\nWhen & where?\n7–11 September 2026\nSMHI, Norrköping (Sweden)\n\nNew to EUMETCAL hackathons?\nSee the invitation and this video for details:\n\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1wgY6vEngV9K2thAW4mNxNRLdLW68gGxH/view?usp=sharing\n\nhttps://youtu.be/-hss36ut76E\n \nReady to contribute?\nAll practical info is in the attached invitation. We’d love to have you with us.\n\nLet’s build better winter weather training—together.  ","country":{"id":"SE","name":"SWEDEN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"forms.office.com/e/D2a9iS0Ud6","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":105,"value":"Hackathon"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2732,"created":1785322348000,"updated":1789458533000,"title":"CACGP-IGAC Early Career Short Course","titleNative":"CACGP-IGAC Early Career Short Course","startDate":1788480000000,"endDate":1788652800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Heraklion","host":"iCACGP-IGAC","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico ","contactEmail":"trainings@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The IGAC Early Career Short Course is a 40 person three-day peer-designed course, with hands-on training, on atmospheric chemistry, data analysis, international network building, and soft skills training.\n\nAs part of the course, EUMETSAT experts will deliver a three-hour interactive workshop on remote sensing that combines theoretical concepts with practical applications. Participants will gain hands-on experience exploring atmospheric composition data using EUMETView and Jupyter notebooks, through guided demonstrations and interactive exercises, providing a practical introduction to satellite-based atmospheric observations.","country":{"id":"GR","name":"GREECE","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"*  Participants will become familiar with the EUMETSAT data access tools and AC resources.\n*  Participants will learn to use EUMETView in the GUI and through QGIS.\n*  Participants will learn how to visualise a volcanic eruption from space, visualise ash, SO2, and dust plumes, and follow their evolution.\n*  Participants will gain experience in using WEkEO.","summary":"Part of the IGAC Early Career Short Course, this 3-hour workshop offers hands-on training in atmospheric composition remote sensing EUMETSAT products, using EUMETView and Jupyter.","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is intended for 'early career researchers', defined for this purpose as PhD or Masters students, or people within three years of graduation from a PhD or Masters programme. Undergraduates, or people not yet enrolled in a PhD or Masters programme, are not eligible.","registrationHowto":"Please fill in the [survey](https://icacgp-igac2026.org/early-career-short-course/).","registrationEndDate":1772755140000,"fees":"Yes","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":11805,"name":"Noemi Fazzini","email":"noemi.fazzini@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"title":"Aerosols","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":20,"name":"WEkEO"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":57,"name":"Sentinel-5P"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":121,"name":"IASI","uniqueName":"IASI (Metop)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":165,"name":"TROPOMI","uniqueName":"TROPOMI (Sentinel-5P)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2734,"created":1785925281000,"updated":1786628654000,"title":"EUMETSAT Sea Surface Temperature and Ice Surface Temperature: Recent Updates to Products, Tools and User Support","titleNative":"EUMETSAT Sea Surface Temperature and Ice Surface Temperature: Recent Updates to Products, Tools and User Support","startDate":1788350400000,"endDate":1788357600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT marine training team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=619","description":"Sea Surface Temperature (SST) and Ice Surface Temperature (IST) products are fundamental to a wide range of applications, from numerical weather prediction and ocean forecasting to climate monitoring and polar research. Over recent years, EUMETSAT has introduced significant developments across its operational temperature product portfolio, including new Copernicus Sentinel-3 SLSTR products, enhancements delivered through the Ocean and Sea Ice Satellite Application Facility (OSI SAF), and an expanding range of user support resources.\n\nThis two-hour online event provides a concise update on the latest developments to EUMETSAT's SST and IST products. Participants will gain an overview of recent changes to the operational product suite, including the introduction of new geophysical parameters, such as Sea Surface Temperature at Depth (SSTdepth) and Sea Ice Surface Temperature (IST), alongside updates to processing, product availability, and access services.\n\nThe session will also showcase the latest user support resources available through EUMETSAT, including documentation, software tools, training materials, and practical examples, designed to help users transition to new products and workflows with confidence.\n\nThis event is intended for existing and prospective users of EUMETSAT SST and IST products who wish to stay up to date with the latest developments. It will be particularly valuable for participants planning to attend the EUMETSAT Meteorological Satellite Conference, providing an opportunity to become familiar with recent product and service developments in advance of the meeting. Attendees will, therefore, be well prepared to engage with EUMETSAT product experts and take full advantage of technical discussions throughout the conference.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this event, participants will be able to:\n\n* Describe the recent developments across EUMETSAT's Sea Surface Temperature and Ice Surface Temperature product portfolio.\n* Understand the new capabilities offered by recent Sentinel-3 SLSTR and OSI SAF product developments.\n* Identify the most appropriate EUMETSAT products, and supporting resources, for their applications.\n* Access and make use of the latest documentation, software tools, and training materials.\n* Engage with EUMETSAT experts and the wider user community on current and forthcoming developments.","summary":"A two-hour update on recent developments to EUMETSAT SST and IST products, tools and user support.","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is open to all, but is primarily designed for:\n\n* Established and early career remote sensing researchers with an interest in thermal radiometry\n* Private and public sector specialists engaged in marine and coastal monitoring activities\n* Marine forecasters\n* Those attending the EUMETSAT conference who wish to discuss marine applications","registrationHowto":"Please [register](https://eumetsat.zoom.us/j/88698010964?pwd=4a2SowkiNt2dj1FpumsbricCHJaCwZ.1) to attend the webinar.\n","registrationEndDate":1788350400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":241,"value":"OSI SAF","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":21,"value":"Not Applicable"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id"