 one for developers, the other for labelers.\n\nThe event aims to bring together researchers, developers, and stakeholders from the domains of climate and weather from EUMETSAT member states. Preference will be given to national meteorological services, but all meteorological organisations may nominate participants. Researchers from marine, terrestrial, and atmosphere domains are also welcome.\n","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Developers will gain the skills to:\n•\tleverage the European Weather Cloud for Earth Observation (EO) data preparation, using S3 buckets;\n•\tinteract with the Earth System Feature database;\n•\texport feature labels for downstream ML model development on the European Weather Cloud.\n\nLabelers will work with domain experts to learn to:\n•\timport EO data from the European Weather Cloud to LabelStudio;\n•\tnavigate and use tools on the LabelStudio platform, including SAM2;\n•\taccurately label key features in the prepared EO data.","summary":"As part of Machine learning (ML) activities for detection and forecasting of extreme events, EUMETSAT is committed to support its member states by providing data, tools, and commun","content":null,"targetAudience":"Primary: Researchers, developers, and stakeholders from the domains of climate and weather from EUMETSAT member states. \nSecondary: Researchers from marine, terrestrial, and atmosphere domains.","registrationHowto":"National meteorological services and universities, as well as other meteorological organisations from EUMETSAT member states are invited to nominate participants from their organisations. \nNominated candidates should register at https://ec.europa.eu/eusurvey/runner/98cfbcdd-dff7-9eb6-0eaa-baec3334e97d.\n\n\n\n","registrationEndDate":1771200000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":""