TG launches and commissioning (Natasa Strelec Mahovic, EUMETSAT).\n- The Forecaster Testbed 2025 in retrospect and lessons learned from expert workshops (Alois Holzer, ESSL).\n- Testimonial from forecasters who participated in the Forecaster Testbed 2025.\n- Information on how to register for the upcoming Forecaster Testbeds (Natasa Strelec Mahovic, EUMETSAT).\n- Interesting thunderstorm cases from 2025 revisited (Tomas Pucik, ESSL). ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"A two-hour online event to reflect upon the ESSL-EUMETSAT Severe Storms Testbeds organised in 2025, and to announce the 2026 Testbeds.\n\nMTG-related information relevant to forecast","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters","registrationHowto":"Please register on \n[the event page](https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/96eeb2af-f46e-42b9-a3ae-7490cc675570@df7e8a07-a3fd-42a8-b745-17aa52648828).\n\n","registrationEndDate":1774310340000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":235,"value":"ESSL","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":140,"name":"LI","uniqueName":"LI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2678,"created":1770985185000,"updated":1775813980000,"title":"Short Course: Introduction to Fire Products - Part 1","titleNative":"Short Course: Introduction to Fire Products - Part 1","startDate":1773147600000,"endDate":1773153000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KEOAYteCTtOw5u3mlK7u7w","description":"This first session of the two-part webinar series builds a foundational understanding of fires, remote sensing principles, and key Earth Observation products to support more advanced analysis in part 2.\n\nThe session begins with a brief introduction to fire behaviour and dynamics; setting the scene by exploring the environmental relevance of wildfires, and focusing on the role of satellite observations in fire detection and monitoring. An overview of the main satellite missions and fire-related products will be presented to support this fundamental knowledge.\n\nParticipants will then follow a guided demonstration using EUMETView, EUMETSAT’s user-friendly visualisation platform, to identify and explore a real fire event. The demonstration will include:\n\n- Sentinel-3 OLCI RGB imagery to observe smoke plume development and surface features.\n- Sentinel-3 SLSTR Fire Radiative Power (FRP) products to detect active fires and assess their intensity.\n- MTG Fire Temperature RGB data to illustrate fire intensity.\n\nBy combining these datasets, participants will see how different satellite sensors work together to provide a view of fire activity and plume evolution.\n\nThe session concludes with a summary of key resources and guidance for further exploration of fire products and visualisation tools.\n\nThis first session lays the groundwork for the second, which will move beyond the basics into more advanced fire monitoring, analysis techniques, and practical workflows.\n\nResources available here -> https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=600 ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the session, users should be able to:\n\n- Explain the basic principles of wildfire behaviour and the role of satellite remote sensing in detecting, monitoring, and observing fires.\n\n- Identify key Earth Observation fire products used for monitoring active fires and smoke plumes, such as RGB imagery and Fire Radiative Power (FRP).\n\n- Use EUMETView to visualise a fire event, generating images or animations to observe fire activity and plume evolution.\n\n- Recognise key resources and tools for further exploration of fire data following the course.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Beginners","registrationHowto":"Fill in the [Zoom registration form](https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_KEOAYteCTtOw5u3mlK7u7w).","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":11762,"name":"Noemi Marsico","email":"noemi.marsico@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":90,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":36,"title":"Fires","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":163,"name":"SLSTR","uniqueName":"SLSTR (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":162,"name":"OLCI","uniqueName":"OLCI (Sentinel-3)"}]},{"id":2677,"created":1770906647000,"updated":null,"title":"1 year of MTG LI data in action","titleNative":"1 year of MTG LI data in action","startDate":1773144000000,"endDate":1773147600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem80","description":"The Meteosat Third Generation Lightning Imager (MTG-LI) has been operational since 31 October 2024. MTG-LI enables the monitoring of lightning activity from global scales down to single storms. During the year 2025, it observed 608 million lightning flashes, providing users with the most complete characterization of total lightning activity over Europe, Africa, most of the Atlantic Ocean, and parts of South America, the Indian Ocean, and the Middle East. The presentation will illustrate key properties of the lightning activity observed by MTG-LI over the whole year of 2025 including global-scale statistics, regional and high-latitude storm monitoring, and flash level details that the instrument is able to resolve.\n\nThis webinar will be presented by Sven-Erik Enno (EUMETSAT) on 10 March 2026 at 12:00 UTC / 13:00 CET.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/27583ba4-1cfb-494c-a888-1d4cba503377@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSen