Baltic+)","titleNative":"Monitoring warm season frontal precipitation online course (Baltic+)","startDate":1773014400000,"endDate":1774569600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service LHMS","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=586","description":"This course will focus on using Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) products for monitoring warm season frontal precipitation. Topics of the course include the typical challenges forecasters need to deal with forecasting frontal precipitation. Particular emphasis will be given to enhancing the preparedness of the participants to use satellite soundings to identify temperature and moisture structures within fronts. \n\nAn essential part of the course is to work on case studies, to help refresh your skills using the satellite and other products when working in weather forecasting.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Skills in identifying the frontal systems using satellite images.\n- Skills in using satellite soundings for monitoring the temperature and moisture structures within the fronts.  \n- Skills in using satellite-derived precipitation products for frontal cases.\n- Skills in effective use of radar for detecting precipitation. \n- Skills in using NWP guidance for precipitation forecasts. ","summary":"This course will focus on using Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) products for monitoring warm season frontal precipitation. Topics of the course include the typical challenges forec","content":null,"targetAudience":"Weather forecasters in Baltic States, Poland, and Ukraine. ","registrationHowto":"Contact your national point of contact for training for more information on the nomination and application process.\nThis course is open solely for the weather forecasters in Baltic States, Poland, and Ukraine.","registrationEndDate":1769817600000,