, MTG-S (IRS & UVN), MTG data","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\nResearchers\nStudents","registrationHowto":"View the agenda: https://resources.eumetrain.org/events/DraftAgenda-EWDec2025.pdf\n\nRegister on: https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/a2e20758-ae37-4e12-a0d5-01588b036d07@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":1765152000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9945,"name":"Dominik Rukavina","email":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"nan","country":"HR","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2578,"created":1751535879000,"updated":1762861780000,"title":"IOCS Multi-Sensor Ocean Colour Course","titleNative":"IOCS Multi-Sensor Ocean Colour Course","startDate":1765098000000,"endDate":1765472400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Benjamin Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","description":"From 1-5 December 2025, the International Ocean Colour Science meeting (IOCS) will return to Darmstadt, Germany for its 6th iteration. The meeting, which covers optical radiometry of all water types, brings the scientific community and space agencies together to support open communication between the two, informing future missions and driving forward science and applications.\n\nAs part of this year's programme, EUMETSAT, in partnership with the IOCCG, will offer an advanced, multi-sensor ocean colour training course. The event, held from 7-11 December, will be hosted on site at EUMETSAT in Darmstadt and will cover key aspects of satellite ocean colour, including atmospheric correction, bio-optical algorithm selection, product quality, validation and multi-sensor synergy. It will be supported by Copernicus Sentinel-3 OLCI, NASA PACE OCI and Copernicus Sentinel-2 MSI experts and be highly interactive, introducing hands-on examples throughout. Alongside training sessions, participants will have opportunities to learn more about satellite operations.\n\nIn addition to gaining skills needed to access and work with a variety of ocean colour data streams, participants should expect to leave the course with a clear understanding of the challenges we face in ocean colour and the approaches we take to addressing them.\n\n**Important: Please remember that you need to register separately for the IOCS meeting. This can be done via https://iocs.ioccg.org/. Limited support funding is available. Registration costs for the IOCS meeting will be waived for course participants that receive support funding. While you are welcome, and encouraged to, submit abstracts, please do not pay the IOCS registration fee if you are applying for the course with support funding. More information is available on the course application page.**","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants completing this course will:\n\n- be able to access, download and work with single-sensor ocean colour data from multiple sensors\n- understand the advantages, consequences and limitations associated with differing approaches to atmospheric correction\n- appreciate the complexity of selecting bio-optical algorithms for ocean colour retrievals \n- know how to assess and apply product flags, determine product quality, and construct match-up validation workflows\n- be familiar with the key considerations needed for multi-sensor synergy\n- gain experience of operational satellite data production","summary":"From 1-5 December 2025, the International Ocean Colour Science meeting (IOCS) will return to Darmstadt, Germany for its 6th iteration. The meeting, which covers optical radiometry ","content":null,"targetAudience":"This is an advanced level training event, designed to support those already engaged in satellite ocean colour activities. Training is aimed at, but not restricted to:\n\n* early and mid-career researchers who are already working with ocean colour in some capacity at the graduate or postgraduate level\n* oceanographers involved in marine monitoring activities and applications, either public or private, who are looking to expand their understanding of new sensors and approaches\n* service and application developers who are looking to exploit ocean colour data in their workflows\n* ocean colour practitioners interested in working in an operational agency context.\n","registrationHowto":"A limited number of places are available on this course. Visit the “Apply for courses” section of our course <b><a href=\"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158\">Moodle page</a></b> for more information on how to apply and information on travel support.","registrationEndDate":1756166340000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":30,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":237,"value":"IOCCG","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":20,"name":"WEkEO"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":162,"name":"OLCI","uniqueName":"OLCI (Sentinel-3)"}]},{"id":2639,"created":1763135573000,"updated":1763135630000,"title":"NASA Satellite Laser Altimetry for Coastal and Near-Shore Bathymetry","titleNative":"NASA Satellite Laser Altimetry for Coastal and Near-Shore Bathymetry","startDate":1764687600000,"endDate":1764880200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":" brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/nasa-satellite-laser-altimetry-coastal-near-shore-bathymetry-0","description":"This two-part training focuses on NASA data providing near global coverage of coastal and near-shore satellite-derived bathymetry (SDB) measurements from the Advanced Topographic Laser Altimeter System (ATLAS) instrument — a space-based lidar instrument flying on the Ice, Cloud, and land Elevation Satellite 2 (ICESat-2) platform. ATLAS’s green wavelength, photon-counting lidar signal can reach depths of up to 40 meters in regions with adequate water clarity to provide shallow, near-shore bathymetric data for a range of applications, including coastal and marine science management, nearshore habitat research, marine navigation, and engineering applications. The ATL24 product provides near global along-track coastal and nearshore SDB, consisting of refraction-corrected seafloor and sea surface heights, as well as associated uncertainties. This Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET) training will improve users' knowledge of ICESat-2, the ATL24 product, and how to access, plot, and analyze ICESat-2 bathymetry data.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\nIdentify NASA bathymetry data used for global coastal and near-shore bathymetry mapping for risk reduction relating to shipping and navigation.\n\nIdentify the applications and limitations of ICESat-2 bathymetry data (ATL24) for coastal and near-shore bathymetry mapping.\n\nPlot and download ICESat-2 bathymetry data (ATL24) using SlideRule Web Client.\n\nAnalyze ICESat-2 bathymetry data (ATL24) using SlideRule Python Client.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Remote sensing scientists and geospatial analysts public (local, regional, and federal), private industry, and international institutions who use satellite altimetry for bathymetric applications pertaining to risk reduction in coastal and near-shore waters.\n\n","registrationHowto":"Register Here: https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/nasa-satellite-laser-altimetry-coastal-near-shore-bathymetry-0\n\nTwo 1.5-hour parts\nTwo identical sessions will be hosted at two different times of day:\nSession A: 10:00 a.m. to 11:30 a.m. EST (UTC-5)\nSession B: 14:00 p.m. to 15:30 p.m. EST (UTC-5)\nEach part will include a 30-minute live Q&A.","registrationEndDate":1764860400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"title":"Maritime safety","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2616,"created":1759169716000,"updated":1761914979000,"title":"Marine weather workshop","titleNative":"Atelier de prévision maritime","startDate":1764579600000,"endDate":1764939600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Casablanca","host":"General Directorate of Meteorology of Morocco ","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"Cet atelier vise à renforcer les capacités en télédétection spatiale et son application à la prévision maritime. Le cours combinera des séances pratiques et des présentations axées sur l’utilisation opérationnelle efficace des données satellitaires altimétriques et diffusiométriques.\n\n\n","country":{"id":"MA","name":"MOROCCO","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"À l’issue de l’atelier, les participants seront capables de :\n\n- Analyser les conditions de surface réelles à l’aide des données altimétriques et diffusiométriques.\n- Surveiller l’évolution des conditions de surface de la mer.\n- Intégrer ces données satellitaires avec les données issues de modèles numériques pour valider les sorties de modèle.\n- Accéder aux données et les visualiser efficacement.\n- Déterminer comment l’utilisation de la vaste gamme de produits disponibles auprès d’EUMETSAT peut améliorer la qualité de l’analyse météorologique maritime.\n\n","summary":"Cet atelier vise à renforcer les capacités en télédétection spatiale et son application à la prévision maritime. Le cours combinera des séances pratiques et des présentations axées","content":null,"targetAudience":"Experts des centres opérationnels chargés de la prévision et de la surveillance des eaux maritimes africaines, en particulier ceux spécialisés dans l’exploitation des données satellitaires à des fins opérationnelles.","registrationHowto":"","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGrou