aribbean - November 2025 Weather and Climate Discussion","titleNative":"Regional Focus Group of the Americas and the Caribbean - November 2025 Weather and Climate Discussion","startDate":1762963200000,"endDate":1762968600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Erin Sanders","contactEmail":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"https://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup/","description":"The monthly weather and climate discussions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and focus on WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean). The sessions highlight the use and interpretation of satellite imagery and products for meteorological applications, using SLIDER (http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu) for imagery. Anyone with an interest is welcome to attend.\n\nGoToWebinar is the software platform used. The session will begin at 16:00 UTC, with the webinar opening 10 minutes earlier (15:50 UTC) for those who wish to check their microphone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/3035339737088225373","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5874,"name":"Erin Sanders","email":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":30,"value":"CIRA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true},{"id":257,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":true},{"id":267,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":true},{"id":265,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":true},{"id":266,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2636,"created":1762543729000,"updated":1762543762000,"title":"Advanced NASA Earth Observations and Tools for Active Fire, Smoke, and Post-Fire Monitoring","titleNative":"Advanced NASA Earth Observations and Tools for Active Fire, Smoke, and Post-Fire Monitoring","startDate":1762963200000,"endDate":1763586000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/advanced-nasa-earth-observations-tools-active-fire-smoke-post-fire-monitoring","description":"Satellite observations can be used to detect active fires as well as monitor the impacts of fires on air quality and ecosystems. Monitoring post-fire impacts to vegetation is essential for evaluating burn severity, which informs post-fire debris flow risk; understanding patterns in ecosystem recovery; and identifying areas that require restoration intervention. Wildfire smoke monitoring is also critical for air quality and public health applications, as exposure to fine particulate matter within smoke can cause respiratory issues and other health complications. \n\nAlong with active fires, satellite sensors can detect static thermal anomalies (STA) from natural heat sources, such as volcanoes, or industrial heat sources such as mineral processing plants, gas flares, and waste incinerators. Multiple sources of satellite imagery and derived data products relevant to smoke, post-fire conditions, and STA identification are available within NASA's Fire Information for Resource Management System (FIRMS). \n\nThis two-part training led by NASA's Applied Remote Sensing Training (ARSET) program will introduce participants to several capabilities within FIRMS that were not included in the previous ARSET training, Introduction to NASA Earth Observations and Tools for Wildfire Monitoring and Management. Participants will learn how to use the FIRMS aerosol index indices, burned area products, post-fire indices and imagery, static thermal anomaly information, and how to use Jupyter Notebooks to ingest and visualize active fire detection data.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\nAccess relevant post-fire imagery in the FIRMS Burned Area Mode to assess burned area, burn severity, and other factors for an event of interest.\n\nIdentify and track wildfire smoke over time using Corrected Reflectance, OMPS Aerosol Index, and PyroCB layers available in the FIRMS Smoke/Aerosols Mode. Understand when to use the PyroCb layer.\n\nUse relevant data in FIRMS to identify STA associated with industrial or natural sources that are not vegetation fires.\n\nUse Jupyter Notebooks to access and visualize FIRMS data for different case studies.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Federal, state agency, local government representatives, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), and representatives from academia who are interested in exploring a range of advanced capabilities available in FIRMS to support the identification, monitoring, and management of wildfires and their impacts.\n\nAcademia and research organizations interested in understanding NASA data products and tools provided in FIRMS and considerations for their use for science applications.","registrationHowto":"Two 1-hour parts; An identical session will be offered for each part at two different times of day (Session A: 11 a.m.-12 p.m. EST; Session B: 3-4 p.m. EST)\nRegister here: \nhttps://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/learn/trainings/advanced-nasa-earth-observations-tools-active-fire-smoke-post-fire-monitoring","registrationEndDate":1763582400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":37,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Atmosphere","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":36,"title":"Fires","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":42,"name":"Landsat"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":56,"name":"Sentinel-1"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"name":"NOAA"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":31,"name":"GOES"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":17,"name":"Aqua/Terra"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":189,"name":"VIIRS","uniqueName":"VIIRS (JPSS)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":46,"name":"MODIS","uniqueName":"MODIS (Aqua/Terra)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":97,"name":"AHI","uniqueName":"AHI (Himawari)"}]},{"id":2630,"created":1761298132000,"updated":1761298202000,"title":"AI Meets EO Education: Smarter Content for Smarter Learning","titleNative":"AI Meets EO Education: Smarter Content for Smarter Learning","startDate":1762952400000,"endDate":1762957800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eotecdev.net/%f0%9f%a7%a0-ai-meets-eo-education-smarter-content-for-smarter-learning/","description":"Transforming How We Teach Earth Observation\n\nArtificial intelligence is reshaping the way we design and deliver training. Across the Earth observation (EO) and geospatial community, educators are beginning to use AI tools to generate learning materials, create localized examples, and produce interactive content that connects more effectively with learners around the world.\nThis interactive webinar will explore how AI can empower EO trainers by making their daily work easier, faster, and more effective. Participants will see real-world demonstrations of AI-assisted tools, including ESA’s EVE, and learn how emerging virtual assistants are being developed to make complex data more accessible to learners everywhere.\n\n\nSpeakers and Topics\n\nHosted by EOTEC DevNet, VLab, and EO College, the 90-minute session brings together speakers from:\n- ESA’s Earth Virtual Environment (EVE) initiative\n- VLab’s Training and Education Programme, with its new Generative AI Community of Practice\n- EO College, moderating and sharing insights from generative-AI learning experiments\n\nTogether, they’ll discuss the practical opportunities and real challenges of integrating AI into EO education, from ensuring quality and factual accuracy to managing bias, copyright, and ethics.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/d81615ea-c6c6-440a-b95a-c0de84fc2f8c@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":107,"value":"Webinar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regio