ons, including perceived versus actual learning gains, ethical risks, and audience trust. Whether you're considering adopting this tool or are already experimenting with it, this session will help you make informed and responsible decisions about how—and when—to use AI avatars effectively.\n\nPresenters: Tsvet Ross–Lazarov (COMET) & Fabienne Werder (MeteoSwiss & EUMETCAL Programme)","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/a805096b-3b1b-451a-b7ce-1473d19a493e@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2556,"created":1747130096000,"updated":1756367657000,"title":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: Ocean surface scatterometer winds from OSI SAF and Copernicus Marine Service","titleNative":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: Ocean surface scatterometer winds from OSI SAF and Copernicus Marine Service","startDate":1756800000000,"endDate":1756803600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=566","description":"The Royal Netherlands Meteorological Institute (KNMI) satellite wind team is specialized in retrieving sea surface winds from scatterometer observations. The team is responsible for the production and distribution of OSI SAF wind products and for the scatterometer winds products in the Copernicus Marine Service catalogue. This event will focus on presenting the particularities of these products and their access.\n\nThe different products will be presented by KNMI team members responsible for these products. They will provide a short introduction on scatterometer wind retrieval, explain the differences between the wind products and illustrate how the datasets are organized.\nUsage of these products will then be presented through a specific use case.\n\nThe short course will consist of a 1-hour webinar. Two sessions with the same content will be held on September 2 (08:00 - 09:00 and 13:00 - 14:00 UTC). Participants are invited to choose the session that fits them best. The session will include a Q&A and feedback session. To support participants in using the datasets and tools we highlight, the online Q&A platform will remain open for one week following the webinar. Any queries posted will be quickly responded to.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will:\n- understand the basics of wind retrieval from scatterometers.\n- understand the value and the limitations of these products.\n- know how to access OSI SAF’s and Copernicus Marine Service wind products.\n- have a better understanding of the products available.\n- know which product fits which purpose.\n- learn about planned product evolutions.\n","summary":"The Royal Netherlands Meteorological Institute (KNMI) satellite wind team is specialized in retrieving sea surface winds from scatterometer observations. The team is responsible fo","content":null,"targetAudience":"- Marine/weather forecasters\n- Climate scientists\n- Oceanographers\n- Sailors and sailing application users\n- Private and public sector specialists, e.g. from the wind energy and marine transport sectors\n","registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ttbEXoGaR1inBIbjwSFraw ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":51,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":241,"value":"OSI SAF","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":222,"value":"Copernicus Marine Service","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[{"id":3,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"title":"Maritime safety","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2491,"created":1731073227000,"updated":1751982456000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1756720800000,"endDate":1757077200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes.\n\nThe testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. At these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the are operational forecasters with a strong background in severe storms forecasting.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. \nNominated candidates may apply at: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.ph