 trainings.\n\nThis webinar will be presented by Laura Beaudouin (MeteoSwiss) on 12 June at 12:00 UTC. It is free and open for everyone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/f52b8c53-7054-4713-857e-888fb3913782@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2561,"created":1748460746000,"updated":1748485745000,"title":"Sea Level Change Tools for Planning and Decision Support:","titleNative":"Sea Level Change Tools for Planning and Decision Support:","startDate":1749567600000,"endDate":1750188600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/42kVL8K","description":"Global sea level has been rising at a rate of 3 mm/yr, and this rate is projected to continue to increase sea level over the next century. Scientists use observations from the ground, air, and space, along with theoretical models and scenarios of future emissions, to monitor and study past, present, and future sea-level rise. This information is a fundamental basis for mitigation, adaptation, and risk management planning in all parts of the world and across many elements of society and ecosystems. \n\nThis two-part introductory training series will focus on NASA products and tools available to assess historical sea-level rise, access and understand projections of sea level, and investigate impacts. Participants will be exposed to the causes behind regional and global sea-level changes and explore climate and analysis tools to access, visualize, and perform statistical analysis using NASA data. \n\nCourse Format: Two 1.5-hour sessions including Q&A.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: \n \n1.\tIdentify underlying Earth processes contributing to global and regional, relative sea-level change.\n2.\tRecognize remote sensing and modeled data used for assessing sea level change on a regional to global scale.\n3.\tIdentify how sea level change influences flooding at the coast and how this may impact communities and infrastructure.\n4.\tUse the Sea Level Explorer tool to assess the processes that are contributing to past and future sea-level change, both at global and regional scales.\n5.\tUse the IPCC AR6 Projection Tool to access future projections of relative sea-level change under different emissions scenarios.\n6.\tUse the Pacific Islands Flooding Tool to visualize oceanic and groundwater flooding maps.\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for local, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations, wanting to integrate NASA Earth observations and IPCC projections of sea-level change, as well as impacts, for considerations into their work in different sectors; as well as any practitioners of sea-level observations or projections.","registrationHowto":"Time: 11:00-12:30 and 14:00-15:30 EDT [UTC-4]. An identical session for each part will be offered at two different times of day.\n\nTo Register: https://go.nasa.gov/42kVL8K\n","registrationEndDate":1750183200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2544,"created":1743593414000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Accessing, Customising and Downloading MTG data","titleNative":"Accessing, Customising and Downloading MTG data","startDate":1749549600000,"endDate":1750244400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=567","description":"This series of sessions aims at improve user's understanding of the EUMETSAT processes to download and customise MTG data. It can be used as pre-training in preparation for the MTG week organised by EUMETrain.\n\nAs with every Data Access course, we will focus on the main Data Access Services such as Data Store and its main customisation tool, Data Tailor. We will teach how to access and interpret essential information about the data from the Flexible Combined Imager (FCI) and the Lightning Imager (LI) sensors on the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) satellite.\n\nThe course is organised into three sessions, each featuring presentations and demonstrations. Each session will include a dedicated Q&A segment, providing participants the opportunity to ask for any type of support related to Data Access Services.\n\nThe sessions will be based on User's skills and preferred methodologies to use our services:\n\nSession 1 will be based on using Data Store and Data Tailor Graphical User Interface to download smaller amounts of products and perform basic customisations.This session is designed for users who need to quickly access and tailor smaller datasets to their specific needs.\n\nSession 2 will involve the use of the EUMETSAT Python Library through the use of Command Line Interface (CLI). This session is tailored for users requiring access to larger datasets, providing a comprehensive guide to managing and downloading significant volumes of data.\n\nSession 3 will involve the use of the Data Access Jupyter Notebooks. The session will help users to use pre-built Notebooks for various tasks and supporting them in finding their own solutions by modifying the notebooks.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Users should be able to understand the keywords such as API, GUI, CLI.\n\nUsers will be able to understand the different Pull Data Access Services of EUMETSAT (Data Store and Data Tailor).\n\nUsers will be able to create an account to access the services.\n\nUsers will be able to access the different services and understand their capabilities.\n\nUsers will be able to find the resources on the User Portal.","summary":"This series of sessions aims at improve user's understanding of the EUMETSAT processes to download and customise MTG data. It can be used as pre-training in preparation for the MTG","content":null,"targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Session 1 - 10-06-2025 12:00-13:00 CEST: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_beGaX0pFQrq_ZAM2TPrbIw\n\nSession 2 - 17-06-2025 12:00-13:00 CEST: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_yOg3-l7HSoGnn2HGQ3ahJQ\n\nSession 3 - 18-06-2025 12:00-13:00 CEST: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_69lLF3ZjTW-_vdmNK0iH1A","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":172,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2558,"created":1747299708000,"updated":null,"title":"Met Éireann: Storm Éowyn & Warning Systems","titleNative":"Met Éireann: Storm Éowyn & Warning Systems","startDate":1749121200000,"endDate":1749124800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/75516b31-2087-4a95-8656-eb32531e981c@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","description":"A talk consisting of a review of the recent record-breaking Storm Éowyn which brought hurricane force strength winds to the west coast of Ireland, followed by a discussion on Met Éireann’s warning system.\n\nWe will also discuss current plans on next steps implementing a recently formed impact-based forecasting unit in Met Éireann into our warning systems.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/75516b31-2087-4a95-8656-eb32531e981c@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2555,"created":1746809708000,"updated":1746809916000,"title":"LiDAR Profiling Satellite Observations for Air Quality Applications","titleNative":"LiDAR Profiling Satellite Observations for Air Quality Applications","startDate":1749049200000,"endDate":1749670200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/4jIlOwr","description":"Active remote sensing observations, like those from LiDAR (Light Detection And Ranging), can provide information on the vertical structure of atmospheric trace gases, aerosols, and clouds, complementing passive remote sensors. Lidars transmit laser pulses and measure laser light scattered back to determine the altitude of gases, aerosols, and clouds with high accuracy. This training introduces data-users to the fundamentals of lidar remote sensing, highlighting strengths, limitations and differences when compared to passive remote sensors. Case studies will be used to demonstrate how to interpret lidar imagery from a variety of past and current spaceborne lidars, including the Cloud-Aerosol Lidar with Orthogonal Polarization (CALIOP), the Cloud-Aerosol Transport System (CATS), the Ice, Cloud, and Elevation Satellite, version 2 (ICESat-2), and the Earth Cloud Aerosol Radiation Experiment (EarthCARE) and provide instruction on how to acquire lidar data for analysis by the user.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to:\n\n1.\tIdentify past and currently available lidar missions and their characteristics\n2.\tRecognize the capabilities of LiDAR active remote sensing in measuring vertical profiles of aerosols and clouds for informing air quality applications\n3.\tInterpret information within LiDAR curtains to discern cloud phase, aerosol type, and aerosol plume altitude for a given scene\n4.\tRecognize the strengths and limitations of LiDAR observations\n5.\tFind LiDAR images and data for a particular time period and location using NASA Earthdata and mission websites\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for Local, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations, wanting to integrate NASA Earth observations and IPCC projections of sea-level change, as well as impacts, for considerations into their work in different sectors; as well as any practitioners of sea-level observations or projections.","registrationHowto":"To Register: https://go.nasa.gov/4jIlOwr\n\nCourse Format: Two 1.5-hour parts including Q&A. An identical session for each part will be offered at two different times of day (10:00-11:30 and 14:00-15:30 EDT [UTC-4]).","registrationEndDate":1749654000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"title":"Aerosols","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":22,"title":"Air quality","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":26,"title":"Cloud types","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2490,"created":1731073196000,"updated":1731073958000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1748858400000,"endDate":1749214800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes.\n\nThe testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. At these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the are operational forecasters with a strong background in severe storms forecasting.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. \nNominated candidates may apply at: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158\n","registrationEndDate":1742342340000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{