escription":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corresponding numerical weather prediction data. A basic knowledge on conceptual models used in satellite meteorology is of advantage to follow the presentations.\n\nThis session will be done through Webex.\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corr","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\n\nStudents","registrationHowto":"To join, go to: https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html and follow the instructions.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9945,"name":"Dominik Rukavina","email":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"nan","country":"HR","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":38,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2559,"created":1747320109000,"updated":null,"title":"EUMETSAT Earth System Feature Detection Workshop","titleNative":"EUMETSAT Earth System Feature Detection Workshop","startDate":1747825200000,"endDate":1747909800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Roope Tervo","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT will host a Workshop on “Earth System Feature Detection”, 21-22 May 2025 at EUMETSAT Headquarters, in Darmstadt, Germany and online. This hybrid event aims to bring together developers and stakeholders from Member States to discuss ongoing and future efforts in feature detection from Earth Observation data.\n\nThe workshop aims to foster collaboration and exchange on feature detection methodologies among Member States and with EUMETSAT. It is planned to prioritise the features that are relevant for key applications and to develop a work programme that considers the division of work between Member States and EUMETSAT. \n\nKey topics will include:\n1.\tExploring member state initiatives and EUMETSAT’s activities.\n2.\tDeveloping a joined working environment for feature detection, including an annotation platform and database. This entails discussions on:\n-\tScope and content of joined working environment.\n-\tProcesses related to joined activities in the working environment.\n-\tTechnical design.\n3.\tDefining how we will work together to maximise effectiveness with existing resources. \n","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT will host a Workshop on “Earth System Feature Detection”, 21-22 May 2025 at EUMETSAT Headquarters, in Darmstadt, Germany and online. This hybrid event aims to bring togeth","content":null,"targetAudience":"EUMETSAT Member States","registrationHowto":"Registrations are now closed.","registrationEndDate":1745971200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":65,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2553,"created":1746116665000,"updated":1746116769000,"title":"Introduction to the Integration of Animal Tracking and Remote Sensing","titleNative":"Introduction to the Integration of Animal Tracking and Remote Sensing","startDate":1747756800000,"endDate":1747935000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/4iPMFWW  ","description":"Animals are sentinels of environmental change, and animal telemetry is a commonly used tool to quantify habitat use and help understand environmental changes. NASA data can be used to characterize the environmental parameters that infer the habitats that animals use. This training course will provide participants with an overview of animal tracking sensors, NASA’s history of animal tracking, and the types of remote sensing data that can be paired with animal telemetry. Because animal telemetry collects frequent animal location data, it is important to consider time-matched remote sensing in data analyses. In remote marine environments, for example, Level 3 and Level 4 products provide the most complete spatiotemporal coverage, such as OSCAR for ocean surface currents. \n \nParticipants will then learn how to integrate telemetry and remote sensing data by applying a basic data standardization process to animal tracking data, visualizing the animals’ distribution via home ranges with utilization distributions, downloading remote sensing data, and characterizing animals’ habitats in a species distribution model to infer habitat use. The balance of tradeoffs (spatiotemporal mismatches; computational power and time) from pairing remotely sensed data with animal tracks will be discussed. Examples for both marine and terrestrial environments will be provided. \n\nCourse Format: Two 1.5-hour sessions including Q&A.\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: \n1.\tIdentify the types of animal tracking tags and sensors that are commonly used in animal tracking.\n2.\tIdentify the types of remote sensing data and products that can be used for species distribution models and step-selection functions.\n3.\tRecognize the process for integrating remote sensing and animal tracking data in species distribution models and step selection functions to facilitate an understanding of animal movements in relation to their environment.\n4.\tRecognize key takeaways from examples of terrestrial and marine applications that inform and characterize animals’ habitats. \n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for movement ecologists and natural resource managers. Remote sensing scientists developing products usable by the primary audience may also find this training of interest.","registrationHowto":"To Register: https://go.nasa.gov/4iPMFWW  ","registrationEndDate":1747929600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"we