,"learningOutcome":"1.Assess start-of-the-art in the use of IR-based geophysical products in forecasting (e.g., T/q profiles, instability indices, winds, …), possibly in combination with other data sources\n\n2.Explore use scenarios of meteorological MTG-IRS L2 products in forecasting\n\n3.Outline guidance material for the training of forecasters on MTG-IRS L2 products\n\nWe aim to also consider:\n\nIRS L2 test dataset released in Sep 2024\nthe JMA Himawari-10 GHMS test dataset\nVisualisation options (2D, 3D)","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"We bring together expertise from Europe, North America, China and Japan, along the following lines:\n\nInstrument experts\nDevelopers of IR-based L2 products (EUM/RSP; IASI L2, NUCAPS, GIIRS, CrIS-based, …)\nEuropean Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL) experts\nTrainers (EUMETSAT, EUMETrain, ESSL)\nUsers and senior forecasters with experience with IR sounder-derived L2 product","registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":1747645200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":35,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2498,"created":1732114949000,"updated":1732271647000,"title":"NOMEK 2025 - Nordic Forecaster Training Course","titleNative":"NOMEK 2025 - Nordic Forecaster Training Course","startDate":1747612800000,"endDate":1747958400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Copenhagen","host":"Danish Meteorological Institute","contactPerson":"Henning Gisselø","contactEmail":"hg@dmi.dk","contactUrl":null,"description":"This course is intended for Nordic operational meteorologists and will be organized by Danish Meteorological Institute in collaboration with the Nordic meteorological institutes and with support from EUMETSAT.\n\nThe objective of the course is to develop and deliver a training program that brings the new developments in meteorology and forecasting tools to the forecasters and to promote networking amongst forecasters and experts from the participating countries. The core topics at the course are Satellite Image Interpretation, Radar Image Interpretation and Numerical Weather Prediction. ","country":{"id":"DK","name":"DENMARK","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Operational Meteorologists from the Nordic countries, with invitations to forecasters from the Baltic States and Ireland.","registrationHowto":"Please contact your national point of contact for training for more information on the nomination and application process.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":35,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2547,"created":1744362116000,"updated":1744363751000,"title":"OpenStack Infrastructure as Code in the EWC","titleNative":"OpenStack Infrastructure as Code in the EWC","startDate":1747209600000,"endDate":1747213200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT & ECMWF","contactPerson":"Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the second thematic EWC webinar of 2025.\n\nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at new or prospective users of the EWC service, provided by EUMETSAT and ECMWF, which is available to all ECMWF and EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating States. Our primary objective is to provide guidance to users on how to effectively use the different capabilities of the EWC.\n\nIn this webinar, we will focus on automating common tasks using Infrastructure as Code in the European Weather Cloud, through the recently announced Openstack API using Openstack Application Credentials in EWC.\n\nBy the end of this 1-hour session, participants will have gained a better understanding of how to use standard DevOps tools (OpenTofu, Ansible) to automate the creation of computer resources on the EWC, to query data on ECMWF (MARS) or EUMETSAT (EUMDAC).","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the second thematic EWC webinar of 2025.\n\nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at n","content":null,"targetAudience":"The main target audience of this webinar are existing and prospective tenancy administrators as well Computing Representatives; however the webinar remains open to anyone interested from an ECMWF or EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating State","registrationHowto":"Apply here: https://events.ecmwf.int/event/477/registrations/344/.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":11305,"name":"Uroosa Farooq ","email":"uroosa.farooq@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":221,"value":"ECMWF","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2552,"created":1745954531000,"updated":1745957264000,"title":"Monitoring Global Terrestrial Surface Water Height using Remote Sensing","titleNative":"Monitoring Global Terrestrial Surface Water Height using Remote Sensing","startDate":1747141200000,"endDate":1747773000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-monitoring-global-terrestrial-surface-water-height-using-remote","description":"This two-part introductory training, delivered in English and Spanish, will focus on introducing SWOT freshwater data products and their applications for water resources and disaster management.\n\nOceans, lakes, and rivers are major components of Earth’s surface water. Freshwater lakes and rivers are primary sources of water supply for drinking, agriculture, energy, and transportation, and support aquatic ecosystems and wildlife. A series of NASA satellites (e.g., TOPEX-Poseidon, Jason 1, 2, 3, & 6) with altimeter observations have been used to estimate ocean surface and inland lake surface heights (> 50 km2) since 1992. The latest NASA mission, Surface Water and Ocean Topography (SWOT), which was launched on December 16, 2022, allows the first ever mapping of global surface freshwater components, including rivers, lakes, and wetlands, with high-resolution measurements (~200 m). Environmental changes, land use, and other water supply and demand changes affect these freshwater sources. Particularly, rivers spanning multiple countries or states within countries pose challenges in estimating water availability and usage. The SWOT data provides unique capability of monitoring changes in freshwater, including river and lake level elevations, river width, slope, and discharge. This training will focus on introducing SWOT freshwater data products and their applications for water resources and disaster management.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: \n\n1.\tIdentify available historic and current lake elevation data using satellite remote sensing.\n2.\tRecognize key science and technology advances behind how SWOT measures surface water bodies.\n3.\tIdentify ways to access SWOT data for water resources and disaster management applications, monitoring parameters such as elevation, slope, width, and discharge for global river reaches.\n4.\tIdentify ways to apply SWOT data for water resources and disaster management applications.\n5.\tRecognize how to utilize the SWOT rivers data visualization tools such as SWOTviz and WISP to monitor water availability and flooding potential.\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for federal, state, local agencies and international governmental and non-governmental organizations engaged in the management of water resources and disasters, reservoir and dam managers, hydropower companies and managers, ecosystem managers, academic faculty and students, river transportation entities, freshwater fisheries/aquaculture.","registrationHowto":"To Register: \n•\tEnglish: 11:00-12:30 EDT (UTC-4): https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-monitoring-global-terrestrial-surface-water-height-using-remote\n•\tSpanish: 15:00-16:30 EDT (UTC-4): https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/spanish/arset-el-monitoreo-global-del-nivel-de-la-superficie-del-agua\n","registrationEndDate":1747767600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5857,"name":"Zoya Andreeva","email":"zandreeva@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":29,"value":"WMO"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":69,"name":"SWOT"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2489,"created":1731073062000,"updated":1751981470000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1747044000000,"endDate":1747400400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes.\n\nThe testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. At these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the are operational forecasters with a strong background in severe storms forecasting.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. \nNominated candidates may apply at: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158\n","registrationEndDate":1742515140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":14,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":235,"value":"ESSL","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":137,"name":"SEVIRI","uniqueName":"SEVIRI (MSG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":140,"name":"LI","uniqueName":"LI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2499,"created":1732117103000,"updated":1765467353000,"title":"Satellite Application Course for African Users","titleNative":"Satellite Application Course for African Users","startDate":1747008000000,"endDate":1747353600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Nairobi","host":"Institute for Meteorological Training and Research (IMTR)","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The objective of the satellite applications training courses is to optimise the use of data from meteorological satellites and to increase the knowledge and skills of operational meteorologists, contributing to improve forecasting.\n\nThis course in English language is for participants from Africa, nominated by their Permanent Representatives (PR) with WMO. PRs will be informed about eligible participants within their country meeting the requirements for nominations. These requirements include a successful completion and a certificate from a recent online satellite applications course organised by EUMETSAT and its training partners in Africa. PRs are further kindly requested to ensure that the right candidates are nominated for the courses, and subsequently deployed so that they are able to apply their competences from the courses. Application deadline is 10 April 2025. ","country":{"id":"KE","name":"KENYA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"- Analyze satellite data interpretation to monitor and detect severe weather.\n- Be a proficient user in RGB images.\n- Develop skills in using PUMA 2025 for weather applications. \n- Use the satellite data in the forecasting process. ","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters in Africa with good English language skills. ","registrationHowto":"Permanent Representatives with WMO will propose one, maximum two, participants from the list of eligible candidates within their country.\n\nThe final selection of accepted candidates will be made by EUMETSAT and IMTR and PRs will be informed of the selection.","registrationEndDate":1744502340000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":20,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"name":"EUMETCast Africa"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":140,"name":"LI","uniqueName":"LI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2549,"created":1745413439000,"updated":null,"title":"ECMWF forecast products and tools to support NMHS warnings","titleNative":"ECMWF forecast products and tools to support NMHS warnings","startDate":1746702000000,"endDate":1746705600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem57","description":"The European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECMWF) is both a research institute and a 24/7 operational service, producing global numerical weather predictions and other data to its Member and Co-operating States and the broader meteorological community. We support National Meteorological and Hydrological Services (NHMS) in issuing warnings though providing forecast products and tools to support operational forecasting.\n\nThis webinar will showcase key ECMWF products including ensemble-based products, the Extreme Forecast Index (EFI), and ecPoint, highlighting their role in supporting the issuing of warnings. It will also provide an overview of tools ecCharts and OpenCharts, which facilitate access to ECMWF forecast products and data. Additionally, recent developments—such as machine learning-based products—will be highlighted, showcasing how ECMWF continues to enhance forecasting capabilities and decision-making for high-impact weather events.\n\nWebinar will be presented by Becky Hemingway (ECMWF) on 8 May 2025 at 13:00 CEST / 11:00 UTC. It is free and open to everyone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/c2a689d3-3e8f-4172-8fe9-7f706c7bd571@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2545,"created":1743665807000,"updated":1743758122000,"title":"Assimilating altimetry: supporting ocean forecasting with surface topography mission data","titleNative":"Assimilating altimetry: supporting ocean forecasting with surface topography mission data","startDate":1746619200000,"endDate":1746626400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=563","description":"Predicting the state of the ocean allows us to determine its likely effect on weather, to advise on maritime operations and safety, and to better understand long-term climate trends. At their heart, the ocean forecasting systems that make these predictions use mathematical models and physical laws to describe the evolution of the ocean in four dimensions, analogous to the approaches meteorologists use to forecast the weather. These models allow us to inform future ocean circulation and sea state. To make these predictions as reliable as possible, a large volume of frequently updated measurements has to be included in the models via assimilation. While these measurements include situ observations, satellite altimetry is a particularly valuable data source, providing a near-global, high-density record of sea surface heights that integrate what is happening from the ocean floor to the surface. Consequently, these models rely extensively on the near real-time and multi-decadal data streams provided by operational satellite altimetry missions, including those under the Copernicus Programme, Sentinel-3 and Sentinel-6.\n\nThe short course will consist of a 2-hour webinar on May 7 (12:00 - 14:00 UTC). During the event we will describe the relevant altimetry data sets for ocean forecasters, giving practical examples of how to handle them in the form of open-source Jupyter Notebooks. Following this, ocean forecasting experts will detail how these data sets are incorporated into their systems, giving examples of relevant applications of the systems, and providing their perspectives. The course will be led by experts from both EUMETSAT and Mercator Ocean International, who together bring extensive expertise in altimetry and the development of ocean forecasting systems. The webinar will conclude with a Q&A and feedback session.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this webinar, participants will:\n\n* know the operational altimetry data streams that are available from EUMETSAT\n* understand the nature of these data sets and how to work with them\n* appreciate how this data is assimilated into ocean forecasting models and be aware of its value\n* be aware of some ocean forecasting applications that altimetry supports","summary":"Predicting the state of the ocean allows us to determine its likely effect on weather, to advise on maritime operations and safety, and to better understand long-term climate trend","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is open to all, but is primarily designed for:\n\n* Established and early career remote sensing researchers with an interest in altimetry\n* Private and public sector specialists engaged in marine monitoring activities\n* Marine forecasters\n* Previous attendees of EUMETSAT Supporting Marine Applications courses that focussed on altimetry applications","registrationHowto":"This webinar is freely open to all. The course registration form can be found here: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_suja8tMGSZSK_wv7ER-Fug.\n\n<h5>Important information</h5>\n\nAll course information and resources will be hosted on our Moodle page. This can be accessed using the \"more information\" button on the right. This page will remain openly accessible until 1 day before the course commences. To access the course materials after this time, you will need to register, for free, for an account on our Moodle platform. You can register for an account at https://classroom.eumetsat.int/login/signup.php. Please include your Moodle username in the course registration form. Once you have an account you will be able to enroll in the course.\n\nEnrolling in the course will allow you to:\n* access the course materials long term\n* access the webinar recording (which will also be posted on YouTube)\n* ask follow up questions to the trainers\n* receive a course certificate upon completion of a short assessment and feedback form","registrationEndDate":1746615600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":46,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[