janic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The RGB Experts and Developers Workshop 2025 will be hosted by SMHI, EUMETSAT, and WMO on 1-3 April 2025 at headquarters of Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute (SMHI), Norrköping, Sweden. It will be the fifth in a series of RGB-related community events after 2007, 2012, 2017 and 2022, which resulted in widely-agreed RGB composite standards used in operations, training and research. The primary goal of this workshop is to agree on RGB standards for the contemporary GEO-ring imagers (namely AHI, ABI and FCI) to be published in the WMO RGB Report. Secondary aim is to share knowledge on RGB creation and applications, plus to identify common platforms to share the RGB recipes and info. ","country":{"id":"SE","name":"SWEDEN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- To agree on RGB standards for the contemporary GEO-ring imagers.\n- To share knowledge on RGB creation and applications\n- To identify common platforms to share the RGB recipes and info. ","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"RGB experts and developers.","registrationHowto":"The workshop is intended for invited RGB experts and developers only. ","registrationEndDate":1743498000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":33,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":100,"value":"WMO","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2530,"created":1740046740000,"updated":1740055113000,"title":"High Impact Weather webinar #1","titleNative":"High Impact Weather webinar #1","startDate":1743411600000,"endDate":1743417000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem54","description":"The High Impact Weather Summer Course is an online course designed for the EUMETCAL community. It consists of an online part with learning materials that you can explore at your convenience, and two accompanying webinars provided by Rob Groenland. \n\nThey will take place on 31 March 09:00-10:30 UTC and 6 May 09:00-10:30 UTC. The High Impact Weather Summer Course will focus on the use of a specific convective forecasting method based on Doswell's ingredient based forecasting method IBM (1996).\n\nOn completion of this course, participants will be able to:\n- determine where and when deep convection will be initiated using the convection scheme (IBM),\n- find the overlapping regions of moisture, instability and lift,\n- determine the type of convection to expect: single cell/pulse cell, multi-cell, squall line or supercell,\n- determine the correspo