n data. A basic knowledge on conceptual models used in satellite meteorology is of advantage to follow the presentations.\n\nThis session will be done through ZOOM.\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corr","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\n\nStudents","registrationHowto":"To join, go to: https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html and follow the instructions.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9945,"name":"Dominik Rukavina","email":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"nan","country":"HR","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":38,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2482,"created":1728566699000,"updated":1728569898000,"title":"NWC SAF CDOP4 Users Workshop 2025","titleNative":"NWC SAF CDOP4 Users Workshop","startDate":1740441600000,"endDate":1740614400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Madrid ","host":"AEMET","contactPerson":"Pilar Rípodas","contactEmail":"safnwchd@aemet.es","contactUrl":"https://www.nwcsaf.org/web/guest/2025_users_ws","description":"The next NWC SAF Users Workshop  is going to take place from 25 - 27 February, 2025 at the AEMET Headquarters in Madrid, Spain.\n\nThe main topics of the conference will include NWC SAF future plans, presentations and posters from both NWC SAF developers and NWC SAF users, as well as working groups on user requirements. Due to limited capacity for onsite attendance (92 seats), only selected participants will be able to take part in the workshop in Madrid. However, online participation will be possible for all registered participants.\n\nPlease take into account that for an oral presentation or presenting a poster, an abstract must be sent at https://es.surveymonkey.com/r/R32CYCP. \n\nAbstracts can be sent either by uploading a PDF, a .doc or a .docx file or sharing them directly in the survey form. Abstracts should be no longer than 400 words.\n\nThe deadline for submission of abstracts is 24 November 2024. A confirmation of acceptance will be sent by 9 December 2024.","country":{"id":"ES","name":"SPAIN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"All interested participants (for either onsite or online participation) can register at this link: https://es.surveymonkey.com/r/R37S6PW.","registrationEndDate":1734048000000,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":3,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":244,"value":"NWC SAF","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2500,"created":1732182504000,"updated":1737132494000,"title":"Supporting Marine Earth Observation Applications","titleNative":"Supporting Marine Earth Observation Applications","startDate":1740355200000,"endDate":1742515200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"In early 2025, EUMETSAT will convene the next iteration of the \"Supporting Marine Earth Observation Applications (SMA)\" course, introducing you to our marine data catalogue and helping you develop workflows that support your own application-specific goals. If you wish to learn about, or work more extensively with our satellite derived, ocean colour, sea surface temperature, altimetry, sea ice or wind data, then we encourage you to apply. This year, the course will be delivered in partnership with the <b>University of Hull</b>.\n\nDuring this course you will learn how to independently access and process data from the EUMETSAT product catalogue for your marine workflows and applications. The focus will be on data streams from <b>EUMETSAT Copernicus marine missions (Sentinel-3; Sentinel-6)</b> and derived downstream products, those derived from Copernicus supporting missions, and those made available by the <b>Ocean and Sea-Ice Satellite Application Facility (OSI SAF)</b>.\n\nTraining will take place entirely online and through two phases, which will be support by experts in the relevant fields;\n\n* The first, self-paced phase will take place between 24 February and 14 March 2025 and will take approximately 9-15 hours in total to complete. It will involve self-paced flexible learning through webinars, forums and technical checks (particularly for software installations), documentation and assignments.\n\n* The second, virtual classroom phase will be take place between 17 March and 21 March 2025 using Zoom and other collaborative tools. This phase will be made up of interactive tutorials, live demos, group work, and 1:1 meetings. During this intensive week, which will require 5-8 hours of participation each day, we will focus on co-creating a mini-project directly relevant to your application of interest.\n\nDuring the course, you will;\n* Learn about the specifics of the marine products that EUMETSAT provides (variables, timeliness, resolution, data formats)\nSelect appropriate products from the EUMETSAT marine catalogue and access them using GUI-based and automated services.\n* Use relevant software tools, such as SNAP, and scripting languages, such as Python, to acquire, visualise and process Earth observation data from multiple sources.\n* Work with trainers to design workflows around these products and tools, tailoring approaches to the specific needs of your participant-defined application.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants completing this course will:\n\n* Learn about the operational role EUMETSAT plays in marine Earth observation, understand the range of products it provides and appreciate how it supports downstream services.\n* Be able to select and download the appropriate data for their marine application of interest.\n* Be able to manipulate these products for their own purposes using appropriate software packages and code-based approaches.\n* Produce a use-case specific to their needs, in collaboration with other participants and trainers.","summary":"In early 2025, EUMETSAT will convene the next iteration of the \"Supporting Marine Earth Observation Applications (SMA)\" course, introducing you to our marine data catalogue and hel","content":null,"targetAudience":"This workshop is a technical training event, designed to increase the ability of all attending to access and use EUMETSAT marine products for their own applications. Training is aimed at, but not restricted to;\n\n* Early career researchers (masters, PhD, PostDoc) who are new to marine remote sensing and/or the EUMETSAT marine product catalogue\n* Marine scientists who may be working in a cross-disciplinary capacity and are looking to widen their skills into the marine Earth observation\n* Experienced professionals from any relevant sector (industry, government, environment, research) who have clear motivations for working with satellite-based ocean observation data for marine applications.","registrationHowto":"A limited number of places are available on this course. Visit the “Apply for courses” section of our course <b><a href=\"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158\">Moodle page</a></b> for more information on how to apply.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"M