l-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":46,"name":"MODIS","uniqueName":"MODIS (Aqua/Terra)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":162,"name":"OLCI","uniqueName":"OLCI (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":138,"name":"FCI","uniqueName":"FCI (MTG)"}]},{"id":2522,"created":1736933744000,"updated":null,"title":"Use of EUMETSAT MTG FCI and LI data and products in weather monitoring and nowcasting","titleNative":"Use of EUMETSAT MTG FCI and LI data and products in weather monitoring and nowcasting","startDate":1739448000000,"endDate":1739451600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem53","description":"MTG is one of the most complex and innovative geostationary meteorological satellite systems ever built. The complete constellation consists of three spacecraft: two imaging satellites and one sounding satellite.\n\nThe first imaging satellite, MTG-I1 is now operational under the name Meteosat 12. The satellite carries two important instruments – Flexible Combined Imager (FCI), a successor of SEVIRI on MSG, and a Lightning Imager (LI), the first space-based instrument monitoring lightning occurrence over Europe, Africa and South America from geostationary orbit.\n\nOne of the biggest benefits from MTG observations is the improvement to nowcasting, or very short-range forecasting. Forecasters should now able to track the development of storms in near-real time with better accuracy, issue more precise and timely warnings about severe and dangerous weather events but also monitor fog development and dissipation, dust outbreaks, forest fires and many other features.\n\nThe webinar will offer a short introduction of the FCI and LI, acquisition of data and description of baseline products, followed by the demonstration of the application of FCI and LI products in selected cases.\n\nWebinar will be presented by Natasa Strelec Mahovic, Vesa Nietosvaara and Ivan Smiljanic (EUMETSAT). It will take place on Thursday 13 Feb 2025 at 12:00 UTC / 13:00 CET. It is free and open for everyone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/90071fae-ab25-46aa-94ad-ac32ca5b3f27@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":194,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2523,"created":1736959138000,"updated":1764317464000,"title":"Training course on Satellite Products and Applications in Central America and the Caribbean","titleNative":"Productos y Aplicaciones de Satélite en Centroamérica y Caribe","startDate":1739145600000,"endDate":1739491200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"La Antigua","host":"AEMET","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This training course is designed for marine weather forecasters from Central America and the Caribbean who have successfully completed a five-week online phase previously conducted. The goal is to enhance capacity in using satellite products from polar-orbiting satellites to improve the diagnosis of current marine weather conditions, thereby strengthening forecasting capabilities. ","country":{"id":"GT","name":"GUATEMALA","region":"RA-IV","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will develop:\n1.\tProficiency in analysing marine weather situations, supporting the preparation and issuance of accurate forecasts.\n2.\tCompetence in forecasting key phenomena, parameters, and variables, including the following:\n\nWind, including directional variability, speed, and wind gusts;\n\nSea State (temperature, ocean color, salinity, waves, surface height);\n\nHorizontal visibility due to fog, mist, or precipitation;\n\nTropical Cyclones and Hurricanes and their tracking movement.\n","summary":"This training course is designed for marine weather forecasters from Central America and the Caribbean who have successfully completed a five-week online phase previously conducted","content":null,"targetAudience":"Marine Weather forecasters, general forecasters in areas highly influenced by marine events, and professionals involved in science-to-operations processes.","registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":9959,"name":"Madalina System Admin Ungur ","email":"madalina.ungur@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSA