mSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2484,"created":1729852963000,"updated":null,"title":"EUMeTrain Monthly Weather Briefing ","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Monthly Weather Briefing ","startDate":1729857600000,"endDate":1729860000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMetrain","contactPerson":"Dominik Rukavina","contactEmail":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corresponding numerical weather prediction data. A basic knowledge on conceptual models used in satellite meteorology is of advantage to follow the presentations.\n\nThis session will be done through ZOOM.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corr","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\n\nStudents","registrationHowto":"To join, go to: https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html and follow the instructions.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9945,"name":"Dominik Rukavina","email":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"nan","country":"HR","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2476,"created":1727080301000,"updated":1727702753000,"title":"Applying Case 2 Regional Coast Colour (C2RCC) Algorithms to EUMETSAT OLCI Products","titleNative":"Applying Case 2 Regional Coast Colour (C2RCC) Algorithms to EUMETSAT OLCI Products","startDate":1729771200000,"endDate":1729864800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":null,"contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=541","description":"This comprehensive two-day online course will focus on the application of Case 2 Regional Coast Colour (C2RCC) algorithms to Copernicus Sentinel-3 OLCI (Ocean and Land Colour Instrument) marine products, provided by EUMETSAT. It will take place on October 24th and 25th 2024, and is designed to cater for users and researchers interested in enhancing their understanding of water quality through ocean colour remote sensing over complex waters. This course presents an opportunity to improve your knowledge of OLCI ocean colour products, both current and planned, and enhance your practical skills and understanding of the advantages and limitations of the C2RCC algorithm on coastal and other complex waters. The agenda for the online session is as follows:\n\nDay 1 (2 hours) 12-14h UTC\n\n* Introduction to OLCI and demonstrations on accessing and navigating OLCI data.\n* Demo sessions using SNAP for Level 1 and Level 2 data analysis, with a focus on the results of the atmospheric correction (AC) and the inverse problem of in-water retrieval by analysing the water quality products and flags.\n\nDay 2 (2 hours) 12-14h UTC\n\n* In-depth presentations on the architecture and development of the C2RCC algorithm.\n* Advanced demos on C2RCC processing using SNAP, including batch processing and model comparison using Jupyter Notebooks.\n* Custom vs operational processing and OLCI product developments\n* Q&A and feedback\n\nThe course will be led by experts from both EUMETSAT and Brockmann Consult GmbH, including Dagmar Müller, Jorrit Scholze and Ana B. Ruescas  who bring extensive experience in ocean colour remote sensing and algorithm development. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this 2-part event, participants will:\n\n* recall how to identify and access the Sentinel-3 OLCI marine products via the EUMETSAT Data Store via GUI and API\n* learn how to navigate and manipulate these products using the ESA SNAP software package\n* appreciate the need for different approaches to atmospheric correction and the need for special approaches in complex waters\n* understand the theoretical basis, suitability and practical implementation of the C2RCC processor\n* be aware of differences between the EUMETSAT operational and external implementations of the C2RCC processor, and of upcoming developments in OLCI ocean colour products\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This event is open to all, but is primarily designed for;\n\n* Established and early career remote sensing/ocean colour researchers\n* Private and public sector specialists engaged in marine monitoring activities\n* Previous attendees of EUMETSAT Supporting Marine Applications courses that focussed on ocean colour applications\n","registrationHowto":"The course will be hosted on Zoom, a web-based video conferencing tool. Reserve your spot using this registration link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_7nTrQZXGQWKIeKA5OwWsMA\n\nDuring the webinar, we will be using Slido to answer your questions. Go to Slido.com on your computer or your phone and find the event with the code #EUMSC48. No login is required.\n\nThe sessions will be recorded. After the webinar, the recordings and other resources will be made available at this link: https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=541 ","registrationEndDate":1729771200000,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":48,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":162,"name":"OLCI","uniqueName":"OLCI (Sentinel-3)"}]},{"id":2441,"created":1720179652000,"updated":1720184167000,"title":"Workshop on latest developments on satellite-based climate data supporting climate services and NMHSs","titleNative":"Workshop on latest developments on satellite-based climate data supporting climate services and NMHSs","startDate":1729753200000,"endDate":1729780200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Offenbach","host":"CM SAF","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"contact.cmsaf@dwd.de","contactUrl":"https://www.cmsaf.eu/EN/Outreach/Workshops/upcoming_workshops/User_WS_operational_User_2024/User_WS_operational_User_2024_node.html","description":"Join us on October 24, 2024, for a one-day workshop at Deutscher Wetterdienst in Offenbach, Germany, focused on the application of satellite-based climate data records in climate services and National Meteorological and Hydrological Services (NMHSs).\n\nThis workshop will provide an overview of the latest European developments in satellite-based climate data and offer a platform to discuss your specific requirements. \n\nHighlights include:\n\n    * Presentation of the upcoming anomaly service\n    * Overview of EUMETSAT climate products and services supporting climate services and policy-making\n    * Best practices and use cases from existing NMHS and Climate Service users\n    * Interactive discussions with satellite experts and colleagues\n    * Discussion tables addressing needs and challenges, such as suitable satellite reference periods, \n      compatibility with national applications, data interfaces, and interoperability\n\nThe workshop will feature presentations and interactive discussion sessions. You will also have opportunities to engage with developers and raise user requirements to improve products and services. Present your use cases a