ataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":165,"name":"TROPOMI","uniqueName":"TROPOMI (Sentinel-5P)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":141,"name":"S4/UVN","uniqueName":"S4/UVN (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":163,"name":"SLSTR","uniqueName":"SLSTR (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":139,"name":"IRS","uniqueName":"IRS (MTG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":132,"name":"S5/UVNS","uniqueName":"S5/UVNS (Metop-SG)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":162,"name":"OLCI","uniqueName":"OLCI (Sentinel-3)"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":126,"name":"IASI-NG","uniqueName":"IASI-NG (Metop-SG)"}]},{"id":2366,"created":1703069722000,"updated":1703073826000,"title":" ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbeds on Severe Convective Storms in Preparation for MTG","titleNative":" ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbeds on Severe Convective Storms in Preparation for MTG","startDate":1726477200000,"endDate":1726840800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes. \n\nThe testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. At these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the 2024 testbeds is operational forecasters who train other forecasters and forecasters with a strong background in severe storms meteorology.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. Nominated candidates may apply at: \nhttps://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1707955200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":15,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2435,"created":1719404640000,"updated":1726065037000,"title":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: OSI SAF sea ice climate records","titleNative":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: OSI SAF sea ice climate records","startDate":1725955200000,"endDate":1725978600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=531","description":"This event will focus on presenting the Sea Ice Climate Records produced and distributed by OSI SAF team at the Norwegian Meteorological Institute. It will detail the characteristics of those multi-sensor products allowing studies of the sea ice extent over 40 years.\nThe main contributing experts will then present the different products. They will explain how the datasets are organized, and what user need to know to properly use it.\n\nA practical demonstration will show the remote use of the data and their use at a basic level.\nThe short course will consist of a 1.5-hour webinars. Two sessions with the same content will be held on September 21 (08:00 - 09:30 and 13:00 to 14:30 UTC). The participants are invited to choose which of the two session fits him better. The session will include a Q&A and feedback session. To support participants in using the data sets and tools we highlight, we will keep the online Q&A platform open for one week following the webinar, responding quickly to any queries posted.\n\n\nRESOURCES\n\n\nThe recording of the webinar is available at this link: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MrT3R6wc5F4 \n\nPresentations will be soon accessible on the course page: https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=531\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will:\n- Understand how the climate data records have been constituted.\n- Understand the limitations and the importance of these products.\n- Learn about evolution to come on these products.\n- Know to access OSI SAF’s Sea Ice Climate Data Records.\n- Know which product to access for what purpose.\n- Know how to use Sea Ice Climate Data Records without downloading the full dataset.\n","summary":"This event will focus on presenting the Sea Ice Climate Records produced and distributed by OSI SAF team at the Norwegian Meteorological Institute. It will detail the characteristi","content":null,"targetAudience":"- Established and early career sea ice researchers.\n- Researchers from other fields than sea ice studies, but needing climatic sea ice data.\n- Private and public sector specialists engaged in polar ocean monitoring activities.\n- Climate related scientific communication specialists.\n","registrationHowto":"The course will be hosted on Zoom, a web-based video conferencing tool. Reserve your spot using this registration link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_LElaAKWDToWlG0d-y8jzWQ#/registration. During the webinar, we will be using Slido to answer your questions. Go to Slido.com and find the event with the code #EUMSC45. No login is required. You can also join Slido from your phone. The session will be recorded. After the session, you will find on this page a link to the recording and other resources.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":74,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":80,"value":"Other","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":35,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Cryosphere","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2446,"created":1721137156000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"European Weather Cloud Webinar:  Tenancy Administration","titleNative":"European Weather Cloud Webinar:  Tenancy Administration","startDate":1725955200000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT & ECMWF","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the fourth thematic EWC webinar of 2024.\n \nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at users of the EWC service, provided by EUMETSAT and ECMWF, which is available to all ECMWF and EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating States. Our primary objective is to provide guidance to users on how to effectively use the different capabilites of the EWC.\n \nWhile the first two webinars in 2023 focused on the basics to get you started (you can find more information, including the video recordings, here and here), in this series we explore various aspects of cloud utilisation through examples, with a specific emphasis on key functionalities and cloud skills. The previous EWC webinars and their recordings can be found here.\n \nIn the upcoming webinar, we will focus on the tenancy administration, starting from describing the role and responsibilities of the tenant administrator and covering different aspects that include the tenancy users management, permissions to access functionalities and blueprints, security, communications and accounting of the cloud resources consumption.\n \nIn this 1 hour session webinar the participants will have gained a better understanding of how to manage and administer an EWC tenancy as well as the duties and responsibility of the tenant administrator role.\n ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the fourth thematic EWC webinar of 2024.\n \nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at ","content":null,"targetAudience":"The main target audience of this webinar are existing and prospective tenancy administrators as well Computing Representatives; however the webinar remains open to anyone interested from an ECMWF or EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating State","registrationHowto":"Apply here: https://events.ecmwf.int/event/424/registrations/280/.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":221,"value":"ECMWF","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2460,"created":1721741393000,"updated":1725606614000,"title":"EUMETSAT short course: EUMETSAT MTG-I1 Lightning Imager: background, data and application in thunderstorm detection and forecasting","titleNative":"EUMETSAT short course: EUMETSAT MTG-I1 Lightning Imager: background, data and application in thunderstorm detection and forecasting","startDate":1725519600000,"endDate":1725534000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":null,"contactPerson":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=534","description":"This short course on MTG-I1 Lightning Imager (LI) is the first in the series of short courses on the MTG data and applications. \n\nLI is the first space-based instrument monitoring lightning occurrence over Europe, Africa and South America from geostationary orbit, with pre-operational level 2 data available to all users through EUMETCast and via the Data Store since 8 July 2024. \n\nThe event will start at 07:00 UTC and last about 4 hours. It will offer insight into the theory of lightning discharges and lightning measurements, details on the LI instrument, acquisition of data, filtering, noise removal, processing, LI baseline products and applications. You will also receive preliminary information about the quality and accuracy of LI data against ground-based lightning detection networks, based on real examples.\n\nA practical part will offer a demo on data retrieval from the EUMETSAT Data Store and visualisation using the SIFT software and/or Jupyter Notebooks.\n\nThe second part of the course will focus on data applications. You will see recent thunderstorm cases over Europe with LI data “in action”.\n\nFinally, experts from meteorological services will demonstrate how to deal with reception, visualisation and use of LI data in the operational work.\n\n\n\nAGENDA\n\n--> Download the agenda of the short course at this link: https://bit.ly/shortcourseAgenda .\n\n\nThe course will be jointly delivered by Bartolomeo Viticchie and Sven-Erik Enno (EUMETSAT), Jean-Marc Moisselin (Meteo France), Tomas Pucik (ESSL) et al.\n\n\n\n\n\nRESOURCES\n\nThe recording of this short course is available here: https://youtu.be/DjUx37bIi3g .\nThe presentations can be accessed on the course page at this link: https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=534 . \n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course, participants will be able to:\n- Understand how the lightning is monitored from space; \n- Learn about the details of the LI instrument;\n- Get insight in the way data is acquired, filtered and how the products are derived;\n- Understand the strengths and weaknesses of LI compared to ground-based lightning detection networks;\n- Learn how to download and visualise the data;\n- Know how the data behaves in real weather situations;\n- Understand how the data is used in the operational forecast offices.\n","summary":"This short course on MTG-I1 Lightning Imager (LI) is the first in the series of short courses on the MTG data and applications. \n\nLI is the first space-based instrument monitoring ","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, students and researchers in meteorology, interested public","registrationHowto":"The course will be hosted on Zoom, a web-based video conferencing tool. Reserve your spot using this registration link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webi