,"city":null,"host":"EUMetrain","contactPerson":"Dominik Rukavina","contactEmail":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corresponding numerical weather prediction data. A basic knowledge on conceptual models used in satellite meteorology is of advantage to follow the presentations.\n\nThe session is online and is done through the Webex software.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"Once a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to discuss the present weather situation. The basis of the discussions are todays satellite images and the corr","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\n\nStudents","registrationHowto":"To join, go to: https://resources.eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html and follow the instructions.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9945,"name":"Dominik Rukavina","email":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"nan","country":"HR","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2422,"created":1718025312000,"updated":1718101479000,"title":"Applications of Carbon Dioxide Measurements for Climate-Related Studies","titleNative":"Applications of Carbon Dioxide Measurements for Climate-Related Studies","startDate":1720533600000,"endDate":1721163600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA ARSET","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/4asZvWE","description":"Space-based CO2 measurements have become an important capability in support of climate studies and to inform policy decisions. This intermediate, three-part webinar series will build on the previous CO2 training from 2022, providing a more in-depth review of OCO-2 and OCO-3 measurements along with demonstrations of case-studies. The latter will focus on how to read, visualize and interpret the data, how to account for quality flags in an analysis, how to use the data from the OCO missions to analyze impacts of an El Niño event on atmospheric CO2 and carbon sources and sinks, and how to examine spatial variations of CO2 over a metropolitan area. The demonstration will be conducted using Jupyter Notebook.\n \nThis training is also available in Spanish.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable\n•\tGoal 12: Ensure sustainable consumption and production patterns\n•\tGoal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n \n1.\tIdentify the characteristics and limitations of the NASA Orbiting Carbon Observatory, OCO-2 and OCO-3 XCO2 measurements.\n2.\tAccess and download data through the Distributed Active Archive Center (GES DISC), and open and visualize XCO2 data from OCO-2/OCO-3 in GES DISC Earthdata.\n3.\tInterpret XCO2 data from OCO-2/OCO-3 for global, regional, and local scales.\n4.\tAssess the  level of confidence to place in XCO2 measurements using the quality flags incorporated into each dataset.\n5.\tAnalyze OCO-2 data for assessing the impacts of  an El Nino event on Level 2 CO2 concentrations and Level-4 fluxes over tropical regions. \n6.\tAnalyze OCO-3 data for assessing the variations in Level-2 CO2 concentrations over a metropolitan area.\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for scientists in the field and local, regional, and federal organizations from climate agencies.","registrationHowto":"To Register: \n•\tEnglish: https://go.nasa.gov/44ECuyD\n•\tSpanish: https://go.nasa.gov/3wBmgtr\n","registrationEndDate":1721163600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":38,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Ocean","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate",