Bojinski","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and the EUMETSAT Polar System Second Generation (EPS-SG) Programmes. \n\nThis is the first of a series of 6 testbeds that will be offered in 2024.\n\nThe testbeds teach (i) forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or experimental forecasting tools, and (ii) the evaluation of such tools. At these events, forecasters learn by simulating an operational forecasting situation, making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, and then evaluating the quality of the forecast and the value of the data and tools.\n\nParticular focus is given to the use of novel MTG satellite data from the FCI spectral imager and from the LI lightning imager instrument. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"EUMETSAT, in partnership with the European Severe Storms Laboratory (ESSL), offers a series of testbeds to prepare operational meteorologists / forecasters to use data from the Met","content":null,"targetAudience":"The target group of the 2024 testbeds is operational forecasters who train other forecasters and forecasters with a strong background in severe storms meteorology.","registrationHowto":"Applications to this course are based on the nominations by the heads of delegations of EUMETSAT members. Nominated candidates may apply at: \nhttps://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1707955200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":14,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2346,"created":1697704602000,"updated":1700688868000,"title":"FICE-2024: A Training Event on In situ Ocean Colour Above-Water Radiometry towards Satellite Validation in Acqua Alta Oceanographic Tower and Venice","titleNative":"FICE-2024: A Training Event on In situ Ocean Colour Above-Water Radiometry towards Satellite Validation in Acqua Alta Oceanographic Tower and Venice","startDate":1714953600000,"endDate":1715904000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Venice","host":" Istituto delle Scienze Marine (ISMAR)","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"FICE2024_training@ut.ee","contactUrl":"https://frm4soc2.eumetsat.int/post/fice-2024-training-event-are-now-open","description":"An advanced training course aiming to support those making measurements of in situ ocean colour towards satellite validation and biogeochemical applications. Building on the FRM4SOC project, the Copernicus FICE-24 course will bring experts in ocean colour measurements, satellite validation, and algorithm development together to provide training on the latest measurement and data processing protocols. Participants will have the opportunity to make measurements at the Acqua Alta Oceanographic Tower, learn how to process these measurements, characterise their uncertainties, and ultimately match them up with satellite ocean colour data. Data collected will contribute to the Copernicus Ocean Colour Database. \n\nTravel funding is available for selected participants, with priority given to those working for institutions in Copernicus contributing countries.","country":{"id":"IT","name":"ITALY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- Generalities of ocean colour radiometry and the FRM context\n- Relevance of calibration and characterisation of OC radiometers\n- In situ measurement procedures\n- Guidelines for the estimation of uncertainties\n- Introduction of HyperCP: HyperInSPACE – Community Processor to calculate remote sensing reflectance and associated uncertainties from TriOS and SeaBird raw measurements.\n- Training on OCDB: Copernicus’ Ocean Colour Data Base\n- Training on FidRadDB: a database of radiometric calibrations and characterisations obtained during FRM4SOC-2.\n- Training on acquiring ocean colour satellite data from Copernicus Sentinel-3 via the EUMETSAT Data Store\n- Training on ThoMaS – a toolkit to perform matchups with Copernicus’ S3/OLCI\n- Assessment and recording of measurement conditions in the tower for the campaign date.\n- Deployment and measurements with TriOS RAMSES OC radiometer systems above water, following procedures as detailed in block 1.\n- Debrief on continuous measurements done in the tower with other radiometric systems.\n- Analysis of the field experience and challenges faced.\n- Processing the data obtained at AAOT with HyperCP. Interpretation of results.\n- Processing outputs of HyperCP with ThoMaS to perform matchups with S3/OLCI.\n- Submitting HyperCP outputs to OCDB and SeaBASS.\n- Analytical methods to perform comparisons of in situ measurements (between TriOS sets but also continuous measurements done at AAOT).","summary":"An advanced training course aiming to support those making measurements of in situ ocean colour towards satellite validation and biogeochemical applications. Building on the FRM4SO","content":null,"targetAudience":"A maximum of 20 participants will be accepted to join the training event. Anyone interested in the topics above with at least introductory experience in field measurements (not exclusively Ocean Colour radiometry) is welcome to submit. Advanced or senior experts are encouraged to apply, but priority will be given to PhD students, postdocs and early career scientists. Priority (not exclusive) will be given to applicants affiliated with institutions from Copernicus-contributing countries. Training, travel expenses, accommodation and per-diem will be covered either fully or partially by the Copernicus Programme.","registrationHowto":"Applicants must submit: \n- A summarised CV, no longer than 2 A4 pages.\n- A motivation letter, no longer than 1 A4 page. The motivation letter must include information on:\n- The background and interests of the applicant\n- The ongoing and future projects in which the applicant is involved where he/she/they will apply the knowledge acquired during the training, e.g. planned fieldwork in different water types, algorithm development-related research, etc.\n- Details on background expertise in Ocean Colour fieldwork\n- Specifically, if existent, knowledge of above-water radiometry.\n- Details on specific instruments with which the applicant already operated\n- Technical experience working with large data sets in a suitable programming language.\n\nApplicants can submit using the application form link below:  \n*[application form](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSciecAC_O1RY1N_p3Av6NIDmLcuvnq6v5xq6Tdcgfk5iAN0AQ/viewform?usp=sf_link)*","registrationEndDate":1702288800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":14,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2385,"created":1706700900000,"updated":1706708091000,"title":"RA-I Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Course","titleNative":"RA-I Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Course","startDate":1714953600000,"endDate":1716508800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"ASMET - African Satellite Meteorology Education and Training","contactPerson":"Vesa Nietosvaara","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=514","description":"The online course on Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation will take place 6-24 May 2024. It is offered both in English and French language, by the ASMET instructors from DGM Morocco, EAMAC Niger, EUMETSAT, IMTR Kenya and SAWS South Africa. This course helps you to improve skills in using basic, generally available satellite imagery for identifying various weather and surface features in Africa. The course is suitable for all forecasters in Africa, both early career operational forecasters and more experienced meteorologists.\n\nThe course will consist of live sessions with discussions and weather briefings, with the focus on basic interpretation of satellite images used in weather rooms. We will also explore the new Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) satellite products, which are becoming operational in the forecasting offices. The participants should reserve minimum 4 hours each week for going through the learning resources, attending the live meetings and completing assignments. We will use the COMET MetEd Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Lesson to guide us through the basic use of satellite images.\n\nA successful completion of this course will make you better prepared for advanced level online and residence courses offered by the African training centres and EUMETSAT.\n\nApplications are open till Friday 26 April 2024. Please apply to the online course by completing an online questionnaire.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Improved skills in : (a) Identifying the main weather systems and features in Africa and their characteristics in satellite imagery and products; (b) understanding benefits of new generation weather satellites; (c) Being a competent user of virtual course technology; (d) Developing relationships with course participants via discussion forums and online briefings.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Operational forecasters or users of satellite data, with the possibility of passing on the skills acquired on the course to other operational staff.","registrationHowto":"The candidates are invited to register for the course online by completing an online questionnaire. Applications will open in February 2024 at http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1714089600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":203,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":8,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Kenya","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2386,"created":1706702811000,"updated":1706708063000,"title":"Online Course: RA-I Basic Interpretation of Satellite Imagery Course","titleNative":"Cours en ligne: RA-I Cours Intérpretation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire","startDate":1714953600000,"endDate":1716508800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"ASMET - African Satellite Meteorology Education and Training","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=515","description":"Le cours en ligne sur l'interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire se déroulera du 6 au 24 mai 2024. Il est proposé en anglais et en français par des instructeurs ASMET de la DGM Maroc, de l'EAMAC Niger, d'EUMETSAT, de l'IMTR Kenya et du SAWS Afrique du Sud. Ce cours vous permet d'améliorer vos compétences concernant l'utilisation de l'imagerie satellitaire, qui est généralement disponible pour l'identification de diverses caractéristiques météorologiques et de surface en Afrique. Le cours s'adresse à tous les prévisionnistes d'Afrique, qu'ils soient en début de carrière ou plus expérimentés.\n\nLe cours consistera en des sessions en direct avec des discussions et des briefings météorologiques, se concentrant sur l'interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire utilisée dans les bureaux de météorologie. Nous explorerons également les nouveaux produits satellitaires Meteosat de troisième génération (MTG), qui deviennent opérationnels dans les bureaux de prévision. Les participants devront consacrer au moins 4 heures par semaine à l'étude des ressources pédagogiques, à la participation aux réunions en direct et à la réalisation des travaux. \n\nLa réussite de ce cours vous préparera mieux aux cours de niveau avancé en ligne et en présentiel proposés par les centres de formation africains et d'EUMETSAT.\n\nLes inscriptions sont ouvertes jusqu'au 26 avril 2024. Veuillez vous inscrire au cours en ligne en complétant un questionnaire en ligne.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Amélioration des compétences en: (a) Identifier les principaux systèmes et caractéristiques météorologiques en Afrique et leurs caractéristiques dans l'imagerie et les produits satellitaires ; (b) comprendre les avantages des satellites météorologiques de nouvelle génération; (c) Être un utilisateur compétent de la technologie des cours virtuels; (d) Développer des relations avec les participants aux cours via les forums de discussion et les briefings en ligne","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Prévisionnistes opérationnels ou des utilisateurs de données satellitaires, avec la possibilité de transmettre les compétences acquises lors du cours à d'autres membres du personnel opérationnel.","registrationHowto":"Les candidats sont invités à s'inscrire au cours en ligne en remplissant un questionnaire en ligne. Les candidatures sont ouvertes à février 2024 à l'adresse suivante http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1714089600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false},{"id":10,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Niger","visible":false},{"id":14,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Morocco","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":4,"value":"French","iso639":"fr"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2402,"created":1712652800000,"updated":null,"title":"AIs in Education: Customizing ChatGPT for Enhanced Support and Interaction in Educational Activities","titleNative":"AIs in Education: Customizing ChatGPT for Enhanced Support and Interaction in Educational Activities","startDate":1714654800000,"endDate":1714658400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem39","description":"In the rapidly evolving landscape of educational technology, artificial intelligence (AI) emerges as a pivotal tool in enriching learning environments and streamlining instructional design. This webinar delves into an array of AI solutions currently transforming educational activities, spotlighting ChatGPT’s versatile applications. We'll guide you through the process of tailoring ChatGPT to meet specific educational needs, enhancing its utility in creating learning materials. Join us to explore how AI not only augments current educational practices but also paves the way for future innovations.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://knmi.webex.com/weblink/register/r438e01a985be6d86bf4b5912740d927b","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2394,"created":1709039698000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"EUMDAC Series - Session 5: Practical approaches to EUMETSAT marine data access","titleNative":"EUMDAC Series - Session 5: Practical approaches to EUMETSAT marine data access","startDate":1714482000000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=527","description":"This series is designed to familiarise participants with EUMETSAT data access services, focusing on interacting with Data Store and Data Tailor APIs through the EUMDAC Python library and Command Line Interface.\n\nIn Session 5, we will give an overview of currently available marine collections, including reprocessings, and provide a series of hands-on demonstrations of how to use EUMDAC to support a variety of practical marine workflows. Demonstrations will show how to;\n\n· configure automated downloads,\n\n· search for, and download, products to match in situ sets, including cruise tracks,\n\n· extract products across collections (reprocessed and operational),\n\n· streamline data access and extractions (e.g., by cycle, by flag criteria).\n\nSession 5 does not require attendance at previous sessions as a prerequisite, but we will refer to the these to reinforce understanding and facilitate seamless integration of concepts. Some familiarity with code will be required to get the most out of this event, but many examples will be presented using fully described Jupyter Notebooks that will be shared for use post event.\n\nThis session represents a collaboration between the EUMETSAT Data Access Services and marine training teams, and experts from both teams will be available to answer your questions.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"· Users should be able to understand the EUMETSAT marine catalogue\n\n· Users should be able to search, download and tailor EUMETSAT marine products\n\n· Users should acquire proficiency in integrating concepts and methodologies introduced in previous sessions (Sessions 1-4) into real-world scenarios, reinforcing their understanding and enhancing their analytical capabilities.\n\n· Users should be able to find marine and Data Access resources on the EUMETSAT User Portal.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the data access services","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_PngHDbfzRS6TmKP6H_cWyQ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":40,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"title":"Maritime safety","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":38,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Ocean","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":41,"title":"Ocean dynamics","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":9,"name":"Sentinel-6"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2401,"created":1711635125000,"updated":1711636510000,"title":"","titleNative":"Introduction to Machine Learning for Earth Observation - A practical approach ","startDate":1714377600000,"endDate":1714660200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Mark Higgins","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=526","description":"This online course is an introduction to Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning and Deep Learning applied to Earth observation data. The aim of the course is to provide an overview of machine learning potential for EUMETSAT data and the main machine learning techniques, with hands-on modules using real world data. The course is composed of different modules, addressing both theory and practical examples.\n\nThe course will cover: \n\n- The main branches of machine learning: Supervised and Unsupervised Learning\n- Deep Learning\n- Existing open source tools \n- How to build AI workflows\n- Hands on: classification, regression, clustering and image classification tasks\n- Agents, bots and Large Language Models \n\nDates: 29, 30 April and 2 May 2024.\n\nThe course hours will be from 10:00 to 16:30 CEST each day, with a longer break from 12:00 to 13:30.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"At the end of the course you will be able to:\n\n- understand how to address your problem using machine learning techniques;\n- create your own workflow based on the templates provided in the course;\n- find tools from the various existing libraries;\n- appreciate the limitations of you knowledge and where to find expert knowledge. ","summary":"This online course is an introduction to Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning and Deep Learning applied to Earth observation data. The aim of the course is to provide an ","content":null,"targetAudience":"Member State weather and associated services starting to work in AI/ML on weather data.\nThe course is aimed at people with little prior knowledge. You will need to be comfortable to edit some python using Jupyter notebooks. ","registrationHowto":"If you already have an account on EUMETSAT's virtual classroom, visit the following page to submit your application form: https://classroom.eumetsat.int/mod/questionnaire/view.php?id=15727. \n\nOtherwise, please make sure you create an account on the platform: click on Login (on the top right section of the page), create a new user (Create an account), and follow the procedure. With your new account, please log in, then access the 'Apply for Courses' section (https://classroom.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158) to submit your application form.","registrationEndDate":1713398400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":27,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2399,"created":1711110356000,"updated":null,"title":"The National Severe Weather Warning Service at the Met Office","titleNative":"The National Severe Weather Warning Service at the Met Office","startDate":1714003200000,"endDate":1714046400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem35","description":"The National Severe Weather Warning Service at the Met Office Established in the wake of a major windstorm over the UK in October 1987, the National Severe Weather Warning Service is the Met Office’s flagship weather warning service. This impact-based public warnings services uses a matrix to communicate the likelihood and impact of a number of weather hazards, in particular the general public and emergency planning and responder communities.\n\nIn this webinar, one of the Met Office’s Chief Operational Meteorologists, who is responsible for issuing these warnings, will talk through the warnings service, explaining how warnings are made and what the matrix used to communicate the warnings is used. One of the Senior Scientists in the Weather Impacts Science Team who has developed some of the decision aids used to make these warnings will discuss aspects of these decision aids. Finally, there will also be input from the Met Office Civil Contingencies Advisors who are involved in communicating these warnings to the emergency responder community.","country":null,"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/ba2631f9-05e2-4671-a2f6-55816787f04a@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2381,"created":1706102915000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"EUMDAC Series - Session 4: EUMDAC Advanced use of EUMDAC as a Python Library - Data Access Services","titleNative":"EUMDAC Series - Session 4: EUMDAC Advanced use of EUMDAC as a Python Library - Data Access Services","startDate":1713877200000,"endDate":1713884400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This series is designed to familiarize participants with EUMETSAT's data access services, focusing on interacting with Data Store and Data Tailor APIs through the Python Library EUMDAC.\n\nSession 4 aims to introduce participants to leveraging EUMDAC's capabilities through scripting languages, focusing on Jupyter Notebooks. The content includes an overview of Jupyter Notebooks, their integration with EUMDAC, and a demonstration of using the DAS Jupyter Notebooks. Participants will engage in guided sessions, running pre-created Jupyter Notebooks, understanding exceptions thrown by the library, and learning the data tailor job management process as a practical example.\n\nParticipants who attend every session of this series will have the opportunity to receive a certificate of participation.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Users should have competence in leveraging EUMDAC's capabilities through Jupyter Notebooks \n\n-Users should be able to find the correct comprehensive documentation and resources for ongoing learning and reference beyond the course sessions.","summary":"This series is designed to familiarize participants with EUMETSAT's data access services, focusing on interacting with Data Store and Data Tailor APIs through the Python Library EU","content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using EUMETSAT Data Access Services","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_kiQ6lZ5gRQGzfN7rQjnkFw ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":41,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2400,"created":1711464384000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Using Jupyter on the EWC to interact with ECMWF datasets","titleNative":"Using Jupyter on the EWC to interact with ECMWF datasets","startDate":1713859200000,"endDate":1713862800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT & ECMWF","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the second thematic EWC webinar of 2024.\n\nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at new or prospective users of the EWC service, provided by EUMETSAT and ECMWF, which is available to all ECMWF and EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating States. Our primary objective is to provide guidance to users on how to effectively use the different capabilites of the EWC.\n\nWhile the first two webinars in 2023 focused on the basics to get you started (you can find more information, including the video recordings, here and here), in this series we explore various aspects of cloud utilisation through examples, with a specific emphasis on key functionalities and cloud skills.\n\nThroughout this webinar, we will guide you through the step-by-step process of spinning up your personalised Jupyter instance on the cloud including the provisioning of the virtual infrastructure required, as well as how to automate the deployment of the necessary software stack with ansible and git.\n\nOnce our Jupyter platform is up and running, we will explore various examples illustrating how to work with ECMWF datasets. From downloading and processing data to visualising insights in an interactive manner, this webinar aims to equip you with additional tools and knowledge needed to leverage the power of the European Weather Cloud to access your favourite weather and climate datasets.\n\nBy the end of this 1-hour session, participants will have learnt about how to automate the provisioning of a cloud service such as Jupyter as well as familiarised themselves with different tools to access the ECMWF Data Services portfolio.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the second thematic EWC webinar of 2024.\n\nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at n","content":null,"targetAudience":"This webinar is open to anyone from an ECMWF or EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating State.","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://events.ecmwf.int/event/400/","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2358,"created":1701339676000,"updated":1701341033000,"title":"SEEMET Regional Training Course ","titleNative":"SEEMET Regional Training Course","startDate":1713769200000,"endDate":1714132800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Sarajevo","host":"Federal Hydrometeorological Service of Bosnia and Herzegovina","contactPerson":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"Natasa.StrelecMahovic@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"Regional course for forecasters, covering the training on satellite data in combination with other data used in the operational forecast environment.\nSouth-East Europe Meteorological training course SEEMET-2024 is  hosted by Federal Hydrometeorological Service of Bosnia and Herzegovina in Sarajevo and supported by EUMETSAT,  EUMETCAL and ECMWF. It is the ninth in the series of courses aiming to regularly train operational staff of the  South-East European Meteorological and Hydrological Services.\n\nThe course will be a basic satellite course. The lectures and exercises will focus on applications of satellite data and products with a special emphasis on the applications of MTG data. Additionally, ECMWF products available as Open Charts will be introduced. \n\nThe course will consist of a 4.5-day classroom workshop in Sarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina. The course will be composed of lectures and practical exercises.","country":{"id":"BA","name":"BOSNIA AND HERZEGOVINA","region":"RA-VI","type":"RA-VI"},"learningOutcome":"Improved skills in forecasting.\nBasic satellite data interpretation skills - channel interpretation, RGBs and their applications, with special emphasis on MTG data. \n\n","summary":"Regional course for forecasters, covering the training on satellite data in combination with other data used in the operational forecast environment.\nSouth-East Europe Meteorologic","content":null,"targetAudience":"Operational forecasters, in particular junior forecasters.","registrationHowto":"This course application requires prior nomination. The link for application is sent with the invitation to the SE Europe Meteorological Services directors. If you wish to participate, please contact your Director or Head of service.\nApplication site will open in January 2024.","registrationEndDate":1708819200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":23,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false},{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"title":"Data Applications","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"name":"SAF archive"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2360,"created":1701965531000,"updated":1707991824000,"title":"13th EARSeL Workshop on Imaging Spectroscopy: EUMETSAT tools for ocean colour validation and hyperspectral radiometry","titleNative":"13th EARSeL Workshop on Imaging Spectroscopy: EUMETSAT tools for ocean colour validation and hyperspectral radiometry","startDate":1713520800000,"endDate":1713535200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Valéncia","host":"University of Valencia","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://is.earsel.org/workshop/13-IS-Valencia2024/","description":"EUMETSAT operate the <b>Copernicus Sentinel-3</b> mission and are responsible for the generation and dissemination of marine products, including those from the multi-spectral <b>Ocean and Land Colour Instrument (OLCI)</b> sensor. We also offer a number of tools for managing and processing multi- and hyperspectral in situ radiometry data for the purposes of ocean colour validation. During this 4-hour training event we will demonstrate how to access our data, and give an overview of some of these tools. We will cover;\n\n* Programmatic access to Copernicus Sentinel-3 OLCI data, using <a href=\"https://gitlab.eumetsat.int/eumetlab/data-services/eumdac/\">EUMDAC</a> and the <a href=\"https://data.eumetsat.int/\">EUMETSAT Data Store</a>\n* How to format data for, and submit data to, the Copernicus Ocean Colour Database (<a href=\"https://ocdb.readthedocs.io/en/latest/index.html\">OCDB</a>)\n* An overview of the <a href=\"https://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.948492\">GLORIA</a> hyperspectral in situ data base\n* How to use the <a href=\"https://gitlab.eumetsat.int/eumetlab/oceans/ocean-science-studies/ThoMaS\">ThoMaS</a> match-up toolkit to validate OLCI multi-spectral ocean colour products in OCDB/SeaBass format in situ data\n* Provide an overview and demonstration of the <a href=\"https://github.com/nasa/HyperCP\">FRM4SOC Hyper CP processor</a>\n\nThe tutorial will provide examples of how to work with our data using open-source Python packages and freely shareable Jupyter Notebooks. In addition, we will outline future EUMETSAT training opportunities in 2024 and beyond, and provide a platform for an open discussion on any facet of EUMETSAT ocean colour data.","country":{"id":"ES","name":"SPAIN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the workshop, you will:\n\n* know how to access to our Copernicus ocean colour products, supported by practical examples\n* be aware of, and be able to submit to, the Copernicus Ocean Colour Database\n* understand how to use OLCI ocean-colour validation toolkit, ThoMaS\n* be familiar with new approaches for processing hyperspectral radiometry data using HyperCP","summary":"EUMETSAT operate the <b>Copernicus Sentinel-3</b> mission and are responsible for the generation and dissemination of marine products, including those from the multi-spectral <b>Oc","content":null,"targetAudience":"The tutorial is open to all EARSeL workshop attendees, but would particularly benefit;\n\n* marine remote sensing scientists interested in ocean colour product validation\n* researchers and field scientists conducting either multi- or hyperspectral in situ radiometry measurements","registrationHowto":"All applications should be made via the 13th EARSeL Workshop on Imaging Spectroscopy <a href=\"https://is.earsel.org/workshop/13-IS-Valencia2024/\">conference website</a>.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"Yes","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Cop