Long Course - Using Data Store and Data Tailor through EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC)","startDate":1712016000000,"endDate":1714435200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"DAS training team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The duration of the online course will be five weeks, during which you are invited to join five live sessions for listening to presentations from other experts and to share your experiences with other course participants.\n\nThis course is designed to familiarize participants with EUMETSAT's data access services, focusing on EUMDAC. The duration of the online course will be four weeks, during which you are invited to join five live sessions. Following, a summary of the course:\n\n- Session 1 provides an overview of EUMETSAT's data access services, introducing key concepts.\n\n- Sessions 2 focuses into EUMDAC basics features using the Command Line Interface (CLI) and offering scenario-based exercises. \n\n- Session 3 of the course dives deeper into the advanced features and capabilities of EUMDAC through the Command Line Interface, offering participants an in-depth exploration of advanced CLI commands and options, including a focus on understanding all capabilities, complex customizations, and tasks such as cleaning jobs.\n\n- Session 4 explores advanced use of EUMDAC as a Python Library, specifically integrating with Jupyter Notebooks, and includes guided sessions on running pre-created notebooks and managing data tailor jobs.\n\n-Session 5: Practical approaches. Using EUMDAC from a marine perspective.\n\n\nParticipants who attend every session of this course will have the opportunity to receive a certificate of participation.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Users should gain a comprehensive understanding of EUMETSAT's key services.\n\n- Users should acquire proficiency in executing fundamental Command Line Interface (CLI) commands in EUMDAC\n\n- Users should demonstrate competence in leveraging EUMDAC's capabilities through Jupyter Notebooks \n\n- Users should be equipped with the ability to independently create, run, and troubleshoot Jupyter Notebooks within the EUMDAC library\n\n- Users should be able to find the correct comprehensive documentation and resources for ongoing learning and reference beyond the course sessions.\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the EUMETSAT's Data Access Services","registrationHowto":"1st session(1h): https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_CotT4G6tRAifP93XaeBzOg\n\n2nd session(1h): https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_AZ2vmbKIT8aT0t4a-nKxTg\n\n3rd session(2h): https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9rrc2MzrSce-Ho2oARIF2A\n\n4th session(2h): https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_kiQ6lZ5gRQGzfN7rQjnkFw\n\n5th session(2h): https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_PngHDbfzRS6TmKP6H_cWyQ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2397,"created":1710357926000,"updated":1710399663000,"title":"Introduction to Lightning Observations and Applications","titleNative":"Introduction to Lightning Observations and Applications","startDate":1711461600000,"endDate":1712079000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA ARSET","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3OwyOYE","description":"It is well-documented that there are approximately 24,000 worldwide fatalities from lightning each year, with about 10 times more being injured from lightning (NIH-NCBI). In addition, lightning strikes are one of the leading causes of wildfire ignition. During storms, lightning strikes on trees, utility poles, and infrastructure, can damage power lines resulting in power outages. Lightning flashes also generate electromagnetic fields (Sferics) that interfere with electrical devices on ground. As the intensity and frequency of extreme weather events are likely to increase due to climate change impacts, lightning activity will likely increase as well, causing more power outages, increased risks of wildfire ignition, and increased numbers of injuries and fatalities. Therefore, information about lightning activity is critical for better preparedness against these disasters. This three-part, introductory training focuses on global and regional lightning data products that can be applied to disaster risk preparedness.\n ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\tIdentify common lightning causes, patterns, and potential for causing damage\n\tIdentify how space- and ground-based lightning observations are used to monitor lightning frequency and intensity\n\tIdentify resources for accessing lightning data products\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for remote sensing scientists, geospatial analysts, managers from local, state, and federal government, power companies, fire responders, geospatial analysts, academic faculty and students, and other practitioners in the field of remote sensing.","registrationHowto":"Course Dates: March 26, 28, and April 2, 2024\n\nTime: 11:00 -12:30 or 2:00-3:30 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\nhttps://go.nasa.gov/3OwyOYE\n","registrationEndDate":1713801600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":36,"title":"Fires","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":31,"name":"GOES"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2393,"created":1709022546000,"updated":null,"title":"IPMA warning system","titleNative":"IPMA warning system","startDate":1711022400000,"endDate":1711026000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/bded1d8f-497b-462c-b598-dc82086edf46@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","description":"This webinar will cover the following topics:\n- Meteoalarm warnings and close collaboration with civil protection authorities are the basis of the IPMA warning system.\n- Warning criteria are being reviewed to adapt to impact warnings.\n- Examples of critical situations in issuing a red precipitation warning are given.\n\nWebinar will be presented by Paula Leião (IPMA). It will take place on Thursday 21 March 2024 at 12:00 UTC / 13:00 CET. It is free and open for everyone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/bded1d8f-497b-462c-b598-dc82086edf46@396b9e20-59c1-4cf1-bc03-d43fd5759427","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2395,"created":1709630488000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Using the European Weather Cloud to download data from the EUMETSAT Data Access Services","titleNative":"Using the European Weather Cloud to download data from the EUMETSAT Data Access Services","startDate":1711011600000,"endDate":1711015200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT & ECMWF","contactPerson":"DAS Training Team","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The European Weather Cloud (EWC) teams at ECMWF and EUMETSAT are pleased to invite you to the first thematic EWC webinar of 2024, following two successful introductory webinars held last year.\n\nThese recurring thematic webinars are aimed at new or prospective users of the EWC service, provided by EUMETSAT and ECMWF, which is available to all ECMWF and EUMETSAT Member and Co-operating States. Our primary objective is to provide guidance to users on how to effectively use the different capabilities of the EWC.\n\nWhile the first two webinars in 2023 focused on the basics to get you started (you can find more information, including the video recordings, here and here), in this webinar participants will explore various aspects of cloud utilization, with a specific emphasis on key functionalities such as provisioning and configuring virtual machines. Furthermore, we will explore how to access the EUMETSAT data catalogue made available through the Data Access Services, more precisely, using the EUMETSAT Data Access Client. Additionally, we will show the utilization of the pre-installed application, Data Tailor, which offers customization options, enabling users to tailor datasets according to their requirements and preferences. \n\nBy the end of this 1-hour session, participants will not only have gained valuable insights into the operational dynamics of the EWC, but will also possess the practical skills needed to navigate the EUMETSAT Data Access Services.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"t