t online courses. \n\nRespective Permanent Representatives (PR) with WMO will be informed about eligible participants within their country meeting the mandatory requirements, out of which they can propose one or maximum two candidates. PRs are further kindly requested to ensure that the right candidates are nominated for the courses, and subsequently deployed so that they are able to apply their competences from the courses. \n\nApplication deadline is 31 December 2023. ","country":{"id":"ZA","name":"SOUTH AFRICA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"- Analyze satellite data interpretation to monitor and detect severe weather.\n\n - Be a proficient user in RGB images.\n\n- Use the satellite data in the forecasting process. ","summary":"The objective of the satellite applications training course is to optimise the use of data from meteorological satellites and to increase the knowledge and skills of operational me","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters in Africa","registrationHowto":"Permanent Representatives with WMO will propose one, maximum two, participants from the list of eligible candidates within their country.\n\nThe final selection of accepted candidates will be made by EUMETSAT and SAWS and PRs will be informed of the selection. ","registrationEndDate":1704153540000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":23,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2384,"created":1706283009000,"updated":1706285030000,"title":"Large Scale Applications of Machine Learning using Remote Sensing for Building Agriculture Solutions","titleNative":"Large Scale Applications of Machine Learning using Remote Sensing for Building Agriculture Solutions","startDate":1709650800000,"endDate":1710880200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-large-scale-applications-machine-learning-using-remote-sensing?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=LargeScaleAgg","description":"Remote sensing data is becoming crucial to solve some of the most important environmental problems, especially pertaining to agricultural applications and food security. Effectively working with this large data source requires different tools and processing, such as cloud computing and infrastructure. Participants will become familiar with data format and quality considerations, tools, and techniques to process remote sensing imagery at large scale from publicly available satellite sources, using cloud tools such as AWS S3, Databricks, and Parquet. Additionally, participants will learn how to analyze and train machine learning models for classification using this large source of data to solve environmental problems with a focus on agriculture. Participants will have a basic understanding of tools such as Pyspark and TensorFlow. We hope that participants in this course will walk away with the skills and tools to train algorithms using satellite imagery to solve environmental problems anywhere on the planet.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 2: End hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition and promote sustainable agriculture\n\nCourse Format: Three 1.5-hour parts including Q&A.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n\n\tUse recommended techniques to download and process remote sensing data from Sentinel-2 and the cropland data layer (CDL) at large scale (> 5GB) with cloud tools (Amazon Web Services [AWS] Simple Storage Service [S3], Databricks, Spark, Parquet)\n\tFilter data from both the measured (satellite images) and target (CDL) domains to serve modeling objectives based on quality factors, land classification, area of interest [AOI] overlap, and geographical location\n\tBuild training pipelines in TensorFlow to train machine learning algorithms on large scale remote sensing/geospatial datasets for agricultural monitoring\n\tUtilize random sampling techniques to build robustness into a predictive algorithm while avoiding information leakage across training/validation/testing splits\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for remote sensing scientists, practitioners, and geospatial analysts from local, regional, federal, and non-governmental organizations who use remote sensing for agricultural applications. Agronomists, data scientists/data engineers/ML engineers may also be interested in this training.","registrationHowto":"To Register: https://go.nasa.gov/4aSQmYP\n\nCourse Dates: March 5, 12, and 19, 2024\n\nTimes: 10:00 -11:30 or 2:00-3:30 EST (UTC-5, UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\n","registrationEndDate":1710874800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true},{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2527,"created":1738761122000,"updated":1738762071000,"title":"WMO Nowcasting Course for Africa","titleNative":"WMO Nowcasting Course for Africa","startDate":1709542800000,"endDate":1709910000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Nairobi","host":"Kenya Meteorological Department/Institute for Meteorological Training and Research (KMD/IMTR)","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://classroom.eumetsat.int/enrol/index.php?id=511","description":"World Meteorological Organization (WMO) Education and Training Office in collaboration with the WMO Regional Training Centre in the Kenya Meteorological Department, Institute for Meteorological Training and Research (KMD/IMTR – RTC Nairobi) and the European Organization for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), has designed a training course for the development of competencies on the use of satellite data and products in weather nowcasting. The course is focused on enabling English-speaking operational meteorologists from WMO Regional Association I (RA-I) to issue warnings and alerts on hazards and extremes related to weather and climate to the public and communities using satellite data and products as support to the implementation of the Early Warnings for All initiative (EW4ALL) in RA I.","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Skills in using satellite imagery in nowcasting. ","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecaster in RA-I.","registrationHowto":"For invited participants only. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":23,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":100,"value":"WMO","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":8,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Kenya","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639