ery and products for meteorological applications, using SLIDER (http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu) for imagery. Anyone with an interest is welcome to attend.\n\nGoToWebinar is the software platform used. The session will begin at 16:00 UTC, with the webinar opening 10 minutes earlier (15:50 UTC) for those who wish to check their microphone.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://register.gotowebinar.com/register/6956542335214270549","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5874,"name":"Erin Sanders","email":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":30,"value":"CIRA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2455,"created":1721387253000,"updated":1721716771000,"title":"Monthly Regional Weather and Climate Forums - February 2024 Weather Briefings for Middle East Region","titleNative":"Monthly Regional Weather and Climate Forums - February 2024 Weather Briefings for Middle East Region","startDate":1707980400000,"endDate":1707984000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Ibrahim AbdulSalam","contactEmail":"Ibrahim AbdulSalam@caa.gov.om","contactUrl":"https://coemct.met.gov.om/course/view.php?id=83","description":"Monthly Regional Weather and Climate Forums- Weather Briefings generally focus on the latest hot topics related to weather and climate in the Middle East Region and the latest updates on satellite earth observations.\n\nThe February Forum is scheduled for Thursday, February 15, 2024, from 07:00 to 08:00 UTC, and it will focus on \"Comprehending Extreme Heat Services: Exploring Heatwaves, Standardizing Forecasts, and Warnings\":\n1. State of Extreme Heat Servecies.\n2. Road Map for Extreme Heat Services.\n3. Handbook of Extreme Heat Indicators, Indices and Metrics.\n4. Heatwaves and Heat Health, Guidance on Early Warning Systems.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"•\tMeteorologists & Weather Forecasters\n•\tEnvironment and Atmospheric Scientists\n•\tGeneral users of weather and Satellite Applications","registrationHowto":"To join the upcoming forum go to https://coemct.met.gov.om/course/view.php?id=83","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":8109,"name":"Zamzam AL-Rawahi ","email":"Zamzam.Rawahi@caa.gov.om","agency":"","country":"OM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":7,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Oman"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false},{"id":7,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Oman","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2383,"created":1706206070000,"updated":1707387122000,"title":"Overview of SeaDAS 8.4.1 for the Processing, Analysis, and Visualization of Optical Remote Sensing Data for Water Quality Monitoring","titleNative":"Overview of SeaDAS 8.4.1 for the Processing, Analysis, and Visualization of Optical Remote Sensing Data for Water Quality Monitoring","startDate":1707836400000,"endDate":1707858900000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-overview-seadas-840-processing-analysis-and-visualization?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SeaDAS2024","description":"SeaDAS software, developed by the NASA Ocean Biology Processing Group (OBPG), is used in the processing, analysis, and visualization of satellite images. SeaDAS uses OBPG algorithms to produce water quality data and can be used to obtain water quality parameters from current optical sensors such as OLI (Operational Land Imager), MSI (MultiSpectral Instrument), OLCI (Ocean and Land Colour Instrument), VIIRS (Visible Infrared Imaging Radiometer Suite), and MODIS (MODerate resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer). SeaDAS can also be used to apply atmospheric correction and obtain remote sensing reflectance at the water surface level from these sensors.\n\nThis two-hour training will provide an overview and demonstration of the latest version of SeaDAS 8.4.1, which is  useful for remote sensing of water quality monitoring. This training will also serve as a prerequisite for future ARSET training on remote sensing of water quality. \n\nUN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 6: Ensure availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation for all\n•\tTarget 6.6: By 2030, protect and restore water-related ecosystems, including mountains, forests, wetlands, rivers, aquifers and lakes\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to:\n\n•\tIdentify expanded sensor data processing capability of the latest version of SeaDAS for sensors such as OLCI and MSI\n•\tUse SeaDAS tools to analyze and visualize a water quality parameter, such as chlorophyll-a concentration, from Sentinel-3 OLCI for a given water body\n•\tImprove awareness of the plans for incorporating future PACE (Plankton, Aerosol, Cloud ocean Ecosystem) data processing into SeaDAS\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Local, state, and federal water quality managers, fisheries advisors, aquaculture managers, freshwater and coastal ecosystems managers, and academic researchers working on remote sensing of water quality. ","registrationHowto":"Times: 10:00-12:15 or 14:00-16:15 EST (UTC-5); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\nTo Register: https://go.nasa.gov/48mcmZW\n","registrationEndDate":1707850800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":26,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2376,"created":1706088959000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"","titleNative":"Data Access Services - Data Store and Data Tailor through Graphical Interface and EUMDAC","startDate":1707786000000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"online","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Data Access Services Training Team ","contactEmail":"das-training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This session aims to provide a comprehensive understanding of utilizing the EUMETSAT Data Store and Data Tailor, emphasizing both the Graphical User Interface (GUI) and Application User Interface (API). Participants will gain understanding of the Python Library EUMDAC for effective interaction with APIs. Furthermore, it offers a unique opportunity for participants to engage in discussions with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues.The session will cover 1 hour and will be divided into three segments:\n\n- Data Store/Data Tailor UIs and APIs\n- EUMDAC features\n- Questions and answers\n\nWe encourage you to post your questions on sli.do  ( https://app.sli.do/event/flsdivtc ) so that we can adapt the content of the next session to answer them!\n\nThe sessions are open to all and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to scientists and forecasters. Registration via Zoom is required. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Users should be able to use the Data Store service to browse, search for, download and eventually subscribe to, collections and products of interest using EUMDAC, as required.\nUsers should be able to use the Data Tailor Web Service to customise products to create bespoke data streams that fit their applications, via EUMDAC, as required\nUsers should know where to find resources to support the use of the new data access services\nUsers should know where to go for further help in using the new data access services","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the EUMETSAT data ","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_RDs3dulNRc-vIGVHviOk0A ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"prev