s, frontal sub-structures and mesoscale features. Depending on the operational readiness of MTG, the participants will also have an opportunity to apply Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) imagery in their learning.","summary":"The Synoptic and Mesoscale System Analyses will be delivered in autumn 2023. The classroom period will be held 4-8 December. The course will be hosted by DWD with the course venue ","content":null,"targetAudience":"This course is intended to European forecasters, who have attended the preceding online phase 23 October - 1 December.","registrationHowto":"Applications will open in summer 2023. Follow the information at EUMeTrain web site https://eumetrain.org. There is no course fee. The participants are expected to come self-funded. Some limited travel support may be possible for selected participants.","registrationEndDate":1701693720000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":25,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2342,"created":1696839371000,"updated":1700688753000,"title":"Operational Satellite Oceanography Workshop ","titleNative":"Operational Satellite Oceanography Workshop ","startDate":1701043200000,"endDate":1701647940000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":null,"contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=492","description":"In response to needs identified by the Third International Operational Satellite Oceanography Symposium in June 2023, the hosts (EUMETSAT, NOAA, KHOA and KIOST) are convening a follow-up **Operational Satellite Oceanography Workshop** which will offer further training on how to exploit operational marine Earth observation data streams. The training event, which will take place online from 27 to 29 November, will give an overview of satellite products from the partners as well as provide guidance and tutorials on using available tools and software packages to facilitate data analysis, automated data access and processing and product validation.\n\nThe workshop will be split into three sessions, scheduled as follows:\n\n* Session 1: Monday 27 November, NOAA CoastWatch (15:00 - 21:00 UTC)\n* Session 2: Tuesday 28 November, EUMETSAT (10:00 - 18:00 UTC)\n* Session 3: Wednesday 29 November, KIOST/KHOA (12:00 - 15:00 UTC) \n\nNote that the sessions are timed to accommodate audiences in multiple time zones, and so shift each day.\n\nDuring Session 1, the **<a href=\"https://coastwatch.noaa.gov/cwn/index.html\">NOAA CoastWatch</a>** team will give an overview of the CoastWatch program, conduct demos of the **<a href=\"https://coastwatch.noaa.gov/cw_html/cwViewer.html\">(CoastWatch Data Portal)</a>**, **<a href=\"https://coastwatch.noaa.gov/cwn/data-access-tools/erddap-noaa-coastwatch.html\">ERDDAP</a>**, and the \n**<a href=\"https://coastwatch.noaa.gov/cwn/data-access-tools/coastwatch-utilities.html\">CoastWatch Utilities</a>**. Participants will then follow a self-paced tutorial to learn how to make different types of visualisations and how to use command line tools to extract information from satellite data files. In Session 2, the **<a href=\"https://www.eumetsat.int/\">EUMETSAT</a>** marine training team will discuss automated product access from the **<a href=\"https://data.eumetsat.int/search?query=\">EUMETSAT Data Store</a>**, batch-processing with **<a href=\"https://step.esa.int/main/download/snap-download/\">SNAP</a>**, and Copernicus Sentinel-3 OLCI ocean colour product validation with the **<a href=\"https://gitlab.eumetsat.int/eumetlab/oceans/ocean-science-studies/ThoMaS\">ThoMaS</a>** software package. In Session 3, the KIOST and KHOA team will give an overview of the GOCI-II geostationary ocean colour instrument, outlining data access approaches and showcasing examples of its operational use in tracking sargassum. For more information on each session, please consult the \n**<a href=\"https://umd.instructure.com/courses/1356565\">course overview and preparation page</a>**.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"* Visualise CoastWatch data\n* Use command line tools to perform data extractions from CoastWatch products\n* Access data operationally through the EUMETSAT Data Store APIs and EUMDAC client.\n* Conduct batch processing using SNAP and supporting Jupyter notebooks\n* Extract and analyse in situ matchups with Sentinel-3 ocean colour data using ThoMaS - a Tool to generate Matchups of OC products with Sentinel-3/OLCI\n* Work with GOCI-II data","summary":"In response to needs identified by the Third International Operational Satellite Oceanography Symposium in June 2023, the hosts (EUMETSAT, NOAA, KHOA and KIOST) are convening a fol","content":null,"targetAudience":"* Established and early career marine remote sensing scientists\n* Application/service developers looking to incorporate remote sensing into operational processing systems\n* Oceanographers of all disciplines who are looking to expand their research into Earth observation","registrationHowto":"Please note that this event is limited to 50 participants. To register for the course, please begin by registering for one of the pre-check events on Nov. 20, 2023, via this **<a href=\"https://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/tZIvduivrzMjHtQjfE2dWq7_LOLuU7k1j8wM?_x_zm_rtaid=tJoJnU6rRaiYtyn6bBVCXw.1696835710576.857f4472f2ef585471239bab251e95fe&_x_zm_rhtaid=4#/registration\">link</a>**.  You need only attend one of the pre-check sessions.\n\nPrior to the pre-check event, please work through the following \n**<a href=\"https://forms.gle/aBayvaMidyD51XDC9\">checklist</a>** to ensure you have all the tools you require for the event itself. If you run into any issues, you will be able to get some help during the pre-check meeting. Once you have submitted your completed checklist, you will receive the links to the full workshop. Attendance at the workshop will only be possible if you attend the pre-check event and complete the checklist, on a first come, first serve basis.\n\nIf you are not able to attend the pre-check event, please email us at **ops@eumetsat.int** with \"OSOW23 pre-check event\" as the email title.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":9,"name":"Sentinel-6"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2304,"created":1684142273000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Data Access Services - How to use the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface ","titleNative":"Data Access Services - How to use the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface ","startDate":1700740800000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=436","description":"This series of 30-minute sessions is designed to support the transition from the EUMETSAT Data Centre in favour of the Data Store. This particular session focuses on using the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface (CLI) . Due to the reduction of products in the Data Centre, this session will be a great opportunity to remove any technical challenges in using the Data Access Services GUIs, APIs, and EUMDAC, and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues. Please, read more information about the transition here: https://eumetsatspace.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EUM/blog/2023/03/22/1965359114/Switching+the+data+access+from+the+Data+Centre+to+the+Data+Store+for+faster+delivery+times.\n\nThe session w