id":19,"name":"EUMETView"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":31,"name":"GOES"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2247,"created":1673355565000,"updated":1700688256000,"title":"FMI-EUMETSAT Aviation Forecast Testbed ","titleNative":"FMI-EUMETSAT Aviation Forecast Testbed ","startDate":1698624000000,"endDate":1698883200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Helsinki","host":"FMI","contactPerson":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"Aviation Forecaster Testbed for the new generation satellite data offer aviation forecasters the opportunity to apply novel satellite data together with other products in the operational aviation forecast environment, and to evaluate these data and products. \nAt these events forecasters will learn by doing, by making aviation forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, followed by a verification. Particular focus will be given to the use of proxy-MTG satellite data (e.g., from the NASA MODIS, NOAA VIIRS and Sentinel-3/OLCI instruments) and, once operationally available, real data from MTG in order to prepare forecasters for the use of next-generation satellite data. ","country":{"id":"FI","name":"FINLAND","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Enhancing skills in using satellite data and products in aviation forecasting.\n","summary":"Aviation Forecaster Testbed for the new generation satellite data offer aviation forecasters the opportunity to apply novel satellite data together with other products in the opera","content":null,"targetAudience":"Aviation forecasters from EUMETSAT Member States.","registrationHowto":"The invitations will be sent to Heads of Delegations of the EUMETSAT Member states. The applications should follow the nominations by the NMS.","registrationEndDate":1690761600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":24,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":1,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Forecaster"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":27,"title":"Atmospheric phenomena","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":26,"title":"Cloud types","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2343,"created":1697214889000,"updated":1697271753000,"title":"SAR for Detecting and Monitoring Floods, Sea Ice, and Subsidence from Groundwater Extraction","titleNative":"SAR for Detecting and Monitoring Floods, Sea Ice, and Subsidence from Groundwater Extraction","startDate":1698159600000,"endDate":1698868800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-measuring-floods-subsidence-and-sea-ice-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23","description":"This training is a follow-on to the SAR training held in October 2022, which covered detection and monitoring of oil spills, landslides, and floods. This training will expand on the theory and applications of SAR data to detect and monitor floods through the use of SAR time-series in order to more closely monitor the increase/recession of flood waters. This training will also cover two new application areas: the use of InSAR to measure subsidence due to groundwater extraction, and the use of SAR to detect and monitor sea ice. \n \nThese application areas are important for environmental managers from local, regional, and federal governments concerned with 1.) the impact of groundwater extraction on infrastructure as well as diminishing hydrological resources; 2.) the risk of sea ice on ships and shipping routes as well as the impact of diminishing sea ice on coastal erosion - especially as related to indigenous communities in Alaska and Canada; and 3.) the impact of floods and how monitoring their extent and increase/decrease can help with disaster response activities. This training will address these applications through the use of open-source tools and SAR data to inform on disaster awareness and response and how to best allocate resources to mitigate their impacts.\n \nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 12: Ensure sustainable consumption and production patterns\n•\tGoal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts \n\nCourse Dates: October 24, 31, & November 1, 2023\n \nTime: 11:00 -13:00 EDT (UTC-4); This training is also available in Spanish: 14:00-16:00 EDT (UTC-4).\n \nTo Register: \nEnglish Session – https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-measuring-floods-subsidence-and-sea-ice-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23\n\nSpanish Session –  https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/spanish/arset-medicion-de-inundaciones-hundimiento-y-hielo-marino-con-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23-spanish\n \nCourse Format: Three 2-hour parts including Q&A.\n \n\nSAR para la Detección y el Monitoreo de Inundaciones, el Hielo Marino y la Subsidencia del Suelo por Extracción de Agua\n\nEsta capacitación es una continuación de la capacitación de SAR que se realizó en octubre de 2022, la cual cubrió la detección y el monitoreo de derrames de petróleo, deslizamientos de tierra e inundaciones. Esta capacitación profundizará la teoría y aplicaciones de datos de SAR para detectar y monitorear inundaciones mediante el uso de imágenes temporales de radar con la finalidad de monitorear más de cerca el incremento/disminución de las inundaciones. Esta capacitación también cubrirá dos nuevas aplicaciones: el uso de interferometría por radar de apertura sintética (InSAR) para medir la subsidencia del suelo por la extracción de aguas subterráneas y el uso de SAR para detectar y monitorear hielo marino. Estas aplicaciones son importantes para gestores ambientales de gobiernos locales, regionales y federales (centrales) encargados de informar sobre 1) el impacto de la  extracción de aguas subterráneas en la infraestructura así como la disminución de recursos  hidrológicos; 2) el riesgo del hielo marino en barcos y rutas marítimas y también el impacto de la disminución del hielo marino en la erosión costera - especialmente cuanto concierne a poblaciones indígenas en Alaska y Canadá; y 3) el impacto de las inundaciones y cómo el monitoreo de su extensión e incremento/disminución puede ayudar con las actividades de respuesta a desastres. Esta capacitación abordará estas aplicaciones a través del uso  de herramientas y datos de fuente abierta para informar acerca de la concientización sobre desastres y la respuesta a estos y cómo mejor asignar recursos y mitigar sus impactos.\n\nObjetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible de la ONU Relevantes:\nObjetivo 12: Garantizar modalidades de consumo y producción sostenibles\nObjetivo 13: Adoptar medidas urgentes para combatir el cambio climático y sus efecto\n\nFechas: El 24, 31 de octubre y 01 de noviembre, 2023\n\nInscripciones: \n \nespañol: 14h a 16h Horario Este de EE.UU (UTC-4):  https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/spanish/arset-medicion-de-inundaciones-hundimiento-y-hielo-marino-con-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23-spanish\n\ninglés: 11h a 13h Horario Este de EE.UU. (UTC-4):  https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-measuring-floods-subsidence-and-sea-ice-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23\n\nObjectivos de Aprendizaje: Al finalizar esta capacitación, las/los participantes habrán desarrollado la capacidad para poder:\n•\tGenerar mapas de subsidencia de la superficie debido a la extracción de agua subterránea para informar sobre la gestión del riesgo y de recursos\n•\tDetectar y monitorear hielo marino para identificar posibles riesgos a la navegación y erosión costera\n•\tDetectar y monitorear inundaciones para monitorear más de cerca el incremento/disminucion de las inundaciónes e informar mejor la respuesta y gestión de desastres\n\nAudiencia Meta: Agencias de gestión de desastres, agencias de gobiernos nacionales e internacionales, organizaciones benéficas, poblaciones indígenas, estudiantes y académicos.\n\nFormato del Curso: Tres sesiones de dos horas\n\n\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n•\tGenerate subsidence maps due to groundwater extraction to inform risk and resource management\n•\tDetect and monitor sea ice to identify potential risks to shipping and coastal erosion\n•\tDetect and monitor floods in order to more closely monitor increase/recession of flood waters and better inform disaster response and management","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for disaster management agencies, including domestic and international government agencies, aid organizations, indigenous communities, students, and academics.\n ","registrationHowto":"To Register: \n\nEnglish Session – https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/english/arset-measuring-floods-subsidence-and-sea-ice-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23\n\nSpanish Session –  https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/get-involved/training/spanish/arset-medicion-de-inundaciones-hundimiento-y-hielo-marino-con-sar?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=SAR-23-spanish","registrationEndDate":1698861600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2303,"created":1684141906000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Data Access Services - How to use the Jupyter Notebooks from the EUMETSAT Data Access Services ","titleNative":"Data Access Services - How to use the Jupyter Notebooks from the EUMETSAT Data Access Services ","startDate":1698148800000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=436","description":"This series of 30-minute sessions is designed to support the transition from the EUMETSAT Data Centre in favour of the Data Store. This particular session focuses on using the Jupyter Notebooks to download, filter and customize EUMETSAT data. Due to the reduction of products in the Data Centre, this session will be a great opportunity to remove any technical challenges in using the Data Access Services Jupyter Notebooks, and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues. Please, read more information about the transition here: https://eumetsatspace.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EUM/blog/2023/03/22/1965359114/Switching+the+data+access+from+the+Data+Centre+to+the+Data+Store+for+faster+delivery+times.\n\nThe session will cover 30 minutes approximately.\n\nWe encourage you to post your questions on sli.do ( https://app.sli.do/event/flsdivtc ) so that we can adapt the content of the next session to answer them!\n\nThe sessions are open to all and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to scientists and forecasters. Registration via Zoom is required.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Users should be able to use the Data Store and Data Tailor Jupyter Notebooks.\n- Users should know where to find resources to support the use of the new data ac