r the most important features of the CLARA-A3 data record and its improvements compared to its predecessor. Attendees should know the data format and how to handle the data. One measure of a successful short course would be a measurable increase in the download numbers of CLARA data.","summary":"This online short course presents CLARA-A3, the latest edition a global climate data record on clouds, surface albedo and surface radiation, generated by the Satellite Application ","content":null,"targetAudience":"Users of the previous editions of the CLARA data record and all new users, who are interested in high quality long-term global data of clouds and surface radiation. This includes for instance, climate services and research institutes with focus on climate.","registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_8eWx4p9jSaam9LC3HjX-tw ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2324,"created":1693253198000,"updated":1693296128000,"title":"Building Climate Risk Assessments from Local Vulnerability and Exposure","titleNative":"Building Climate Risk Assessments from Local Vulnerability and Exposure","startDate":1695135600000,"endDate":1695328200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/46VbpaZ","description":"This ARSET Training will describe climate risk assessment approaches that originate with stakeholder expertise in the fundamental climate vulnerability and exposure of their system. By identifying at-risk assets and the types of climate conditions that drive problematic responses, stakeholders and scientists can co-develop risk information targeting specific climatic impact-drivers and utilizing climate observations and projections sets selected to suitably address those risks. \n \nThe training will provide an assessment and engagement framework and utilize examples from the NASA Climate Adaptation Science Investigators (CASI) Program that is preparing NASA facilities for future climate resilience.\n \nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 3: Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being for all at all ages\n•\tTarget 3.d: Strengthen the capacity of all countries, in particular developing countries, for early warning, risk reduction and management of national and global health risks\n•\tGoal 9: Build resilient infrastructure, promote inclusive and sustainable industrialization and foster innovation\n•\tGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable\n•\tTarget 11.b: By 2020, substantially increase the number of cities and human settlements adopting and implementing integrated policies and plans towards inclusion, resource efficiency, mitigation and adaptation to climate change, resilience to disasters, and develop and implement, in line with the Sendai Framework for Disaster Risk Reduction 2015-2030, holistic disaster risk management at all levels\n•\tGoal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts\n•\tTarget 13.1: Strengthen resilience and adaptive capacity to climate-related hazards and natural disasters in all countries\n•\tGoal 15: Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, and halt and reverse land degradation and halt biodiversity loss\n\nCourse Format: Two 1.5-hour parts including Q&A\n \n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n•\tTheory: Plan for a risk assessment tailored to their system of interest\n•\tResources: Identify NASA resources for climate risk assessment\n•\tContextual: Recognize importance of developing contextual intervention strategies for specific stakeholder decisions\n•\tDemonstration: Connect climate risk information to specific vulnerabilities and exposed assets to support climate action decision \n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for local, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations to use NASA Earth observations and modeled climate projection datasets for integration into their climate change-related work in different sectors.","registrationHowto":"To Register: https://go.nasa.gov/46VbpaZ","registrationEndDate":1695322800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":fa