vitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":60,"value":"EUMETSAT & NMS","visible":false},{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false},{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"title":"Mesoscale systems and convective storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2302,"created":1684141322000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Data Access Services - How to use the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface and as a Python library","titleNative":"Data Access Services - How to use the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface and as a Python library","startDate":1694692800000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=436","description":"This series of 30-minute sessions is designed to support the transition from the EUMETSAT Data Centre in favour of the Data Store. This particular session focuses on using the EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC) through Command Line Interface (CLI) and as a Python Library. Due to the reduction of products in the Data Centre, this session will be a great opportunity to remove any technical challenges in using the Data Access Client Services (EUMDAC), and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues. Please, read more information about the transition here: https://eumetsatspace.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EUM/blog/2023/03/22/1965359114/Switching+the+data+access+from+the+Data+Centre+to+the+Data+Store+for+faster+delivery+times.\n\nThe session will cover 30 minutes approximately.\n\nWe encourage you to post your questions on sli.do ( https://app.sli.do/event/flsdivtc ) so that we can adapt the content of the next session to answer them!\n\nThe sessions are open to all and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to scientists and forecasters. Registration via Zoom is required.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Users should be able to use the Data Store service to browse, search for, download and eventually subscribe to, collections and products of interest using EUMDAC, as required; \n- Users should be able to use the Data Tailor Web Service to customise products to create bespoke data streams that fit their applications, via EUMDAC, as required; \n- Users should know where to find resources to support the use of the new data access services;\n- Users should know where to go for further help in using the new data access services","summary":"This series of 30-minute sessions is designed to support the transition from the EUMETSAT Data Centre in favour of the Data Store. This particular session focuses on using the EUME","content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the new EUMETSAT Data Access Services, especially users of the Data Centre.","registrationHowto":"Register for the session: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9ScreMSbQg6dvA6fmM5ldQ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2344,"created":1697660363000,"updated":1752481180000,"title":"5th Joint Atmospheric Composition Training School","titleNative":"5th Joint Atmospheric Composition Training School","startDate":1694649600000,"endDate":1695945600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Innsbruck","host":null,"contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://atmostraining.info/","description":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECMWF) with the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) are organising the fifth joint training course on Atmospheric Composition in September 2023.\n\nThe school will introduce the participants to state-of-the-art remote sensing and in-situ measurement techniques for atmospheric composition monitoring in a global context. Key course topics include combining different ground based approaches for the validation of satellite retrievals in different scenarios, underlying how high quality satellite retrievals can improve the reliability of global atmospheric model simulations. Additional aims include fostering collaboration amongst participants and encouraging the development of individual and team projects using the data, resources and methodologies presented.\n\nInitiative: ESA \nTraining Partner: ECMWF, EUMETSAT, Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"The school will introduce the participants to state-of-the-art remote sensing and in-situ measurement techniques for atmospheric composition monitoring in a global context. Key course topics include combining different ground based approaches for the validation of satellite retrievals in different scenarios, underlying how high quality satellite retrievals can improve the reliability of global atmospheric model simulations. Additional aims include fostering collaboration amongst participants and encouraging the development of individual and team projects using the data, resources and methodologies presented.","summary":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECM","content":null,"targetAudience":"The school is of interest for PhD students, early-career scientists, researchers from academia and research institutes, young scientists from industry, and anyone interested in atmospheric composition monitoring and modeling.\nOnsite school is limited to 30 participants. Students from ESA, EUMETSAT and ECMWF member states are given preference. Students from all other countries are also welcome to apply, subject to availability of space. Webinars prior to the practicals will be accessible to all.","registrationHowto":"\n","registrationEndDate":1682640000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":null,"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":224,"value":"ECMWF","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"title":"Aerosols","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2323,"created":1692975422000,"updated":1692978629000,"title":"Comprehensive analysis of observational information for the detection of aerosols in the atmosphere","titleNative":"Análisis integral de la información observacional para la detección de aerosoles en la atmósfera","startDate":1693828800000,"endDate":1696550400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"CoE SMN-Argentina","contactPerson":"Diana Marina Rodriguez","contactEmail":"dmr@smn.gob.ar","contactUrl":null,"description":"The aim of this training is for forecasters to have skills to:\nRecognize the different types of aerosols present in the atmosphere, their emission sources and their impact on human health, land and air transport.\nIdentify the role of aerosols in the climate system and its impact on the different meteorological variables.\nRecognize the main characteristics of aerosols to characterize their presence in the atmosphere and distinguish different types of aerosols.\nAnalyze and integrate observation methods that currently exist from the surface and remotely to monitor aerosols in the atmosphere.\nPromote the use of available observations for the diagnosis of meteorological situations and the forecast of their evolution.\nThis training uses satellite products to detect fire sources, smoke plumes, volcanic ash and mineral dust.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"At the end of the activity, the participating agents are expected to have the necessary skills to interpret and combine the different observations to detect aerosols in the atmosphere and to be able to implement it for the preparation of forecasts and their verification.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":" Meteorological Forecasters","registrationHowto":"Applicants must register before  september 1st, 2023 at the following link:\nhttps://forms.gle/UZdzL5ceFqnGv8CQ7\nImportant: Applicants must be authorized by their respective PR.","registrationEndDate":1693569600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5863,"name":"Diana Marina Rodriguez","email":"dmr@smn.gov.ar","agency":"","country":"AR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyC