dDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Erdem Erdi","contactEmail":"Erdem.Erdi@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This is a training exclusively for the HNMS from Greece.","country":null,"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Staff from HNMS Greece.","registrationHowto":"By invitation only.","registrationEndDate":1687165200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":5,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2273,"created":1678362303000,"updated":1700686204000,"title":"Third International Operational Satellite Oceanography Symposium (OSOS-3): Short course on operational processing of EUMETSAT Copernicus marine products.","titleNative":"Third International Operational Satellite Oceanography Symposium (OSOS-3): Short course on operational processing of EUMETSAT Copernicus marine products.","startDate":1686902400000,"endDate":1686934800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Busan","host":"EUMETSAT, NOAA, KHOA","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://www.eventsforce.net/eumetsat/frontend/reg/thome.csp?pageID=16613&eventID=41","description":"Building upon the foundation set during the first symposium gathering in June 2019, and second virtual meeting in May 2021, the Third International Operational Satellite Oceanography Symposium (OSOS-3) will involve community members from all levels of the observation-to-information value chain, to determine mission requirements and priorities, demonstrate the use of satellite data in coupled numerical models and emphasise socio-economic benefits from Earth Observation. As part of OSOS-3, the host organisations (EUMETSAT, [NOAA](https://www.noaa.gov/) and [KHOA](http://www.khoa.go.kr/eng/Main.do)) are offering a series of training sessions, each dedicated to their own activities and product portfolios. These training sessions will be held in person at the [conference venue](https://m.shillastay.com/haeundae/index.do) on the 16 June 2023, between 09:00 and 17:00 Korean Standard Time.\n\nThe EUMETSAT component of this training will introduce our marine products, including those from the Copernicus programme, presenting a bank of tools and methods for working with data in an operational capacity. These approaches will cover routine data access, batch processing and validation of ocean colour products. Trainers will provide guidance on the use and adaptation of these tools, in which they are experts, as well as advice on expanding their use to suit the participants needs.\n\nDue to the limitations on space at the venue, we are limited to 45 participants. We encourage you to apply as early as possible. For more information, please see the links below.","country":{"id":"KR","name":"KOREA, REPUBLIC OF","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to:\n\n* Find information about the various data products available in the EUMETSAT marine product portfolio, as well as support and further training opportunities.\n* Access data operationally through the EUMETSAT Data Store APIs and EUMDAC client.\n* Conduct batch processing using SNAP and supporting Jupyter notebooks\n* Extract and analyse in situ matchups with Sentinel-3 ocean colour data using **T**h**oMaS** - a **To**ol to generate **Ma**tchups of OC products with **S**entinel-3/OLCI","summary":"Building upon the foundation set during the first symposium gathering in June 2019, and second virtual meeting in May 2021, the Third International Operational Satellite Oceanograp","content":null,"targetAudience":"* Established and early career marine remote sensing scientists\n* Application/service developers looking to incorporate remote sensing into operational processing systems\n* Oceanographers of all disciplines who are looking to expand their research into Earth observation","registrationHowto":"For more information on registering for the conference and applying for the training course, please visit the following page: https://www.eventsforce.net/eumetsat/frontend/reg/thome.csp?pageID=16613&eventID=41","registrationEndDate":1683936000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":3,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":6,"title":"Marine","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":12,"title":"Ocean biogeochemistry","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":14,"title":"Water quality","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":20,"name":"WEkEO"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2293,"created":1682001632000,"updated":1700686542000,"title":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: SARAH – A Climate Data Record on Surface Solar Radiation","titleNative":"EUMETSAT series of short courses: SARAH – A Climate Data Record on Surface Solar Radiation","startDate":1686744000000,"endDate":1686751200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=484","description":"This online short course presents SARAH-3, the latest edition of the SEVIRI-based climate data record on surface radiation, generated by the Satellite Application Facility on Climate Monitoring (CM SAF).\n\nDuring the approximately two-hour course, participants get the chance to learn from CM SAF experts about all important features and highlights of the data record. In a hands-on session, users start working with the data to get insights into data handling and data formats.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the event, we want participants to be able to remember the most important features of the SARAH-3 data record and its improvements compared to its predecessor. Attendees should know the data format and how to handle the data. One measure of a successful short course would be a measurable increase in the download numbers of SARAH data.  ","summary":"This online short course presents SARAH-3, the latest edition of the SEVIRI-based climate data record on surface radiation, generated by the Satellite Application Facility on Clima","content":null,"targetAudience":"Users of the previous editions of the SARAH data record and all new users, who are interested in high quality long-term data of surface radiation and sunshine duration. This includes for instance, climate services and research institutes with focus on climate.","registrationHowto":"Please register in advance for this webinar:\nhttps://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9mL7ctjHSUSy5asAABmNnQ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":36,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"title":"Climate","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":37,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Atmosphere","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":39,"title":"Climate system monitoring - Terrestrial","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"name":"SAF archive"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":10,"name":"MFG"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2243,"created":1673281602000,"updated":1696575413000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms","startDate":1686528000000,"endDate":1686873600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Krakow","host":"IMGW, ESSL","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"Stephan.Bojinski@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"Testbeds are organized both to teach forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or even experimental forecasting tools, and to evaluate such tools. At these events forecasters will learn by doing, by making severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, followed by a verification. Particular focus will be given to the use of proxy-MTG satellite data (e.g., from the NASA MODIS, NOAA VIIRS and Sentinel-3/OLCI instruments) and, once operationally available, real data from MTG in order to prepare forecasters for the use of next-generation satellite data. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance (i.e. from DWD, ZAMG, ESSL, and ECMWF) will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"PL","name":"POLAND","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Enhancing skills in forecasting severe convective storms.\nEvaluating different products for convection nowcasting, including satellite products. ","summary":"Testbeds are organized both to teach forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or even experimental forecasting tools, and to evaluate such tools. At these events","content":null,"targetAudience":"Weather forecasters from EUMETSAT Member States who train other forecasters and forecasters with a strong background in severe storms meteorology.","registrationHowto":"Invitation has been sent to EUMETSAT Heads of Delegations. If you wish to apply for the testbed please c