m MTG-I1 missions. SIFT is an open-source software released by EUMETSAT and University of Wisconsin, which utilizes the popular Satpy python-package for data reading. We also show an upgraded version of the web-based EUMETView tool. For the demonstration, we are using FCI data and proxy datasets, and encourage active participation by the audience.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"In this event, EUMETSAT is demonstrating a multi-mission data visualisation tool SIFT which is suited for viewing and analysing data from MTG-I1 missions. SIFT is an open-source so","content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ZgLflC_bROmgunumRxUcMw ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":153,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2295,"created":1682581038000,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"Event Week on Heatwaves and Droughts","titleNative":"Event Week on Heatwaves and Droughts","startDate":1685361600000,"endDate":1685626200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"Dominik Rukavina","contactEmail":"drukavina@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"https://eumetrain.org/","description":"EUMETrain will promote the Event Week on Heatwaves and Droughts, from 29th May to June 1st. We have an exciting program with multidisciplinary speakers which will cover different aspects of heatwaves and droughts, mainly focusing on satellite observations that can be used to study their impacts and causes.\nHeatwaves are becoming increasingly more frequent and more intense, with Europe being one of the areas where these increases are more significant.  ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Be able to adopt the kind of data and methodologies discussed during Event Week in your daily shifts\n\nUnderstand the physical processes involved in heatwaves and their\nintensification by droughts, with a special focus on satellite products describing relevant variables for those mechanisms","summary":"EUMETrain will promote the Event Week on Heatwaves and Droughts, from 29th May to June 1st. We have an exciting program with multidisciplinary speakers which will cover different a","content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters\n\nClimatologists\n\nResearchers\n","registrationHowto":"You can see the agenda here: https://shorturl.at/ftLZ8\n\nRegister here: https://shorturl.at/gnD14","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2296,"created":1683284538000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"Data Access Services - How to session - Transitioning from Data Centre to Data Store, Data Tailor and Data Access Client (EUMDAC)","titleNative":"Data Access Services - How to session - Transitioning from Data Centre to Data Store, Data Tailor and Data Access Client (EUMDAC)","startDate":1684929600000,"endDate":1684936800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Noemi Marsico","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=436#section-1","description":"This series of sessions focuses on using the EUMETSAT Data Store, Data Tailor, and Data Access Client. It is particularly designed for users working with the EUMETSAT Data Centre who need to shift to the Data Store. Due to the reduction of products in the Data Centre, this session will be a great opportunity to remove any technical challenges in using the Data Access Services GUIs, APIs, and EUMDAC, and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues. Please, read more information about the transition here: https://eumetsatspace.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/EUM/blog/2023/03/22/1965359114/Switching+the+data+access+from+the+Data+Centre+to+the+Data+Store+for+faster+delivery+times.\n\nThe session will cover 2 hours and will be divided into three segments:\n\nData Store/Data Tailor UIs and APIs\nEUMDAC features\nQuestions and answers\nWe encourage you to post your questions on sli.do ( https://app.sli.do/event/flsdivtc ) so that we can adapt the content of the next session to answer them!\n\nThe sessions are open to all and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to scientists and forecasters. Registration via Zoom is required. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"-Users should be able to use the Data Store service to browse, search for, download and eventually subscribe to, collections and products of interest using EUMDAC, as required;\n-Users should be able to use the Data Tailor Web Service to customise products to create bespoke data streams that fit their applications, via EUMDAC, as required;\n-Users should know where to find resources to support the use of the new data access services\n-Users should know where to go for further help in using the new data access services","summary":"This series of sessions focuses on using the EUMETSAT Data Store, Data Tailor, and Data Access Client. It is particularly designed for users working with the EUMETSAT Data Centre w","content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the new EUMETSAT Data Access Services, especially users of the Data Centre.","registrationHowto":"To apply, register at the following link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ZBFs7L4ZTgWSTKL1d7YP6g ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":2,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2261,"created":1675265267000,"updated":1700685988000,"title":"Introduction to Machine Learning for Earth Observation - A practical approach","titleNative":"Introduction to Machine Learning for Earth Observation - A practical approach","startDate":1684828800000,"endDate":1685026800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Mark Higgins","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This course is an introduction to Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning and Deep Learning applied to Earth observation data. The aim of the course is to provide an overview of machine learning potential for EUMETSAT data and the main machine learning techniques, with hands-on modules using real world data. The course is composed of different modules, addressing both theory and practical examples.","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"At the end of the course you will be able to:\n- understand how to address your problem using machine learning techniques;\n- create you own workflow based on the templates provided in the course;\n- find tools from the various existing libraries;\n- appreciate the limitations of you knowledge and where to find expert knowledge. ","summary":"This course is an introduction to Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning and Deep Learning applied to Earth observation data. The aim of the course is to provide an overvie","content":null,"targetAudience":"Member State weather and associated services starting to work in AI/ML on weather data.\nThe course is aimed at people with little prior knowledge. You will need to be comfortable to edit some python using Jupyter notebooks. ","registrationHowto":"Please visit the EUMETSAT training platform to apply for this course: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158  \nPlease make sure you create an account on the platform, if you do not have one. Click on Login (on the top right section of the page), create a new user (Create an account), and follow the procedure. With your new account, please log in, then access the 'Apply for Courses' section, and submit your application form.\n\nIn case of any problem, please contact the training team at training@eumetsat.int.","registrationEndDate":1678874400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":12,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2234,"created":1671630621000,"updated":1673257743000,"title":"NOMEK - Enhancing the skills of operational meteorologists for the Nordic region","titleNative":"NOMEK - Enhancing the skills of operational meteorologists for the Nordic region","startDate":1684738800000,"endDate":1685019600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Norrköping","host":"Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute (SMHI)","contactPerson":"Paulina Hellgren","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This course is intended for Nordic operational meteorologists and will be organized by Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute in collaboration with the Nordic meteorological institutes and with support from EUMETSAT.","country":{"id":"SE","name":"SWEDEN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Skills in monitoring summer convective development using various observational systems and NWP guidance. \nImproved understanding of the communication between customers and authorities during high impact weather events.\nUpdated understanding of the available and future observation networks.\n\nAfter the course, participants are expected to share their newfound knowledge with their colleagues at home.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"The course is intended for operational forecasters involved in the daily forecasting work in the weather office. Candidates should have some forecasting experience, as well as a university level degree in meteorology or similar qualifications. ","registrationHowto":"This course is intended primarily for the Nordic meteorologists. \nDenmark, Finland, Iceland and Norway are each guaranteed 3 participants, while Estonia, Lithuania, Latvia and Ireland are guaranteed 1 seat each. The hosting country, Sweden, is guaranteed 10 participants.\nThe national contact persons are able to provide further information on how to apply. ","registrationEndDate":1675123200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":42,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":8,"value":"PWS: Weather Broadcasters and Communicators"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2297,"created":1683632085000,"updated":1752481244000,"title":"HNMS/EUMETSAT Trainings: Fundamentals of the European Weather Cloud & EUMETSAT Data Access Services","titleNative":"HNMS/EUMETSAT Trainings: Fundamentals of the European Weather Cloud & EUMETSAT Data Access Services","startDate":1684713600000,"endDate":1685664000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Training team at EUMETSAT","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This training session series is purposely designed for the scientists and developers of the Hellenic National Meteorological Service. The series aims to explore the features of the European Weather Cloud (EWC) and provide an in-depth explanation of the EUMETSAT Data Access Services, such as Data Store, Data Tailor, and EUMEView. A dedicated session on the EUMETSAT Data Access Client CLI and Python library is included.\n\nThe series is structured as follows:\n\n1. First Session: Fundamental of the EWC and its user interface, Morpheus;\n2. Second Session: Demonstration of the use of Morpheus by creating and managing Virtual Machines, S3 Buckets, NFS, and Block Storage;\n3. Third Session: Using the EWC: an external perspective. (This session involves a guest speaker chosen from the EWC users)\n4. Fourth session: How to use EUMETView's latest features. This includes GUI, APIs, and direct application to GIS;\n5. Fifth session: How to use the Data Store GUI and APIs;\n6. Sixth session: How to use the Data Tailor GUI and APIs;\n7. Seventh session: How to use EUMETSAT Data Access Client (EUMDAC).\n\nAll sessions, except for the third, are divided into a theoretical introduction, a demonstration of the services, and a Q&A. The third session includes an introduction and a presentation from a guest speaker.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"- Users should be able to comprehend the basic concepts of the European Weather Cloud, find information about its use, and understand the features of the user interface, Morpheus;\n- Users should be able to use Morpheus to create and manage Virtual Machines, S3 Buckets, NFS, and Block Storage;\n-Users should be able to understand how the use of the EWC has facilitated the work of external researchers;\n- Users should be able to use the EUMETView OMS GUI to: i) discover layers, ii) craft their own views, iii) manipulate and share views, iv) export data from layers as time series, images and animations, and v) link layers to Data Store collections where appropriate.\n- Users should be able to use the Data Store service to browse, search for, download, and eventually subscribe to, collections and products of interest, as required;\n- Users should be able to use the Data Tailor to customise products and create bespoke data streams that fit their applications, as required;\n- Users should be able to use EUMDAC CLI and Python library to discover, search, customise, and download products;\n- Users should be able to install EUMDAC on their own machine;\n- Users should know where to find resources to support the use of the data access services;\n- Users should know where to go for further help in using the new data access services.","summary":"This training session series is purposely designed for the scientists and developers of the Hellenic National Meteorological Service. The series aims to explore the features of the","content":null,"targetAudience":"Scientists and developers from the Hellenic  National Meteorological Service.","registrationHowto":"","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":9985,"name":"Deleted Trainer","email":"deleted.trainer@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"--","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":19,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2298,"created":1683725103000,"updated":1683725178000,"title":"Application of NASA SPoRT-Land Information System (SPoRT-LIS) Soil Moisture Data for Drought","titleNative":"Application of NASA SPoRT-Land Information System (SPoRT-LIS) Soil Moisture Data for Drought","startDate":1684332000000,"endDate":1685563200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3FQLXrj","description":"This training is focused on the introduction of the NASA Land Information System (LIS) output of soil moisture at various depths for drought analysis and monitoring. Traditional drought applications and indices focus on sensible weather (temperature, wind, etc.) and precipitation trends and their impacts on the hydrologic system. As a result of the NASA Short-term Prediction Research and Transition Center (SPoRT) program and its research-to-operations (R2O) work, this training will demonstrate how LIS output of soil moisture from a land surface model (LSM) can be included in traditional drought monitoring applications. The NASA SPoRT Program has implemented a version of NASA LIS (SPoRT-LIS) that utilizes near real-time Green Vegetation Fraction (GVF) from S-NPP/VIIRS retrievals, as opposed to static, climatology values of GVF.\n\nAdditionally, near real-time forcing of the LSM by the Multi-Radar Multi-Sensor (MRMS) precipitation and the Global Data Assimilation System (GDAS) sensible weather data provide near real-time, observation-driven products with ~2–8 hours latency. Each of these enable a more accurate depiction of vegetation and soil moisture impacts related to both long-term and short-term drought events, including rapid-onset flash drought events. Research-to-Operations work at SPoRT has led to the development of value-added products such as the derived percentile products for soil moisture. For example, low percentile values from SPoRT-LIS have been shown to correspond well to areas experiencing short-term drought within the U.S. Drought Monitor (USDM). Via Operations-to-Research (O2R) activities with end-users, soil moisture changes on various timescales pertinent to drought applications have been added to the SPoRT-LIS output data suite.\n\nThis training will improve the user’s understanding of how soil moisture is modeled within LIS in order to improve the interpretation and application of this output for drought monitoring. Conducted by experts in LIS and operational drought monitoring, the overall course will enable users to interpret SPoRT-LIS soil moisture percentile products for drought applications. Examples from operational applications as well as practice exercises (for using LIS data for drought monitoring) will be included in this course. Access to the SPoRT-LIS products via online viewer, in GIS formats, and GIS-based display tools, will also be included. Moreover, self-paced microlessons will be available to help users confirm their understanding and improve their skill via homework lessons between live sessions.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals:\n•\tGoal 2: End hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition and promote sustainable agriculture \n•\tTarget 2.4: By 2030, ensure sustainable food production systems and implement resilient agricultural practices that increase productivity and production, that help maintain ecosystems, that strengthen capacity for adaptation to climate change, extreme weather, drought, flooding and other disasters and that progressively improve land and soil quality \n•\tTarget 6.4: By 2030, substantially increase water-use efficiency across all sectors and ensure sustainable withdrawals and supply of freshwater to address water scarcity and substantially reduce the number of people suffering from water scarcity\n•\tTarget 15.3: By 2030, combat desertification, restore degraded land and soil, including land affected by desertification, drought and floods, and strive to achieve a land degradation-neutral world\n\nCourse Dates: May 17, 24, & 31, 2023\n\nTimes: 10:00-11:30 or 15:00-16:30 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, A user will be able to apply LIS output to efficiently analyze drought over large spatial areas in conjunction with current practices and to integrate this capability with existing data.\n•\tIdentify the NASA/LIS basics regarding the framework, input forcing, static fields, LSM structure, and output most relevant to drought\n•\tSummarize the derived soil moisture percentile products and how these are created\n•\tApply SPoRT-LIS output and/or derived products to both complement existing data and overcome limitations to monitoring drought over large areas\n•\tRecognize ‘best practices’ for LIS impact related to drought\n•\tConfigure LIS output file for viewing within a GIS-based display tool and for tailored output products and graphics\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training series is intended for local, state, regional, federal, and international governmental and non-governmental organizations interested in using NASA data for drought monitoring and forecasting. Appropriate for operational end-users, decision-makers, and researchers with interests/needs in assessing drought, water resources, agriculture, and wildland fire management.","registrationHowto":"There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\nRegister Here: https://go.nasa.gov/3FQLXrj\n","registrationEndDate":1685559600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLIN