, collections and products of interest using GUI, API and EUMDAC, as required.\n- Users should be able to use the Data Tailor Web Service to customise products to create bespoke data streams that fit their applications, via GUI, API and EUMDAC, as required.\n- Users should be able to use the Data Tailor Web Service to customise products to mirror existing processing chains that rely on EUMETCast and/or the Data Centre.\n- Users should know where to find resources to support the use of the new data access services.\n- Users should know where to go for further help in using the new data access services.","summary":"This session will focus on how to use the Data Tailor to customise Sentinel-3 products and is scheduled on:\n\nThursday 18 May 2023, 10:00-11:00 UTC\n\nThis is part of a monthly series","content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the new EUMETSAT Data Access Services, especially users of the Data Centre, CODA/CODAREP (and possibly also EUMETCast).","registrationHowto":"You can register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/8516728376577/WN_wta4RXKoTIGRlPhLQzoqrA","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":25,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2294,"created":1682501027000,"updated":1682501113000,"title":"Earth Observation Data Visualisation Workshop Series","titleNative":"Earth Observation Data Visualisation Workshop Series","startDate":1684238400000,"endDate":1687269600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://eodata4storytelling.eu/","description":"Imagery is a powerful way to convey an impactful message. With the increased availability of satellite data and petabytes of Copernicus Sentinel open data, data visualisation and data journalism have significantly developed in recent years. Earth observation has emerged as a new, easily available way to illustrate environmental and climate change-related challenges and communicate complex information to a broad audience. \n\nWith a wealth of satellite data and geospatial products available on a full, free and open basis, the European Union, with Copernicus, is providing journalists and all those interested in data visualisation with a vast amount of raw material as well as processed information and model outputs. \nAlso, the tools to access and process this data for storytelling are increasingly easy to use and have made considerable progress in recent years. \n\nWith this in mind, EUMETSAT is hosting a series of short online workshops over a six-week period on Earth observation and Copernicus data visualisation:\n\n- 16 May: Introduction to EO data visualisation\n- 23 May: Air quality and wildfires\n- 30 May: Oceans and sea ice\n- 6 June: Climate and weather\n- 13 June: Climate extremes\n- 20 June: How to access and process Copernicus and EUMETSAT data","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By attending, participants will gain a comprehensive understanding of how to use data visualisation to illustrate societal and environmental challenges and communicate complex information to a broad audience.","summary":"Imagery is a powerful way to convey an impactful message. With the increased availability of satellite data and petabytes of Copernicus Sentinel open data, data visualisation and d","content":null,"targetAudience":"The series of workshops are designed to meet the needs of attendees with diverse backgrounds, ranging from beginners to experts. It includes high-level testimonials, case studies, and practical examples.","registrationHowto":"For more information and registrations, please go to  https://eodata4storytelling.eu/ ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2275,"created":1678702580000,"updated":1700689250000,"title":"EUMETSAT MTG-I data reception and visualization","titleNative":"EUMETSAT MTG-I data reception and visualization","startDate":1684195200000,"endDate":1684281600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"WMO Centers of Excellence for Satellites Applications -Muscat and Casablanca ","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The objective of this online event is to enhance the participants' understanding  about the requirements to receive data through the EUMETCast-Satellite and EUMETCast-Terrestrial systems in the near future, as well as to raise awareness for the new data coming from the third generation of meteorological satellites (MTG-I). During this webinar participants will be able to:\n- Understand the evolutions on EUMETCast-Europe Service\n- Understand what is EUMETCast terrestrial - how can it be used\n- Understand the common challenges in countries to get prepared for next generation of satellites and try to find solutions through the exchange of knowledge between participants from neighbouring countries\n- Acquire a basic understanding of visualization and processing aspects of MTG-I FCI Level 1 and LI Level 2 data\n- Be aware of data rates and volumes\n- Understand the data format and compression schema\n- Be aware of some open-source software options for data processing and visualization (pytroll/satpy and Jupyter notebooks examples)\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"The objective of this online event is to enhance the participants' understanding  about the requirements to receive data through the EUMETCast-Satellite and EUMETCast-Terrestrial s","content":null,"targetAudience":"Technical staff from Arabic speaking countries of National Meteorological Services working with satellite data reception and from remote sensing divisions.","registrationHowto":"An invitation letter will be sent by the host countries to the directors of the Met Services. The Directors of the Met Services are invited to propose a candidate among experienced users of satellite data to participate in this workshop.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":1,"value":"Arabic","iso639":"ar"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":15,"name":"EUMETCast Terrestrial"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":13,"name":"EUMETCast Europe"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2230,"created":1670571613000,"updated":1681733506000,"title":"Online Course: Basic Interpretation of Satellite Imagery for RA-I","titleNative":"Cours en ligne: L'interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire pour RA-I","startDate":1684108800000,"endDate":1685664000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"ASMET - African Satellite Meteorology Education and Training","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://asmet.africa/2023/02/cours-enligne-linterpretation-de-base-de-limagerie-satellitaire-pour-ra-i/","description":"Le cours en ligne sur l'interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire se déroulera du 15 mai au 2 juin 2023. Il est proposé en anglais et en français par des instructeurs ASMET de la DGM Maroc, de l'EAMAC Niger, d'EUMETSAT, de l'IMTR Kenya et du SAWS Afrique du Sud. Ce cours vous permet d'améliorer vos compétences concernant l'utilisation de l'imagerie satellitaire, qui est généralement disponible pour l'identification de diverses caractéristiques météorologiques et de surface en Afrique. Le cours s'adresse à tous les prévisionnistes d'Afrique, qu'ils soient en début de carrière ou plus expérimentés.\n\nLe cours consistera en des sessions en direct avec des discussions et des briefings météorologiques, se concentrant sur l'interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire utilisée dans les bureaux de météorologie. Les participants devront consacrer au moins 4 heures par semaine à l'étude des ressources pédagogiques, à la participation aux réunions en direct et à la réalisation des travaux. Nous utiliserons le cours COMET MetEd Interprétation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire pour nous guider dans l'utilisation de base de l'imagerie satellitaire.\n\nLa réussite de ce cours vous préparera mieux aux cours de niveau avancé en ligne et en présentiel proposés par les centres de formation africains et d'EUMETSAT.\n\nLes inscriptions sont ouvertes jusqu'au 30 avril. Veuillez vous inscrire au cours en ligne en complétant un questionnaire en ligne.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Amélioration des compétences en : (a) améliorer les compétences concernant l’utilisation de l’imagerie satellitaire, qui est généralement disponible pour l’identification de diverses caractéristiques météorologiques et de surface en Afrique; (b) Être un utilisateur compétent de la technologie des cours virtuels ; (c) Développer des relations avec les participants aux cours via les forums de discussion et les briefings en ligne.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Prévisionnistes opérationnels ou des utilisateurs de données satellitaires, avec la possibilité de transmettre les compétences acquises lors du cours à d'autres membres du personnel opérationnel.","registrationHowto":"Les candidats sont invités à s'inscrire au cours en ligne en remplissant un questionnaire en ligne. Les candidatures sont ouvertes à mars 2023 à l'adresse suivante http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1682812800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":54,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false},{"id":10,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Niger","visible":false},{"id":14,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Morocco","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":4,"value":"French","iso639":"fr"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2231,"created":1670571764000,"updated":1681733550000,"title":"RA-I Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Course 2023","titleNative":"RA-I Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Course 2023","startDate":1684108800000,"endDate":1685664000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"ASMET - African Satellite Meteorology Education and Training","contactPerson":"Vesa Nietosvaara","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://asmet.africa/2023/02/new-training-opportunity-ra-i-basic-satellite-imagery-interpretation-course-2023/","description":"The online course on Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation will take place 15 May – 2 June 2023. It is offered both in English and French language, by the ASMET instructors from DGM Morocco, EAMAC Niger, EUMETSAT, IMTR Kenya and SAWS South Africa. This course helps you to improve skills in using basic, generally available satellite imagery for identifying various weather and surface features in Africa. The course is suitable for all forecasters in Africa, both early career operational forecasters and more experienced meteorologists.\n\nThe course will consist of live sessions with discussions and weather briefings, with the focus on basic interpretation of satellite images used in weather rooms. The participants should reserve minimum 4 hours each week for going through the learning resources, attending the live meetings and completing assignments. We will use the COMET MetEd Basic Satellite Imagery Interpretation Lesson to guide us through the basic use of satellite images.\n\nA successful completion of this course will make you better prepared for advanced level online and residence courses offered by the African training centres and EUMETSAT.\n\nApplications are open till 30 April. Please apply to the online course by completing an online questionnaire.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Improved skills in : (a) using basic, generally available satellite imagery for identifying various weather and surface features in Africa. \n(b) Being a competent user of virtual course technology; (c) Developing relationships with course participants via discussion forums and online briefings.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Operational forecasters or users of satellite data, with the possibility of passing on the skills acquired on the course to other operational staff.","registrationHowto":"The candidates are invited to register for the co