Caribbean). Session time is 15:00 UTC; it will start 10 minutes earlier (14:50 UTC) for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection. GoToWebinar is used for both images and voice through the internet. \n\nSatellite imagery shown during the session is from SLIDER: http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/9019166769095025753 ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5874,"name":"Erin Sanders","email":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":30,"value":"CIRA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2288,"created":1679063144000,"updated":1679063360000,"title":"High Impact Weather webinar #2","titleNative":"High Impact Weather webinar #2","startDate":1683619200000,"endDate":1683622800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"EUMETCAL","contactPerson":"EUMETCAL","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/catalog/course/bf6cad61-bc88-4eb5-b0d1-3dab2abaa5b6","description":"This HIW course is an online course for EUMETCAL and will focus on the use of a particular forecasting method based on Doswell’s ingredient-based forecasting method  IBM (1996). This method assumes that three ingredients are needed for convection: moisture, lift, instability (and vertical wind shear to take the modes in convection into account).\nAs a part of this course, Rob Groenland (KNMI) will be presenting two webinars.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://knmi.webex.com/weblink/register/r774ac5470fbc745c9d9221eeaadc6414","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2271,"created":1678356493000,"updated":1679324194000,"title":"54th International Liege Colloquium on Ocean Dynamics short course: AI/machine-learning approaches in ocean remote sensing","titleNative":"54th International Liege Colloquium on Ocean Dynamics short course: AI/machine-learning approaches in ocean remote sensing","startDate":1683536400000,"endDate":1683910800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Liège","host":"University of Liège","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://www.ocean-colloquium.uliege.be/","description":"This year, the 54th International Liège Colloquium on Ocean Dynamics will focus on machine learning and data analysis in oceanography. As part of this event, EUMETSAT and the Colloquium organisers are convening two training sessions on machine learning approaches for the analysis of marine Earth observation data. These sessions, each one hour in length and available only to onsite attendees, will begin by introducing the EUMETSAT product catalogue and, through a series of Python based Jupyter Notebooks, culminate in interactive demonstrations of machine learning and statistical approaches to ocean colour retrievals, pan-sensor data synthesis, and addressing missing data in sea surface temperature fields.\n\nWe will focus entirely on open source tools and participant will be free to engage with our resources beyond the constraints of the course. EUMETSAT marine product experts and machine learning application developers will be on hand to answer your questions and provide guidance on next steps you can take to advance your engagement with marine remote sensing if this is a new field to you.\n\nThe training sessions will occur between 08:00 and 09:00 on Tuesday 9 May and 17:00 to 18:00 on Thursday 11 May. ","country":{"id":"BE","name":"BELGIUM","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the course, participants will be able to;\n\n* recall what Copernicus marine data is available from EUMETSAT and downstream services\n* access this data using EUMETSAT data access services and the Copernicus WEkEO harmonised data access API\n* interact with ocean remote sensing products via our Jupyter Notebook training catalogue\n* implement machine learning approaches for remote sensing retrievals, sensor synthesis and gap filling","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Participants will be able to;\n\nrecall what Copernicus marine data is available from EUMETSAT and downstream services\naccess this data using EUMETSAT data access services and the Copernicus WEkEO harmonised data access API\ninteract with ocean remote sensing products via our Jupyter Notebook training catalogue\nimplement machine learning approaches for remote sensing retrievals, sensor synthesis and gap filling","registrationHowto":"Information for registering for the 54th International Liège Colloquium on Ocean Dynamics can be found at https://www.ocean-colloquium.uliege.be/. All colloquium attendees are welcome at the training.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2250,"created":1673538568000,"updated":1674817431000,"title":"Marine weather forecasting workshop","titleNative":"Atelier de prévision maritime","startDate":1683504000000,"endDate":1683849600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Casablanca","host":null,"contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"L'objectif de cet atelier est le renforcement des capacités en télédétection spatiale et son application en prévision maritime. Ce cours se déroulera avec des séances pratiques, ainsi que des présentations sur une utilisation opérationnelle efficace des données satellitaires Altimétriques et Diffusiométriques.","country":{"id":"MA","name":"MOROCCO","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"Les participants pourront:\nAnalyser les conditions de surface réelles à l'aide des données des Altimètres et Diffusiomètres.\nSurveiller l'évolution des conditions de surface de la mer.\nIntégrer ces données satellitaires avec les données issues de modèles numériques pour la validation des sorties du modèle.\nAccéder aux données et les visualiser.\nDéterminer comment l'utilisation de la vaste gamme de produits disponibles auprès d'EUMETSAT peut améliorer la qualité de l'analyse météorologique maritime.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Experts des centres opérationnels chargés de la prévision et de la surveillance des eaux maritimes africaines, quel que soit leur niveau d'expérience dans l'utilisation des données satellitaires à des fins d'analyse maritime.","registrationHowto":"Une lettre d'invitation sera envoyée par le pays hôte aux directeurs des Met Services. Les Directeurs des Services Météorologiques sont invités à proposer un candidat parmi les utilisateurs expérimentés des données satellitaires pour participer à cet atelier. ","registrationEndDate":1677542400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":15,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":14,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Morocco","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":4,"value":"French","iso639":"fr"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2277,"created":1678892552000,"updated":1700686380000,"title":"EUMETSAT short course: Dust monitoring and forecasting","titleNative":"EUMETSAT short course: Dust monitoring and forecasting","startDate":1683028800000,"endDate":1683034200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Federico Fierli","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=477","description":"Europe experiences regular Saharan dust transports across the Iberian peninsula, France, Spain that sometimes even reach central and northern Europe. In 2023, the first large-scale dust transport episode took place in mid-February. Taking this event as a case study, this short course will give you an overview of how you can use satellite and ground-based observation as well as model forecasts to monitor and forecast Saharan dust episodes. \n\nThe course consists of two parts: it will give you first a high-level introduction to the Saharan dust transport event in February 2023 and relevant data that can be used to monitor and forecast such events. This high-level introduction is followed by a practical data exploration part. This part gives you a hands-on introduction to satellite-, ground- and model-based data for dust monitoring and forecasting. For each dataset featured, you will learn how to access, process, visualize and interpret it. \n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"Europe experiences regular Saharan dust transports across the Iberian peninsula, France, Spain that sometimes even reach central and northern Europe. In 2023, the first large-scale","content":null,"targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_ON1en-n4S_mfq_Iwfr86jg","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":64,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"title":"Aerosols","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2340,"created":1696515813000,"updated":null,"title":"Expert workshop for preparation of Aviation Forecasters Testbed","titleNative":"Expert workshop for preparation of Aviation Forecasters Testbed","startDate":1682586000000,"endDate":1682697600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Helsinki","host":"FMI","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":null,"contactUrl":null,"description":null,"country":{"id":"FI","name":"FINLAND","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Experts from NMSs and/or research community that can discuss on the topic of applying MTG data in forecasting fog/low clouds for aviation.","registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":1682586000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5845,"name":"Ivan Smiljanic","email":"ivan.smiljanic@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2269,"created":1678263784000,"updated":1679302383000,"title":"EGU General Assembly 2023 short course (SC5.8): Satellite data for Marine Applications: open source tools for working with data available from EUMETSAT and the Copernicus Programme.","titleNative":"EGU General Assembly 2023 short course (SC5.8): Satellite data for Marine Applications: open source tools for working with data available from EUMETSAT and the Copernicus Programme.","startDate":1682411400000,"endDate":1682417700000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vienna","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Ben Loveday","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EGU23/session/46700","description":"The catalogue of marine data and services available from EUMETSAT continues to grow. Between mandatory missions and those operated under the Copernicus programme, and their respective downstream services, the opportunities for users to access data relevant for marine applications have never been greater. However, with increasing volume and diversity of data comes challenges.\n\nThis short course will provide an overview of the suite of services and training resources available from EUMETSAT to support users to work with data relevant to the marine community. There will be a strong focus on practical aspects of accessing and working with data, with a particular focus on open source tools. The course will support participants in the use of suite of Python based Jupyter notebooks, and API clients, in both local and cloud computing environments. Trainers will be available to support participants in designing their own workflows for using satellite data in their own marine applications.\n\nThe course will be hosted in Room 2.85/86 from 08:30 to 10:15 on Tuesday 25th April.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the course, participants will;\n\n* recall what data is available from EUMETSAT via its mandatory and Copernicus missions, satellite applications facilities, and through contributions to the Copernicus services. There will be a strong focus on the Sentinel-3 and 6 missions.\n* access data using EUMETSAT data access services, including harmonised data access through the Copernicus WEkEO service.\n* work with data using open source tools, based around repositories of Python based code and Jupyter Notebooks.\n* learn about the options presented to work with Copernicus data by cloud computing in WEkEO.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"* Oceanographers of all disciplines with an interest in acquiring and using Earth observation products.\n* Remote sensing users from all disciplines, with an interest in marine applications.\n* Service providers and application developers focussing on the marine domain.","registrationHowto":"The course will be given in person and all attendees of the 2023 EGU General Assembly are welcome to attend. However space for attendees is limited by the room size and places will be given on a first come first serve basis.","registrationEndDate":1682411400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5877,"name":"Ben Loveday","email":"Ben.Loveday@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2339,"created":1696515789000,"updated":null,"title":"Eumetcal Hackathon","titleNative":"Eumetcal Hackathon","startDate":1682334000000,"endDate":1682676000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Norrköping","host":"Eumetcal in partnership with Swedish Hydro-Meteorological Institute (SMHI)","contactPerson":"Eumetcal ","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/Newsitem8","description":"During the hackathon, functional prototypes of 2-3 online learning modules about topics relevant for all\nEumetcal members will be developed. The topics for these modules come from the needs assessment\nand will to some extent depend on the number of participants and their preferences.","country":{"id":"SE","name":"SWEDEN","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- Collaborative development of a functioning prototype of one online learning module per group that can then be finalized by the Eumetcal IDs and made available for the whole community.\n- Participants learn about rapid prototyping and gain new skills in developing online learning modules.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"- Trainers, Instructional Designers\n- Subject Matter Experts (Forecasters, Researchers)\n- Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) are needed to help gather information for the modules.\n- There is no need for expertise in developing online learning.","registrationHowto":"Please register by filling out this form: \nhttps://www.surveymonkey.com/r/JQMYZPQ\nDeadline 24 February 2023.","registrationEndDate":1677362400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5845,"name":"Ivan Smiljanic","email":"ivan.smiljanic@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":