)\n- Subject Matter Experts (SMEs) are needed to help gather information for the modules.\n- There is no need for expertise in developing online learning.","registrationHowto":"Please register by filling out this form: \nhttps://www.surveymonkey.com/r/JQMYZPQ\nDeadline 24 February 2023.","registrationEndDate":1677362400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2290,"created":1681240574000,"updated":1681279445000,"title":"Fundamentals of Machine Learning for Earth Science","titleNative":"Fundamentals of Machine Learning for Earth Science","startDate":1681999200000,"endDate":1683158400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3ENDODH","description":"Artificial intelligence and machine learning have grown in popularity in recent decades as a result of advances in high-performance computing and open-source software. At the core, machine learning provides a statistical inference based on the inputs provided by the user, in which algorithms learn relationships between input data and output results. The complexity of these algorithms allows for the discovery of patterns and trends invisible to the human analyst, making it important to create analysis-appropriate input for these models to ensure that they answer the questions we are asking. This training will provide attendees an overview of machine learning in regards to Earth Science, and how to apply these algorithms and techniques to remote sensing data in a meaningful way. Attendees will also be provided with end-to-end case study examples for generating a simple random forest model for land cover classification from optical remote sensing. We will also present additional case studies to apply the presented workflows using additional NASA data.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \n•\tGoal 2: End hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition and promote sustainable agriculture\n•\tGoal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts\n•\tGoal 14: Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources for sustainable development\n•\tGoal 15: Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, and halt and reverse land degradation and halt biodiversity loss\n\nCourse Dates: April 20, 27, and May 4, 2023\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to: \n\n•\tRecognize the most common machine learning methods used for processing Earth Science data\n•\tDescribe the benefits and limitations of machine learning for Earth Science analysis \n•\tExplain how to apply basic machine learning algorithms and techniques in a meaningful manner to remote sensing data\n•\tUse an analysis-appropriate training dataset to evaluate conditions and solutions for a given case study\n•\tComplete basic procedures to interpret, refine and evaluate the accuracy of the results of machine learning analysis\n\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Research and applied scientists interested in learning how to apply basic machine learning techniques to Earth science data (e.g., satellite data such as MODIS, Landsat, Sentinel-2, etc.)\n","registrationHowto":"Times and Registration Information:  \n  \nEnglish Session: 10:00-11:30 EDT (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3ENDODH\nSpanish Session: 13:00-15:30 EDT (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3J5GCyx\n","registrationEndDate":1683219600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2274,"created":1678455559000,"updated":1698908350000,"title":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Annual Forecaster Event","titleNative":"ESSL-EUMETSAT Annual Forecaster Event","startDate":1681992000000,"endDate":1682002800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"Stephan.Bojinski@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"This webinar features key 2022 results from the joint ESSL-EUMETSAT activity introducing MTG data to operational weather forecasters in Europe. ESSL trainers describe highlights of severe convective weather cases that were analysed by forecasters during the testbeds in Wiener Neustadt, Austria. Forecasters provide testimonials on their testbed experience and the importance of satellite products in the forecasting process. In addition, the ESSL expert workshops put the spotlight on novel MTG products such as the 0.9um FCI channel to detect low-level moisture, or the Lightning imager. The audience will learn about key take-aways from these workshops, for later use in training on MTG for all users.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Key results and findings from the 2022 EUM-ESSL testbed activity , and benefits for forecasting.","summary":"This webinar features key 2022 results from the joint ESSL-EUMETSAT activity introducing MTG data to operational weather forecasters in Europe. ESSL trainers describe highlights of","content":null,"targetAudience":"European weather forecasters, users of satellite products, developers of Meteosat-based products for nowcasting. ","registrationHowto":"You can register here: https://events.teams.microsoft.com/event/517ea179-3349-405b-92ac-1a7cb04faa93@df7e8a07-a3fd-42a8-b745-17aa52648828","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,