 on the handling of data and products derived from the Meteorological Geostationary satellites covering Central America, as well as from polar orbiting satellites, namely those operated by EUMETSAT.  Participants will learn about where and how to obtain the data and how to process it. Several case studies will be covered, and daily weather briefings will be held by the course participants from the different National Meteorological Services in Central America, focusing on the different geographic regions.","country":{"id":"GT","name":"GUATEMALA","region":"RA-IV","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"This course is the second part of a blended course, whose online phase took place in 2021; participants who successfully passed the online phase were invited to this face-to-face course.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5848,"name":"Carla Barroso ","email":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2178,"created":1659708273000,"updated":1665497766000,"title":"Workshop in satellite data processing with emphasis on desert dust","titleNative":"Formation pratique au traitement des données satellitaires Formation pratique au traitement des données satellitaires avec l'accent sur les poussières désertiques","startDate":1667811600000,"endDate":1668175200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Casablanca","host":"Direction Générale de la Météorologie (DGM)","contactPerson":"Carla Barroso","contactEmail":"carla.barroso@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":"The aim of this course is to teach about the meteorological satellite data and products that are disseminated via EUMETCAST, namely how to manipulate these data and to create new products. Through practical exercises course participants will: 1) understand the different data levels and formats; 2) learn to inspect the contents of the files and how to handle level 1b data; 3) select a given Area Of Interest; 6) reproject the data; 7) display the data; 8) learn to create a workflow that produces RGB composites from the single image files received via EUMETCAST.\n\nIn the second part of the course, participants will continue the hands on data exploration with a focus on Dust events, with an in-depth insight in the principles of Dust observation and forecasting.\n\nData exploitation and manipulation will be done using python scripting language, supported by Jupyter notebooks.\n\nThis course is organized by la Direction Générale de la Météorologie (DGM), with the contribution from Météo France and WMO Barcelona Dust Regional Centre and supported by EUMETSAT. The target audience are meteorologists working in African Meteorological Services that have already knowledge about the basics of remote sensing.\n","country":{"id":"MA","name":"MOROCCO","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"Invitation letters have been sent to the Meteorological services of French-speaking countries to designate one person to par