n":null,"contactEmail":null,"contactUrl":null,"description":null,"country":{"id":"NL","name":"NETHERLANDS","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":null,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2184,"created":1660814657000,"updated":1664960633000,"title":"Eumetcal Workshop 2022 – Successful training through collaboration!","titleNative":"Eumetcal Workshop 2022 – Successful training through collaboration!","startDate":1666162800000,"endDate":1666348200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"De Bilt","host":"Eumetcal","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/EumetcalWorkshop2022","description":"Dear Community!\n\nWe are very much looking forward to the Eumetcal Workshop which will take place from Wednesday, 19th of October to Friday, 21st of October. To make sure that as many of you as possible can attend, we will make it a hybrid one. This means, it is up to you whether you want to attend in person in De Bilt or whether you prefer joining from home.\n\nEither way, come to the workshop to meet new friends, share knowledge and experience, build new skills, strengthen collaboration among institutions and contribute your expertise and talents towards meeting the most urgent training needs of our community.\n\nOur goal is that you and the whole community can benefit to a great extent from the event! We would like to hear from you about what you would like to learn in the second day of the workshop! Right now the program shows four empty slots for skill-building sessions. Please use the short survey (https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/eumetcalworkshop) to select the topics that you would like to fill those empty slots.\n\nPlease answer the survey by the end of August latest, but it only takes you 2 minutes, so better go for it right now!\n\nAll future updates and news will be posted on Workshop webiste: https://eumetcal.eu/en/ui#/page/EumetcalWorkshop2022","country":{"id":"NL","name":"NETHERLANDS","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":"https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/eumetcalworkshop","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2198,"created":1664908524000,"updated":1664968917000,"title":"Disaster Assessment Using Synthetic Aperture Radar","titleNative":"Evaluación de Desastres Usando Radar de Apertura Sintética","startDate":1666137600000,"endDate":1666900800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3x3N56x","description":" \nLos sensores de Radar de Apertura Sintética o SAR (por sus siglas en inglés) son ideales para el monitoreo de ciertos desastres o áreas que son vulnerables a desastres, sobretodo porque la señal puede “ver” la superficie de la Tierra de día o de noche bajo casi cualquier tipo de condiciones meteorológicas. Además, la señal puede penetrar a través de la vegetación y es sensible a la rugosidad de la superficie y a pequeños desplazamientos de la superficie terrestre. Esta capacitación de nivel intermedio consiste en tres partes y se centrará en el uso de SAR para 1) evaluar las áreas en riesgo de desastres debido a deslizamientos de tierra mediante el uso del SAR interferométrico (INSAR). Esto se logra midiendo pequeños movimientos (del orden de centímetros) de la superficie de la tierra que son causados por el movimiento gradual de los deslizamientos, y cómo estos movimientos varían con el tiempo; 2) caracterizar la extensión de derrames de petróleo y sus impactos. Los datos SAR son sensibles a la rugosidad de la superficie, lo que permite identificar áreas donde hay derrames de petróleo; 3) y caracterizar la extensión de las inundaciones. La señal SAR puede penetrar a través de la vegetación y detectar inundaciones provocadas por grandes eventos de precipitación o por eventos naturales. Esta capacitación incluirá porciones teóricas para cada catástrofe en relación con la interacción de la señal SAR con las condiciones de la superficie y demostraciones utilizando Google Earth Engine, Jupyter Notebooks y la caja de herramientas SNAP, todas de disponibilidad libre y abierta.\n \nObjetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible de la ONU Relevantes:\n•\tObjectivo 11: Ciudades y comunidades sostenibles \n•\tObjetivo 11.5: De aquí a 2030, reducir significativamente el número de muertes causadas por los desastres, incluidos los relacionados con el agua, y de personas afectadas por ellos, y reducir considerablemente las pérdidas económicas directas provocadas por los desastres en comparación con el producto interno bruto mundial, haciendo especial hincapié en la protección de los pobres y las personas en situaciones de vulnerabilidad\n•\tMeta 13.1: Fortalecer la resiliencia y la capacidad de adaptación a los riesgos relacionados con el clima y los desastres naturales en todos los países\n\nFormato del Curso: Tres sesiones de dos horas  cada una \n\nRetweet: https://twitter.com/NASAARSET/status/1571861685421322240/photo/1\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Al final de esta capacitación, los participantes podrán entender por qué la señal de SAR es sensible a las inundaciones, los derrames de petróleo y los deslizamientos de tierra. También podrán utilizar datos SAR para monitorear derrames de petróleo e inundaciones, y para identificar áreas en peligro de deslizamientos de tierras.","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Agencias de gestión de desastres, incluyendo agencias gubernamentales domésticas e internacionales (p.ej. FEMA y agencias gubernamentales equivalentes fuera de EE.UU.) además de organismos de ayuda (p.ej. La Cruz Roja, ONU).","registrationHowto":"Fechas: El 19, 20, y 27 de octubre de 2022\n \nInscripciones: \n \nespañol: 14h a 16h Horario Este de EE.UU (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3KQBoWm\ninglés: 11h a 13 Horario Este de EE.UU. (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3BkK4S2","registrationEndDate":1666893600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":25,"name":"Jochen Kerkmann","email":"jochen.kerkmann@web.de","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2172,"created":1657109317000,"updated":1700665367000,"title":"Earth Observation Products for Wildfires Monitoring and Forecast - Hybrid event","titleNative":"Earth Observation Products for Wildfires Monitoring and Forecast - Hybrid event","startDate":1666094400000,"endDate":1666263600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Lisbon","host":"","contactPerson":"Federico Fierli","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=462","description":"National services are at the forefront of gathering early-warning, forecasting, and monitoring fires, together with preparedness actions. Earth observation data feeds monitoring and forecasting, by generating specific products and data-sets tailored to support each phase of the observation and management of a wildfire event. \n\nThis three-day hybrid workshop aims to:\n- discover and train on existing and new earth observation products;\n- learn from national services' activities and users' networks;\n- discuss needs and priorities for a better user guidance and preparation.\n\nParticipation can either be online or onsite, at IPMA, in Lisbon. Online attendance is open to all interested participants for all the sessions in the workshop. Attendance at IPMA premises is restricted to a maximum of 25 participants. Registration is required for both online and onsite participation. \nDuring the registration process, it is possible to submit a poster to be discussed during the poster session.","country":{"id":"PT","name":"PORTUGAL","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":"National services are at the forefront of gathering early-warning, forecasting, and monitoring fires, together with preparedness actions. Earth observation data feeds monitoring an","content":null,"targetAudience":"Services in Europe with mandate/role to monitor, forecast or mitigate fires, interested participants from all European countries with focus on vulnerable regions.","registrationHowto":"Registration is required for both online and onsite participation.\nPriority for onsite attendance will be given to applicants working in wildfires monitoring and forecasting already engaged or wishing to engage with earth observation, and to nationals and institutions of countries adhering to the Copernicus programme.\n\nPlease follow this link for registration: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","registrationEndDate":1660521600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"BLENDED","attendeeCount":179,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":4,"title":"Atmospheric composition","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":3,"name":"MTG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2225,"created":1669902349000,"updated":null,"title":"ICPAC/ TAMSAT -ALERT workshop","titleNative":"ICPAC/ TAMSAT -ALERT workshop","startDate":1666083600000,"endDate":1666285200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Nairobi","host":"IGAD Climate Prediction and Applications Centre","contactPerson":"Vicky Boult ","contactEmail":"v.l.boult@reading.ac.uk","contactUrl":null,"description":"Training on TAMSAT-ALERT for the NMSs they represent through the Institute of Meteorological Training and Research in countries like Ethiopia, South Africa, Tanzania, Kenya, Sudan, Uganda, Namibia, Eswatini, Malawi, Zambia, Zimbabwe, South Sudan, Rwanda, Burundi, Lesotho, Botswana.This is a workshop for African forecasters to establish capacity across Africa, enabling the scale-up of TAMSAT-ALERT forecasts and improving the ability to anticipate drought and its impacts. ","country":{"id":"KE","name":"KENYA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":24,"name":"Partners"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"RESIDENCE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":80,"value":"Other","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2194,"created":1664263042000,"updated":null,"title":"RGB Developers Workshop ","titleNative":"RGB Developers Workshop ","startDate":1666051200000,"endDate":1666224000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Fort Collins, USA ","host":"EUMETSAT, NOAA & CIRA ","contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://www.cira.colostate.edu/conferences/rgb_workshop/","description":"NOAA, CIRA, EUMETSAT, and WMO are co-hosting an RGB Developers and Users Workshop on Oct. 18-20, 2022, at the Cooperative Institute for Research in the Atmosphere in Fort Collins, Colorado, USA. It will be an in-person event, with a portion of the workshop being available for virtual participation. Intended participants include those users, trainers, and developers with RGB expertise. The last RGB Experts and Developers Workshop was held in Tokyo, Japan, November 2017. Since that time, NOAA and International Weather Service forecasters have adopted the use of RGB displays from the GOES-R ABI and Himawari AHI, in addition to VIIRS and other platforms. Our colleagues continue to develop new RGBs and learn new RGB applications from various platforms and apply them to MTG FCI and EPS-SG METimage moving forward. The primary goal of this workshop will be to share knowledge on RGB applications.\n \nMore details such as the objectives of the workshop and travel logistics can be found on the Workshop Webpage here: https://www.cira.colostate.edu/conferences/rgb_workshop/\n \nPlease use this link to register for the workshop by August 31, but it would be most helpful if you could register ASAP: https://forms.microsoft.com/r/2p0CUbU3dG\n \nYou'll notice that the workshop is somewhat non-traditional in that Day 2 will be an \"Open Space\" format, described in the agenda. The reason for this is to avoid falling into the \"death by powerpoint\" trap that these types of meetings tend to do, and instead encouraging as much discussion and problem-solving as possible. There will be time allotted for some attendees to present and share new and interesting findings/information, but given this format we likely won't have formal presentations from everyone.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Experts in the development and application of RGBs for operational meteorology ","registrationHowto":"https://forms.microsoft.com/r/2p0CUbU3dG","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2222,"created":1669882621000,"updated":1700679582000,"title":"European Weather Cloud (EWC) User Workshop","titleNative":"European Weather Cloud (EWC) User Workshop","startDate":1665651600000,"endDate":1665680400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":"Roope Tervo","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":null,"country":null,"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":null,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":null,"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":107,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2188,"created":1663773704000,"updated":1663847720000,"title":"Accessing and Analyzing Air Quality Data from Geostationary Satellites","titleNative":"Accessing and Analyzing Air Quality Data from Geostationary Satellites","startDate":1665496800000,"endDate":1666713600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Annapolis","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3Jqdnor","description":"The next generation of sensors in geostationary orbit offer unprecedented temporal resolution for air quality observations. Low Earth orbit satellites (e.g., MODIS, VIIRS, OMI, TROPOMI) can provide global coverage, but typically observe a given location one to two times per day. Sensors in geostationary orbit observe the same geographic region at all times of the day. These datasets are essential for understanding diurnal changes in air quality, monitoring real-time movement of smoke and dust events, and improving model forecasting capabilities via data assimilation.\n\nThis will be a three-part webinar series in partnership with the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) and the National Institute Of Environmental Research (NIER, South Korea) on air quality (AQ) data analysis from geostationary satellites. The webinar series will a) provide an overview of geostationary capabilities for monitoring air quality around the world; b) introduce geostationary aerosol datasets from GOES-East, GOES-West, Himawari 8, and the Geostationary Environment Monitoring Spectrometer (GEMS); and 3) present data access and python tools to read and analyze the datasets.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \n•\tTarget 3.9: By 2030, substantially reduce the number of deaths and illnesses from hazardous chemicals and air, water and soil pollution and contamination\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will have:\n•\tAn understanding of aerosol and trace gas datasets from geostationary satellites\n•\tThe capability to access, visualize, and download datasets\n•\tPython scripts to read and analyze air quality datasets\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This webinar series is intended for (AQ) forecasters, the AQ modeling and monitoring community, and local, state, and federal agencies","registrationHowto":"Register Here: https://go.nasa.gov/3Jqdnor","registrationEndDate":1666656000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":25,"name":"Jochen Kerkmann","email":"jochen.kerkmann@web.de","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2098,"created":1637086115000,"updated":null,"title":"3rd ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms 2022","titleNative":"3rd ESSL-EUMETSAT Testbed on Severe Convective Storms 2022","startDate":1665360000000,"endDate":1665705600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"ESSL and EUMETSAT organise a series of testbeds to prepare forecasters for data from next-generation Meteosat Third Generation (MTG) and Metop Second Generation (Metop-SG) satellites. These testbeds are organized both to teach forecasting severe convective storms using state-of-the-art or even experimental forecasting tools, and to evaluate such tools. At these events we will learn by doing, by making experimental severe weather forecasts and nowcasts using a mix of new nowcasting and forecasting tools, followed by a verification. Particular focus will be given to the capabilities of the VIIRS instrument on polar-orbiting satellites, which serves as a proxy for MTG's FCI instrument, and other proxy data for MTG instruments. In addition, a range of state-of-the-art nowcasting tools and numerical weather prediction-based guidance from DWD, ZAMG, ESSL, and ECMWF will be evaluated.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Forecasters who train other forecasters and forecasters with a strong background in severe storms meteorology. Have a look at this self-evaluation before applying: https://www.surveymonkey.com/r/D3B3PBM. \r\n\r\nCandidates will also need to have a nomination by their home institution. \r\n\r\nFor accepted candidates, EUMETSAT plans to sponsor the cost of testbed attendance and, upon request, the cost for travel, accommodation and subsistence.","registrationHowto":"In order to apply, go to https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158. Make sure you read all instructions and fill in the application form. Please note that you will need to register before applying, if you do not already have an account. ","registrationEndDate":1645747200000,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2830,"name":"Madalina Ungur as sysadmin","email":"Madalina.Ungur@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2121,"created":1642171998000,"updated":1653315348000,"title":"Baltic+ 2022 Workshop - Improving the skills in cold season forecasting","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2022 Workshop - Improving the skills in cold season forecasting","startDate":1664841600000,"endDate":1665014400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vilnius","host":"Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service","contactPerson":"Izolda Marcinoniene","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\n\r\nThis workshop will be a follow-up on-site event for the preceding online course. The duration of the workshop will be three days, the location will be in Vilnius and the event hosted by the Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service. ","country":{"id":"LT","name":"LITHUANIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"By completing this course, the participants will have practised cold season forecasting through case study work, simulations and  group discussions with other experts. The participants will discuss their work challenges face to face with other experts, in a creative and efficient atmosphere, to make the learning process successful and results implemented in operational work. The live discussions and meetings with experts from different countries will allow the participants to solve their issues quickly and productively.","summary":null,"content":"At this workshop, we will work further on the aspects of cold season weather forecasting. Topics of the workshop include discussions, simulations and weather forecasting exercises related to selected cold season weather phenomena. The workshop will include presentations and discussions on how the new generation satellite capabilities soon available for the forecasters will assist them to better monitor the cold season weather systems.\r\n\r\nAn essential part of the workshop will be the participant presentations about interesting cases they have collaboratively created during the weeks preceding this workshop.\r\n","targetAudience":"This training workshop is intended for the operational meteorologists from Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania, Poland and Ukraine, and who have successfully completed the preceding online course.  ","registrationHowto":"Please contact your national point of contact for training for more information on the nomination and application process. ","registrationEndDate":1656547200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":8,"value":"PWS: Weather Broadcasters and Communicators"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2110,"created":1638960587000,"updated":1700654462000,"title":"Recent Developments in Altimetry Measurements - Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"Recent Developments in Altimetry Measurements - Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich - Series of online short courses","startDate":1664452800000,"endDate":1664460000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=445","description":"This course is part of the autumn 2022 edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate. \n\nIn this short course we will focus on the new capabilities of the Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich altimeter and new data access routes to obtain its products.\n\nThe Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich altimetry satellite was launched on Nov. 21 2020. It is now fully operational and is the new altimetry reference mission, taking over from its predecessor, Jason-3.\n\nDuring this event, we will revisit the concept of sea-surface height, outlining why it is an essential variable to measure. We will discuss the Sentinel-6 in the context of history and the family of altimetry satellites, detailing the novelties of this particular mission and commenting on future developments in the science.\n\nWe will also introduce the current data distribution methods and plans for the near future.\n\nThe event will feature presentations and code-based demonstrations of ways in which users may interact with the Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich data.\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"In this course you will learn:\r\n- the key concepts of \"sea (surface) height\", why the height of the sea matters, and how sea surface height is measured from space.\r\n- the origin of Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich, its history and its important role as the altimetry reference mission.\r\n- what is new on this mission\r\n- how to access Sentinel-6 Michael Freilich data from EUMETSAT\r\n- what products are available, and how you can work with them.\r\n","summary":"This course is part of the autumn 2022 edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate. \n\nIn this short cour","content":"","targetAudience":"This course is aimed at scientists in the altimetry community, early career researchers, physical oceanographers, climate scientists and marine professionals working in the coastal zone.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar at the course page: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=445.\r\n\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2830,"name":"Madalina Ungur as sysadmin","email":"Madalina.Ungur@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":89,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"title":"Maritime safety","i