ferent modules, addressing both theory and practical examples.\n\nWe will cover: \n- the main branches of machine learning: Supervised and Unsupervised Learning.\n- Deep Learning.\n- Existing open source tools.\n- How to build AI workflows.\n- Hands on: classification, regression, clustering and image classification tasks.","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"At the end of the course you will be able to:\n- understand how to address your problem using machine learning techniques;\n- create you own workflow based on the templates provided in the course;\n- find tools from the various existing libraries;\n- appreciate the limitations of you knowledge and where to find expert knowledge. ","summary":"This course is an introduction to Artificial Intelligence (AI), Machine Learning (ML) and Deep Learning (DL) applied to Earth observation data. The aim of the course is to provide ","content":null,"targetAudience":"Member State weather and associated services starting to work in AI/ML on weather data.\nThe course is aimed at people with little prior knowledge. You will need to be comfortable to edit some python using Jupyter notebooks. ","registrationHowto":"On the EUMETSAT training platform, please go to https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158, and you will be able to select the course and find the access link to the application form. Please note that to enter your registration, you will need to create an account on the platform.\n","registrationEndDate":1654826400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"e