 challenges in using the Data Access Services GUIs and APIs, and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"This session will focus on answering frequently asked question about EUMETView (https://eumetsatspace.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DSEV/overview):\n\nThursday 22 September 2022, 12:00-1","content":null,"targetAudience":"Anyone interested in using the new EUMETSAT Data Access Services, especially users of the Data Centre, CODA/CODAREP (and possibly also EUMETCast).   ","registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/4716608187725/WN_qTkd9OnISTuk4sR6qxRZFg","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":7,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":19,"name":"EUMETView"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2187,"created":1661283696000,"updated":1661322227000,"title":"Selecting Climate Change Projection Sets for Mitigation, Adaptation, and Risk Management Applications","titleNative":"Selecting Climate Change Projection Sets for Mitigation, Adaptation, and Risk Management Applications","startDate":1663599600000,"endDate":1663632000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3pmU1Yk","description":"Projections of climate change from global climate models are a fundamental basis for mitigation, adaptation, and risk management planning across many elements of society and ecosystems around the world. Depending on the application need, scientists can use a variety of climate modeling projection sets with a range of distinguishing factors. Although the future will likely be shaped by a combination of mitigation, adaptation, and risk planning, the distinctions between these application areas can impact the choice of which climate projection set to use. \n\nClimate projection sets begin with global climate model outputs and often include additional observational data to produce variables that are more relevant for certain applications. These datasets are constructed according to specific choices about source material, domain, resolution, and scenarios or storylines, among other factors. Different projection sets provide their own unique advantages but are often limited by tradeoffs shaped by resource constraints and the availability of supporting materials. \n\nThis two-part webinar series will provide an overview of resources for choosing climate projection sets for mitigation, adaptation, and risk management applications. The webinar will give an overview of application areas, define a list of distinguishing characteristics of climate projection sets, and then highlight the main benefits and drawbacks of different types of projection sets.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \n•\tGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable  \n•\tGoal 13: Take urgent action to combat climate change and its impacts\n•\tGoal 14: Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources for sustainable development\n•\tGoal 15: Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, and halt and reverse land degradation and halt biodiversity loss\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: After participating in the training, attendees will be able to:\n•\tUnderstand the differing needs of mitigation, adaptation, and risk management applications\n•\tRecognize the main components and distinguishing factors of climate projection sets\n•\tSummarize the benefits and tradeoffs of different climate projection sets and versions\n•\tDiscuss selection of the best climate projection set for various application needs\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for local, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations wanting to select among candidate NASA Earth observations and modeled climate projection datasets for integration into their climate change-related work in different sectors. The training will introduce the data, tools, and knowledge needed to identify important features and tradeoffs in climate information that can help them assess and manage climate-related risks and opportunities.\n\nThe training is also likely to be of interest to undergraduate and graduate students looking to expand their understanding of these topics\n","registrationHowto":"Times: 11:00-12:30 or 15:00-16:30 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\nRegister Here: https://go.nasa.gov/3pmU1Yk\n","registrationEndDate":1663696800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2166,"created":1654886261000,"updated":1654923422000,"title":"RFG of the Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"RFG of the Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","startDate":1663167600000,"endDate":1663171200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Bernie Connell","contactEmail":"Bernie.Connell@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup.asp","description":"The sessions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean). Session time is 15:00 UTC, but as usual, it will start 10 minutes earlier (14:50 UTC) for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection. GoToWebinar is used for both images and voice through the Internet. \n\nSatellite imagery shown during the session is from SLIDER: http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu \n\nMore information can be found on our webpage: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup.asp","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/1227564474130087694","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5874,"name":"Erin Sanders","email":"Erin.Sanders@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":30,"value":"CIRA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2182,"created":1660577890000,"updated":1660582247000,"title":"Monitoring and Modeling Floods using Earth Observations","titleNative":"Monitoring and Modeling Floods using Earth Observations","startDate":1663164000000,"endDate":1663790400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3Osj32h","description":"Recent studies have shown that globally, riverine and coastal floods are increasing in intensity and duration. In addition, the number of people living in flood-prone areas has increased substantially during the last two decades. Therefore, monitoring and predicting floods in support of early warning, response, and relief operations have become major foci for disaster management activities worldwide. Remote sensing observations from optical and Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) sensors are routinely used for detecting and mapping flooding. Moreover, empirical methodologies developed using remote sensing observations of rainfall, terrain, soil moisture, and landcover, as well as weather modeling data have been used for flood monitoring. Sophisticated and complex land hydrology and runoff routing models are also being used for mapping and predicting riverine and urban flooding.\n\nARSET has offered several trainings on flood monitoring based on optical and SAR observations in the past. This two-part training will focus on recent developments and updates in flood monitoring tools and flood modeling techniques. Specifically, an overview of the Hydrological Modeling and Analysis Platform (HyMAP), a routing model used with NASA’s Land Information System (LIS), and examples of flood modeling cases will be presented in this training.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \n•\tGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable\n•\tTarget 11.5: By 2030, significantly reduce the number of deaths and the number of people affected and substantially decrease the direct economic losses relative to global gross domestic product caused by disasters, including water-related disasters, with a focus on protecting the poor and people in vulnerable situations\n•\tTarget 13.1: Strengthen resilience and adaptive capacity to climate-related hazards and natural disasters in all countries\n\nCourse Format: Two, 2-hour parts\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, participants will be able to:\n•\tIdentify and use observation-based flood monitoring and mapping tools \n•\tUnderstand and plan for using hydrologic and flood routing modeling techniques\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"Local, city, state, federal, and private institutions involved in disaster management, water resources management, urban planning, dams and hydropower management.","registrationHowto":"Times: 10:00-12:00 or 14:00-16:00 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\n\nRegister Here: https://go.nasa.gov/3Osj32h\n","registrationEndDate":1663783200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2152,"created":1650530801000,"updated":1700654926000,"title":"How to explore the new Sentinel-3 Data (III) - Data Access Services","titleNative":"How to explore the new Sentinel-3 Data (III) - Data Access Services","startDate":1662638400000,"endDate":1662642000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT User Helpdesk ","contactEmail":"OPS@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=436","description":"This session will focus on how to explore the new Sentinel-3 data available from the EUMETSAT Data Store (https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-data-store).\n\nThis is part of a monthly series of open, online short sessions on the Data Access Services and their usage via GUIs and APIs, answering top questions posted by participants in an open sli.do (event code #data-services, link https://app.sli.do/event/flsdivtc).\n\nWe encourage you to post your questions in sli.do now so that we can adapt the content of the next session to answer them.\n\nThe sessions are open to all and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to scientists and forecasters. Each session requires registration via Zoom. A great opportunity to remove any technical challenges in using the Data Access Services GUIs and APIs, and engage users in discussion with EUMETSAT experts and colleagues.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"This session will focus on how to explore the new Sentinel-3 data available from the EUMETSAT Data Store (https://www.eumetsat.int/eumetsat-data-store).\n\nThis is part of a monthly ","content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Please register at this link: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/2616505305018/WN_nbUdvaHiTxiukkWeVDWo9Q.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":30,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":11,"name":"Data Store"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":8,"name":"Sentinel-3"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2217,"created":1669628504000,"updated":1700679381000,"title":"Expert workshop for preparation of Aviation Forecasters Testbed","titleNative":"Expert workshop for preparation of Aviation Forecasters Testbed","startDate":1661932800000,"endDate":1662033600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":null,"contactPerson":null,"contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":null,"description":null,"country":null,"learningOutcome":null,"summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":null,"registrationHowto":null,"registrationEndDate":null,"fees":null,"awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":null,"attendeeCount":7,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2120,"created":1642171481000,"updated":1653315382000,"title":"Baltic+ 2022 Online Course - Preparing for the cold season forecasting","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2022 Online Course - Preparing for the cold season forecasting","startDate":1661731200000,"endDate":1663286400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service","contactPerson":"Izolda Marcinoniene","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\n\r\nThis online training course is intended for the operational meteorologists. The duration of the online course will be three weeks, during which you are invited to join a few live sessions for listening to presentations from other experts and to share your experiences with other course participants. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By completing this course, you will have refreshed your skills in working with winter weather events using satellite imagery together with other observations as well as numerical weather prediction output, You will also have an opportunity to discuss and exchange valuable forecasting experiences with other colleagues from neighbouring weather services.","summary":null,"content":"This online course will focus on the cold season weather. Topics of the course include the typical challenges forecasters need to deal with  during the cold season: the type of cloudiness, the types of precipitation - rain, snow, freezing rain, and their impacts on people and property. An essential part of the course is to work on case studies that help you to refresh your skills in using the satellite and other products when preparing for winter.\r\n","targetAudience":"The participants for this course come from the Baltic States, Poland and Ukraine.","registrationHowto":"Please contact your national point of contact for training for more information on the nomination and application process. ","registrationEndDate":1656547200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":8,"value":"PWS: Weather Broadcasters and Communicators"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2177,"created":1658847811000,"updated":1658850383000,"title":"Evaluating Ecosystem Services with Remote Sensing","titleNative":"Evaluating Ecosystem Services with Remote Sensing","startDate":1661252400000,"endDate":1661862600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/arset-evaluating-ecosystem-services-remote-sensing?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=EcoServices-22","description":"Healthy ecosystems provide essential pieces of daily life for humans such as clean water, food, medicines, carbon sequestration, protection against extreme weather, and much more. Natural capital accounting recognizes that these assets must be maintained, managed, and measured for critical decision-making activities. NASA data can be used to accurately map ecosystems to support effective planning and sustainable decision-making. \n\nThis training will outline the basics of ecosystem services and natural capital accounting. It will also provide an overview of how Earth Observations (EO) can be used to support global frameworks and initiatives such as standards set by the United Nation’s System of Environmental Economic Accounting (UN-SEEA). Participants will receive information on techniques and tools for using EO in natural capital accounting such as the use of land cover mapping, time series analysis, and modeling efforts conducted with the Natural Capital Project via the InVEST software, The Artificial Intelligence for Environment and Sustainability (ARIES) Project, and more. Case-study examples will be provided to highlight locally specific efforts such as valuation of native pollinators, urban ecosystem accounts, valuation of coastal resilience and coral reef habitats, and forest conservation and carbon sequestration.\n\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \n•\tGoal 14: Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources for sustainable development\n•\tGoal 15: Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, and halt and reverse land degradation and halt biodiversity loss \n\nCourse Dates: August 23, 25, & 30, 2022\n\nTime: 11:00-12:30 EDT (UTC-4)\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will be able to:\n•\tSummarize primary concepts of ecosystem services and natural capital accounting\n•\tRecall global frameworks and initiatives for ecosystem assessments\n•\tOutline the role of NASA Earth Observations (EO) in conducting ecosystem assessments \n•\tIdentify natural capital accounting models that incorporate EO\n•\tDiscover case study examples of the use of EO for ecosystem assessments\n\n","summary":null,"content":null,"targetAudience":"This webinar series is intended for local, regional, state, federal, and non-governmental organizations involved in land and coastal ecosystems management and natural capital accounting. Applied scientists and GIS professionals interested in learning how to use NASA EO data for ecosystem assessments and accounting are encouraged to participate.","registrationHowto":"Please Register Here: https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/arset-evaluating-ecosystem-services-remote-sensing?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=EcoServices-22","registrationEndDate":1661857200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":3,"name":"VLAB"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":null,"format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2173,"created":1657116106000,"updated":1657116148000,"title":"INTERNATIONAL DISTANCE TRAINING COURSE ON  THE APPLICATION OF METEOROLOGICAL  SATELLITE PRODUCTS","titleNative":"INTERNATIONAL DISTANCE TRAINING COURSE ON  THE APPLICATION OF METEOROLOGICAL  SATELLITE PRODUCTS","startDate":1661126400000,"endDate":1662076800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":null,"host":"China Meteorological Administration Training Centre (RTC-Beijing)","contactPerson":"Ms. DENG Jingmian, Ms. HAN Guolin","contactEmail":"applycmatc@cma.gov.cn","contactUrl":"https://forms.office.com/r/7AU6Bkvpse","description":"The course is committed to offering high quality, advanced knowledge and skills of Fengyun satellites, and enhancing the trainees’ professional skills in the application of meteorological satellite products as well as in weather forecasting, surface meteorological disaster monitoring and climate data processing. Trainees will be expected to improve their capabilities in data acquisition and assimilation, utility of satellite monitoring system and satellite remote-sensing application.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course, the participants are expected to: \n1) have a better understanding of Fengyun satellites and the application of Fengyun products, especially the geostationary satellite products;\n2) access, select, display and manipulate satellite data;\n3) carry out weather analysis by using meteorological satellite imagery and data;\n4) familiarize with Satellite Weather Application Platform (SWAP) and Satellite Monitoring Analysis Remote-sensing Tool