in","contactPerson":"TSO EUMeTrain","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations and features. Every month the weather briefing is hosted by a different European country.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Gaining knowledge about analyzing weather situations using satellite data.\r\nMaintaining a healthy basis of knowledge about satellite meteorology.\r\nUnderstanding the difference between RGBs as well as their benefits and limitations.\r\n","summary":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imag","content":"Weather briefings are recorded. Find a collection of past briefings at http://eumetrain.org/briefings.html and on YouTube at https://www.youtube.com/user/eumetrain/videos.","targetAudience":"The primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, although other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome.","registrationHowto":"In order to join the discussion, please go to http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html. For any questions, please use the Contact email.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2138,"created":1647339592000,"updated":1700654827000,"title":"International Summer School ","titleNative":"International Summer School ","startDate":1655715600000,"endDate":1656518400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Bracciano","host":"Italian Air Force","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The course provides an in depth explanation of methods and techniques used to extract information from environmental satellite data, with emphasis on the latest measuring technologies and newest channels.\r\n\r\nThe course consists of lectures and practical sessions. Three different analysis and visualization tools are introduced: McIDAS V - installed locally; and Jupyter Notebooks and SIFT, run in EUMETSAT virtual environment. ","country":{"id":"IT","name":"ITALY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"understanding the basic principles of remote sensing;\r\n\r\nunderstanding the physical background of data in different channels and channels combinations including new FCI channels 0.9, 1.3 and 2.25 micron;\r\n\r\nmastering satellite data visualization using different methods and tools;\r\n\r\nsuccessfully using new tools in virtual environment - Jupyter notebooks and SIFT on EUMETSAT virtual machines (VM);\r\n\r\napplying single channels and RGB images in the analysis and recognition of various cloud structures and land features including fires.","summary":"The course provides an in depth explanation of methods and techniques used to extract information from environmental satellite data, with emphasis on the latest measuring technolog","content":"","targetAudience":"The course is targeted to intermediate and advanced users of satellite data for weather/EO applications. ","registrationHowto":"By invitation only.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":18,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":29,"title":"Severe storms","identifier":"dataApplication"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":18,"title":"Weather","identifier":"dataApplication"}],"eumDataAccessTypes":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":21,"name":"European Weather Cloud"}],"eumSatelliteMissions":[{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":1,"name":"Metop"},{"eventMetadataGroup":{"id":1,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"id":2,"name":"MSG"}],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2157,"created":1652122525000,"updated":1652159156000,"title":"Humanitarian Applications Using NASA Earth Observations","titleNative":"Humanitarian Applications Using NASA Earth Observations","startDate":1655218800000,"endDate":1656018000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3Mkh3IA","description":"Conflict, war, and forced displacement affect millions of people each year and have immediate and long-term consequences for human health and development, in addition to causing the degradation of natural and managed landscapes. Analysis with NASA satellite imagery can help target humanitarian response and relief by i) offering a timely understanding of region-specific environmental conditions and change, and ii) capturing contextual information over broad geographic regions and time spans.\r\n\r\nThis 4-part introductory training will focus on using NASA data products for monitoring human settlements and landscapes during armed conflict and forced displacement. This ARSET training is the first dedicated to humanitarian applications of NASA satellite imagery with topics including monitoring urban damage, mapping refugee settlement dynamics, and gauging climate hazards at refugee settlements. For each topic, we will discuss relevant satellite sensors and methodologies, data access and analysis using Google Earth Engine, as well as assumptions, opportunities, and limitations of various remote sensing-based approaches in humanitarian applications.\r\n\r\nThis training supports quantitative and visual understanding of short- and long-term conflict effects that are evident in satellite imagery, complements analysis of georeferenced humanitarian data, and builds on previous ARSET trainings associated with cropland monitoring, human settlement detection, disaster risk assessment, nighttime lights, and Google Earth Engine.\r\n\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \r\n\tGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable\r\n\tGoal 15: Life on Land\r\n\tGoal 16: Peace, Justice, and Strong Institutions\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After participating in the training, attendees will be able to:\r\n\r\n\tConceptualize landscape- and settlement-level monitoring with satellite remote sensing\r\n\tSelect a range of satellite image data (i.e., optical, radar, nighttime lights, etc.) for humanitarian applications\r\n\tRecognize the value of time series analysis for monitoring acute and long-term changes in humanitarian contexts\r\n\tIdentify opportunities and limitations of using satellite data in humanitarian applications\r\n\tIntegrate satellite-derived humanitarian data with other open-access geospatial products on population, building footprints, infrastructure, etc.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Four, 2-hour parts","targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for stakeholders, academics, researchers, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), international agencies, and government ministries involved in humanitarian response and decision support activities.","registrationHowto":"Times: 11:00-13:00 or 15:00-17:00 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\r\n\r\nRegister Here : https://go.nasa.gov/3Mkh3IA\r\n","registrationEndDate":1655942400000,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":