the Spanish Meteorological State Agency, AEMET) with the support of Copernicus and ACTRIS programmes.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"The Training School and Workshop on Dust Aerosol Detection and Monitoring aims to provide an awareness of state-of-the-art satellite-based, ground-based, and model-based products f","content":"Overview of the course structure:\r\n\r\nSelf-study in preparation for the live sessions - All resources available on the course page (https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=447): webinars and presentations, targeting those willing to learn or refresh their knowledge on the basics of aerosol and dust, principles of observations, modelling and forecast; including retrievals and uncertainty.\r\n \r\n25 and 27 January 2022  live sessions open to all:\r\n\r\nData discovery sessions with assignments, targeting those willing to be introduced to the access, content and manipulation of the key satellite, ground-based, and modelling products. No prerequisites on coding in python or data handling are needed. Basic knowledge of EO data would be an advantage. \r\n\r\n31 January  2 February 2022 (for selected participants - additional seats available)\r\n\r\nInteractive workshop, targeting those willing to progress on data discovery, develop practical case studies and exercises. During the practical training, you will learn basic principles in data handling, management and processing with Python on real-cases.\r\n\r\nHow to join the workshop? Send an email to training@eumetsat.int by 20 January stating Dust course 2022 in the subject and outlining briefly (max 200 words) your motivation for applying to this workshop.\r\n","targetAudience":"- Actors in Meteorological and transnational Agencies, focusing on Europe, North Africa, Middle East, and Sahelian Africa. \r\n- Researchers / academics from the above regions, with a focus on beginners. \r\n","registrationHowto":"You can register at this link to join the live session on 25 and 27 January: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/tZUkfuqurT8vE9wRwZl5HKvdB4H6Wl5aFXWS\r\n\r\nTo apply for the interactive workshop: please send an email to training@eumetsat.int by 20 January stating \"Dust course 2022\" in the subject and outlining briefly (max 200 words) your motivation for applying to this workshop.\r\n\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2083,"created":1634806036000,"updated":null,"title":"5th H SAF User Workshop","titleNative":"5th H SAF User Workshop","startDate":1642982400000,"endDate":1643328000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"EUMeTrain","contactEmail":"tso@eumetrain.org","contactUrl":"http://www.eumetrain.org/events/schedule_H_SAF_WS.pdf","description":"We are pleased to announce the 5th H SAF User Workshop supported by EUMeTrain. It will be held in online mode from 24 - 28 January 2022. The Hydrology SAF is the satellite application facility of the EUMETSAT distributed ground segment that has the aim to provide satellite derived products related to precipitation, soil moisture and snow over land in support to hydrology and water management. In addition to satellite derived products provision H SAF provides both continuous quality assessment of products and evaluation of their hydrological impact for the benefit of the end user communities. \r\n\r\nThe workshop objectives will be:\r\n- Review of the H SAF products status and their evolution in view of the opportunities and challenges of the future European satellite missions;\r\n- Drought monitoring and water resources management;\r\n- H SAF products quality assessment and applications;\r\n- Integrated approach between H SAF products and risk management;\r\n- H SAF products use cases over African region.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"We are pleased to announce the 5th H SAF User Workshop supported by EUMeTrain. It will be held in online mode from 24 - 28 January 2022. The Hydrology SAF is the satellite applicat","content":"See the event agenda and register at http://www.eumetrain.org/events/schedule_H_SAF_WS.pdf. ","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Please register at http://www.eumetrain.org/events/schedule_H_SAF_WS.pdf. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2830,"name":"Madalina Ungur as sysadmin","email":"Madalina.Ungur@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id