on the flow that is used, regardless of programming language, to produce statistics or imagery from raw data files. We will also highlight resources that are available in multiple programming languages to further your exploration of coding for EO.  \r\n\r\nIn the short course we will use python and R. however, the principles can be applied to many other programming languages.","targetAudience":"Anyone interested in gridded Earth Observation Data, with no or little experience in coding. ","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar at the course page: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=428\r\n\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2093,"created":1636379457000,"updated":1636454402000,"title":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated FOrecastiNg sYstem of DWD III","titleNative":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated FOrecastiNg sYstem of DWD III","startDate":1638865800000,"endDate":1638869400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Eumetcal","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/app#/catalog/course/f521e69e-fe6e-41b3-89b1-5ed098e0732d","description":"Project SINFONY is an ongoing project at DWD for developing the new Seamless INtegrated FOrecastINg sYstemSINFONY  that yields very-short-range forecasts from 0-12 hours without inconsistencies. Presently, forecasts of up to 2 h are based upon nowcasting whereas longer forecasts are mainly done by NWP, both separately and independently. There is no seamless transition of structures in forecast fields over lead time from Nowcasting to NWP.\r\n\r\nTo narrow down this gap, SINFONY works on different aspects oft the problem with an integrated team: Improving the two forecast techniques by themselves (Nowcasting and NWP with its associated ensemble data assimilation) and, in postprocessing, develop optimally combined seamless forecast products for each lead time. The combined products shall also reduce the vast forecast information to a manageable level to be efficiently used in forecasting practice. The last point is especially important because SINFONY will be based on full NWP- and Nowcasting ensembles at all levels. In a first project stage the focus will be upon precipitation related quantities for summertime convection (thunderstorms and heavy precipitation) such as precipitation and radar reflectivity fields as well as convective cell objects.\r\n\r\nIn this third presentation on SINFONY the general concept and the NWP component will shortly be recapitulated before the focus will be laid on recent developments and future plans, which comprises advanced data assimilation of new remote sensing data sources (3D radar volume data, visible satellite channels, lightning) and hourly new forecasts of a regional convection allowing km-scale ICON-D2 model (Rapid Update Cycle). In addition, to support a quick and easy interpretation, SINFONY seeks to strengthen the visualization of model forecasts in observation space (radar, satellite, cell objects).","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"https://knmi.webex.com/mw3300/mywebex/default.do?siteurl=knmi&service=7&main_url=%2Ftc3300%2Ftrainingcenter%2Fdefault.do%3Fsiteurl%3Dknmi%26main_url%3D%252Ftc3300%252Ftrainingcenter%252Fmeeting%252FsessionInfo.do%253Fsiteurl%253Dknmi%2526confID%253D4817800524969452567%2526sessionNO%253D0","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2089,"created":1634889238000,"updated":null,"title":"Third joint training course on Atmospheric Composition ","titleNative":"Third joint training course on Atmospheric Composition ","startDate":1638748800000,"endDate":1639699200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":" ECMWF, EUMETSAT, ESA","contactPerson":"Chris Stewart","contactEmail":"Chris.Stewart@ecmwf.int","contactUrl":"https://atmosphere.copernicus.eu/3rd-eumetsatesaecmwf-joint-training-atmospheric-composition","description":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECMWF) with the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) are organising a third joint training course on Atmospheric Composition from 6 to 17 December 2021. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts (ECM","content":"The training will present the state-of-the-art in atmospheric monitoring and modelling. It aims to provide an end-to-end overview of observations, remote sensing, modelling, data assimilation and applications; and to enhance the capacity to access and analyse data. The training course also aims to foster collaboration amongst participants and encourage the development of individual and team projects using the data, resources and methodologies presented.\r\n\r\nMain topics of the training: \r\n\r\n- Atmospheric processes: Chemical species, aerosols, GHG\r\n- Modelling: Global / regional; analysis / re-analysis / forecast; bias correction & downscaling; inverse modelling / DA\r\n- Emissions: Inventories, inverse modelling, anthropogenic effects (link to COVID)\r\n- Observations: Spaceborne, in-situ, remote sensing retrievals\r\n- Operational applications and services: Policies; public & private sector needs; applications & services.\r\n\r\nThe training is taking place entirely online with five days of lectures and practical sessions distributed over two weeks.\r\n","targetAudience":"The training is beneficial for early-career scientists, researchers from academia and research institutes, young scientists from industry, and anyone interested in atmospheric composition monitoring and modelling.","registrationHowt