g products.  The workshop will consist of daily invited talks, poster session and small group discussions.\r\n\r\nMore information about the workshop can be found here: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=421 ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"The Remote Sensing for Ocean-Atmosphere Interactions Studies and Applications Workshop, co-organized by EUMETSAT with the support of SOLAS and the Copernicus EU programme, is desig","content":"Workshop objectives:\r\n\r\n- Report and inform about ongoing research in the thematic area, satellite based data. \r\n- Discuss unexplored potential of satellite (based) data in the field and identify gaps in terms of monitoring capability.\r\n- Inform on developments, tools, ways of access, available and upcoming training material and training opportunities by satellite product providers. \r\n- Identify needs and associated material and collaborations for improved data access, usage, training and capacity building.\r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"- Scientists & Academy (all levels of seniority) in a wide range of disciplines: climate, remote sensing, atmospheric physics and chemistry, physical oceanography, ocean biology.\r\n- Representatives of services and data provider agencies.","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJYqf-mtpjkjHtfOdEsBZp19hjrx023hxbUX\r\n\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the workshop in Zoom.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2094,"created":1636488273000,"updated":1636529447000,"title":"Monitoring Coastal and Estuarine Water Quality Using Remote Sensing and In Situ Data","titleNative":"Monitoring Coastal and Estuarine Water Quality Using Remote Sensing and In Situ Data","startDate":1638284400000,"endDate":1638910800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3met1tg","description":"This two-part, advanced webinar series is a follow-on to the training on coastal and estuarine water quality held in September 2021. It is a hands-on training with demos provided by instructors, followed by an hour of lab time for participants to use Level-1 MODIS and VIIRS data provided by the Ocean Biology DAAC (OB.DAAC) and SeaDAS and OCSSW software for deriving water quality parameters. These will include chlorophyll-a concentration, sea surface temperature, and suspended particulate matter from optical satellite imagery and in situ measurements using the SeaWiFS Bio-optical Archive and Storage System (SeaBASS), a public repository of in situ oceanographic and atmospheric data, and SeaDAS, a comprehensive software package for the processing, display, analysis, and quality control of remote sensing data. This training will provide participants with the skills to combine in situ measurements and optical remote sensing data to assess water quality for their area of interest.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: \r\n\tGoal 14: Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources for sustainable development\r\n\tTarget 14.2: By 2020, sustainably manage and protect marine and coastal ecosystems to avoid significant adverse impacts, including by strengthening their resilience, and take action for their restoration in order to achieve healthy and productive oceans\r\n\tGoal 6: Ensure availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation for all\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this series, attendees will be able to:\r\n\tSelect in situ water quality data from SeaBASS\r\n\tDevelop algorithms from MODIS and VIIRS imagery using SeaDAS to obtain chlorophyll-a, sea surface temperature, and suspended particulate matter\r\n\tMonitor water quality in selected coastal and estuarine regions\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Two, 2-hour parts (with lab time)","targetAudience":"This training series is intended for federal, state, regional, and local public and private organizations involved in water quality and estuarine ecosystem management.\r\n\r\n","registrationHowto":"Please register here: https://go.nasa.gov/3met1tg","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120