actEmail":"Natasa.StrelecMahovic@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=427","description":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from October 2021.\r\n\r\nSimilar to snow covered hills with its unique view, but also hidden dangers, winter weather for the operational meteorologists offers a unique concept to handle, quite a different view in the satellite imagery, and hidden hurdles when it comes to interpretation of that imagery. Join us for this session and you will hear satellite application experts talking about: \r\n\r\n- Specifics of winter weather.\r\n- Analysis of winter weather through satellite data.  \r\n- Utility of the satellite data and products for winter season.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from October 2021.\r\n\r","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar at the course page:\r\n\r\nhttps://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=427\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme"