ts to apply these datasets in their area of research interests. Junior and advanced researchers working in academy and public/private services as well as candidates from other continents are invited to apply but will be considered based on availability.","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Starters in Science, PhD, PDRAs, National Services providers","registrationHowto":"https://training.eumetsat.int/mod/questionnaire/view.php?id=14358","registrationEndDate":1620950400000,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":4858,"name":"Elena Ebert","email":"Elena.Ebert@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":80,"value":"Other","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"}],"qualification":[{"id":23,"value":"Instrumentation (OBS) "}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1998,"created":1612468102000,"updated":1612949099000,"title":"A Climate Data Record of Soil moisture in the root zone - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"A Climate Data Record of Soil moisture in the root zone - Series of online short courses","startDate":1623844800000,"endDate":1623852000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Christine Träger-Chatterjee","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=404","description":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r\nEnvironmental (e.g. floods, droughts) and weather prediction systems rely on an accurate representation of soil moisture (SM). The availability of moisture in the root zone of plants is critical and especially in recent years has become an issue in large areas of Europe, as a series of dry summers have been experienced.  \r\n\r\nAs an H SAF partner ECMWF is producing scatterometer-derived root zone SM. In this short course you will learn about the retrieval approach and the strengths and limitations of the climate data record. You will also have the chance to explore the data yourself in a hands-on session.\r\n\r\nA feedback session will be organised later in the day at 15:00 UTC. Both sessions will be recorded. \r\n\r\nTo get ready for the course, please visit the course page at https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=404.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar at the course page:\r\n\r\nhttps://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=397.\r\n\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2043,"created":1622532088000,"updated":1622532635000,"title":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated Forecasting sYstem of DWD II","titleNative":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated Forecasting sYstem of DWD II","startDate":1623742200000,"endDate":1623747600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Eumetcal","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.trainingscatalogus.nl/en/app#/catalog/course/2918bed3-f6bb-4061-9ae1-92ca9f638a2a","description":"Project SINFONY is an ongoing project at DWD for developing the new Seamless INtegrated FOrecastINg sYstemSINFONY that yields very-short-range forecasts from 0-12 hours without much inconsistencies. At present, forecasts of up to 2 h are based upon nowcasting whereas longer forecasts are mainly done by NWP, both separately and independently. There is no seamless transition of structures in forecast fields over lead time from Nowcasting to NWP.\r\nTo narrow down this gap, SINFONY works on different aspects of the problem with an integrated team: Improving the two forecast techniques by themselves (Nowcasting and NWP with its associated ensemble data assimilation) and, in postprocessing, develop optimally combined seamless forecast products for each lead time. The combined products shall also reduce the vast forecast informations to a manageable level to be efficiently used in forecasting practice. The last point is especially important because SINFONY will be based on full NWP- and Nowcasting ensembles at all levels. In the current first project stage the focus is on precipitation related quantities for summertime convection (thunderstorms and heavy precipitation) such as precipitation and radar reflectivity fields as well as convective cell objects. \r\nIn this second presentation on SINFONY the general concept will shortly be recapitulated before the focus will be laid on the NWP component, which comprises advanced data assimilation of new remote sensing data sources (3D radar volume data, visible satellite channels, lightning) and hourly new forecasts of a regional convection alllowing km-scale ICON-D2 model (Rapid Update Cycle). In addition, to support a quick and easy interpretation, SINFONY seeks to strengthen the visualization of model forecasts in observation space (radar, satellite, cell objects).","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"To register for the webinar, please see instruction at: https://eumetcal.trainingscatalogus.nl/en/app#/catalog/course/2918bed3-f6bb-4061-9ae1-92ca9f638a2a","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"appr