tter understand the operational realities of marine forecasters in Africa, what training needs there are and the regional capacities to meet those needs. ","country":{"id":"ZA","name":"SOUTH AFRICA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"    -Analyze and monitor continually the marine weather situation.\r\n     -Forecast marine weather phenomena, variables and parameters.\r\n     -Warn of hazardous marine phenomena.","summary":null,"content":"The following skills were trained:\r\n\r\n     1. Interpret satellite imagery and products to identify potentially dangerous phenomena.\r\n     2. Using satellite altimeters and scatterometers.\r\n     3. Use of NWP in waves and swell forecasting.\r\n     4. Identify characteristics of waves and swell.\r\n     5. Monitor sea ice characteristics.\r\n     6. Identify non-routine weather conditions.\r\n     7. Use forecasting model outputs in hazardous conditions.","targetAudience":"Marine forecasters and trainers from WMO region I (Africa). ","registrationHowto":"The classroom course invitations are sent to participants having successfully completed the online course (certificate required), priority being given to participants without previous classroom course experience. For more information on the online course, please see: http://trainingevents.eumetsat.int/#!details/1847","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5845,"name":"Ivan Smiljanic","email":"ivan.smiljanic@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":f