tions.","summary":"For preparing users to data from the next-generation spectral imaging missions on Meteosat Third Generation satellites (Flexible Combined Imager  FCI) and Metop-SG satellites (MET","content":"The webinar provides:\r\n- an overview of instrument and measurement principles;\r\n- details on product generation, product characteristics, and expected performance;\r\n- user-relevant information about data formats, test datasets, dissemination, and application perspectives.\r\n\r\nThe event describes the new spectral channels and improvements in resolution and performance over the MSG SEVIRI, Metop AVHRR and other heritage sensors. This Webinar focuses on product generation activities at EUMETSAT Central Facility.","targetAudience":"The Webinar is intended for an audience with a good level of scientific and technical understanding of satellite remote sensing and weather forecasting, and some experience in using MSG SEVIRI products and/or METimage proxy data such as NOAA VIIRS or NASA MODIS.","registrationHowto":"Please read more at \r\nhttps://www.eumetsat.int/user-preparation-webinar-next-generation-spectral-imagers-fci-metimage.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2039,"created":1620663772000,"updated":1621055941000,"title":"NASA Earth Observations for Energy Management","titleNative":"NASA Earth Observations for Energy Management","startDate":1622556000000,"endDate":1624397400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3deAcgl","description":"Energy impacts everything we do, from providing basic services such as cooking and cleaning to providing development opportunities and improving overall quality of life. However, energy management, through energy production, transmission, and distribution, is impacted by environmental and climate conditions, including weather patterns or extremes and climate change. Energy providers are turning to cleaner and renewable energy sources, as well as assessing and implementing actions to make their energy management activities more resilient to environmental hazards. Decision-makers need to better understand where energy resources exist and how they are impacted by physical environmental conditions, weather, and climate. \r\n\r\nThis training will offer participants an introduction to how NASA EOs can contribute to a greater understanding of energy management applications. The course will summarize priorities and challenges for energy management and how various NASA EOs can support decision-making. Attendees will gain familiarity with a broad set of relevant NASA datasets, tools, platforms, and resources, as well as hear about case studies and real-world applications related to climate resilience, energy efficiency, and renewable energy.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \r\n\tGoal 7: Ensure access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this series, attendees will:\r\n\tBe able to summarize priorities and challenges in the energy management sector and how Earth observations can support decision-making\r\n\tBecome familiar with online tools for acquiring data from satellite missions and visualizing data or conducting analyses\r\n\tBe aware of various use cases for Earth Observations in energy management for renewable energy, energy efficiency, and climate resilience\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Four, 90-minute parts\r\n\r\nCourse Dates: Tuesdays, June 1, 8, 15, & 22, 2021\r\n\r\nTimes: 10:00-11:30 or 16:00-17:30 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\r\n","targetAudience":"The audience is primarily energy management professionals and decision makers from local government, state agencies, the private sector, or other stakeholders (e.g. electric utilities).","registrationHowto":"Register Here: https://go.nasa.gov/3deAcgl","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2035,"created":1620057323000,"updated":1620142835000,"title":"EUMETSAT New Data Services for Data Centre Users - Accessing and tailoring SEVIRI 1.5 Data","titleNative":"EUMETSAT New Data Services for Data Centre Users - Accessing and tailoring SEVIRI 1.5 Data","startDate":1622458800000,"endDate":1622462400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Harald Rothfuss","contactEmail":"Harald.Rothfuss@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=419","description":"We inform you on the availability of new and modern Data Services at EUMETSAT that you can already employ to access a selection of EUMETSAT data, including the MSG level1.5. \r\n\r\nThe key new service for existing Data Centre users is the EUMETSAT Data Store. The Data Store and the associated Data Tailor Service provides users with a download and data tailoring service for online data which will eventually replace the ordering service from the Data Centre. Users can discover, apply customisation changes (format transformations, regional sub-setting, file aggregation, etc.) and download data. The service provides access through an online interface (GUI) and additionally for the first time also via Application Programming Interfaces (API). The service is currently in a pilot phase and is planned to go operational in July 2021.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the training people will:\r\n\r\n- Have an understanding of the capabilities of the new Data Services\r\n- Be able to use the GUIs to access, download and tailor the MSG l1.5 data\r\n- Be able to use the API to discover and download native data from the data store in python \r\n- Be able to use the APIs to discover and download HRIT or NetCDF data via the data tailor in python \r\n- Be able to use a chain via the API that was created and saved in the GUI\r\n","summary":"We inform you on the availability of new and modern Data Services at EUMETSAT that you can already employ to access a selection of EUMETSAT data, including the MSG level1.5. \r\n\r\nTh","content":"The core materials will be made available via scripts on eumetlab (gitlab.eumetsat.int/eumetlab).\r\n\r\n- Python scripts in the form of Jupiter notebooks that users can use locally.\r\n","targetAudience":"Existing Data Centre users who are ordering\r\n\r\n- MSG High Rate SEVIRI L1.5 data with various customisations (e.g. format changes to NetCDF or HRIT, selecting a Region of Interest)\r\n- NetCDF can be with or without area of interest\r\n- RSS and IODC data use is included\r\n- HRV data use is included\r\n","registrationHowto":"By invitation only.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":4858,"name":"Elena Ebert","email":"Elena.Ebert@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1961,"created":1605880779000,"updated":1615465964000,"title":"Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications Online Training course - Summer 2021","titleNative":"Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications Online Training course - Summer 2021","startDate":1622419200000,"endDate":1624579200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Lauren Biermann","contactEmail":"Copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The purpose of this EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CMDS) training course is to share knowledge, skills, resources and code so attendees are able to independently access and process data from Sentinel-3, supporting missions and CMEMS for their marine work-flows and applications.\r\n\r\nTraining will take place entirely online and through two phases. The first self-paced phase will take place between 31 May and 18 June and will take approximately 6-8 hours in total to complete. This will involve self-paced flexible learning through webinars, forums (particularly for software installations), documentation and assignments. The second virtual classroom phase will be held during the week 21 - 25 June and will be hosted over Zoom, made up of interactive tutorials, live demos, group work, and 1:1 meetings. This will require 5-7 hours of participation each day.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course participants will have the skills to:\r\n\r\n- Understand what data and products the Copernicus Marine Data Stream provides (variables, timeliness, resolution, data formats)\r\n- Design tailored workflows appropriate to individual requirements and needs\r\n- Select, access and download relevant products for specific tasks from the Copernicus Marine Data Stream\r\n- Know how to work with CMDS data in SNAP, GIS, and Python (Jupyter Notebooks)\r\n","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Training is aimed at, but not restricted to, early career scientists: Masters / PhD students, Post-Docs, and/or experienced scientists from any relevant sector (industry, government, environment, research) who have clear motivations for working with satellite-based oc