ntry":{"id":"CN","name":"CHINA","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"1)apply the basic theory and principles of radiation to the interpretation of meteorological satellite imagery and products;\r\n2)access, select, display and manipulate satellite data;\r\n3)carry out weather analysis and forecasting by using meteorological satellite imagery and data;\r\n4)use SWAP and SMART tools;\r\n5)have a better understanding of the Fengyun (FY) satellites","summary":null,"content":"The training course includes:\r\n1)Concepts of satellite remote-sensing;\r\n2)Satellite cloud image recognition and interpretation;\r\n3)Satellite Weather Application Platform (SWAP) and Satellite Monitoring Analysis Remote-sensing Toolkit (SMART);\r\n4)Case study on satellite products application in disaster mitigation and prevention;\r\n5)Introduction to the latest development of Fengyun satellites and the application of FY products, especially the geostationary satellite products.","targetAudience":"Officials, specialist, forecasters engaged in satellite meteorology, especially for freshman. ","registrationHowto":"Open-path candidates could create their own account with enroll key: Cmatc2021\r\nCertificate-path candidates are requested to submit the completed Application Forms to CMATC and then they will be provided the enroll key for certificate path.","registrationEndDate":1621728000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5868,"name":"JI Wenbin","email":"jiwenbin@cma.cn","agency":"","country":"CN","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":1,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence China-Beijing"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":190,"value":"RTC","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":19,"value":"CMA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2044,"created":1622625543000,"updated":1622625654000,"title":"Satellite Application Course: Dust events","titleNative":"Satellite Application Course: Dust events","startDate":1621756800000,"endDate":1622116800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Muscat","host":"Public Authority for Civil Aviation (PACA)","contactPerson":"Hilal Al-Hajri","contactEmail":"h.alhajri@met.gov.om","contactUrl":"","description":"This course will focus on Dust detection, monitoring and forecasting, as well as the basics of remote sensing and application of satellite data to regional forecasting problems. It will also cover the role and the benefits of MTG mission in the forecasting processes. ","country":{"id":"OM","name":"OMAN","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn to:\r\n- Describe Dust events (where and when they form);\r\n- Identify distinguishing features of Dust storms/events;\r\n- Describe ingredients needed for genesis of Dust events;\r\n- Define the Dust cycles;\r\n- Detect Dust cloud types using satellite remote sensing;\r\n- Describe key storm and environmental factors that affect  Dust event formation;\r\n- Describe the mechanisms that influence Dust cloud motion;\r\n- Describe the Dust modeling principles and limitations;\r\n\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Dust detection, monitoring and forecasting. MTG utility in the region.\r\n","targetAudience":"Operational weather forecasters","registrationHowto":"By invitation letter.","registrationEndDate":1612137600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5845,