 briefing. Satellite imag","content":"Weather briefings are recorded. Find a collection of past briefings at http://eumetrain.org/briefings.html and on YouTube at https://www.youtube.com/user/eumetrain/videos.","targetAudience":"The primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, although other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome.","registrationHowto":"In order to join the discussion, please go to http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html. For any questions, please use the Contact email.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2019,"created":1616577562000,"updated":1616676286000,"title":"EGU Short Course: Using Copernicus data for Atmospheric Composition Applications","titleNative":"EGU Short Course: Using Copernicus data for Atmospheric Composition Applications","startDate":1619593200000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"European Geophysical Union","contactPerson":"Federico Fierli, Christian Retascher (ESA), Mark Parrington (CAMS)","contactEmail":"Federico.Fierli@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EGU21/session/38924","description":"The course will be accessible from the EGU online page https://www.egu21.eu/.\r\n\r\nThis ONLINE short course is an opportunity to learn about Copernicus data for Atmospheric Composition and to get examples how to develop your own workflows based on sample applications.\r\n\r\nThe European Union Copernicus programme is open and free for everyone - whether from academic, government, or commercial backgrounds. The programme has an operational focus, with satellite constellations and services. Satellite data provides composition vital information on key atmospheric constituents at different spatial and temporal scales with a continuous improvements in observational spatial and temporal resolution, coverage and measured species as well as a constantly evolving added value products from the Copernicus Atmospheric Monitoring Services.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"The sessions will be hands-on and supported by Earth Observation and Model experts to discover data, handle them and produce plots out of a sample of the Copernicus data. You will make use of a series of freely available tools specifically developed for these applications including Jupyter Notebook modules, to have an easy and intuitive way to make use of Python programming. No experience is necessary as various exercises will be provided for a wide range of skill levels and applications.","targetAudience":"Academic, Young Researchers, PhD, Senior Scientists, Services","registrationHowto":"The course is held within the 2021 EGU conference. \r\n\r\nRegistration fees are divided into categories which you will find here: EGU21 - Register\r\nThe course is free of cost if you fall in the category of Emeritus non-member, undergraduate or master student, low- & lower-middle income countries or PhD candidate from a middle income country.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":4858,"name":"Elena Ebert","email":"Elena.Ebert@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2038,"created":1620226029000,"updated":null,"title":"European Weather Cloud User Preparation workshop","titleNative":"European Weather Cloud User Preparation workshop","startDate":1619481600000,"endDate":1619481600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Darmstadt","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"n.a.","contactEmail":"n.a.","contactUrl":"","description":"Regular Joint User Workshop with ECMWF on the European Weather Cloud.","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Info and needs sharing for the upcoming operations phase of the EWC.","summary":null,"content":"Interactive sessions and Q&A","targetAudience":"Member States","registrationHowto":"n.a.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2029,"created":1619438958000,"updated":1619439433000,"title":"EGU21 EUMETSAT Data services Short Course","titleNative":"EGU21 EUMETSAT Data services Short Course","startDate":1619424000000,"endDate":1619443800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"online","host":"EGU/ EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Pablo Benedicto","contactEmail":"Pablo.Benedicto@external.eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EGU21/session/38946","description":"EUMETSAT offers over 35 years of meteorological satellite data. New data consistency with previous satellites is ensured by intercalibration and reprocessing. This is a valuable resource for the geoscience communities. EUMETSAT produces 26% of the Essential Climate Variable records identified by the Global Climate Observing System that can be observed from space.\r\n\r\nWith the new satellite programmes, the volume and complexity of the data products will increase significantly, making it unfeasible for traditional workflows, relying on accessing local data holdings, to exploit these observations. EUMETSATs new Data Services, the subject of this course, address this issue.","country":null,"learningOutcome":"In this short course you will learn:\r\n- what EUMETSAT offers the geoscience communities within Europe (Data Store, Data Tailor, and visualisation service)\r\n- how to set up access and how to use the GUIs and APIs, Jupiter notebooks and documentation will be available to take away","summary":"EUMETSAT offers over 35 years of meteorological satellite data. New data consistency with previous satellites is ensured by intercalibration and reprocessing. This is a valuable re","content":"The Data Store provides online access for directly downloading satellite data via a web-based user interface and APIs usable in processing chains. Users can download the data in its original format or customise it before download by invoking the Data Tailor Service. The View Service provides access via standard OGC Web Map, Web Coverage and Web Feature Services (WMS, WCS, WFS) which visualise data available in the Data Store. It is accessible via a web-based interface and APIs allowing the integration of visualisations in end-user applications.\r\n\r\nThis short course is open to all attending the EGU and will give you an introduction in how to use the services. User guides will be made available before the event and there will be time for questions and answers.\r\nThis short course will be divided in two blocks:\r\n\r\n1st Block (10:00-11:00 CEST)\r\n- Introduction\r\n- EUMETView\r\n- Q&A\r\n\r\n2nd Block (14:30-15:30 CEST)\r\n- Introduction\r\n- Data Store\r\n- Data Tailor\r\n- Q&A","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Enter live sessions via this Webpage: https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EGU21/session/38946.","registrationEndDate":1619789400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":4858,"name":"Elena Ebert","email":"Elena.Ebert@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2018,"created":1616164301000,"updated":1617803856000,"title":"Eumetcal webinar: KNMI warning system","titleNative":"Eumetcal webinar: KNMI warning system","startDate":1619082000000,"endDate":1619087400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Eumetcal","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/app#/catalog/course/8d8f9f44-14eb-41a9-a193-17928a3fa2d7","description":"KNMI is redesigning its warning system. Nowadays KNMI uses a hybrid way of issuing warnings. For the less severe warnings (yellow), the system is criteria based, warnings with increased severity (orange/red) are increasingly impact based. For this way of warning there is a close cooperation with the Civil Protection Authorities on national level. The new system will endure in this philosophy but will however try to weigh meteorology and impact as independent variables. With use of an online objective impact tool, warnings will be weighed by an impact team and finally a waring will be issued.\r\nAnother aspect of the new system will be the essence of Early Warnings, where it is the ambition to alert both the general public as the professional users a week in advance. Also the next generation warnings will be more regionalized on a scalable level of detail (from province to municipality) given the interest of the user.\r\nIn the end it also requires new skills of the forecasters in the change of mind to communicate not what the weather will be, but what the weather will do.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"le