:null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course participants will have the skills to:\r\n- Understand the data and data products that the CMDS provides (timeliness, resolution, data formats, variables).\r\n- Select most relevant and appropriate products from the CMDS for specific tasks.\r\n- Access / download data and products provided in the CMDS.\r\n- Know how to work with CMDS data in SNAP and Python (Jupyter Notebooks).\r\n- Apply the satellite data products from the CMDS for tailored applications.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"This training is aimed at those working in the operational marine sector and government agencies who are interested in working with satellite-based ocean observation data for marine applications. Please note that this does not include marine weather forecasting (meteorology). \r\n\r\nIt would be beneficial for participants to have introductory experience using GIS software and/or a scripting language such as Python (or similar), but this is not a prerequisite. Please note that this course is aimed primarily at European audiences and Copernicus programme member states. ","registrationHowto":"Apply for the course here: https://training.eumetsat.int/mod/questionnaire/view.php?id=13998 ","registrationEndDate":1615507200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":3925,"name":"Kim Hockley","email":"khock@pml.ac.uk","agency":"EUM","country":"GB","programme":"PML","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPart