. If there is no confirmation within your spam/junk inbox, contact moodle@bom.gov.au giving their name and email address, stating they had not received their site registration confirmation email for our training site.\r\nC.\tFor users who have already registered, please click \"Continue\" on the Self enrolment (Student) option. Log in using the above Username and Password. If you have forgotten the password then you can use the 'forgot password' function: https://learn.bom.gov.au/login/forgot_password.php\r\nD.\tAustralian Bureau of Meteorology staff please use the 'Bureau staff log in' button to log in to the site. \r\n\r\nPlease use either the Google Chrome or Modzilla Firefox web browsers when you join the session.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":21,"value":"Not Applicable"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2028,"created":1618994799000,"updated":null,"title":"Environmental Data and Products produced by EUMETSAT and COPER","titleNative":"Environmental Data and Products produced by EUMETSAT and COPER","startDate":1616803200000,"endDate":1616889600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Campina Grande","host":"Sociedade Brasileira de Meteorologia","contactPerson":"Humberto Barbosa","contactEmail":"barbosa33@gmail.com","contactUrl":"","description":"This year the annual training course of Eumetsat in Brazil will be organized by the Laboratory of\r\nAnalysis and Processing of Satellite Images (LAPIS) and by the Brazilian\r\nSociety of Meteorology and will be held in a fully face-to-face format.\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"BR","name":"BRAZIL","region":"RA-III","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"The purpose of the event is to train participants in the areas of monitoring and assessing environmental impacts in Brazil, using images from the Sentinel (1 and 2) and Meteosat-11 satellites.","summary":"This year the annual training course of Eumetsat in Brazil will be organized by the Laboratory of\r\nAnalysis and Processing of Satellite Images (LAPIS) and by the Brazilian\r\nSociety","content":"The central theme of the event will be the discussions with specialists from the main national institutions about the anthropogenic disasters in Brazil. In\r\nthe context of the current environmental crisis and the fight against the pandemic in Brazil.\r\n","targetAudience":"Weather forecasters, Researchers.","registrationHowto":"Bz invitation only.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":5,"value":"Portuguese","iso639":"pt"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1994,"created":1611175481000,"updated":1611224136000,"title":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","startDate":1616598000000,"endDate":1616601600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Bernie Connell","contactEmail":"bernie.connell@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8266201397826815504","description":"The sessions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean).  Session time is 15:00 UTC, but as usual, it will start 15 minutes earlier (at 14:45 UTC for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection).  GoToWebinar is used for both images and voice through the Internet.  Images during the session are from SLIDER: http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu  More Information: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup.asp","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8266201397826815504","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1963,"created":1606406351000,"updated":1613126348000,"title":"How to build a case study - a demo session - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"How to build a case study - a demo session - Series of online short courses","startDate":1615982400000,"endDate":1615989600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Ivan Smiljanic and Natasa Strelec Mahovic","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=397","description":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r\nHave you ever done a case study yourself? What is a case study anyway  is this a nice short story about the event that happened, supported by some scientific variables? Or this is research paper triggered by a certain event that did not go under public or scientific radar? Why and how experts produce case studies, and who needs them anyway?\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r","content":"In this short course webinar we will try to answer aforementioned questions and hint to you the tools and know-how to assist your own potential venture into case studies. \r\n\r\nThere must be a situation or event in your own work where your algorithm did not perform well for some reason, or you gave a wrong forecast, or there was so much freezing rain that you could not enter your car in the morning  and you ask yourself why, perhaps you want to investigate more and share your finding with the world. For those interested, we will also reserve time and means to build and go together through your own case studies in the follow-up event, a week after the initial webinar. \r\n\r\nWebinar on 17th March at 12UTC, and follow-up on the following Wednesday, 24th March also at 12 UTC. The webinars will be recorded.\r\n\r\nA course page has been set up at https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=397. ","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar:\r\nhttps://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=397.\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\r\n\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2009,"created":1614697879000,"updated":1614709852000,"title":"Use of Solar Induced Fluorescence and LIDAR to Assess Vegetation Change and Vulnerability","titleNative":"El Uso de la Fluorescencia Inducida por el Sol y LIDAR para Evaluar los Cambios y la Vulnerabilidad de la Vegetación","startDate":1615917600000,"endDate":1616702400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3iWMaN5","description":"This introductory webinar series will cover the fundamentals of Solar Induced Fluorescence (SIF) and LIDAR, their applications, and an overview of different satellite data sources that are openly available. In addition, it will also include a step-by-step guide on how to access, open, and interpret SIF and LIDAR data. It serves as a strong proxy to gross primary production (GPP), capturing dynamic responses of vegetation to stressors such as drought and temperature.\r\n\r\nLIDAR is a sensor system that illuminates a target and measures distance through the time taken for a pulse to reflect back to the sensor. LIDAR can be used to generate topography and vegetation height maps and retrieve digital elevation data necessary for flood modeling and vulnerability, along with risk analysis. They are valuable datasets for disaster assessment of debris deposition, vegetation loss, and flooding.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to understand the basic concepts of SIF and LIDAR sensors, how to interpret the measurements, and how they can be used to address different applications. In addition, attendees will also be able to access, open, and analyze SIF and LIDAR data.","summary":null,"content":"Four, 2-hour parts","targetAudience":"Academia as well as local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in using satellite imagery to support applications related to vegetation studies and disasters.","registrationHowto":"Spanish Session: 14:00-15:00 EDT (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3iWMaN5\r\n\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":26,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2008,"created":1614697707000,"updated":1614709894000,"title":"Use of Solar Induced Fluorescence and LIDAR to Assess Vegetation Change and Vulnerability","titleNative":"Use of Solar Induced Fluorescence and LIDAR to Assess Vegetation Change and Vulnerability","startDate":1615906800000,"endDate":1616691600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/3pmdN4C","description":"This introductory webinar series will cover the fundamentals of Solar Induced Fluorescence (SIF) and LIDAR, their applications, and an overview of different satellite data sources that are openly available. In addition, it will also include a step-by-step guide on how to access, open, and interpret SIF and LIDAR data. It serves as a strong proxy to gross primary production (GPP), capturing dynamic responses of vegetation to stressors such as drought and temperature.\r\n\r\nLIDAR is a sensor system that illuminates a target and measures distance through the time taken for a pulse to reflect back to the sensor. LIDAR can be used to generate topography and vegetation height maps and retrieve digital elevation data necessary for flood modeling and vulnerability, along with risk analysis. They are valuable datasets for disaster assessment of debris deposition, vegetation loss, and flooding.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: \r\n\tTarget 13.1: Strengthen resilience and adaptive capacity to climate-related hazards and natural disasters in all countries\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to understand the basic concepts of SIF and LIDAR sensors, how to interpret the measurements, and how they can be used to address different applications. In addition, attendees will also be able to access, open, and analyze SIF and LIDAR data.","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Four, 2-hour parts","targetAudience":"Academia as well as local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in using satellite imagery to support applications related to vegetation studies and disasters.","registrationHowto":"English Session: 11:00-13:00 EDT (UTC-4): https://go.nasa.gov/3pmdN4C","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1837,"created":1576668206000,"updated":1606921127000,"title":"XVII Ibero-American Course ","titleNative":"XVII Curso Iberoamericano ","startDate":1615802820000,"endDate":1623492480000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"AECID","contactPerson":"Patricio López","contactEmail":"malopezc@aemet.es","contactUrl":"","description":"There will be an online phase of the course that will take place mid March- mid June 2021. The classroom phase has also been postponed to next year, 2021. Dates to be confirmed. The course will focus on tropical meteorology and the application of Meteosat and GOES satellites to weather phenomena in 