rse is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for the weather, oceanography, air quality, and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r\nThis short course focuses on the ozone dataset from the GOME-2 instrument. We will discuss the basics of stratospheric ozone science and observational techniques. Then we will bring participants in working with datasets on an intuitive series of Notebooks to (1) familiarize with data and (2) get ready to make their own analysis and animations.\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"(1) Refresh (or learn) on ozone in the stratosphere\r\n(2) Satellite-based observations of compounds\r\n(3) Handle datasets and make plots in intuitive way with Python","summary":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for the weather, oceanography, air quality, and climate running from January 202","content":"The course has three components:\r\n- A science webinar on the story of ozone science and an introduction on the satellite instruments to measure the ozone in the atmosphere.\r\n- A guided data discovery with assignments.\r\n- A self-paced phase where everyone can handle the data and prepare an exercise with a recap session to gather additional questions and discuss the outcome of the practical phase.\r\n\r\nThe webinar will be recorded. \r\n\r\nA course page has been set up at https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=395 where you can find more information and resources. ","targetAudience":"We address a wide rage of audiences from students to professionals to enthusiasts of atmospheric sciences.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=395.\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\r\n\r\nA feedback session will take place on 23 February 2021, 14: