Focus Monthly Sessions - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"Interpretación de los Aspectos e Índices Climáticos discutidos durante las Sesiones Mensuales de Enfoque Regional de las RA-III/IV de la OMM","startDate":1613055600000,"endDate":1613061000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA/WPC International Desk","contactPerson":"Jose Galvez","contactEmail":"jose.galvez@noaa.gov","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8261906705779675661","description":"The session is for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean) and useful for others.  Session time is 15:00 UTC, it will start 15 minutes earlier (at 14:45 UTC for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection).   ","country":null,"learningOutcome":"To gain a better understanding of the Climate indices used during the monthly RA-III&IV Regional Focus Group Sessions. ","summary":null,"content":"Nuestro grupo de Enfoque Regional de las RA-III/IV de la OMM conduce sesiones virtuales mensuales, en las que se discute el estado actual del tiempo y clima usando productos satelitales y algunos aspectos e índices climáticos clave. Durante estas sesiones, el análisis de los índices climáticos es conciso, para destinar tiempo para abordar otros aspectos interesantes y para discusiones grupales. Esta sesión tiene como objetivo concentrarse en en la interpretación y aplicación de los diferentes aspectos e índices climáticos discutidos durante las sesiones mensuales. Nos concentraremos en el rol de las temperaturas de la superficie del mar y sus anomalías, El Niño-Oscilación del sur (ENSO), la oscilación de Madden-Julian (MJO) y otras perturbaciones tropicales ecuatoriales; y en patrones de circulación sobre las Américas. ","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8261906705779675661","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":9,"value":"Climate Services: Provision of Climate Services"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":2000,"created":1612571380000,"updated":1612627666000,"title":"Interpretation of the Climate Aspects and Indices discussed during the WMO RA-III/IV Regional Focus Monthly Sessions - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"Interpretation of the Climate Aspects and Indices discussed during the WMO RA-III/IV Regional Focus Monthly Sessions - 15:00 UTC","startDate":1612969200000,"endDate":1612974600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA/WPC International Desk","contactPerson":"Jose Galvez","contactEmail":"jose.galvez@noaa.gov","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/1982514435675436048","description":"The session is for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean) and useful for others.  Session time is 15:00 UTC, it will start 15 minutes earlier (at 14:45 UTC for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection).   ","country":null,"learningOutcome":"To gain a better understanding of the Climate indices used during the monthly RA-III&IV Regional Focus Group Sessions. ","summary":null,"content":"Our WMO RA-III/IV Regional Focus group conducts monthly virtual sessions in which the current state of the weather and climate are discussed using satellite imagery and a few key climate aspects and indices.  During these sessions, the analysis of the climate indices is concise, to allocate time for addressing other interesting aspects and for group discussions.  This session aims to have a closer look into the interpretation and application of the climate aspects and indices discussed during the monthly sessions.  We will focus on the role of sea surface temperatures and anomalies, El Niño-Southern Oscillation (ENSO), the Madden-Julian Oscillation (MJO) and other equatorial tropospheric waves, and atmospheric circulation patterns over the Americas.  A Spanish version of this presentation will be offered on February 11, 2021 at 15 UTC. ","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/1982514435675436048","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":9,"value":"Climate Services: Provision of Climate Services"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1990,"created":1610035552000,"updated":1610045482000,"title":"Mapping and Monitoring Lakes and Reservoirs with Satellite Observations","titleNative":"Mapping and Monitoring Lakes and Reservoirs with Satellite Observations","startDate":1612882800000,"endDate":1614119400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/mapping-and-monitoring-lakes-and-reservoirs-satellite-observations?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=Reservoir-21","description":"Natural lakes and man-made reservoirs are a part of Earths surface water. Freshwater lakes and reservoirs are used for drinking water, fishing, and recreational activities. Aside from the aesthetic and scenic value added by their presence, lakes support surrounding plant and aquatic ecosystems and wildlife. A variety of factors affect lakes and reservoirs, including climate variability and change, land use, and other watershed activities influencing surface runoff and groundwater. Therefore, monitoring the water quantity and quality of lakes and reservoirs is crucial for their sustainable management. This training focuses on introducing remote sensing observations for monitoring the water level of lakes; a critical surface water component affecting the residential, economical, and recreational sectors in the area. Recent observations of lake bathymetry based on remote sensing observations will also be presented.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \r\n\tTarget 6.4: By 2030, substantially increase water-use efficiency across all sectors and ensure sustainable withdrawals and supply of freshwater to address water scarcity and substantially reduce the number of people suffering from water scarcity \r\n\tTarget 6.6: By 2020, protect and restore water-related ecosystems, including mountains, forests, wetlands, rivers, aquifers and lakes \r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training attendees will learn to:\r\n\tIdentify the remote sensing data and methodology required to obtain water level and bathymetry of lakes\r\n\tAccess water height and bathymetry data for monitoring lake levels\r\n\tIllustrate the use of lake level and bathymetry data for lake and reservoir management\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Three, one and a half hour parts","targetAudience":"Federal, state, regional, and local public and private organizations involved in water resources and ecosystem management, dam and hydropower operations, and waterfront recreation and development planning","registrationHowto":"Register Here: https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/mapping-and-monitoring-lakes-and-reservoirs-satellite-observations?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=Reservoir-21\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1991,"created":1610365856000,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"EUMeTrain Snow Event Week","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Snow Event Week","startDate":1612789200000,"endDate":1613127600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"Marko Blaskovic, Yasmin Markl, Andreas Wirth","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr, yasmin.markl@zamg.ac.at, andreas.wirth@zamg.ac.at","contactUrl":"http://eumetrain.org/events/snow_ew_2021_agenda.pdf","description":"Within this week several presentations will take place online and cover many topics around snow and ice. We will have presentations about climate, case studies, modelling, snow in aviation, snow and radar, satellite facilities, winter sport aspects and many more.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"Within this week several presentations will take place online and cover many topics around snow and ice. We will have presentations about climate, case studies, modelling, snow in ","content":"Please see the agenda at: http://eumetrain.org/events/snow_ew_2021_agenda.pdf","targetAudience":"General meteorologists and other geoscientists interested in the usage of satellite and other products in their everyday work concerning snow.","registrationHowto":"In order to register for each session, please go to http://eumetrain.org/events/snow_ew_2021_agenda.pdf","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUME