or both images and voice through the Internet.  Images during the session are from SLIDER: http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu  More Information: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup.asp","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/5862412793298774799","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1989,"created":1609770310000,"updated":1609928952000,"title":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated Forecasting sYstem of DWD","titleNative":"SINFONY - The Seamless INtegrated Forecasting sYstem of DWD","startDate":1611651600000,"endDate":1611655200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Eumetcal","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.trainingscatalogus.nl/en/app#/catalog/course/8eccaf96-b387-4cbd-ba5f-cb9b221027b3","description":"Project SINFONY is an ongoing project at DWD for developing the new Seamless INtegrated FOrecastINg sYstemSINFONY  that yields very-short-range forecasts from 0-12 hours without inconsistencies. Presently, forecasts of up to 2 h are based upon nowcasting whereas longer forecasts are mainly done by NWP, both separately and independently. There is no seamless transition of structures in forecast fields over lead time from Nowcasting to NWP.\r\n\r\nTo narrow down this gap, SINFONY works on different aspects oft the problem with an integrated team: Improving the two forecast techniques by themselves (Nowcasting and NWP with its associated ensemble data assimilation) and, in postprocessing, develop optimally combined seamless forecast products for each lead time. The combined products shall also reduce the vast forecast information to a manageable level to be efficiently used in forecasting practice. The last point is especially important because SINFONY will be based on full NWP- and Nowcasting ensembles at all levels. In a first project stage the focus will be upon precipitation related quantities for summertime convection (thunderstorms and heavy precipitation) such as precipitation and radar reflectivity fields as well as convective cell objects.\r\n\r\nIn the first presentation the general concept of SINFONY will be discussed, as well as its specific methods of radar based Nowcasting products and first test results.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"To register for the webinar, please see instruction at: https://eumetcal.trainingscatalogus.nl/en/app#/catalog/course/8eccaf96-b387-4cbd-ba5f-cb9b221027b3","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1965,"created":1606489001000,"updated":1606916486000,"title":"Learn to use an R based toolbox to analyse climate time series - Basics - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"Learn to use an R based toolbox to analyse climate time series - Basics - Series of online short courses","startDate":1611144000000,"endDate":1611151200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Christine Träger-Chatterjee","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=394","description":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r\nIn this short course you will be introduced to the CM SAF R Toolbox and its functionalities. The CM SAF R Toolbox is a software based on R, specifically developed to analyse satellite based climate data records.\r\nThe CM SAF R Toolbox will be introduced. Information and support on how to install the CM SAF R Toolbox will be provided. Participants will be invited to play with the visualization and analysis functionalities provided in the software and to join also a feedback / Q&A session on Monday, 25 January 2021 at 12:00 -13:00 UTC.\r\nTo prepare yourself for the course, you are invited to install the CM SAF R Toolbox on you computer. Instructions on how to that are here: https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=394.\r\n\r\nThe live sessions will be recorded.\r\n","country":null,"learningOutcome":"After the course you should be able to\r\n- install the CM SAF R Toolbox on your local computer\r\n- to use the CM SAF R Toolbox for analysing time series of EO data records and visualize the results.","summary":"This course is part of the new edition of EUMETSAT series of online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from January 2021.\r\n\r","content":"","targetAudience":"Anybody interested in tools for analysing time series of Earth Observation data.\r\nNo specific prior knowledge required.","registrationHowto":"Register in advance for this webinar:\r\nhttps://eumetsat.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_zonBXvneThKnz0EQK8oAcQ.\r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the webinar.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1981,"created":1608219804000,"updated":1608224567000,"title":"Hyperspectral Data for Land and Coastal Systems","titleNative":"Hyperspectral Data for Land and Coastal Systems","startDate":1611072000000,"endDate":1612305000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/35CQrQF","description":"Hyperspectral data presents a unique opportunity to characterize specific vegetation types and biogeochemical processes across the land and oceans. Applications of hyperspectral data include plant species identification, invasive species management, assessment of phytoplankton functional types, mapping of wetlands and shallow benthic communities, and detection of harmful algal blooms (HABs). The ability of hyperspectral data to characterize chemical, physiological, and morphological traits allows decision-makers to better understand critical components of ecosystem dynamics such as invasive species encroachment, forest decline and pest infestation, and ocean dynamics. This training is also an opportunity to build capacity in a large user community prior to the launch of the highly anticipated global hyperspectral SBG mission.\r\n\r\nCourse Dates: January 19, 26 and February 2, 2021\r\n \r\nTimes and Registration Information:  \r\n  \r\nTimes: 11:00-12:30 & 16:00-17:30 EST (UTC-5); \r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \r\n\tGoal 14: Conserve and sustainably use the oceans, seas and marine resources for sustainable development\r\n\tTarget 14.2: By 2020, sustainably manage and protect marine and coastal ecosystems to avoid significant adverse impacts, including by strengthening their resilience, and take action for their restoration in order to achieve healthy and productive oceans\r\n\tGoal 15: Protect, restore and promote sustainable use of terrestrial ecosystems, sustainably manage forests, combat desertification, and halt and reverse land degradation and halt biodiversity loss\r\n\r\n\r\nRetweet Option: https://twitter.com/NASAARSET/status/1330947458675961858\r\n\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to:\r\n\r\nIdentify characteristics of hyperspectral data including benefits and limitations for land and coastal systems\r\n\r\nRecall various satellite and airborne-based hyperspectral imagers\r\n\r\nRelate past hyperspectral campaigns to future missions\r\n\r\nAccess hyperspectral data from multiple platforms\r\n\r\nIllustrate uses of hyperspectral data for land assessments such as invasive species management, agricultural management, wildfire impacts, forest decline and pest infestation, and more\r\n\r\nIllustrate uses of hyperspectral data for coastal and ocean applications such as coral reef assessments, mapping submerged aquatic vegetation, and identifying marine debris","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Three, one and a half hour parts","targetAudience":"Local, regional, state, federal, and non-governmental organizations involved in invasive species management, forest monitoring, coastal and ocean processes, and innovative remote sensing techniques.","registrationHowto":"There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\r\nhttps://go.nasa.gov/35CQrQF","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":26,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1938,"created":1598969895000,"updated":1601284788000,"title":"Synoptic and mesoscale system analyses","titleNative":"Synoptic and mesoscale system analyses","startDate":1610323200000,"endDate":1613952000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"DWD","contactPerson":"Eumetcal ","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"http://eumetrain.org/","description":"This online course will focus on improving forecaster skills by using the available satellite data in synoptic and mesoscale analysis. The course will contain seven live sessions together with asynchronous learning in between the live sessions. \r\nThe participants will learn to use the satellite imagery in combination with other meteorological data sources in order to interpret mid-latitude cyclones, fronts, frontal sub-structures, mesoscale features in cold air, summer convection, orographic features and shallow clouds.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learn