 climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\n\r\nDownload, plot and explore level 2 data and build a gridded dataset following robust methods using Jupyter Notebooks.\r\nThe activity is structured with a webinar, self-paced and wash-up session to follow on a date to be confirmed.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1974,"created":1607003645000,"updated":1607016861000,"title":"Future climate change: New results from the EC-Earth climate model","titleNative":"Future climate change: New results from the EC-Earth climate model","startDate":1607504400000,"endDate":1607508000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Eumetcal","contactEmail":"info@eumetcal.eu","contactUrl":"https://eumetcal.eu/en/app#/catalog/course/614a4371-85f2-42f1-96a4-cf447f35073b","description":"The newest version of the global climate model EC-Earth has been used to perform new future climate scenarios as part of the 6th Phase of the Coupled Model Intercomparison Project  CMIP6. CMIP6 is a project of the World Climate Research Programme and coordinates global climate model simulations worldwide in order to improve understanding of past, present and future climate change and variability in a multi-model framework.  The results from the CMIP-simulations are the base for the IPCC assessment reports on climate change.\r\n\r\nThis presentation will provide an overview over CMIP6, discuss the different emission scenarios that are used for the future climate simulations and show results from the climate simulations with EC-Earth. The focus will be on changes in temperature, precipitation, sea ice and ocean circulation, and on the importance of the emission scenario and of natural climate variability for the future changes. The EC-Earth results will further be compared to outcomes from other models participating at CMIP6 to show how the climate change signal depends on the choice of the model.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"To register for the webinar, please see instruction at: https://eumetcal.eu/en/app#/catalog/course/614a4371-85f2-42f1-96a4-cf447f35073b. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5854,"name":"Tomislav Marekovic","email":"marekovic@cirus.dhz.hr","agency":"","country":"HR","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1973,"created":1606970853000,"updated":1606987622000,"title":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting, December 2020","titleNative":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting, December 2020","startDate":1607479200000,"endDate":1607482800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"http://www.virtuallab.bom.gov.au/archive/regional-focus-group-recordings/","description":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group online meeting 02UTC 9th December 2020","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"2020/21 Tropical Cyclone pre-season update (facilitator Mr Joe Courtney BMTC)","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"http://www.virtuallab.bom.gov.au/events/regional-focus-group-instructions/","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":21,"value":"Not Applicable"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1956,"created":1605210255000,"updated":1606311273000,"title":"Introduction to NASA Black Marble Night Lights Data","titleNative":"Introduction to NASA Black Marble Night Lights Data","startDate":1607004000000,"endDate":1607011200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/30Rlmpv","description":"At night, satellite images of Earth capture a uniquely human signal - artificial lighting. Remotely-sensed lights at night provide a new data source for improving our understanding of interactions between human systems and the environment. NASA has developed the Black Marble, a daily calibrated, corrected, and validated product suite, so night light data can be used effectively for scientific observations. Black Marble is playing a vital role in research on light pollution, illegal fishing, fires, disaster impacts and recovery, and human settlements and associated energy infrastructures. The data (originally retrieved from the VIIRS day night band sensor) has been corrected by multiple novel algorithms, providing high-quality, cloud-free, atmospheric-, terrain-, vegetation-, snow-, lunar-, and stray light-corrected nighttime radiances.\r\n \r\nThis webinar will focus on building the skills needed to choose the appropriate night lights product, acquire and understand Black Marble data, and how to use the data in analyses for tracking urbanization, electrification, and disaster monitoring.\r\n \r\nThis work was partially supported by the GEO Human Planet Project #16-GEO16-0055.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: \r\nGoal 7: Ensure access to affordable, reliable, sustainable and modern energy for all\r\nGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable\r\nTarget 11.5: By 2030, significantly reduce the number of deaths and the number of people affected and substantially decrease the direct economic losses relative to global gross domestic product caused by disasters, including water-related disasters, with a focus on protecting the poor and people in vulnerable situations\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will: \r\n\r\nUnderstand the new capabilities of NASAs Black Marble product and which nighttime lights product to use for different science applications\r\n\r\nLearn the basics of how to acquire and interpret information in Black Marble data\r\n\r\nManipulate Black Marble data and create time-series analyses\r\n\r\nRecognize distortions that need to be corrected in Black Marble images\r\n\r\nBasic application of Black Marble data for topics relevant to the SDGs: tracking urbanization, disaster monitoring, and electrification\r\n","summary":null,"content":"One, two-hour session","targetAudience":"Local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in global Earth system science and applications to topics relevant to the SDGs: tracking urbanization, disaster monitoring, and electrification.","registrationHowto":"Times and Registration Information:  \r\n  \r\nEnglish Session: 09:00-11:00 EST (UTC-5): https://go.nasa.gov/30Rlmpv\r\nSpanish Session: 14:00-16:00 EST (UTC-5): https://go.nasa.gov/2SHwq4k\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1953,"created":1604451918000,"updated":1604484009000,"title":"RFG of the Americas and the Caribbean - 16:00 UTC","titleNative":"RFG of the Americas and the Caribbean - 16:00 UTC","startDate":1606320000000,"endDate":1606323600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Bernie Connell","contactEmail":"ber