https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":"ONLINE","attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1957,"created":1605747399000,"updated":1605803842000,"title":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","titleNative":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","startDate":1606093200000,"endDate":1606096800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Australan VLab Centre of Excellence","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"https://learn.bom.gov.au/mod/bigbluebuttonbn/view.php?id=13874 ","description":"The next Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting is scheduled for 01UTC, Monday 23rd November 2020\r\n\r\nNote that the start time for this session is one hour earlier than the normal 02UTC start time. \r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"Topic of discussion as follows:\r\nAn introduction to the NOAA Global LEO/GEO Flood Product (facilitator William Straka III Researcher, SSEC/CIMSS, NOAA/JPSS)\r\n\r\nWilliam Straka is a researcher with the Cooperative Institute for Meteorological Satellite Studies (CIMSS), where he has been working for over 15 years. Currently, he focuses on a number of topics, including algorithm integration, utilization of the Day Night Band on VIIRS as well as, for the last several years, interacting with forecasters at the National Weather Service, including at various River Forecast Center and the National Water Center. In addition, his interactions include emergency response stakeholders such as FEMA, CalFires as well as other US stakeholders as well as international stakeholders, such as agencies within the UN as well as emergency management agencies in other countries, regarding the utilization of the NOAA LEO/GEO Flood Product as other satellite products for disaster monitoring and response.\r\n","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"For this session we will be using the Big Blue Button web conferencing system on our training site.\r\nTo register please follow the instructions below:\r\n1.\tThe session homepage is at https://learn.bom.gov.au/mod/bigbluebuttonbn/view.php?id=13874 \r\n2.\tYou can join the session either as a guest or as a registered user. We would prefer you to join as a registered user. There is no cost associated with this. \r\nA.\tFor guest users the session password is VLab@2020\r\nB.\tFor users who choose to join the session as a registered user for the first time, please use the link https://learn.bom.gov.au/login/signup.php to create an account. Please include your details including Country of Origin. After signing up you will receive an automated email with a link to confirm your registration within about 15 minutes. If you have not received the confirmation email within this time, check your spam/junk inbox. If there is no confirmation within your spam/junk inbox, contact moodle@bom.gov.au giving their name and email address, stating they had not received their site registration confirmation email for our training site.\r\nC.\tFor users who have already registered, please click \"Continue\" on the Self enrolment (Student) option. Log in using the above Username and Password. If you have forgotten the password then you can use the 'forgot password' function: https://learn.bom.gov.au/login/forgot_password.php\r\nD.\tAustralian Bureau of Meteorology staff please use the 'Bureau staff log in' button to log in to the site. \r\n\r\nPlease use either the Google Chrome or Modzilla Firefox web browsers when you join the session.\r\n\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1933,"created":1598428134000,"updated":1605537181000,"title":"WMO-EUMETSAT-FAO-MeteoRomania  Virtual training course on the use of satellite products for drought monitoring and agricultural meteorology applications ","titleNative":"WMO-EUMETSAT-FAO-MeteoRomania  Virtual training course on the use of satellite products for drought monitoring and agricultural meteorology applications ","startDate":1606089600000,"endDate":1607731200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"National Meteorological Administration of Romania (NMAR)","contactPerson":"José Camacho","contactEmail":"jcamacho@wmo.int","contactUrl":"https://public.wmo.int/en/events/workshops/joint-eumetsat-fao-wmo-virtual-training-course-use-of-satellite-products-drought","description":"With a focus on resources optimization in Central and Eastern Europe, EUMETSAT joins efforts with WMO and FAO and welcomes the organisational guidance of the  Romanian Meteorological Agency (Meteo-Romania), plus other Agencies contributing with trainers to organise a virtual training course on the use of satellite products for drought monitoring and agrometeorological applications in 6 thematic sessions in November-December 2020, coordinated from Bucharest, Romania.  \r\n\r\nThe main objective of this activity is the provision of convenient weather and climate information for the benefit of food producers and agriculture managers in Central and Eastern Europe and support WMO, FAO and DMCSEE on-going projects. The training is focused on capacity development for National Meteorological Services  and Ministries of Agriculture to improve data and product quality and service delivery in drought monitoring and management in a wide range of agricultural sectors.  That information must be coupled with other tools such as seasonal forecasts, crop models and geographical information systems. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":" Expand the use of Land-SAF and Hydrology SAF products and other related products among European agrometeorologists and water managers to enhance the benefits derived and to collect and exchange experience from that use; \r\n Development of capacity building at the NMHS and Ministries of Agriculture in Central and Eastern Europe in relation with vegetation status monitoring, soil moisture, rainfall estimations, forest fire risk estimations, radiative balance and land use;\r\n Institutional cooperation reinforcement between EUMETSAT, WMO, FAO and the National Institutions of the region in terms of satellite product utilization and reception stations optimization for drought management and agriculture production; \r\n Development of the cooperation between the Drought Management Centre for South Eastern Europe and other WMO and FAO partners at the Region.\r\n Build understanding of regional gaps, needs and priorities for future cooperation between relevant institutions and partners.\r\n","summary":"With a focus on resources optimization in Central and Eastern Europe, EUMETSAT joins efforts with WMO and FAO and welcomes the organisational guidance of the  Romanian Meteorologic","content":"Virtual training would be supported by the WMO Moodle Platform where contents, tests and supporting documents would be found. The course would sctrutured around six modules:  EUMETSAT data and products, LandSAF, FAO-JRC products, H-SAF and Central-Eastern Europe developments.","targetAudience":"This course is devoted in non-exclusive basis to experts in agrometeorology in the NMHS and Ministries of Agriculture of DMCSEE countries plus Belarus, Ukraine, Georgia and Armenia.  ","registrationHowto":"Participation is via invitation only. Invitations would be provided for 4 participants per country (2 Met. Service, 2 Agricultural ministries).","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":24,"name":"Jose Prieto","email":"Jose.Prieto@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":100,"value":"WMO","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1942,"created":1599832582000,"updated":1600070176000,"title":"ESSL course: Optimal use of satellite data in forecasting severe convection","titleNative":"ESSL course: Optimal use of satellite data in forecasting severe convection","startDate":1605520800000,"endDate":1605808800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"ONLINE","host":"ESSL","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"events@essl.org ","contactUrl":"https://www.essl.org/cms/upcoming-events/course-optimal-use-of-satellite-data-in-forecasting-severe-convection/","description":"Have you been wondering about how to use satellite data to detect the convective initiation and how does the satellite appearance of storms relate to their physics? Would you like to learn more about how to best incorporate satellite data in your convective storm forecasting process? ","country":null,"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"This course will concentrate on how to effectively use satellite data in nowcasting severe convection and will provide both the theoretical background on the basic dynamics of severe convective storms, as well as a satellite perspective on each discussed topic. The course will include a variety of practical exercises. ","targetAudience":"Meteorological forecasters, researchers in the field of severe convective storm nowcasting","registrationHowto":"Register at: https://www.essl.org/cms/upcoming-events/event-registration/","registrationEndDate":1605225600000,"fees":"Yes","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":20,"value":"Other (see description)"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1946,"created":1601025506000,"updated":1601376191000,"title":"Second ESA/EUMETSAT/ECMWF Joint Online Training Course on Atmospheric Composition","titleNative":"Second ESA/EUMETSAT/ECMWF Joint Online Training Course on Atmospheric Composition","startDate":1605515400000,"endDate":1605886200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Federico Fierli ","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158","description":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), and the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecast (ECMWF) with the Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) are organising a second joint training course on Atmospheric Composition with a focus on air quality and data interoperability.\r\n\r\nThe school will be fully on-line with lectures, debates and practical sessions. We aim at fully involving participants in an interactive way.\r\n\r\nThe specific goals of this training course are:\r\n\r\n- Present the state-of-the-art in air quality monitoring and modelling.\r\n- Provide an overview of the different observations, tools and applications.\r\n- Enhance the capacity on data access and analysis of existing and new satellite data products and monitoring services.\r\n- Foster participants driven personal and team projects.\r\n\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"The European Space Agency (ESA), the European Organisation for the Exploitation of Meteorological Satellites (EUMETSAT), and the European Center for Medium-Range Weather Forecast (","content":"Course themes:\r\n- air quality observations from satellites and in-situ platforms;\r\n- atmospheric modelling;\r\n- data assimilation;\r\n- comparison and combined use of satellite data;\r\n- software and programming targeted on air quality applications.\r\n\r\nMore information about the second joint training course can be found at https://atmostraining.info/. ","targetAudience":"Attendance is limited to 30 participants to ensure a fully interactive course.\r\n\r\nEarly career scientists, service providers and application developers in the area of atmospheric pollution data analysis from member states of the EU and the hosting agencies including associated countries. Applications from all other countries are welcome, while acceptance is subject to space availability.","registrationHowto":"If you already have an account on the EUMETSAT training platform, please go to 'Apply for courses' (https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158), scroll the list of courses and submit your application form.\r\n\r\nOtherwise, please make sure you create an account: https://training.eumetsat.int/login/index.php. \r\nOnce the account has been created, please log in, then access the 'Apply for Courses' section and submit your application form. If you have any problem, please contact the Training Team (training@eumetsat.int).","registrationEndDate":1603152000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1951,"created":1603179260000,"updated":1607007531000,"title":"WEkEO Online Training Workshop - Focus on Climate Data Products","titleNative":"WEkEO Online Training Workshop - Focus on Climate Data Products","startDate":1605173400000,"endDate":1606993200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"WEkEO","contactPerson":" training@wekeo.eu","contactEmail":" training@wekeo.eu.","contactUrl":"https://www.wekeo.eu/web/guest/news/-/blogs/wekeo-online-training-workshop-focus-on-climate-data-products","description":"The online WEkEO Training sessions have been designed to train existing as well as new WEkEO users. The audience will learn about the use of the original Copernicus & Satellite data through the WEkEO cloud computing platform and their possible applications. Gaining knowledge during the workshop will enable the audience to interact and share its experience and express needs and requirements for new products and tools to be included in the WEkEO portfolio in future.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The workshop aims to bring together experts and users of Earth Observation products. It will consist of a mixture of plenary expert talks, round table discussions and hands-on practical exercises to explore the WEkEO platform. ","summary":null,"content":"The WEkEO training workshop focused on climate data products will be conducted online comprising 3 rounds with an interval of 3 weeks in between for practical homework (Round 2). At the end of the webinar session, participants will access specific online materials like the recording of the webinars, practical sessions (Jupyter Notebooks) created specifically for the workshop and associated tutorial videos. Dedicated experts in Earth Observation and WEkEO User Support specialists will also be at the disposal of the participants to facilitate the exchanges, ask questions and share the best practices. During this period, the participants will have the opportunity to practice themselves with the material provided. During the online debriefing session (Round 3), experts and trainers will review the questions asked during the practical session and participants will also have the possibility to ask live questions.","targetAudience":"The target audience is mainly beginners and new users.","registrationHowto":"https://copernicusmarineservice.clickmeeting.com/wekeo-online-training-focus-on-climate-data-products/register ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":103,"value":"Workshop"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1927,"created":1597735773000,"updated":1597838549000,"title":"The monthly weather briefing of EUMeTrain with EUMeTrain trainer(s), NMHS forecasters - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"The monthly weather briefing of EUMeTrain with EUMeTrain trainer(s), NMHS forecasters - Series of online short courses","startDate":1605096000000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Vesa Nietosvaara","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=97 ","description":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\n\r\nOnce a month EUMeTrain organizes a Weather Briefing open to everyone to present and discuss the present/recent weather situation/events. Discussions mostly rely on actual satellite imagery. Basics of satellite meteorology are often covered with these discussions.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1950,"created":1602782301000,"updated":1602840910000,"title":"Satellite Remote Sensing for Urban Heat Islands","titleNative":"Satellite Remote Sensing for Urban Heat Islands","startDate":1605020400000,"endDate":1606249800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/34RZgEK","description":"The rapid growth of urban populations, the urban heat island (UHI) effect, and a potential increase in the frequency and duration of heat waves due to climate change, raise a series of issues about the increased health risks of sensitive urban populations to extreme heat and the effective means of mitigating impacts of heat waves. According to the US EPA, urban heat islands affect energy consumption, elevate greenhouse gas emissions, and impair water quality by increasing the temperature of urban water runoff. This will be ARSET's first training on UHI and will be in collaboration with the National Integrated Heat Health Information System (NIHHIS) and the Global Heat Health Information Network (GHHIN).\r\n\r\n\r\nThis training will address the use of remote sensing in determining where \"hot spots\" of land surface temperature are located in urban areas, why these areas are experiencing increased temperature, which populations are most vulnerable, and ways to mitigate the effects through adaptive land use planning.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: \r\nGoal 11: Make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient and sustainable  \r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, participants will be able to:\r\n - Define what an urban heat island (UHI) is and why it matters to urban planners and public health experts\r\n - Identify which satellites and sensors can be used for assessing UHI\r\n - Give examples of populations that are especially susceptible to heat stress\r\n - Summarize the limitations of satellite data for understanding UHI\r\n - Recognize new methods that incorporate conventional satellite remote sensing data and in situ observations of temperature and humidity from community science and urban field campaigns\r\n - List what landscape features help to explain variations in urban heat islands\r\n - Compute land surface temperature from Landsat 4, 5, 7, and 8 within Google Earth Engine\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Three one and a half-hour parts including presentations and question and answer sessions","targetAudience":"Community, municipal, city, state, federal, and private institutions involved in urban planning, health care, energy supply and demand management, and climate mitigation.","registrationHowto":"Register Here: https://go.nasa.gov/34RZgEK","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1952,"created":1603882509000,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","startDate":1605013200000,"endDate":1605016800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"TSO EUMeTrain","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations and features. Every month the weather briefing is hosted by a different European country.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Gaining knowledge about analyzing weather situations using satellite data.\r\nMaintaining a healthy basis of knowledge about satellite meteorology.\r\nUnderstanding the difference between RGBs as well as their benefits and limitations.\r\n","summary":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imag","content":"Weather briefings are recorded. Find a collection of past briefings at http://eumetrain.org/briefings.html and on YouTube at https://www.youtube.com/user/eumetrain/videos.","targetAudience":"The primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, although other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome.","registrationHowto":"In order to join the discussion, please go to http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html. For any questions, please use the Contact email.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1944,"created":1600786306000,"updated":1600786625000,"title":"Remote Sensing for Mangroves in Support of the UN Sustainable Development Goals","titleNative":"Remote Sensing for Mangroves in Support of the UN Sustainable Development Goals","startDate":1604584800000,"endDate":1605821400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/remote-sensing-mangroves-support-un-sustainable-development-goals?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSTAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=Mangroves-20","description":"This 3-part series (November 5, 12, 19) focuses on mapping and monitoring mangroves and how it relates to UN sustainable development indicator 6.6.1: Change in the extent of water-related ecosystems over time. Indicator 6.6.1 is used in determining progress toward meeting Sustainable Development Goal 6, which is to Ensure availability and sustainable management of water and sanitation for all.\r\n\r\nUnderstanding mangrove ecosystems and mapping their extent is critical to meeting this goal. Mangroves are critical ecosystems, provide coastal protection from storm surges, maintain our climate, control floods, and stabilize coastlines. Additionally, they serve as nurseries for a number of marine wildlife species. Mangroves are also integral to the blue carbon family. Blue carbon is carbon stored, sequestered, or released from coastal vegetation ecosystems (Heer et al. 2012). Therefore, understanding mangrove extent and biomass is essential to managing the sustainability of our water ecosystems. Attendees will be exposed to the latest tools for mapping mangrove extent in Google Earth Engine and how these observations can be used to report towards SDG quotas.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: \r\n\tTarget 6.6: By 2020, protect and restore water-related ecosystems, including mountains, forests, wetlands, rivers, aquifers and lakes\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, participants will:\r\n\r\nUnderstand Sustainable Development Goals with a focus on understanding SDG 6.6.1\r\n\r\nUnderstand the importance of mangrove ecosystems and the need for mapping them using satellite technology\r\n\r\nHave knowledge of spatial data that is available for studying mangrove ecosystems\r\n\r\nUse Google Earth Engine to:\r\n&#61607;\tMap country-specific mangrove extent (Case Study: Guyana)\r\n&#61607;\tPerform a time series analysis of mangrove ecosystems\r\n&#61607;\tCalculate mangrove extent in hectares\r\n&#61607;\tBuild an app to display data using results from Guyana\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Three, one-and a half hour sessions\r\n\r\nCourse Dates: November 5, 12, 19\r\n\r\nTimes: 10:00-11:30 & 15:00-16:30 EST (UTC-5); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\r\n","targetAudience":"National policymakers involved in sustainable development commitments to mangrove and water-related ecosystem conservation and the UNs Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).","registrationHowto":"Please register here for either daily sessions: https://go.nasa.gov/32Dp6fH\r\n\r\nThere will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one daily session.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1925,"created":1597668030000,"updated":1599577148000,"title":"A Climate Data Record of \"sunshine\", SARAH - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"A Climate Data Record of \"sunshine\", SARAH - Series of online short courses","startDate":1603886400000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Christine Träger-Chatterjee","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=97 ","description":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\n\r\nDetails on the CM SAF SARAH climate data record (available since 1983), focusing on sunshine duration and surface solar radiation, incl. current applications and future developments. In an interactive session you will be able to explore the SARAH data record using the CMSAF R Toolbox and discuss the results.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1947,"created":1601026965000,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","startDate":1603803600000,"endDate":1603807200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"TSO EUMeTrain","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","description":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations and features. Every month the weather briefing is hosted by a different European country.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Gaining knowledge about analyzing weather situations using satellite data.\r\nMaintaining a healthy basis of knowledge about satellite meteorology.\r\nUnderstanding the difference between RGBs as well as their benefits and limitations.\r\n","summary":"Hosted by EUMeTrain, weather briefings are monthly online weather discussions about the phenomena that occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imag","content":"Weather briefings are recorded. Find a collection of past briefings at http://eumetrain.org/briefings.html and on YouTube at https://www.youtube.com/user/eumetrain/videos.","targetAudience":"The primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, although other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome.","registrationHowto":"In order to join the discussion, please go to http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html. For any questions, please use the Contact email.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1853,"created":1578409270000,"updated":1581597288000,"title":"Working with ocean colour data from Sentinel-3","titleNative":"Working with ocean colour data from Sentinel-3","startDate":1603530000000,"endDate":1603645200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Norfolk","host":"Ocean Optics Conference ","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"Hayley.Evers-King@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"This course will share the latest developments around Copernicus Sentinel-3 ocean colour data and tools available from EUMETSAT.","country":{"id":"US","name":"UNITED STATES","region":"RA-IV","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"- Understand the current status and details about OLCI data from the Copernicus Sentinel-3 mission.\r\n- Know where and how to access this data.\r\n- Work with various tools for using this data, provided by EUMETSAT.","summary":null,"content":"Participants will hear about current status and planned developments around Copernicus Sentinel-3 ocean colour data from EUMETSAT, learn how to access and work with the data, and explore a variety of tools including open source Python code to work with the data. Participants are encouraged to come with their own work flows and will receive support from trainers.","targetAudience":"New and experienced ocean colour data users who wish to work with Copernicus Sentinel-3 data for marine applications.","registrationHowto":"Via conference website (pending). Funding support will be available for European participants who are presenting OLCI related work at the conference.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1943,"created":1600783717000,"updated":1600783835000,"title":"MODIS to VIIRS Transition for Air Quality Applications","titleNative":"MODIS to VIIRS Transition for Air Quality Applications","startDate":1603371600000,"endDate":1603402200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://appliedsciences.nasa.gov/join-mission/training/english/modis-viirs-transition-air-quality-applications?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSTAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=MODIS-2-VIIRS","description":"With the end of the MODIS data record approaching, it is important that current MODIS users transition to VIIRS data and visualization tools. As they make this transition, users also need information regarding which MODIS geophysical parameters will be available with VIIRS and vice-versa, and the differences between them. This training will teach users how to access VIIRS data products, the differences involved in using VIIRS as opposed to MODIS, and how to apply VIIRS aerosol optical depth observations for air quality applications.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: \r\n\tTarget 3.9: By 2030, substantially reduce the number of deaths and illnesses from hazardous chemicals and air, water and soil pollution and contamination\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, participants will:\r\n\r\nAccess NASA VIIRS aerosol products through Earthdata\r\n\r\nDescribe the differences between the MODIS and VIIRS instruments and aerosol optical depth (AOD) products\r\n\r\nUnderstand how VIIRS aerosol optical depth observations can be used for modeling and monitoring of air pollution transport\r\n\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: One, 1.5 hour part\r\n\r\nTimes: 09:00-10:30 & 16:00-17:30 EDT (UTC-4); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day. Participants need only to register and attend one session.\r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"Audience: This webinar is designed for MODIS end-users from all around the world, both applied and those involved in research.\r\n\r\n\r\n","registrationHowto":"Please register for either daily session here: https://go.nasa.gov/3lBXWNE","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1949,"created":1602731799000,"updated":1602752577000,"title":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","titleNative":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","startDate":1603159200000,"endDate":1603162800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"https://learn.bom.gov.au/mod/bigbluebuttonbn/view.php?id=13874 ","description":"The Australian Regional Focus Group meeting takes place once a month and is coordinated by Mr. Bodo Zeschke (BMTC), from the VLab Centre of Excellence in Australia. All interested parties are welcome to attend.\r\nTo register please follow the instructions below:\r\n    The session homepage is at https://learn.bom.gov.au/mod/bigbluebuttonbn/view.php?id=13874\r\n    You can join the session either as a guest or as a registered user. We would prefer you to join as a registered user. There is no cost associated with this.\r\n    For guest users the session password is VLab@2020","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"Topics of discussion include:\r\n\r\n    Seven years of Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meetings (facilitator Mr Bodo Zeschke, Bureau of Meteorology Training Centre)\r\n    Overview of the RAMMB/CIRA SLIDER website (facilitator Dr Curtis Seaman, Cooperative Institute for Research in the Atmosphere, Colorado State University)\r\n","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"To register please follow the instructions below:\r\n    The session homepage is at https://learn.bom.gov.au/mod/bigbluebuttonbn/view.php?id=13874\r\n    You can join the session either as a guest or as a registered user. We would prefer you to join as a registered user. There is no cost associated with this.\r\n\r\n    For guest users the session password is VLab@2020\r\n    For users who choose to join the session as a registered user for the first time, please use the link https://learn.bom.gov.au/login/signup.php to create an account. Please include your details including Country of Origin. After signing up you will receive an automated email with a link to confirm your registration within about 15 minutes. If you have not received the confirmation email within this time, check your spam/junk inbox. If there is no confirmation within your spam/junk inbox, contact moodle@bom.gov.au giving their name and email address, stating they had not received their site registration confirmation email for our training site.\r\n    For users who have already registered, please click \"Continue\" on the Self enrolment (Student) option. Log in using the above Username and Password. If you have forgotten the password then you can use the 'forgot password' function: https://learn.bom.gov.au/login/forgot_password.php\r\n    Australian Bureau of Meteorology staff please use the 'Bureau staff log in' button to log in to the site.\r\n\r\nPlease use either the Google Chrome or Modzilla Firefox web browsers when you join the session.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1940,"created":1599261595000,"updated":1599331466000,"title":"WMO RA-IV Virtual Training on Satellite Applications","titleNative":"Entrenamiento Virtual en Aplicaciones de Satélite para la RA-IV de la OMM","startDate":1602687600000,"endDate":1604012400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"University of Costa Rica","contactPerson":"Marcial Garbanzo","contactEmail":"marcial.garbanzo@ucr.ac.cr","contactUrl":"http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/CR_taller_oct2020.asp","description":"The University of Costa Rica (UCR) in San Jose, Costa Rica is hosting a virtual satellite workshop in Spanish for participants from the Latin America and Caribbean region in October 2020. The training will be on Wednesdays and Thursdays for three consecutive weeks, October 14-15, 21-22, and 28-29, 2020. This is a Spanish language only event with no simultaneous interpretation available. \r\nLa Universidad de Costa Rica (UCR), localizada en San José, Costa Rica, está organizando un taller virtual de entrenamiento en Español para participantes de Latino América y El Caribe en Octubre del 2020. El taller tendrá lugar los Miércoles y Jueves durante tres semanas consecutivas que son los días: 14 y 15, 21 y 22, 28 y 29 de Octubre del 2020. El taller será conducido solamente en español, sin interpretación simultánea disponible.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the workshop, participants will have a general working knowledge of the GOES-R Series and JPSS\r\nkey instruments as well as develop competency in working with the data and products for weather\r\nforecasting, prediction, monitoring or research through hands-on exercises and case studies.\r\nAl finalizar el taller, los participantes habrán adquirido conocimientos acerca de los instrumentos principales de GOES-R y JPSS; y habrán desarrollado habilidades para trabajar con datos y productos aplicados a pronóstico del tiempo, predicción, monitoreo o investigación a través de ejercicios prácticos y casos de estudio.","summary":null,"content":"The workshop will cover both GOES-R and JPSS satellite capabilities and data access to support the World Meteorological Organizations (WMO) Region IV forecast challenges.\r\nEl taller cubrirá las capacidades de los satélites GOES-R y JPSS, así como el acceso a datos en apoyo a retos en los pronósticos de la Asociación Regional IV (RA-IV) de la Organización Mundial de Meteorología (OMM).","targetAudience":"Forecasters and Students","registrationHowto":"Information: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/CR_taller_oct2020.asp\r\nRegistration: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1gYmx7gEzba6yJpx_DIStuJvo8Ca7giSwHKrjsNzpbeY/edit\r\n","registrationEndDate":1600819140000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true},{"id":100,"value":"WMO","visible":true},{"id":190,"value":"RTC","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":1,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Forecaster"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1922,"created":1597397251000,"updated":1602845343000,"title":"Summer(s) of fires: the 2019 wildfires in Australia  - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"Summer(s) of fires: the 2019 wildfires in Australia  - Series of online short courses","startDate":1602676800000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Federico Fierli ","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=97 ","description":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\nDownload, plot and explore new fire products and aerosol data to characterise the fire plumes evolution and position during the 2019 wildfire season using Jupyter Notebooks. The activity is structured with a webinar, self-paced and wash-up session to follow on 19 October, 12:00 UTC.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1941,"created":1599635007000,"updated":1599638649000,"title":"EUMETSAT Webinar on User Preparation for Next-Generation Hyperspectral IR Sounders (IRS, IASI-NG)","titleNative":"EUMETSAT Webinar on User Preparation for Next-Generation Hyperspectral IR Sounders (IRS, IASI-NG)","startDate":1602590400000,"endDate":1602684000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Stephan Bojinski","contactEmail":"Stephan.Bojinski@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"In the context of user preparation for the next-generation of hyperspectral infrared sounding data from the Meteosat Third Generation and EPS Second Generation programmes, EUMETSAT is organising a User Preparation Webinar on 13-14 October 2020 (2h on each day, 14.00-16.00 CEST). \r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"With the Webinar, EUMETSAT intends to \r\n- Raise technical awareness.\r\n- Trigger developments in processing, visualisation and analysis software for exploiting the L1/L2 products, and \r\n- Stimulate early development of applications. \r\n","summary":"In the context of user preparation for the next-generation of hyperspectral infrared sounding data from the Meteosat Third Generation and EPS Second Generation programmes, EUMETSAT","content":"The Webinar mainly provides:\r\n- Instrument overviews and measurement principles of the InfraRed Sounder (IRS) and the Infrared Atmospheric Sounder Interferometer Next Generation (IASI-NG).\r\n- A description of satellite-based data (Level-1) and products (Level-2), variables, and how to use them.\r\n- Application examples of the products in meteorology and atmospheric composition.\r\n\r\nData from the geostationary IRS and the polar-orbiting IASI-NG instrument are expected to become available in the 2023-2024 timeframe.\r\n\r\nThe Webinar will be recorded for later re-use by the community.\r\nQ&A session on www.slido.com event code #NG-HSIR.\r\n","targetAudience":"The Webinar is intended for an audience with a good level of scientific and technical understanding of satellite remote sensing, but not with detailed knowledge about hyperspectral sounding, Principal Components, the expected IASI-NG and IRS L1 and L2 products, algorithms, and data formats. \r\n \r\nThe audience are developers and experts in MS-NMHS, in NWP centres, and manufacturers of SW/HW related to satellite data processing and visualisation. \r\n","registrationHowto":"Please register and join the Webinars using zoom here: \r\n\r\n- Instrument overview, measurements, level-1 data and products\r\n13 October 2020, 14.00 CEST (12.00 UTC):\r\nhttps://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJEuf-yurz8rEtdeROOOJsmw-gV8QgXHiCHE \r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the meeting.\r\n\r\n- Geophysical level-2 products and applications\r\n14 October 2020, 14.00 CEST (12.00 UTC): \r\nhttps://eumetsat.zoom.us/meeting/register/tJMlf-qspjwuGtN14CtSgAXpCSG2gaW_80Iz \r\nAfter registering, you will receive a confirmation email containing information about joining the meeting.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5840,"name":"Rosa Ullucci","email":"rosa.ullucci@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1948,"created":1601654837000,"updated":1601662127000,"title":"Introduction to the GLM  Geostationary Lightning Mapper of the satellites GOES-16/17 and applications","titleNative":"Introdução ao Mapeador de Raios (GLM  Geostationary Lightning Mapper) dos satélites GOES-16/17 e suas aplicações","startDate":1602273600000,"endDate":1602277200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"INPE","contactPerson":"Natalia Rudorff","contactEmail":"vlab.cptec@inpe.br","contactUrl":"https://www.gotomeet.me/cptec/vlab","description":"This webinar will present the physical basis of cloud electrification and lightning formation, showing the need for total lightning information in real time and how the GLM Ray Mapper of GOES-16/17 satellites meets these needs. The principles of lightning detection in soil and space will also be addressed, as well as the detection methods and definitions of the variables observed by the GLM. Some products derived from GLM observations and some of the many application areas are shown, such as the immediate forecast of convection and severe weather, warnings of imminent risks of cloud-to-ground discharges, aviation, atmospheric chemistry studies, quantitative estimation of precipitation, tropical cyclones, forest fires, numerical forecast of weather and climate and climate and global studies.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Knowledge on basic concepts and applications for the GLM GOES-16/17.","summary":null,"content":"-Physical basis of cloud electrification and lightning formation, showing the need for total lightning information in real time and how the GLM Ray Mapper of GOES-16/17 satellites meets these needs. \r\n- The principles of lightning detection in soil and space wand the detection methods and definitions of the variables observed by the GLM. \r\n-Some products derived from GLM observations and some of the many application areas are shown, such as the immediate forecast of convection and severe weather, warnings of imminent risks of cloud-to-ground discharges, aviation, atmospheric chemistry studies, quantitative estimation of precipitation, tropical cyclones, forest fires, numerical forecast of weather and climate and climate and global studies\r\n","targetAudience":"Meteorologists of national and regional centers. ","registrationHowto":"Join the meeting at https://www.gotomeet.me/cptec/vlab\r\nNo advance registration required.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2842,"name":"Natalia Rudorff","email":"natalia.rudorff@inpe.br","agency":"INPE","country":"BR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":23,"value":"INPE","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":5,"value":"Portuguese","iso639":"pt"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1926,"created":1597735258000,"updated":1597838570000,"title":"Satellite skills training online: a short introduction- Series of online short courses","titleNative":"Satellite skills training online: a short introduction- Series of online short courses","startDate":1601989200000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Mark Higgins","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=97 ","description":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\n\r\nA framework for teaching skills (Merril, M. D (2002) for teaching satellite skills online. You will consider what activities may best suit your learning objectives drawing on examples from EUMETSAT training. The short course will consist of a webinar followed by a guided design process for those who have active courses to design. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on 