":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The lessons are tailored to enhance following skills for operational forecasters:\r\n1. Identifying different types of cyclones - select the appropriate satellite products for identification of the environments\r\n2. Forecasting cyclone development, life-cycle, track and related weather, incorporating appropriate NWP products into  forecasting chain\r\n3. Choose the right satellite and radar products to identify cyclone-related features\r\n4. Assess the impact of the cyclone activity\r\n5. Warn on the threats related to cyclones and communicate the forecast and warning to the public\r\n\r\n","summary":"The training course is the Advanced South Eastern Europe Meteorological (SEEMET) training course, which will be organised with the EUMETSAT, EUMeTrain and EUMETCAL support. The cou","content":"A three week online meteorological training course for South Eastern European countries, covering topic of mid-latitude cyclones with a special emphasis on satellite image interpretation. ","targetAudience":"The target audiences for the course are meteorological forecasters from the SE European countries: Slovenia, Hungary, Croatia, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Serbia, Republic of North Macedonia, Bulgaria, Moldavia, Romania, Kosovo (UNSCR 1244/1999), Greece and Albania. \r\n\r\nSince it is an advanced course, it is designed for more experienced forecasters.","registrationHowto":"https://training.eumetsat.int/mod/questionnaire/view.php?id=12877","registrationEndDate":1601769540000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5844,"name":"Natasa Strelec Mahovic","email":"natasa.strelecmahovic@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false},{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1849,"created":1578322157000,"updated":1594198814000,"title":"CMDS GMES&Africa Copernicus Marine Data Stream Training Course for Ocean Applications","titleNative":"CMDS GMES&Africa Copernicus Marine Data Stream Training Course for Ocean Applications","startDate":1601798400000,"endDate":1605286800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Accra","host":"Regional Marine Centre, GMES-Africa, University of Ghana","contactPerson":"Kwame Adu Agyekum","contactEmail":"kaagyekum@gmail.com","contactUrl":"","description":"This course is organised by GMES-Africa with support from EUMETSAT. This is a blended course made up of two parts - a self-taught online section and a classroom phase (likely to be held online due to COVID-19)","country":{"id":"GH","name":"GHANA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn:\r\n- To access / download data and products provided in the Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CODA, EUMETSAT Data archive, EUMETCast).\r\n- What data and products the Copernicus Marine Data Stream provides (variables, timeliness, resolution, data format, etc.).\r\n- To work with Copernicus Marine Data in SNAP and / or scripting languages, such as Python.\r\n- To use data / products from the CMDS for their purposes.","summary":null,"content":"Participants will learn the underlying principles of ocean remote sensing, how to access relevant data, and how to work with it using various open source tools. Each participant will be asked to propose a mini project that will be attempted with the support of trainers, allowing them to gain skills directly applicable to their work needs.","targetAudience":"The workshop is aimed at, but not restricted to, early career scientists: Masters / PhD students, Post-Docs, and/or experienced scientists from any relevant sector (industry, government, environment, research) who have clear motivations for wanting to work with satellite-based ocean observation data. Participants should have introductory experience using SNAP and/or a scripting language such as Python (or similar), but this is not a prerequisite.","registrationHowto":"TBC once applications have opened","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":3925,"name":"Kim Hockley","email":"khock@pml.ac.uk","agency":"EUM","country":"GB","programme":"PML","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1924,"created":1597667909000,"updated":1597838577000,"title":"A light on heat: what radiation tells about soil, air and fire - Series of online short courses","titleNative":"A light on heat: what radiation tells about soil, air and fire - Series of online short courses","startDate":1601467200000,"endDate":null,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Jose' Prieto","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=97 ","description":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the end of the year.\r\n\r\nA formula-free approach to remote sensing based on images from GOES and Meteosat satellites. How to twist radiance readings at the satellite into air temperatures and soil characteristics. Guided exercises on viewers will try to make you familiar with satellite data.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"The participants will have the opportunity to learn:\r\n- which are the EUMETSAT and Copernicus free and open data;\r\n- where to access the data and where to find information about the data;\r\n- how to handle the data using the tools proposed.","summary":"This short online course is part of a new series of open, online short courses on data discovery for weather, oceanography, air quality and climate running from September till the ","content":"","targetAudience":"The short courses are open and address a wide range of attendees, from service providers to young (and less young) scientists and forecasters.","registrationHowto":"Fill in a quick form at this link https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 to let us know which courses are of interest to you. Please note that in order to apply you first need to register on the platform if you do not already have an account.\r\nWe will contact you by email to share all access information a few days before courses open. \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{