occurred over the past month, since the last weather briefing. Satellite imag","content":"Weather briefings are recorded. Find a collection of past briefings at http://eumetrain.org/briefings.html and on YouTube at https://www.youtube.com/user/eumetrain/videos.","targetAudience":"The primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, although other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome.","registrationHowto":"In order to join the discussion, please go to http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html. For any questions, please use the Contact email.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1906,"created":1593699694000,"updated":1597157109000,"title":"Using the Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications","titleNative":"Using the Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications","startDate":1601251200000,"endDate":1603411200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Lauren Biermann","contactEmail":"Copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"TBC","description":"The purpose of this EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CMDS) training course is to share knowledge, skills, resources and code so attendees are able to independently access and process Data of EUMETSATs Copernicus Marine Data Stream (or a similar working  it is not only Sentinel-3 data, but also contributing missions such as Jason-3 and others) for their marine work-flows and applications.\r\n\r\nTraining will take place entirely online and through two phases. The first self-taught phase will take place between 28 September and 16 October and will take approximately 6-8 hours to complete. This will involve self-paced flexible learning through webinars, forums (particularly for software installations), documentation and assignments. The second online classroom phase will be held during the week 19  23 October and will be hosted over Zoom, made up of interactive tutorials, live demos, group work, and 1:1 meetings. This will require 5-7 hours of participation each day.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course participants will have the skills to:\r\n\r\n Understand what data and products the Copernicus Marine Data Stream provides (variables, timeliness, resolution, data formats);\r\n\r\n Select from the Copernicus Marine Data Stream appropriate products for specific tasks;\r\n\r\n Access / download data and products provided in the Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CODA, EUMETSAT Data archive, EumetCAST)\r\n\r\n Know how to work with CMDS data in SNAP, GIS, and Python (Jupyter Notebooks)\r\n\r\n Use data / products from the Copernicus Marine Data Stream for their purposes.","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Training is aimed at, but not restricted to, early career scientists: Masters / PhD students, Post-Docs, and/or experienced scientists from any relevant sector (industry, government, environment, research) who have clear motivations for working with satellite-based ocean observation data for marine applications. It would be beneficial for participants to have introductory experience using SNAP and/or a scripting language such as Python (or similar), but this is not a prerequisite. Please note that  this course is aimed primarily at European audiences and participants from Copernicus programme member states.","registrationHowto":"TBC once applications open. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":3925,"name":"Kim Hockley","email":"khock@pml.ac.uk","agency":"EUM","country":"GB","programme":"PML","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1934,"created":1598619571000,"updated":null,"title":"GMES&Africa and Copernicus Marine Earth Observation","titleNative":"GMES&Africa and Copernicus Marine Earth Observation","startDate":1601251200000,"endDate":1602201600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"MarCoSouth GMES&Africa Consortia","contactPerson":"Marie Smith","contactEmail":"MSmith2@csir.co.za","contactUrl":"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScssYiVT-StWuR-WOPvwlftqWIq_otylU8vXEAuLl2BgoydGg/viewform","description":"Applications are now open for the GMES&Africa and Copernicus Marine Earth Observation Online Training Course. This training is organised by the MarCoSouth GMES&Africa consortia in collaboration with EUMETSAT. The course will take place entirely online and will run in two different phases between 28 September and 16 October 2020.\r\n\r\nThis training course is designed to support the development of GMES&Africa activities and Copernicus marine data use around the African continent. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn the underlying principles of ocean remote sensing, how to access relevant data, and how to work with it using various open source tools. Each participant will be asked to propose a mini project that will be attempted with the support of trainers, allowing them to gain skills directly applicable to their work needs.","summary":null,"content":"\r\n\r\nParticipants will learn the underlying principles of ocean remote sensing, how to access relevant data, and how to work with it using various open source tools. Each participant will be asked to propose a mini project that will be attempted with the support of trainers, allowing them to gain skills directly applicable to their work needs. The online self-taught phase will run from 28 September until 9 October 2020  this will involve flexible learning through online videos, forums, software installation instructions, documentation and assignments that participants will be able to complete at their own pace. The online classroom phase will take place from the 12th  16th October 2020. The course will be limited to 15 participants. Selected participants will be expected to complete the self-taught phase and attend the entire duration of the full-time classroom phase of the workshop, which will run between approximately 09:00 to 17:00 (GMT+2).","targetAudience":"It is open to applicants from any African nation who wish to use satellite data for research and/or operational marine applications. Candidates affiliated with 