7192000,"title":"The International Distance Training Course on the Application of Meteorological Satellite Products","titleNative":"&#21355;&#26143;&#20135;&#21697;&#24212;&#29992;&#36828;&#31243;&#22269;&#38469;&#22521;&#35757;&#29677;","startDate":1600041600000,"endDate":1600992000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"CMATC/WMO RTC-Beijing","contactPerson":"DENG Jingmian","contactEmail":"applycmatc@cma.gov.cn","contactUrl":"http://mooc.cmatc.cma.cn/course/view.php?id=38&isStay=true&lang=en","description":"The course is committed to offering high quality, advanced knowledge and skills of Fengyun satellite, and enhancing the trainees profession in the application of products in supporting weather analysis, weather forecasting, and climate and so on. Trainees will be expected to improve the capabilities of data acquisition and assimilation, utility of satellite monitoring system, as well as the ability in satellite remote-sensing application.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By studying the online courseware, participants will be able to: 1) have a better understanding of the Fengyun satellites and the application of FengYun products, especially the geostationary satellite products;2) access, select, display and manipulate satellite data; 3) carry out weather analysis by using meteorological satellite imagery and data;4) use Satellite Weather Application Platform (SWAP), Satellite Monitoring Analysis Remote-sensing Toolkit (SMART), CMACast which will cover laboratory practice for torrential rain and strong convective weather monitoring, wild fire monitoring, and drought monitoring.5) apply the knowledge and skills learned in the course to practice, especially in the prevention and mitigation of local meteorological natural disasters.","summary":null,"content":"The training course includes:1) Satellite observations for weather and climate;2) Application of satellite materials in severe weather such as typhoon, heavy rain and so on;3) Application of satellite materials in numerical weather prediction;4) Satellite Weather Application Platform (SWAP), Satellite Monitoring Analysis Remote-sensing Toolkit (SMART) and CMACast;5) Case study and discussion on satellite products application in disaster mitigation and prevention, weather analysis and forecast and so on;6) Introduction to the latest development of Fengyun satellites and the current and future products of geostationary satellite products such as wind profiling radar (WPR), cloud spectral image, lightning image observation, space weather monitoring and so on.","targetAudience":"Officials, specialists, forecasters engaged in satellite meteorology and disaster risk management at National Hydrological and Meteorological Services or equivalent institutions.","registrationHowto":"Please visit http://mooc.cmatc.cma.cn/course/view.php?id=38&isStay=true&lang=en and create your own account. If you have already created an account, please enroll into the course directly. The enroll key for open path participants is: Cmatc2020. If you want to obtain certificate, please e-mail us the application form as required to applycmatc@cma.gov.cn.","registrationEndDate":1600041600000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5868,"name":"JI Wenbin","email":"jiwenbin@cma.cn","agency":"","country":"CN","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":1,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence China-Beijing"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":190,"value":"RTC","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":19,"value":"CMA","visible":false},{"id":1,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence China-Beijing","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1932,"created":1598299372000,"updated":1598353075000,"title":"Identification and Analysis of Fronts in South America","titleNative":"Identificación y Análisis de Fronteras en Sudamérica","startDate":1599750000000,"endDate":1599753600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA/WPC International Desk","contactPerson":"Michel Davison","contactEmail":"michel.davison@noaa.gov","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/1712592023938954764","description":"It is important for the forecaster and analysist to distunguish between various low level weather systems that affect South America. In the special session on 13 August, we explored the characteristics of fronts, troughs, and shear lines. In this additional session, we will finish the topics of lines of instability, and the South American Converence Zone. Please connect 10-15 minutes before the session, we will start promptly at 15 UtC. \r\nPrerequisites: If you did not participate in the 13 August session, please review the recording (parts 1 & 2) available here: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/fg_recording.asp","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Utilize conceptual models, numerical weather model output, and satellite imagery to identify fronts, troughs, shear lines, lines of instability, and the South American Convergence Zone (SACZ in Spanish).","summary":null,"content":"Es importante para el analista y los pronosticadores el poder distinguir entre los diferentes sistemas de bajo nivel que pueden afectar las condiciones del tiempo en América del Sur.  En la sesión especial del 13 agosto, exploramos modelos conceptuales y las características de los frentes, vaguadas, y líneas de cortante (shear lines). En esta sesión adicional, finalizaremos los temas de líneas de inestabilidad y la Zona de Convergencia  del Atlántico Sur (SACZ). Favor de conectarse 10-15 minutos antes de la sesión.  Comenzaremos puntualmente a las 15 UTC. \r\nRequisitos: Si no participó en la sesión del 13 de agosto, vea la grabación (partes 1 y 2), disponible aquí: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/fg_recording.asp","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/1712592023938954764 \r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":1,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Forecaster"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1931,"created":1597953063000,"updated":1598353406000,"title":"Satellite precipitation in South America and application in hydrology","titleNative":"Precipitação por satélite na América do Sul e aplicações em hidrologia","startDate":1598634000000,"endDate":1598637600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"INPE","contactPerson":"Natalia Rudorff","contactEmail":"vlab.cptec@inpe.br","contactUrl":"https://www.gotomeet.me/cptec/vlab","description":"Webinar on satellite precipitation products in South America and hydrological applications. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Knowledge on satellite precipitation products and applications.","summary":null,"content":"Basic concepts\r\nin situ x satellite observations\r\nPrecipitation GEO and LEO\r\nIR x MW x Blended\r\nLatency, scale and applications \r\nHydroestimator: global and adjusted\r\nValidation\r\nProducts\r\n","targetAudience":"Meteorologists of national and regional centers. ","registrationHowto":"Join the meeting at https://www.gotomeet.me/cptec/vlab\r\nNo advance registration required.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2842,"name":"Natalia Rudorff","email":"natalia.rudorff@inpe.br","agency":"INPE","country":"BR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initi