e discussions and hands on exercises. Participants will learn about the range of data products available from Copernicus satellites and downstream services, the harmonised data access that underpins WEkEO and the options for using hosted processing resources to work with the data available.","targetAudience":"Beginners and new users of Copernicus data and hosted processing services. ","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://copernicusmarineservice.clickmeeting.com/wekeo-online-training/register ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1901,"created":1592518122000,"updated":1592767041000,"title":"Tropical Waves and TUTT Induced Perturbations - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"Ondas Tropicales y Perturbaciones Inducidas por Vaguadas TUTT - 15:00 UTC","startDate":1594220400000,"endDate":1594312200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA/WPC International Desk","contactPerson":"Michel Davison","contactEmail":"michel.davison@noaa.gov","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/4668148547025992208","description":"The session is for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean) and useful for other Regions. This is a two part training seminar, with the first part on June 24 at 15 UTC covering theoretical aspects and characteristics of the Tropical Waves and TUTT induced perturbations in the easterly trades.  The second part is scheduled on June 25 at 15 UTC, and we will engage you to apply the information from the first day in practical exercises. The sessions will open 15 minutes earlier (at 14:45 UTC for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection).  GoToWebinar is used for both images and voice through the Internet.  ","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Utilize conceptual models, numerical weather model output, and satellite imagery to identify and distinguish between easterly/tropical waves and Tropical Upper Tropospheric Troughs (TUTT).","summary":null,"content":"A medida que pasamos a la temporada de lluvia en la cuenca del Caribe y en el norte de Sudamérica, los meteorólogos le prestaran mucha atención al impacto que puedan tener en las condiciones del tiempo las ondas del este/tropicales y las vaguadas en la atmósfera superior, Tropical Upper Tropospheric Trough (TUTT).  En esta sesión especial exploraremos modelos conceptuales de ambas, la aplicación de los modelos numéricos y técnicas de meteorología satelital para diferenciar entre los diferentes sistemas.","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/4668148547025992208 \r\nEste seminario de capacitación está dirigido a meteorólogos y técnicos meteorólogos con experiencia en el análisis e interpretación de imágenes satelitales y técnicas de detección de fronteras en bajos niveles.  Como requisito previo para el curso, los participantes deben completar el módulo de capacitación del MetEd (COMET) sobre Ondas del Este Originadas en África.  Para completar este módulo, siga el siguiente enlace: \r\n\r\