reated":1582509848000,"updated":1582545848000,"title":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","titleNative":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","startDate":1582682400000,"endDate":1582686000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/343438359505896705","description":"The topic of discussion of the next Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group (RFG) meeting, scheduled for 02UTC Wednesday, 26th February 2020 is as follows:\r\n\r\n\tForecasting highlights from Tropical Cyclone Damien (facilitator Mr. Joe Courtney BMTC)\r\n\r\nAs for all VLab RFG sessions attendance is free of charge. The Webinar web conferencing software will be used and you can attend the session by using the link https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/343438359505896705\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"\tForecasting highlights from Tropical Cyclone Damien (facilitator Mr. Joe Courtney BMTC)","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":" The Webinar web conferencing software will be used and you can attend the session by using the link https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/343438359505896705","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1840,"created":1576687029000,"updated":1577088516000,"title":"Satellite Application Course: Tropical Cyclones","titleNative":"Satellite Application Course: Tropical Cyclones","startDate":1581825600000,"endDate":1582207200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Muscat","host":"Public Authority for Civil Aviation (PACA)","contactPerson":"Hilal Al-Hajri","contactEmail":"h.alhajri@met.gov.om","contactUrl":"","description":"This course will focus on Tropical Cyclones, the basics of remote sensing and application of satellite data to regional forecasting problems. It will also cover the role and the benefits of MTG mission in the forecasting processes. ","country":{"id":"OM","name":"OMAN","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn to:\r\n- Describe tropical cyclone climatology in the Indian Ocean (where and when they form);\r\n- Identify distinguishing features of tropical cyclone structure;\r\n- Describe ingredients needed for tropical cyclone genesis;\r\n- Define the stages of a tropical cyclone lifecycle;\r\n- Detect cloud types in tropical cyclones using satellite remote sensing;\r\n- Detect TC centre by use of IR/VIS imagery, microwave imagery/products and scatterometer winds;\r\n- Learn key microwave techniques for estimating rainfall in the next 24/48 hours;\r\n- Detect changes in tropical cyclone intensity using satellite remote sensing, in particular the use of the Dvorak TC intensity estimation technique;\r\n- Describe key storm and environmental factors that affect  tropical cyclone intensity;\r\n- Describe the mechanisms that influence tropical cyclone motion;\r\n- Describe the basic mechanisms for tropical cyclone hazards particularly those at landfall;\r\n\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Classification methods of Tropical Cyclone (e.g Devorak); Identification of TC features using Satellite Pictures; Tracking tropical cyclone methods (the use of 1,2,3 rule; The added values of the existing METOSAT 8 over the region (Arabian sea); Estimation of rainfall using satellite products (e.g MPE, TRRM, GPM); Satellite altimetry; The use of Sat. products in modelling TCs; MTG utility in the region.\r\n","targetAudience":"Operational weather forecasters","registrationHowto":"By invitation letter.","registrationEndDate":1572566400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5845,"name":"Ivan Smiljanic","email":"ivan.smiljanic@external.eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false},{"id":7,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Oman","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":1,"value":"Arabic","iso639":"ar"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"}],"qualification":[{"id":11,"value":"Marine: Marine Weather Forecaster"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":10,"value":"PWS: Advisors Supporting Disaster Prevention and Mitigation and Other User Activities"},{"id":17,"