INITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1864,"created":1580263602000,"updated":1580298175000,"title":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","titleNative":"Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group meeting","startDate":1580349600000,"endDate":1580353200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Melbourne","host":"BMTC","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8467109652009196035 ","description":"The next Australian VLab Centre of Excellence Regional Focus Group (RFG) meeting is scheduled for 02UTC Thursday 30th January 2020","country":{"id":"AU","name":"AUSTRALIA","region":"RA-V","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"Extreme rain over Jabodetabek on the first day of 2020 (facilitator Mr. Idhan Abubakar BMKG Indonesia) \r\nA brief summary of the Asia Oceania Meteorological Satellite User Conference 10 (AOMSUC-10) Training Event (facilitator Mr Bodo Zeschke BMTC) \r\nCloud identification from satellite imagery (facilitator Mr Bodo Zeschke BMTC) \r\n","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/8467109652009196035 ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1834,"created":1576610147000,"updated":1576613749000,"title":"Applications of Global Precipitation Measurements for Assessing Extreme Dry and Wet Periods","titleNative":"Applications of Global Precipitation Measurements for Assessing Extreme Dry and Wet Periods","startDate":1580223600000,"endDate":1580833800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/water/webinars/IMERG-2020?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=EUMETSAT-VLAB&utm_campaign=IMERG","description":"It is well recognized that long-term precipitation measurements are necessary for understanding and monitoring regional precipitation characteristics. This includes characteristics crucial for monitoring water resources and hazards, like floods and droughts. TRMM was the first NASA mission dedicated to observing precipitation. It operated from November 1997 to April 2015. The Global Precipitation Measurement (GPM) Mission launched in February 2014 as a follow-on to TRMM. Both TRMM and GPM satellites, together with additional national and international satellites, were used to produce multi-satellite products such as TMPA and IMERG. Until recently these two separate products covered different time periods. There was a lack of long-term, continuous, precipitation time series. \r\n \r\nRecently, GPM-IMERG retrospectively analyzed TRMM-TMPA data to produce a consistent, combined precipitation time series from 2000-present. This extended IMERG data product is available at half-hourly resolution and 0.1x0.1 degree spatial resolution. The product will be useful for deriving long-term mean precipitation as reference. It will also help with monitoring extreme precipitation at regional scale.\r\n \r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goals: Accurate, consistent precipitation measurement can help to achieve:\r\n\tTarget 6.4: By 2030, substantially increase water-use efficiency across all sectors and ensure sustainable withdrawals and supply of freshwater to address water scarcity and substantially reduce the number of people suffering from water scarcity\r\n\tTarget 2.4: By 2030, ensure sustainable food production systems and implement resilient agricultural practices that increase productivity and production, that help maintain ecosystems, that strengthen capacity for adaptation to climate change, extreme weather, drought, flooding and other disasters and that progressively improve land and soil quality\r\n\r\n \r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: \r\nBy the end of this training, attendees will be able to: \r\n\tDerive regional precipitation statistics (mean, standard deviation, anomalies, percentile values) \r\n\tCalculate and interpret the Standardized Precipitation Index (SPI) for assessing extreme dry and wet periods\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Course Dates: January 28, 30, and February 4, 2020.\r\n \r\nTimes: 10:00-12:00 & 16:00-18:00 EST (UTC-5); There will be identical sessions at two different times of the day\r\n\r\nThree, two-hour parts that include lectures and demonstrations, exercises, and question and answer sessions. \r\n\r\nPast ARSET trainings on water resources and flood management covered TMPA and IMERG data and their applications in detail. This advanced webinar will focus on analysis and interpretation of the new long-term IMERG data, focused on extreme dry and wet period monitoring and management. The webinar will include lectures and hands-on exercises to derive regional precipitation statistics.","targetAudience":"Local, regional, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations, engaged in water resources and disaster management.","registrationHowto":"Please register here: Registration Information: https://go.nasa.gov/35oOBQf","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":