"visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1794,"created":1563801602000,"updated":1564142304000,"title":"Introductory Webinar: Earth Observations for Disaster Risk Assessment & Resilience","titleNative":"Introductory Webinar: Earth Observations for Disaster Risk Assessment & Resilience","startDate":1565049600000,"endDate":1565827200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/19-DRA?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=DRA","description":"According to a UN report, between 1998 and 2017, the U.S. alone lost USD 944.8 billion from disasters. Between 1978 and 2017, losses from extreme weather events rose by 251 percent. It is critical to develop disaster management strategies to reduce and mitigate disaster risks. A major factor in regional risk assessment is the evaluating the vulnerability of lives and property to disasters. Environmental information about disasters, their spatial impact, and their temporal evolution can plan an important role as well.\r\n\r\nThis webinar series will focus on Earth observation (EO) data useful for disaster risk assessment. The series will cover natural disasters including tropical cyclones, flooding, wildfires, and heat stress. The training will also include access of socioeconomic and disaster damage data. Sessions 3 & 4 will cover case studies and operational applications of EO for disaster risk assessment.\r\n\r\nRelevant UN Sustainable Development Goal: Target 13.1: Strength resilience & adaptive capacity to climate-related hazards and natural disasters in all countries.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will learn about available NASA remote sensing and socioeconomic data and how to combine them for assessing risk, understand how to apply these data for assessing risk from floods and tropical cyclones in specific regions, and learn how operational agencies are using NASA data for risk management.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Four, two-hour parts that include lectures, demonstrations, and question and answer sessions. ","targetAudience":"The audience for this training are local, regional, state, federal, and international entities, including public and private sector organizations, engaged in disaster management, emergency responders, urban and infrastructure planners.","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register to attend the webinar series. See more information and registration at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/19-DRA?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=DRA","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1759,"created":1551195622000,"updated":1563543155000,"title":"Online RA-I Meteorological Satellite Applications 2019","titleNative":"Online RA-I Meteorological Satellite Applications 2019","startDate":1564963200000,"endDate":1567728000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158&section=3","description":"The objective of the online course is to optimize the use of data from meteorological satellites and to increase the knowledge and skills of meteorological trainers, contributing to improve forecasting and subsequently deployed so that they are able to apply their competence from this course.\r\n\r\nClassroom courses for selected online participants are foreseen to take place at IMTR, Nairobi, 14-18 October 2019, and at SAWS, Pretoria, 25-29 November, 2019. \r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Improved skills in: (a) Identifying key weather systems and features found in Africa and their characteristics in satellite imagery and products; (b) Being a competent user of virtual course technology; (c) Developing relationships with course participants via the discussion forums and online briefings.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"The systems and features that are addressed in this course include: ITCZ, anticyclones, tropical lows, convective systems, dust storms and fog and low clouds. \r\n\r\nThe course only addresses system/feature identification in satellite imagery, it does not cover forecasting.","targetAudience":"Instructors in satellite meteorology, operational forecasters or experienced satellite data users, with the ability to pass on skills acquired at the course to other operational staff.","registrationHowto":"The course is intended primarily for participants from Africa nominated by their Permanent Representatives with WMO. Depending on the seat availability, additional online participants can be accepted. \r\nThe nominated candidates are requested to apply to the online course by completing an online questionnaire. Applications close 21 June 2019. \r\nPlease apply at <a href=\"http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158\">http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158</a>","registrationEndDate":1561078800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":8,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Kenya","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":6,"value":"BIP-M: Basic Instructional Package for Meteorologists"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1774,"created":1556530081000,"updated":1556540286000,"title":"Remote sensing: Introduction to Satellite Images","titleNative":"Sensores Remotos: Introducción a las Imágenes Satelitales","startDate":1564963200000,"endDate":1567123200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"RTC-SMN Argentina","contactPerson":"Marines Campos","contactEmail":"marinescampos27@gmail.com","contactUrl":"https://sites.google.com/site/crfpar3/","description":"This self-directed course offers the first steps in satellite image interpretation for aeronautical observers. Short background information is given and lots of practice. Although this course is available for about one month, it only requires about 1 week dedication by the participant. Interpretation of  satellite images helps observers to be aware of the current and coming meteorological situation as an additional support to in situ observations, and communicate the corresponding information to users as required in his tasks.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEste curso es auto dirigido, estará disponible durante un mes pero solo requiere 1 semana de dedicación. Este curso ofrece información básica y bastante práctica.Las imágenes satelitales proveen un soporte adicional a las observaciones in situ. Interpretación básica de imágenes de satélite para  estar actualizado con el estado de la situación meteorológica y comunicar la información meteorológica.","country":{"id":"AR","name":"ARGENTINA","region":"RA-III","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"1- identify and describe the characteristics for each channel visible , infrared and water vapor.\r\n2- identify cloud height and thickness.\r\n3- Identify dust and volcanic ash\r\n4- identify land and water surfaces using visible and infrared images.\r\n&#9679; Describir qué características mide cada tipo de canal: visible, infrarrojo y de vapor de agua.\r\n&#9679; Diferenciar e identificar si una imagen corresponde al canal visible, infrarrojo o de vapor de agua.\r\n&#9679; Identificar la altura y espesor relativos de las nubes.\r\n&#9679; Identificar presencia de polvo, humo o ceniza suspendidos en la atmósfera en imagenes visible e infrarroja.\r\n&#9679; Diferenciar entre superficies de tierra y agua en imágenes visibles e infrarrojas.\r\n&#9679; Utilizar la información satelital como soporte adicional para complementar la vigilancia continua de la situación meteorológica.","summary":null,"content":"General description of satellite orbits.\r\nIntroduction to ABI sensor\r\nBasic analysis of satellite images \r\nIdentify most commonly used channels\r\nInterpretation of products from 1 channel\r\nPractical exercises of basic satellite interpretation\r\n\r\n&#10063; Descripción general de órbitas satelitales.\r\n&#10063; Descripción general de los sensores a bordo del satélite GOES-16.\r\n&#10063; Introducción al sensor ABI.\r\n&#10063; Análisis básico de imágenes satelitales.\r\n&#10063; Identificación de canales más utilizados.\r\n&#10063; Productos de un único canal y cómo interpretarlos. Algunas características de las nubes y la superficie como aparecen en productos satelitales y la información que se puede generar.\r\n&#10063; Ejercicios prácticos sobre interpretación de imágenes satelitales\r\n","targetAudience":"AMO","registrationHowto":"Se requiere autorización de la autoridad de su organización. Registración personal en el link ( https://sites.google.com/site/crfpar3/ )","registrationEndDate":1564358400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":51,"name":"Claudia Campetella","email":"claudiac@cima.fcen.uba.ar","agency":"UBA","country":"AR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,