resting situations and feat","content":"Every weather briefing concentrates on some new events that occurred since the last weather briefing.","targetAudience":"Primary target audience are forecasters in shifts, though other meteorologists from different areas are also welcome!","registrationHowto":"Use the provided link: http://eumetrain.org/weather_briefings.html","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1775,"created":1556565399000,"updated":1556570240000,"title":"GOES-16, JPSS and GEONETCast Americas Satellite Workshop","titleNative":"GOES-16, JPSS and GEONETCast Americas Satellite Workshop","startDate":1563814800000,"endDate":1564171200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Brigdetown","host":"CIMH/NOAA","contactPerson":"KATHY-ANN CAESAR","contactEmail":"kacaesar@cimh.edu.bb","contactUrl":" https://cimhsatellitetrainingweek.eventbrite.com","description":"This will be a hands-on workshop for users of GOES/JPSS satellite data and products, as well as current and potential users of the GEONETCast Americas (GNC-A) system. All participants should be prepared to submit a case study from their respective office/region that was particularly challenging to forecast. These case studies will be considered for presentation during the workshop, and will be used to create an agenda of specific forecast challenge sessions. Each session will be a mix of topic introduction and interaction where participants share their forecast challenge case study with the Satellite Subject Matter Experts from the GOES and JPSS Programs and other workshop participants. Satellite Subject Matter Experts will then present their analysis of these case studies, and provide suggestions on satellite data or products that could be of value for forecasters to use to improve their forecasts for these types of weather events in the future. Workshop participants will then discuss the use of these suggested capabilities and the operational value they would bring. Note:  The deadline for case study submissions will be 06/14/19. The preliminary plan for the weeks activities can be found in the table below: ","country":{"id":"BB","name":"BARBADOS","region":"RA-IV","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"&#9679;\tWorking knowledge of the GOES-R Series key instruments - Advanced Baseline Imager (ABI) and Geostationary Lightning Mapper (GLM) \r\n&#9679;\tWorking knowledge of the JPSS key instruments - VIIRS, CrIS, and ATMS\r\n&#9679;\tCompetency in working with GOES-E ABI and JPSS/GCOM data and products for forecasting, prediction, monitoring or research through hands-on exercises and case studies.\r\n&#9679;\tKnowledge of the various methods to access GOES East and JPSS/GCOM data and products\r\n&#9679;\tWorking knowledge of the most relevant satellite channels coming from JPSS and GOES-East ABI and the products available from them to address Severe weather - both tropical cyclone and non-tropical cyclone related, Saharan Air Layer, dust, volcanic ash, fires, smoke and lightning \r\n&#9679;\tGeneral understanding of the global GEONETCast and GEONETCast Americas systems.  \r\n&#9679;\tKnowledge of equipment requirements and general cost estimates for GNC-A stations.\r\n&#9679;\tKnowledge of resources to assist in the maintenance and troubleshooting of common issues related to GNC-A station. \r\n&#9679;\tOverview of the data and products on the GNC-A broadcast, including from GOES-16 and JPSS.\r\n&#9679;\tKnowledge of the possible uses of GNC-A in Disaster Scenarios\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Monday\r\nJuly 22\tAM: Introduction to Workshop, GOES-R Series, JPSS & GNC-A. \r\nPM: Severe Weather - Non-Tropical Cyclone Related (Presentation of select case studies, GOES-R/JPSS presentation of products and methods of use, various methods of access to data) \r\nTuesday\r\nJuly 23\tAM: Severe Weather - Tropical Cyclone Related (Presentation of select case studies, GOES-R/JPSS presentation of products and methods of use, various methods of access to data) \r\nPM: The National Hurricane Center (NHC) Perspective on Hurricane Monitoring and Practical Exercises in the Use of Satellite Imagery. \r\nAdditional PM: Demonstration of the GEONETCast Station\r\nWednesday\r\nJuly 24\tAM: Saharan Air Layer & Dust (Presentation of select case studies, GOES-R/JPSS presentation of products and methods of use, various methods of access to data)\r\nPM: Volcanic Ash, Fires, Smoke & Lightning (Presentation of select case studies, GOES-R/JPSS presentation of products and methods of use, various methods of access to data)\r\nThursday\r\nJuly 25\tAM: Introduction of SIGMACast, Practical Exercise in Accessing and Using GNC-A Products, and HRIT/EMWIN Data Access and Products Overview\r\nPM: Building In-House Training Exercises of Severe Weather and Weather Bulletins/Presentations\r\nFriday\r\nJuly 26\tAM: Introduction to Impact-Based Warning and Interacting with Disaster Managers\r\n","targetAudience":"Weather Forecasters and researchers ","registra