vian High module, containing activities and simulations.","country":{"id":"AR","name":"ARGENTINA","region":"RA-III","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"Analyse and diagnose the weather situation.\r\nForecast hazardous weather phenomena.\r\nIdentify cloud types and their characteristics.\r\nIdentify and interpret broad scale, synoptic and mesoscale systems.\r\nIdentify and interpret atmospheric phenomena.\r\nInterpret derived fields and derived products.","summary":null,"content":"Activities and case studies  with simulations applying satellite skills in combiantion with other data:cloud structure in salellite images, meteorological physical background, NWP key parameters, typical appearance in vertical cross sections, weather events.\t","targetAudience":"AMF and PWF","registrationHowto":"Authorisation from national organisation ( National weather Service or other)  is required.\r\nSelf registration ( https://sites.google.com/site/crfpar3/ ). ","registrationEndDate":1563148800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":51,"name":"Claudia Campetella","email":"claudiac@cima.fcen.uba.ar","agency":"UBA","country":"AR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":190,"value":"RTC","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[{"id":1,"value":"Aviation: Aeronautical Meteorological Forecaster"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1790,"created":1562776567000,"updated":1562839197000,"title":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","titleNative":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 15:00 UTC","startDate":1563462000000,"endDate":1563465600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA, CIRA, and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Bernie Connell","contactEmail":"bernie.connell@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/509102871032836620","description":"The sessions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean).  Session time is 15:00 UTC, but as usual, it will start 15 minutes earlier (at 14:45 UTC for those who want to check their microphone and voice connection).  GoToWebinar is used for both images and voice through the Internet.  Images during the session are from SLIDER: http://rammb-slider.cira.colostate.edu  More Information: http://rammb.cira.colostate.edu/training/rmtc/focusgroup.asp","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Satellite imagery and products real-time applications","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Forecasters, Students, Researchers, Trainers","registrationHowto":"Register here: https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/509102871032836620","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5859,"name":"Jose Galvez","email":"jose.galvez@colostate.edu","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":18,"value":"NOAA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1783,"created":1560442683000,"updated":1561130132000,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Remote Sensing for Monitoring Land Degradation and Sustainable Cities SDGs ","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Remote Sensing for Monitoring Land Degradation and Sustainable Cities SDGs ","startDate":1562680800000,"endDate":1563895800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/land/webinars/land-degradation-SDGs19?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=trends.earth","description":"The Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) are an urgent call for action by countries to preserve our oceans and forests, reduce inequality, and spur economic growth. The land management SDGs call for consistent tracking of land cover metrics. These metrics include productivity, land cover, soil carbon, urban expansion, and more. This webinar series will highlight a tool that uses NASA Earth Observations to track land degradation and urban development that meet the appropriate SDG targets. \r\n\r\nSDGs 11 and 15 relate to sustainable urbanization and land use and cover change. SDG 11 aims to \"make cities and human settlements inclusive, safe, resilient, and sustainable.\" SDG 15 aims to \"combat desertification, drought, and floods, and strive to achieve a land degradation neutral world.\" To assess progress towards these goals, indicators have been established, many of which can be monitored using remote sensing. \r\n\r\nIn this training, attendees will learn to use a freely-available QGIS plugin, Trends.Earth, created by Conservation International (CI). Trends.Earth allows users to plot time series of key land change indicators. Attendees will learn to produce maps and figures to support monitoring and reporting on land degradation, improvement, and urbanization for SDG indicators 15.3.1 and 11.3.1. Each part of the webinar series will feature a presentation, hands-on exercise, and time for the speaker to answer live questions. \r\n\r\nThis training has been developed in partnership with Conservation International. \r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will become familiar with SDG Indicators 15.3.1 and 11.3.1, understand the basics on how to compute sub indicators of SDG 15.3.1 such as: productivity, land cover, and soil carbon, understand how to use the Trends.Earth Urban Mapper web interface, and learn the basics of the Trends.Earth toolkit including:Plotting time series, downloading data, use default or custom data for productivity, land cover, and soil organic carbon, calculate a SDG 15.3.1 spatial layers and summary table, calculate urban change metrics, and create urban change summary tables.","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: \r\n\r\nThree, 1.5-hour sessions that include lectures, hands-on exercises, and a question and answer session","targetAudience":"This training will b