":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":20,"value":"Other (see description)"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1726,"created":1542203402000,"updated":1542276928000,"title":"Advanced Training Course for CM SAF Users","titleNative":"Advanced Training Course for CM SAF Users","startDate":1559692800000,"endDate":1559865600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Mainz","host":"EUMETSAT","contactPerson":"Christine Träger-Chatterjee","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://www.eumetsat.int/website/home/TechnicalBulletins/Training/DAT_4128784.html; https://bit.ly/2Onnz32","description":"Subsequent to the 2019 CM SAF User Workshop, EUMETSAT & CM SAF jointly offer a workshop for advanced users of CM SAF data. The key objectives of this workshop is to\r\n- Share knowledge, experiences and best practices for the development of operational applications in using CM SAF data\r\n- Build a network of CM SAF users with different level of experience\r\nWith expert support, the participants of this workshop will develop applications of CM SAF data to be ready for operations. \r\n","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"After this course participants should be able to:\r\n design (operational) applications of CM SAF data records.\r\n find ways to solve issues related to applying CM SAF data, also using established links with other CM SAF users to solve \r\n","summary":"Subsequent to the 2019 CM SAF User Workshop, EUMETSAT & CM SAF jointly offer a workshop for advanced users of CM SAF data. The key objectives of this workshop is to\r\n- Share knowle","content":"This is a peer-to-peer workshop. Users of CM SAF data, who have experience in developing (operational) applications with CM SAF data records, will share their knowledge and experience in working groups.\r\n\r\nParticipants ideas for (operational) applications using CM SAF data will be discussed in the working groups and first steps towards design and implementation of these applications will be undertaken.\r\n\r\nIdeas for operational applications using CM SAF data records are very welcome. Possible applications could be related (but are not limited) to:\r\n National / Regional Climate Atlases\r\n Merging satellite climate data with other sources of climate information \r\n Validation and Quality control of surface data \r\n PV potential resource assessment\r\n Operational Climate Monitoring \r\n Climate Analysis \r\n Target oriented visualisation of Climate information","targetAudience":"Participants of the Advanced Training Course for CM SAF Users are:\r\n\texpected to have practical experiences in working with CM SAF data;\r\n\texpected to contribute the CM SAF User Workshop, taking place prior to the training course;\r\n\tstrongly encouraged to bring ideas for applications using CM SAF data records\r\n","registrationHowto":"Applications for the advanced training course can be submitted until 31.12.2018 via https://bit.ly/2Onnz32. \r\nAs the number of participants is limited, a selection will be made based on the available applications. The selection will be based on the abstract submitted, that describes the idea of an (operational) application using CM SAF data. Apply online via the application form (https://bit.ly/2Onnz32). Those selected will be informed by 18. January 2019.\r\nRegistration to the Advanced Training Course for CM SAF Users is only possible in combination with registering to the 2019 CM SAF Users Workshop.\r\n","registrationEndDate":1546300740000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"va