deeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true},{"id":210,"value":"NOAA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":12,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Costa Rica","visible":false},{"id":18,"value":"NOAA","visible":false},{"id":2,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Barbados","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1764,"created":1553099940000,"updated":1553112607000,"title":"Remote Sensing for Disasters Scenarios","titleNative":"Remote Sensing for Disasters Scenarios","startDate":1555372800000,"endDate":1556582400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/disasters-scenario-2019?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=disasters%20scenario","description":"According to the WHO, every year disasters kill around 90,000 people and affect close to 160 million people worldwide.\" This training will show participants how NASA remote sensing data can be used to characterize and monitor disaster related events and support relief efforts. Each session will cover a different disaster and its supporting data. Disaster scenarios will include tropical storms, flooding, earthquakes, and landslides.\r\n\r\nSegún la Organización Mundial de la Salud, cada año los desastres matan alrededor de 90.000 personas y afectan cerca de 160 millones de personas a nivel mundial.1 Esta capacitación se enfocara en la utilización de datos de satélites de la NASA para caracterizar y monitorear desastres y apoyar actividades de asistencia. Cada sesión enfocará un desastre diferente y los datos correspondientes. Los escenarios de desastres incluirán tormentas tropicales, inundaciones, terremotos y derrumbes.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: By the end of this training, attendees will be able to: Identify NASA data products to characterize and monitor disasters and support decision-making; Understand the different data products available and their shortcomings; Access and interpret data covered in the different sessions","summary":null,"content":"Three, two-hour sessions that include a 30 min Q&A period\r\nSession A will be broadcast in English, and Session B will cover the same content in Spanish. \r\n\r\nDate Range:  Tuesdays, April 16, 2019. April 23, 2019. April 30, 2019. \r\nTimes: 10:00-12:00 and 14:00-16:00 EDT (UTC-4)\r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"Audience: Disaster management agencies including domestic and international government agencies (e.g. FEMA and equivalent government organizations outside the U.S.) as well as aid organizations (e.g. Red Cross, UN).","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register to attend the sessions. Please register through links provided in the training webpage.","registrationEndDate":1555286400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1763,"created":1553099678000,"updated":1553112643000,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Investigating Time Series of Satellite Imagery","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Investigating Time Series of Satellite Imagery","startDate":1555286400000,"endDate":1555459200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/land/webinars/time-series-19?utm_source=direct&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=time","description":"Evaluation of satellite imagery for an area over time can be used to identify trends and changes. This type of time series analysis can be used to assess forest disturbance, land cover changes, vegetation health, and agriculture monitoring and expansion. NASA Earth observations can provide long-term records from Landsat, and frequent imagery from sensors including MODIS. This training will focus on two tools, AppEEARS from the LPDAAC and LandTrendr via Google Earth Engine (GEE). AppEEARS enables users to integrate point or polygon ground-based data with satellite imagery. The GEE implementation of LandTrendr enables users to analyze land cover dynamics, including short-term disturbances and long-term trends. Both sessions will feature a lecture, followed by time for hands-on exercises and questions.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: By the end of this training, attendees will become familiar with time series analysis techniques:\r\n\r\nUnderstand how to evaluate time series of MODIS & Landsat data; Learn how to integrate point data with satellite imagery using the AppEEARS web-based interface; Learn the basics of the GEE implementation of LandTrendr including:Generating annual land surface reflectance images; Plotting a time series of land surface reflectance; Creating a map of change detection, magnitude of change, duration of change event, and pre-change spectral values","summary":null,"content":"Two, two-hour sessions that include lectures, time to complete hands-on exercises, and a question and answer session\r\n\r\nCourse Dates:  Monday, April 15 and Wednesday, April 17, 2019.\r\n\r\n2 Time slots to choose from: 10:00-12:00 or 18:00-20:00 EDT (UTC-4)","targetAudience":"Audience: Advanced users of remote sensing data within local, regional, state, federal, and non-governmental organizations involved in land management and conservation efforts.","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register to attend the sessions. Please register through links provided in the training webpage. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":25,"value":"NASA","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1749,"created":1550664516000,"updated":1593001057000,"title":"Using Copernicus satellite data for ocean applications (co-sponsored by CMEMS, EUM) ","titleNative":"Using Copernicus satellite data for ocean applications (co-sponsored by CMEMS, EUM) ","startDate":1554720300000,"endDate":1554726600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vienna","host":"EUMETSAT and CMEMS","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"Hayley.Evers-King@external.eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://meetingorganizer.copernicus.org/EGU2019/session/30869","description":"This course is a two part (online and classroom) blended course introducing Copernicus marine data to those in the oceanography sector.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"This short course is an opportunity to learn about the data available from the Copernicus Sentinel 3 satellite, and then, with support from marine Earth Observation experts, to develop your own workflows for using data from the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream and Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service. The sessions will be interactive, using the WeKEO DIAS hosted processing, Sentinel Applications Platform (SNAP) software, and Python programming. No experience is necessary as various exercises will be provided for a wide range of skill levels and applications, however participants should bring their own laptops and be prepared to install open source software in advance.","summary":null,"content":"Satellite data provides information on the marine environment that can be used for many applications  from water quality and early warning systems, to climate change studies and marine spatial planning. The most modern generation of satellites offer improvements in spatial and temporal resolution as well as a constantly evolving suite of products. \r\n\r\n Data from the European Union Copernicus programme is open and free for everyone to use however they wish - whether from academic, governance, or commercial backgrounds. The programme has an operational focus, with satellite constellations offering continuity of service for the foreseeable future. There is also a growing availability of open source tools that can be used to work with this data.","targetAudience":"Anyone with an interest in using Copernicus marine data for oceanographic studies or applications","registrationHowto":"N/A ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":20,"value":"Other (see description)"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1751,"created":1550679217000,"updated":1593001049000,"title":"Using the Copernicus Sentinel-3 Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications","titleNative":"Using the Copernicus Sentinel-3 Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications","startDate":1554714000000,"endDate":1554744600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Busan","host":"IOCS","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"Hayley.Evers-King@external.eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"A one-day course to introduce participants of the IOCS conference to the Copernicus marine data stream from EUMETSAT.","country":{"id":"KR","name":"KOREA, REPUBLIC OF","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"This short course is an opportunity to learn about the data available from the Copernicus Sentinel 3 satellite, and then, with support from marine Earth Observation experts, to develop your own workflows for using data from the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream and Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service. Participants will also have the opportunity for one-on-one discussions with the trainers to develop their individual work flows to use satellite data for their own applications and regions of interest.","summary":null,"content":"This training course will introduce participants to the latest satellite data available through the Copernicus Marine Data Stream from EUMETSAT, part of the European Commission Copernicus programme. Daily, Level-1 and Level-2 ocean colour, sea surface temperature, and altimetry data will be covered. The training will include practical sessions on data access, visualisation and analysis using the Sentinel Application Platform (SNAP) and python programming language. The training will comprise of a few formal lectures to supplement several practical sessions where participants can explore the data and tools appropriate to their own levels of experience. ","targetAudience":"Participants with a range of experience are welcome, however they should have some familiarity with the underlying principles of marine Earth observation data, and be intending to use this data in future work.","registrationHowto":"https://iocs.ioccg.org/2019-workshops/","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"}],"qualification":[{"id":20,"value":"Other (see description)"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1733,"created":1543495843000,"updated":1543498831000,"title":"Using Copernicus satellite data for ocean applications","titleNative":"Using Copernicus satellite data for ocean applications","startDate":1554681600000,"endDate":1555027200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vienna","host":"EGU","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"This is a shourt course (about 2 - 3  hours), that will be given during the EGU in Vienna, 8 - 12 April 2019. The exact date is yet to be defined.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- Know where and how to access the EUMETSAT Copernicus Ocean Data Stream.\r\n- Be able to do some basic analysis of CMDS data using SNAP and/or Python.","summary":null,"content":"Satellite data provides information on the marine environment that can be used for many applications. The most modern generation of satellites offer improvements in spatial and temporal resolution as well as a constantly evolving suite of products. \r\n\r\nData from the European Union Copernicus programme is open and free for everyone to use however they wish - whether from academic, governance, or commercial backgrounds. The programme has an operational focus, with satellite constellations offering continuity of service for the foreseeable future. There is also a growing availability of open source tools that can be used to work with this data.\r\n \r\nThis short course is an opportunity to learn about the data available from the Copernicus Sentinel 3 satellite, and then, with support from marine Earth Observation experts, to develop your own workflows for using data from the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream. The sessions will be interactive, using the Sentinel Applications Platform (SNAP) software, and Python programming. No experience is necessary as various exercises will be provided for a wide range of skill levels and applications, however participants should bring their own laptops and be prepared to install open source software in advance.\r\n","targetAudience":"Students, Early Career Scientists.","registrationHowto":"Via the EUMETSAT course management system. A link to the registration page will be provided here in due time.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1734,"created":1543496158000,"updated":1593001042000,"title":"EUMETSATs Climate Data Records: Using satellite data for climate applications","titleNative":"EUMETSATs Climate Data Records: Using satellite data for climate applications","startDate":1554681600000,"endDate":1555027200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vienna","host":"EGU","contactPerson":"Christine Träger-Chatterjee","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"This is a short cours (about 2 - 3 hours) held during the EGU, 8 - 12 April 2019, Vienna, Austria. The exact date is yet to be defined and will be announced here asap.","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- Knowing where and how to access EUMETSAT Thematic Climate Data Records.\r\n- Knowing how to use the CM SAF R Toolbox.","summary":null,"content":"Satellite based climate data records play an increasing role in climate monitoring and help to answer climate related questions. Nowadays satellite based climate data records cover a time period of several decades. EUMETSATs Satellite Application Facilities (SAF) provide a number of high quality climate data records for various geophysical variables, such as solar radiation, land surface temperature, cloud fractional cover, cloud microphysical variables, and many more, derived from both, geostationary and polar orbiting satellites.\r\n\r\nThese climate data records are free and open to everyone. They continue to be reprocessed to account for improvements of the algorithm and to include recent time periods. In addition to the data, free software tools are developed and provided by the SAFs for users to work with the data.\r\n\r\nThis is short course in an opportunity to get an overview about the climate data records available from the EUMETSAT Satellite Application Facilities, learn how to access them and gain some first experiences in how to work with the software tools provided. Participants will have the opportunity do some hands-on exercises using the data and tools provided. Participants are also welcome to bring their own scientific questions, for which the satellite based CDRs may help to find the answer. Data and software developers will be around to hep and answer questions.\r\n\r\nParticipants should be prepared to bring a laptop to the course, to install the software tools beforehand and to download some data of interest from the CM SAF. A guidance on how to do that will be provided online and in due time.\r\n","targetAudience":"Students, Early Career Scientists.","registrationHowto":"Registration via the EUMETSAT course management system. The link to the registration page will be provided here in due time.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1740,"created":1545343696000,"updated":1548443673000,"title":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbea