er conditions.\r\n6 - Use forecasting model outputs in hazardous conditions.","summary":"The course will be conducted online and in asynchronous mode between March 26th and May 17th, 2019. A Moodle platform will be used for this purpose. The course is primarily designe","content":"The 2019 course will cover the following topics:\r\n1) Identification of potentially dangerous conditions over the ocean. \r\n2) Scatterometers and Altimeter products - advantages and limitations.\r\n3) Forecasting extreme weather conditions.\r\n4) Forecasting ocean waves.\r\n","targetAudience":"Marine forecasters and general forecasters","registrationHowto":"More info will soon be available.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":11,"value":"Marine: Marine Weather Forecaster"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1758,"created":1551194994000,"updated":1551276228000,"title":"Baltic+ 2019 - Classroom phase","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2019 - Classroom phase","startDate":1552953600000,"endDate":1553126400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Tallinn","host":"Estonian Environment Agency","contactPerson":"Taimi Paljak","contactEmail":"taimi.paljak@envir.ee","contactUrl":"https://training.eumetsat.int/course/index.php?categoryid=70","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\nThis is a blended course, composed of a 3 weeks online phase and a 3 days face-to-face phase. The online phase will occur from 18 February to 08 March 2019 and is mandatory for classroom participants. The classroom phase will deepen the topics discussed during the Online phase. \r\nThe online (asynchronous) component will include reading materials, exercises and collaborative case study preparatory work. This will take three weeks, including approximately 4 hours of individual work per week. The course will finish with a three-day-classroom course that will consist of exercises, presentations, group work and finalization of case studies started during the online phase. ","country":{"id":"EE","name":"ESTONIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"- Having more skills in using satellite products together with other observations and NWP guidance for monitoring heavy precipitation cases in Baltic Sea region; \r\n- Understand the effects of land and sea interaction for heavy precipitation. \r\n- Understand the importance of communication and delivery of the information to the governmental institutions, the media and the general public. ","summary":null,"content":"The objective of the course is to develop and deliver a training program that brings the new developments in satellite meteorology and in tools and methodology for short range weather forecasting as well as promote networking among meteorologists and experts from the participating countries.","targe