port aquatic and terrestrial ecosystems, provide transportation, and generate hydropower. Managing river basin watersheds is critical for developing policies for sustainable water allocation and development. Over the course of four sessions, this introductory webinar series will address using satellite data and Earth system modeling data sources to estimate surface water budgets.\r\n\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"US","name":"UNITED STATES","region":"RA-IV","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will become familiar with remote sensing and Earth system modeling data sources relevant for river basin watershed management and estimating surface water budgets and their temporal variability in sub-watersheds within river basins","summary":null,"content":"Course Format: Four, one-hour online webinar presentations followed by 30 minutes of Q&A. To be conducted Wednesdays, March 13 through April 3, 2019 at both 09:00-10:30 or 16:00-17:30 EDT (UTC-4). ","targetAudience":"The content of this training was developed for local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations engaged in the management of water resources, river basins, floods, droughts, land development, river transportation, hydroelectric power, and reservoirs. ","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register to attend the sessions through the training webpage: https://go.nasa.gov/2DMij6O","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},