"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1727,"created":1542700502000,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"EUMeTrain Event Week on Aviation Meteorology","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Event Week on Aviation Meteorology","startDate":1543827600000,"endDate":1544198400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"EUMeTrain TSO, Zsofia Kocsis","contactEmail":"tso@eumetrain.org, kocsis.zs@met.hu","contactUrl":"http://www.eumetrain.org/","description":"This event targets aviation forecasters and interested users in Aviation Meteorology. Online sessions will be provided by experts from various countries and services. The lectures will be broadcasted using the WebEx Training Center platform and they are free of any costs.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After completing the event week, the participants will gain knowledge about how other services forecast weather phenomena important in aviation and about some other technologies used in these forecasts.","summary":"This event targets aviation forecasters and interested users in Aviation Meteorology. Online sessions will be provided by experts from various countries and services. The lectures ","content":"The online presentations will cover the following topics important in aviation meteorology, such as: turbulence, fog, convection, volcanic ash, etc.","targetAudience":"Primary target audience are aviation forecasters. Secondary audience is everybody interested in the process of delivering and managing warnings.","registrationHowto":"http://www.eumetrain.org/","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1679,"created":1521192771000,"updated":null,"title":" Operational Marine Forecasting using EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream - Classroom Phase","titleNative":" Operational Marine Forecasting using EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream - Classroom Phase","startDate":1543795200000,"endDate":1544140800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Pretoria","host":"South African Weather Service (SAWS)","contactPerson":"Copernicus Training Team","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for marine weather forecasting to professionals with some previous experience. \r\n\r\nWe will focus on the application of data from Sentinel-3, Jason-3 and use of associated data such as EUMETSATs Scatterometers. \r\n\r\nThis is a blended course, composed of a 2 weeks online phase and a 5 days face-to-face phase. The online phase is mandatory for classroom participants and the dates will be announced soon. The classroom phase will deepen the topics discussed during the Online phase. \r\n\r\nThe online (asynchronous) component will include recorded lectures, modules, readings and quizzes. This will take two weeks, including approximately 3 hours of individual work per week. The course will finish with a Workshop phase, with practical sessions, supported by lectures on how to make an efficient operational use of the data. \r\n","country":{"id":"ZA","name":"SOUTH AFRICA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to:\r\n\r\n- analyze the current surface conditions using scatterometer and altimeter data;\r\n\r\n- monitor the evolution of the surface conditions;\r\n\r\n- integrate these satellite data with data from numerical models, validating the model output;\r\n\r\n- access and visualize the data;\r\n\r\n- identify how the use of the wide range of products available from EUMETSAT, the Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service and other Copernicus partners, can improve the quality of marine analysis.","summary":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for marine weather forecasting to professionals with some previous experie","content":"The course covers: \r\n\r\n- Overview and practice on EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine products with relevance to marine forecasting; \r\n\r\n- Waves from Space (Altimeters);\r\n\r\n- Winds from Space (Scatterometers).","targetAudience":"Experts from operational centers with responsibilities to monitor African Waters, with all levels of experience in the use of satellite data for marine analysis propose.","registrationHowto":"The applications will open soon!","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"even