":"Presentations by Mr Bodo Zeschke (BOM) and Mr. Rion Salman (BMKG Indonesia).","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"As for all VLab RFG sessions attendance is free of charge. The Webinar web conferencing software will be used and you can attend the session by using the link https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/6023501124702795778","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5860,"name":"Bodo Zeschke","email":"bodo.zeschke@bom.gov.au","agency":"","country":"AU","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1670,"created":1519057144000,"updated":1521625759000,"title":"Satellite Application Course (SAC-VII) ","titleNative":"Satellite Application Course (SAC-VII) ","startDate":1543190400000,"endDate":1543536000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Pretoria","host":"South African Weather Service (SAWS) ","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The objective of the satellite applications training course is to optimise the use of data from meteorological satellites and to increase the knowledge and skills of meteorological trainers, contributing to improve forecasting.","country":{"id":"ZA","name":"SOUTH AFRICA","region":"RA-I","type":"RA-I"},"learningOutcome":"Improved skills in: (a) Identifying key weather systems and features found in Africa and their characteristics in satellite imagery and products; (b) Being a competent user of virtual course technology; (c) Developing relationships with course participants via the discussion forums and online briefings.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"The systems and features that are addressed in this course include: ITCZ, anticyclones, tropical lows, convective systems, dust storms and fog and low clouds. \r\n\r\nThe course only addresses system/feature identification in satellite imagery, it does not cover forecasting.","targetAudience":"PRs are invited to nominate up to two candidates. Candidates should either be instructors in satellite meteorology, operational forecasters or experienced satellite data users, with the ability to pass on skills acquired at the course to other operational staff.","registrationHowto":"Application will open soon!\r\n\r\nThe course is intended primarily for participants from Africa nominated by their Permanent Representatives with WMO. Depending on the seat availability, additional online participants can be accepted. \r\n\r\nThe nominated candidates are requested to apply to the online course by completing an online questionnaire. Applications open 12 March 2018 and close 13 April 2018. \r\n\r\nLink for application: http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158.  ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1713,"created":1536329755000,"updated":1593001430000,"title":"Accessing and working with state of the art satellite data for marine applications","titleNative":"Accessing and working with state of the art satellite data for marine applications","startDate":1543104000000,"endDate":1543190400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Iloilo","host":"University of Philippines Visayas","contactPerson":"Hayley Evers-King","contactEmail":"hek@pml.ac.uk","contactUrl":"https://pml.ac.uk/getattachment/Media_and_Events/Events_(1)/Registration_now_open_EUMETSAT_Workshop_Accessing/Registration_Satellite_Data_Course.pdf","description":"Satellite data provides information on the marine environment that can be used for many applications. The most modern generation of satellites offer improvements in spatial and temporal resolution as well as a constantly evolving suite of products.\r\n\r\n Data from the European Union Copernicus programme is open and free for everyone to use however they wish - whether from academic, governance, or commercial backgrounds. The programme has an operational focus, with satellite constellations offering continuity of service for the foreseeable future. There is a growing availability of open source tools that can be used to work with this data.\r\n\r\nThis course is a collaboration between EUMETSAT, PEMSEA, POGO, and ACCORD.\r\n\r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"PH","name":"PHILIPPINES","region":"RA-V","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will gain knowledge of the Copernicus programme and satellite data products available from Sentinel 3. They will also learn how to use open source software for data access and analysis.","summary":null,"content":"Satellite data provides information on the marine environment that can be used for many applications. The most modern generation of satellites offer improvements in spatial and temporal resolution as well as a constantly evolving suite of products.\r\n\r\n Data from the European Union Copernicus programme is open and free for everyone to use however they wish - whether from academic, governance, or commercial backgrounds. The programme has an operational focus, with satellite constellations offering continuity of service for the foreseeable future. There is a growing availability of open source tools that can be used to work with this data.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nThis training course is an opportunity to learn about the data available from Copernicus and other relevant Earth Observation programmes, and then provide opportunities to develop your own workflows for using data from the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream, using the Sentinel Applications Platform (SNAP) software, and Python programming.\r\n","targetAudience":"Stakeholders in the marine environment whose work (research, commercial, governance, or otherwise) may benefit from the use of marine satellite data. ","registrationHowto":"Please see details here: https://pml.ac.uk/getattachment/Media_and_Events/Events_(1)/Registration_now_open_EUMETSAT_Workshop_Accessing/Registration_Satellite_Data_Course.pdf","registrationEndDate":1538352000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5850,"name":"Hayley Evers-King","email":"Hayley.EversKing@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"DE","pr