 will use QGIS, the R statistical program, and the Random Forest algorithm. Both sessions will feature a lecture, time to complete a hands-on exercise, and time for questions. Fridays, September 28 and October 5, with the same content being presented at 10:00 and 18:00 EDT (UTC-4). ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: \r\n\r\nBecome familiar with Landsat bands and color combinations;\r\nUnderstand how to visualize change in land cover using Landsat data;\r\n\r\nLearn the basic steps for change detection by:\r\n\r\nConducting image subtraction between two dates using QGIS;\r\nCreating multi-date Landsat layer stacks;\r\nConducting multi-date land cover classification using the Random Forest classification in R;\r\nIdentifying and analyzing changes in land cover\r\n","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in assessing vegetation conditions and analyzing land cover changes using satellite imagery.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free and open, but you must register at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/land/webinars/adv-change18?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=change to guarantee your place.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPa