erence 2018","startDate":1537142400000,"endDate":1537488000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Tallinn","host":"Estonian Environment Agency","contactPerson":"","contactEmail":"","contactUrl":"","description":"EUMETSAT has organised a meteorological satellite conference every year for over thirty years. During that time, the conference has become a key annual event for the meteorological and scientific communities where participants from around the world can meet to share their experience and knowledge during plenary, poster and workshop sessions.\r\n\r\nThe 2018 conference will discuss such topics as preparing for MTG and EPS-SG, atmospheric chemistry monitoring and applications, and climate and ocean monitoring. The conference location also lends itself to discussions on the topics of observations for the Baltic Basin, as well as Arctic monitoring and applications.\r\n","country":{"id":"EE","name":"ESTONIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"EUMETSAT has organised a meteorological satellite conference every year for over thirty years. During that time, the conference has become a key annual event for the meteorological","content":"","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"Conference webpage: https://www.eumetsat.int/website/home/News/ConferencesandEvents/DAT_3647214.html\r\n\r\nAbstract submission: 1 December 2017  31 January 2018\r\n\r\nThe Second Announcement will be available from mid May 2018 and will be published on the conference webpage (https://www.eumetsat.int/website/home/News/ConferencesandEvents/DAT_3647214.html).\r\n\r\nThe early registration conference fee is EUR 350 (higher if payment is made after the initial registration deadline). Further details on registration fees, deadlines and payment will be provided in the Second Announcement.\r\n","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":102,"value":"Conference"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1704,"created":1531482293000,"updated":1532590162000,"title":"Live Training on Satellite & NWP integration for Convection & Fog ","titleNative":"Live Training on Satellite & NWP integration for Convection & Fog ","startDate":1536915600000,"endDate":1536919200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"IMTR SAWS","contactPerson":"Training","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://met-learning.webex.com/met-learning/k2/j.php?MTID=t4bf39984c5926cf12563b8c5e2003ad3","description":"Operational meteorologists use the Satellite and NWP information for understanding the weather situation better and for preparing weather forecasts for their users and the general public. Integrating the Satellite and NWP information is a necessary skill for forecasters, and helps them to make decisions about the model performance and its impact to their forecasts. \r\n\r\nThis online session will introduce two weather features, convection and fog, and with some examples demonstrate good practices how to integrate satellite and NWP information to better monitor these features. \r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutc