a el Monitoreo de la Calidad del Agua","startDate":1536152400000,"endDate":1537362000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://go.nasa.gov/2AcZXMI","description":"Polluted water influences all aspects of life, including people, animals, and the environment. NASA satellite observations provide near real-time information about water quality. This freely available data can help decision-makers in their work. Satellite data can have applications for managing drinking water, public health, and fisheries.\r\n\r\nThis webinar series will help attendees perform advanced image processing of satellite data. Attendees will also learn about using satellites to track indicators of harmful algal blooms. This will include monitoring water temperature and chlorophyll-a concentrations. Attendees can also use this information for reporting around UN SDG 6.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to: Access MODIS and Landsat data; Perform image processing of MODIS and Landsat data: and Monitor water temperature and chlorophyll-a concentrations as harmful algal bloom indicators  ","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"This training will be focused at water resource managers, water intake managers, and fishery and aquaculture managers and farmers.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free and open but you must register. Please only register for one of the daily sessions by following instructions at https://go.nasa.gov/2AcZXMI","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null