"Participants will be able to handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as climate data operators (cdo) and R (see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/ for further information) and QGIS) and know how to use CM SAF data in their daily work.","summary":"The key objective of this Workshop is to instruct active and future users from Regional Climate Centres (RCCs), Regional Training Centres (RTCs), and National Meteorological Serv","content":"Participants will learn how to access and handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as R, see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/ for further information) and explore the opportunities to use CM SAF and other satellite data to fulfill and improve their institutes services.","targetAudience":"Science and technical staff from RCCs, RTCs, and NMHSs in Africa applying climate data. A profound knowledge of the English language is mandatory for participation. Basic programming / scripting capabilities are of major advantage.","registrationHowto":"Applications for this event will open soon and you will be able to apply for it using the following link: http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158. \r\n","registrationEndDate":1525046400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EU