 the end of the course the trainees should be able to recognize convective clouds and forecast storm development stages and propagation using satellite, radar and NWP products within the Nowcasting web tool developed by CPTEC.","summary":null,"content":"The course will present the following topics: 1. Immediate weather forecasting, 2. What is a satellite imagery?, 3. What is a meteorological radar?, 4. General view of Lightning, 5. Using the Nowcasting web-based tool.","targetAudience":"Operational meteorologists for regional centers and civil defense.","registrationHowto":"For registration requests, please contact the Course Team at treinamento.urc@inpe.br","registrationEndDate":1533556800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2842,"name":"Natalia Rudorff","email":"natalia.rudorff@inpe.br","agency":"INPE","country":"BR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":5,"value":"Portuguese","iso639":"pt"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[{"id":10,"value":"PWS: Advisors Supporting Disaster Prevention and Mitigation and Other User Activities"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1700,"created":1531331008000,"updated":1531335790000,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Radar Remote Sensing for Land, Water, & Disaster Applications ","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Radar Remote Sensing for Land, Water, & Disaster Applications ","startDate":1533600000000,"endDate":1534377600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/advanced-SAR-18","description":"A limitation of optical satellite remote sensing is that it depends on cloudless, well-illuminated areas to produce quality data. This is especially problematic for collecting data during nighttime or when there is cloud cover. Radar is an ideal sensor to study the surface of the Earth because of its ability to see through clouds regardless of day or night conditions. In addition, the radar signal can penetrate through the vegetation canopy and provide information about conditions underneath, such as flooding. Techniques such as interferometry can track surface deformation on the order centimeters, such as ground movement caused by earthquakes.\r\n\r\nThis webinar series builds on ARSET's previous webinar: Introduction to Synthetic Aperture Radar. The training will focus on different radar approaches and techniques including amplitude, time-series, polarimetry, and interferometry for mapping and monitoring disasters and land cover. Attendees will apply these techniques to map land cover and land use change, deforestation, flooding, crop monitoring, and surface deformation for earthquake monitoring.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to understand how to use SAR data to map deforestation, flooding, crop growth, and surface deformation as a result of an earthquake.","summary":null,"content":"Tuesdays and Thursdays, August 7, 9, 14, and 16. One session will be broadcast in Spanish (10:00-12:00 EDT, UTC-4) and one in English 18:00-20:00 EDT (UTC-4).","targetAudience":"Remote sensing users from local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in using SAR for terrestrial applications such as inundation mapping, land cover land use change studies, and surface deformation for volcanic and earthquake activity.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free and open but you must register. One session of this training will be held in Spanish and one in English. Links to register are available in the webinar page at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/advanced-SAR-18","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "},{"id":10,"value":"PWS: Advisors Supporting Disaster Prevention and Mitigation and Other User Activities"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1658,"created":1515770264000,"updated":1521109644000,"title":"Workshop on the Use of Gridded Satellite Data for Climate Services - Online phase","titleNative":"Workshop on the Use of Gridded Satellite Data for Climate Services","startDate":1532908800000,"endDate":1533859200000,"tbdDate"