s","visible":false},{"id":3,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Argentina","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1699,"created":1531323395000,"updated":1531326454000,"title":"Monitoring Urban Floods Using Remote Sensing","titleNative":"Monitoring Urban Floods Using Remote Sensing","startDate":1532476800000,"endDate":1533081600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/urban-flooding-18?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=urban_flooding","description":"Online Course Dates and Times: Wednesdays, July 25th and August 1st, 2018. There are 2 identical sessions provided twice per day to accommodate an international audience. 09:00-11:00 and 18:00-20:00 EDT (UTC-4)\r\n\r\nUrban flooding is already a major risk for cities. Increasing impervious surface area, inadequate storm water drainage, and aging infrastructure all contribute. As a result, growing urban populations will face a greater risk of flooding from extreme weather events. This webinar series will focus on the components of urban flooding that satellite data can track:\r\n\r\n·  extreme precipitation\r\n\r\n·  flooding\r\n\r\n·  waterlogged and ponded surfaces\r\n\r\nUsing satellite data allows individuals and organizations to develop better plans for handling floods. This can include developing better early warning techniques, better plans for rescue and relief, and more effective long-term infrastructure planning. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Learning Objectives: By the end of the training, attendees will be able to:\r\n\r\n·  Describe remote sensing and Earth system model data useful for flood monitoring in urban areas\r\n\r\n·  Identify how remote sensing can aid in planning early warning systems, flood response, and flood recovery efforts","summary":null,"content":" ","targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for urban water and disaster managers, urban planners, emergency responders, transportation and utility providers and planners, public health professionals, and the insurance sector.\r\n\r\n ","registrationHowto":"Registration: This webinar is free and open but you must register. Please only register for one of the daily sessions: You can check your local time to select your session preference. Registration links are available in the announcement page at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/urban-flooding-18?utm_source=social&utm_medium=ext&utm_campaign=urban_flooding","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":110,"value":"NASA","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[],"qualification":[{"id":15,"value":"Training: Education and Training Providers "},{"id":10,"value":"PWS: Advisors Supporting Disaster Prevention and Mitigation and Other User Activities"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1693,"created":1527441257000,"updated":1527587998000,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Techniques for Wildfire Detection and Monitoring","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Techniques for Wildfire Detection and Monitoring","startDate":1531404000000,"endDate":1532016000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/land/webinars/adv-wildfire-2018","description":"Certain areas are experiencing longer fire seasons, with more frequent and severe droughts. Wildfire detection, monitoring, and mitigation is increasingly important in these regions. Satellite remote sensing data is useful for identifying active fires, evaluating burned areas, and assessing fire emissions. \r\n\r\nThursdays, July 12 and July 19, 2018. There are 2 identical sessions provided twice per day to accommodate an international audience. 10:00-12:00 and 18:00-20:00 EDT (UTC-4).","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the training, attendees will be able to:\r\nIdentify active fires, visualize fire emissions, and calculate burn severity\r\nUse the QGIS FMT to enter fire information and order imagery.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"This advanced training will highlight tools useful for local fire managers. Presentations and exercises will introduce participants to tools to identify active fires, visualize fire emissions, and calculate burn severity.","targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations  involved in wildfire management.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free and open but you must register