"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"},{"id":7,"value":"Spanish","iso639":"es"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1667,"created":1519052057000,"updated":null,"title":"IOCCG Summer Lecture Series 2018","titleNative":"IOCCG Summer Lecture Series 2018","startDate":1529884800000,"endDate":1467849600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Villefranche-sur-Mer","host":"Laboratoire d'Océanographie de Villefranche-sur-Mer (LOV)","contactPerson":"Copernicus Training Team","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The International Ocean Colour Coordinating Group (IOCCG) Summer Lecture Series is dedicated to high-level training in the fundamentals of ocean optics, bio-optics and ocean colour remote sensing. \r\n","country":{"id":"FR","name":"FRANCE","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"The emphasis of the course will be on current critical issues in ocean colour science, and will consist of lectures by specialists as well as a few hands-on practical sessions. Participants should be familiar with downloading and processing satellite ocean colour imagery.  Lectures will tentatively cover the following topics (final agenda to be provided at a later date):\r\nFundamentals of inherent and apparent optical properties (IOPs and AOPs);\r\nOptics of marine particles;\r\nIntroduction to hydrolight;\r\nOcean scattering;\r\nRadiometry, AOPs, measurements and uncertainties;\r\nAtmospheric correction;\r\nOcean colour remote sensing in turbid waters;\r\nShallow water remote sensing;\r\nPractical ac-labs;\r\nUsing the Copernicus data sets (practical sessions).\r\n","targetAudience":"This training course is open to young graduate scientists and post-doctoral fellows with a strong background in ocean optics, as well as researchers with a longer record in ocean colour research hoping to broaden their knowledge. ","registrationHowto":"Prospective  students can apply online at:  http://ioccg.org/what-we-do/training-and-education/ioccg-sls-2018/ (deadline 5 March 2018).\r\n\r\nThere is no fee for the lecture series but students are expected to cover some of their own expenses including meals, taxis and airfare. Free accommodation will be available for all students.","registrationEndDate":1520208000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":80,"value":"Other","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1695,"created":1529076274000,"updated":1529076354000,"title":"GEONETCast Americas User Group Webinar","titleNative":"GEONETCast Americas User Group Webinar","startDate":1529510400000,"endDate":1529517600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA GNC-A","contactPerson":"Natalia Donoho","contactEmail":"natalia.donoho@noaa.gov","contactUrl":"http://bit.ly/GNC-A ","descriptio