DataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1843,"created":1576840570000,"updated":null,"title":"ESSL Testbed","titleNative":"ESSL Testbed","startDate":1529280000000,"endDate":1531440000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Wiener Neustadt","host":"European Severe Storms Laboratory ","contactPerson":"Pieter Groenemeijer","contactEmail":"events@essl.org","contactUrl":"","description":"A number of new Testbed products and parameters will be evaluated. They include:\r\n\r\ntemperature and humidity profiles from the hyperspectral sounder instrument IASI, and derived convective parameters in cooperation with EUMETSAT\r\nvarious instability parameters based on the newest version of the ECMWF Integrated Forecast System\r\nthe latest version of the nowcasting system NowcastMIX of the German weather service DWD","country":{"id":"AT","name":"AUSTRIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"A number of new Testbed products and parameters will be evaluated. They include:\r\n\r\ntemperature and humidity profiles from the hyperspectral sounder instrument IASI, and derived co","content":"","targetAudience":"The goal of the Testbed is twofold. First, it caters forecasters who want to learn how to forecast severe convective storms using state-of-the-art forecasting tools. Second, it is a hands-on evaluation of new, sometimes experimental, forecast products. This means that both forecasters and developers of forecast products have an interest in the Testbed. In addition, other people having a background in meteorology are most welcome to participate as well. Still unsure, if the Testbed is the right activity for you? Try out our new Quiz!","registrationHowto":"","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"Yes","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5841,"name":"Regina Hoefenmayer","email":"regina.hoefenmayer@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":false,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1666,"created":1519051165000,"updated":1523355946000,"title":"International Summer School on Applications with the Newest Multi-Spectral Environmental Satellites ","titleNative":"International Summer School on Applications with the Newest Multi-Spectral Environmental Satellites ","startDate":1528675200000,"endDate":1529452800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Bracciano","host":"CNMCA/CIMSS","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"Focus on the explanation of methods and techniques used to extract information from environmental satellite data, with emphasis on the latest measuring technologies. ","country":{"id":"IT","name":"ITALY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"","summary":"Focus on the explanation of methods and techniques used to extract information from environmental satellite data, with emphasis on the latest measuring technologies. ","content":"","targetAudience":"This courses addresses experienced professionals working with remote sensing data (forecasters, researchers, post-gradate students etc.) interested to update their knowledge and skills on the newest developments in remote sensing data. The applicants must have an academic degree either in Meteorology, Physics, Environmental Sciences or Environmental Engineering. Applicants should be proficients in the English language to attend the course.\r\nThe course is intended primarily for the European audience, with preference for the member states. Depending on availability, additional applicants might be accepted. Candidates will be selected on the basis of their proven experiences in environmental remote sensing. ","registrationHowto":"In order to apply for this training event please use the following link: http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 . ","registrationEndDate":1524787200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1621,"created":1509716024000,"updated":1521109626000,"title":"Operational Marine Forecasting using EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream - Classroom Phase","titleNative":"Operational Marine Forecasting using EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream - Classroom Phase","startDate":1528070400000,"endDate":1528416000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Lisbon","host":"Instituto Português do Mar e da Atmosfera (IPMA)","contactPerson":"Copernicus Training Team","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for marine weather forecasting to professionals with some previous experience. \r\nWe will focus on the application of data from Sentinel-3, Jason-3 and use of associated data such as EUMETSATs Scatterometers. \r\nThis is a blended course, composed of a 2 weeks online phase and a 5 days face-to-face phase. The online phase will occur from 2 to 13 April 2018 and is mandatory for classroom participants. The classroom phase will deepen the topics discussed during the Online phase. \r\nThe online (asynchronous) component will include recorded lectures, modules, readings and quizzes. This will take two weeks, including approximately 3 hours of individual work per week. The course will finish with a Workshop phase, with practical sessions, supported by lectures on how to make an efficient operational use of the data.  \r\nCompletion of the online phase is a prerequisite for the Workshop.\r\n","country":{"id":"PT","name":"PORTUGAL","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to:\r\n- analyze  the current surface conditions using scatterometer and altimeter data;\r\n- monitor the evolution of the surface conditions;\r\n- integrate these satellite data with data from numerical models, validating the model output;\r\n- access and visualize the data;\r\n- identify how the use of the wide range of products available from  EUMETSAT, the Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service and other Copernicus partners, can improve the quality of marine analysis.\r\n","summary":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for marine weather forecasting to professionals with some previous experie","content":"The course covers: \r\n- Overview and practice on EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine products with relevance to marine forecasting; \r\n- Waves from Space (Altimeters);\r\n- Winds from Space (Scatterometers).","targetAudience":"The course is primarily intended for experts from operational centers with responsibility of monitoring seas on the Atlantic coasts and Mediterranean Sea, with all levels of experience in the use of satellite data for marine analysis propose.","registrationHowto":"The applications are closed!\r\nTo attend the event, an application is required and must be made through http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 , until 02 March 2018.\r\nFor the Workshop phase, EUMETSAT can support a limited number of participants with travel or/and subsistence, this must be indicated at the time application. This is possible through support from the European Commission. \r\nThere is no event fee. \r\n","registrationEndDate":1519948800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1675,"created":1521122404000,"update