,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1615,"created":1509098111000,"updated":1521109434000,"title":"Baltic+ 2018 - Classroom phase","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2018 - Classroom phase","startDate":1521504000000,"endDate":1521676800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Riga","host":"Latvian Environment Geology and Meteorology Centre","contactPerson":"Andis Rembergs","contactEmail":"lvgmc@lvgmc.lv ","contactUrl":"","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\nThis is a blended course, composed of a 3 weeks online phase and a 3 days face-to-face phase. The online phase will occur from 19 February to 09 March 2018 and is mandatory for classroom participants. The classroom phase will deepen the topics discussed during the Online phase. \r\nThe online (asynchronous) component will include reading materials, exercises and collaborative case study preparatory work. This will take three weeks, including approximately 4 hours of individual work per week. The course will finish with a three-day-classroom course that will consist of exercises, presentations, group work and finalization of case studies started during the online phase. ","country":{"id":"LV","name":"LATVIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to: \r\n- Understand what are the factors that determine additional weather phenomena  hail, wind gusts, heavy precipitation etc. - in non-frontal features and how they can be forecast using satellite images; \r\n- Interpret different non-frontal features using satellite images; \r\n- Improve communication skills between forecasters and clients, media and public, especially on local weather features; \r\n- Apply gained knowledge to improve forecasting skills in local weather features and phenomena.\r\n ","summary":null,"content":"The core topics at the course in 2018 will be:\r\n- operational use of satellite data for non-frontal meso-scale weather systems; \r\n- use of different satellite products derived from the SAF network and the latest multispectral environmental satellite applications;\r\n- communication between different national meteorological services, the media and the general public from a forecaster's perspective.\r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"The course is primarily aimed at weather forecasters working in shifts with at least six months professional experience.","registrationHowto":"Please use email lvgmc@lvgmc.lv for further information on how to apply for this course. \r\nFor the classroom phase, EUMETSAT will support a limited number of participants with travel or/and subsistence.\r\nParticipants are advised to have personal travel and medical insurance. Neither EUMETSAT nor the local organizer are responsible for any incident that could occur during the course.\r\n ","registrationEndDate":1511740800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previ