ls in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for oceanographic appli","content":"The course covers: \r\nOverview and practice on EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine products with relevance to applications in oceanography.","targetAudience":"The workshop is dedicated to (early carrier) scientists: Master / PhD students, Post-Docs, and also experienced scientists with an interest in working with satellite based ocean observation data. Participants should have some working experience in either SNAP, a scripting language such as Python or similar.","registrationHowto":"The applications are closed!\r\n\r\nThere is no course fee. \r\n\r\nEUMETSAT supports a limited number of participants with travel or/and accommodation upon request. \r\n\r\nParticipants are advised to have personal travel and medical insurance. Neither EUMETSAT nor IODE are responsible for any incident that could occur during the course.\r\n","registrationEndDate":1518566400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1642,"created":1511779769000,"updated":1519027700000,"title":"Satellite Application Course on Tropical Cyclones","titleNative":"Satellite Application Course on Tropical Cyclones","startDate":1520726400000,"endDate":1521072000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Muscat","host":"Public Authority for Civil Aviation (PACA)","contactPerson":"Mahmood Al-Khayari","contactEmail":"mahmwood@gmail.com","contactUrl":"","description":"This course will cover the Tropical Cyclones, the basics of remote sensing and application of satellite data to regional forecasting problems. It is aimed at operational weather forecasters.","country":{"id":"OM","name":"OMAN","region":"RA-II","type":"Middle East"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn to:\r\nDescribe tropical cyclone climatology in the Indian Ocean (where and when they form);\r\nIdentify distinguishing features of tropical cyclone structure;\r\nDescribe ingredients needed for tropical cyclone genesis;\r\nDefine the stages of a tropical cyclone lifecycle;\r\nDetect cloud types in tropical cyclones using satellite remote sensing;\r\nDetect TC centre by use of IR/VIS imagery, microwave imagery/products and scatterometer winds;\r\nLearn key microwave techniques for estimating rainfall in the next 24/48 hours;\r\nDetect changes in tropical cyclone intensity using satellite remote sensing, in particular the use of the Dvorak TC intensity estimation technique;\r\nDescribe key storm and environmental factors that affect  tropical cyclone intensity;\r\nDescribe the mechanisms that influence tropical cyclone motion;\r\nDescribe the basic mechanisms for tropical cyclone hazards particularly those at landfall.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"Classification methods of Tropical Cyclone (e.g Devorak); Identification of TC features using Satellite Pictures; Tracking tropical cyclone methods (the use of 1,2,3 rule; The added values of the existing METOSAT 8 over the region (Arabian sea); Estimation of rainfall using satellite products (e.g MPE, TRRM, GPM); 