n shifts with at least six months professional experience.","registrationHowto":"For further information on how to apply for this course please use the email lvgmc@lvgmc.lv .\r\nPlease note that the online phase is mandatory for classroom participants.\r\nFor the classroom phase, EUMETSAT supports a limited number of participants with travel or/and subsistence.\r\nParticipants are advised to have personal travel and medical insurance. Neither EUMETSAT nor the local organizer are responsible for any incident that could occur during the course.\r\n ","registrationEndDate":1511740800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5842,"name":"Vesa Nietosvaara","email":"vesa.nietosvaara@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[{"id":8,"value":"PWS: Weather Broadcasters and Communicators"},{"id":13,"value":"PWS: Public Weather Forecasters"},{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1655,"created":1515006622000,"updated":1515061422000,"title":"Introduction to Using the VIC Hydrologic Model with NASA Earth Observations","titleNative":"Introduction to Using the VIC Hydrologic Model with NASA Earth Observations","startDate":1518652800000,"endDate":1519862400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/water/webinars/VIC18","description":"Hydrologic modeling is useful for flood, drought, and water resources management. The Variable Infiltration Capacity (VIC) Model uses inputs to better understand hydrological processes in near real-time. Many of the inputs are available from NASA remote sensing and Earth system models, allowing the model to provide soil moisture, evapotranspiration and runoff as outputs. Together with precipitation data, these outputs provide quantitative assessment of a regional water budget. This introductory training will include an overview of the model, sources of satellite-derived input data, and implementation of the model. \r\n\r\nCourse Dates:  Three, 1 hour sessions. Sessions will be held on Thursdays, February 15  March 1 from 09:00  10:00 and 18:00  19:00 EST (UTC -5). The session is broadcast twice per day to allow for international participation.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to download, install, and use the VIC model, setup VIC for a watershed or river basin using remote sensing data inputs, and analyze output water resources components\r\n","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for water resources professionals and disaster managers from local, state, and federal agencies, NGOs, and the private sector.","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register through the training's webpage. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1654,"created":1515006297000,"updated":1515061555000,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Accuracy Assessment of a Land Cover Classification","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Accuracy Assessment of a Land Cover Classification","startDate":1518480000000,"endDate":1519084800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/land/webinars/18adv-land-classification","description":"In last years ARSET Advanced Webinar: Land Cover Classification with Satellite Imagery, attendees learned the basic steps to create a supervised land cover classification. The next step to using land cover classifications is being able to evaluate the performance of a land cover map using accuracy assessments. This training will equip attendees to conduct an accuracy assessment on a land cover map and identify which classes might be misrepresented.\r\n\r\nCourse Dates: Two, 2 hour sessions. Sessions will be held on Tuesdays, February 13 and 20, 2018, at 11:00-13:00 or 23:00-01:00 EST (UTC-5). The session is broadcast twice per day to allow for international participation.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, attendees will be able to conduct an accuracy assessment on a land cover map, understand how to create and use reference data, become familiar with sample designs for accuracy assessment, and develop and interpret an error matrix and a Kappa statistic.","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"This training is primarily intended for local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in assessing vegetation condition using satellite imagery.","registrationHowto":"There is no cost for the webinar, but you must register through the training's webpage. ","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1602,"created":null,"updated":1521109388000,"title":"Copernicus Marine Data in Ocean Models and for Operational Applications - Classroom phase","titleNative":"Copernicus Marine Data in Ocean Models and for Operational Applications - Classroom phase","startDate":1517788800000,"endDate":1518134400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Hamburg","host":"Federal Maritime and Hydrographic Agency of Germany (BSH) ","contactPerson":"Copernicus Training Team","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"This user training event being organised by EUMETSAT on behalf of the European Commission as part of the Copernicus Programme, together with its Satellite Application Facility on Ocean and Sea Ice (OSI), the COST Action ES1402 Evaluation of Ocean Synthesis and the Federal Maritime and Hydrographic Agency of Germany (BSH).\r\nThe key objective of this Workshop is to:\r\nSelect appropriate data and/or products from the ocean related Copernicus data providers and Services, for tasks in the fields of a) Ocean / Earth System Modelling and b) Operational Ocean Applications. The variables addressed will be SST, wind/stress, sea ice, ocean colour, and related products;\r\nApply these data / products in:\r\na) Ocean and Earth System Modelling;\r\nb) Operational tasks.\r\nDiscuss applications of Copernicus Marine Data and Products with other experts in the area.\r\n","country":{"id":"DE","name":"GERMANY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will learn:\r\n- What Copernicus Data Providers and Services exist and how they interact;\r\n- What Ocean related data / products are provided by the data providers and services (variables and their exact definition, timeliness, resolution, data format, spatial coverage). The variables addressed will be SST, wind/stress, sea ice, ocean colour, and related products;\r\n- To access / download data and products provided in the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CODA, EUMETSAT Data archive, EumetCAST) and by the Copernicus Marine Environment Monitoring Service (CMEMS);\r\n- To work with data from the EUMETSAT Copernicus Marine Data Stream and CMEMS products in: a) Ocean / Earth System Models; b) SNAP and GIS.\r\n- How other experts in the area are using/intend to use Copernicus Marine Data and Products;\r\n- About interfaces between the marine service with other Copernicus services such as land, atmosphere, and climate-monitoring services.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"This is a blended course, composed of a 2 weeks online phase and a 5 day face-to-face phase. The online phase will occur from 15 to 26 January 2018 and during these two weeks basic information will be provided, which are helpful during the face-to-face workshop. For ocean modellers, it is highly recommended to reserve approximately 10 hours per week to engage with the content.\r\n\r\nThe face-to-face phase will be composed of interactive discussions, group work, and practical exercises.\r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"The workshop is dedicated to Ocean / Earth System Modellers and users interested in Copernicus data for operational applications. Participants should have working experience in either:\r\na) at least one of the programming languages: FORTRAN, C, C++, R, Python;\r\nb) SNAP or GIS.\r\nWe invite:\r\na) (early career) scientists with working experience in Ocean / Earth System Modelling;\r\nb) users interested in Copernicus data for operational ocean / marine applications.\r\n","registrationHowto":"The applications are closed!\r\nIf you're interested to attend this event, please submit your application using the link: http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 \r\n- New application deadline: 6th December 2017\r\n\r\nFor the Workshop phase, the organizers can support a limited number of participants with travel and/or subsistence, this must be indicated at the time of application. \r\