t is expected that participants listening to the presenters will have a good overview of the products other countries, their colleagues, use in their daily warning issuing. Also since one of the topics is Communicating Warnings, this complex part of the forecasters shift will be covered and possibly some new ideas will rise in participants' minds on how to improve their own communication with stakeholders and give them the important information.","summary":"From 11 to 15 December 2017 EUMeTrain is running an event week on Warnings. There will be two main topics that will be covered during this week and these are: 'Effective Warning Me","content":"Presentations include: Warning strategy in Germany, Thomas Kratzsch (DWD); Aspects of forecasting excessive precipitation events in Germany  Examples from 2016, Marcus Beyer (DWD); Black Ice Case in January 2017, Lars Kirchhuebel (DWD); Avalanche Warning and Weather Forecast, Andreas Gobeit and Gernot Zenkl (ZAMG); EFI and SOT products, Ivan Tsonevsky (ECMWF); A case study of the severe storm from 11 July 2016, Izolda Marcinoniene (LHMS); Forecasting extreme weather using probabilistic tools, Shay Frenkel (IMS); Warning procedures at MeteoSwiss and the handling of a severe warning case, Daniel Murer (MeteoSwiss); Weather events connected with advection of warm tropic air mass into the middle latitude, Barbara Wrona (IMGW); Challenges of issuing meteorological warnings - The Portuguese experience, Nuno Moreira (IPMA); How we use social media to communicate a dangerous weather events?, Justyna Wodziczko (Met.No); Customers side of view, Jyri Silmari (Finnish Emergency Services Department); ANYWHERE in a nutshell, Ilona Láng and Tuomo Bergman (FMI); The ZAMG warning procedures presented on the basis of the late winter event 18th and 19thApril 2017, Thomas Turecek (ZAMG); Severe Weather follow-up product (LUOVA), A-J Punkka and Kaisa Solin (FMI); Warnings and interpretation  which is the weakest link?, Tamás Allaga (Met.Hungary)","targetAudience":"Primary target audience are weather forecasters working in shifts. Secondary audience is everybody interested in the process of delivering and managing warnings.","registrationHowto":"http://www.eumetrain.org/events/warning_week_2017_register.html","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":106,"value":"Seminar"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1609,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 16:00 UTC","titleNative":"RFG of Americas and the Caribbean - 16:00 UTC","startDate":1512662400000,"endDate":1512666000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NOAA and CoEs: Costa Rica/Barbados/Argentina/Brazil","contactPerson":"Bernie Connell","contactEmail":"bernie.connell@colostate.edu","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/2034292610574341889","description":"The sessions are bilingual (English and Spanish) and for WMO regions III (South America) and IV (Central America/Caribbean).  Session time is 16:00 UTC, but as usual, it will start 15 minutes earlier (at 15:45 UTC for those who want t