o instruct active and future users from Regional Climate Centres (RCCs), Regional Training Centres (RTCs), and National Meteorological Services in Africa in the use of CM SAF products for operational climate monitoring and climate research. The workshop will focus on project work with supporting presentations and group work on the application of satellite data to climate monitoring. There will be a classroom phase in Pretoria, South Africa from 20 to 24 November 2017. ","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as climate data operators (cdo) and R (see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/ for further information) and QGIS) and know how to use CM SAF data in their daily work.","summary":"The key objective of this Workshop is to instruct active and future users from Regional Climate Centres (RCCs), Regional Training Centres (RTCs), and National Meteorological Serv","content":"Participants will learn how to access and handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as R, see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/ for further information) and explore the opportunities to use CM SAF and other satellite data to fulfill and improve their institutes services.","targetAudience":"Science and technical staff from RCCs, RTCs, and NMHSs in Africa applying climate data. A profound knowledge of the English language is mandatory for participation. Basic programming / scripting capabilities are of major advantage.","registrationHowto":"The applications are closed.","registrationEndDate":1503014400000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1559,"created":null,"updated":1511522785000,"title":"Using the Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications - Online phase","titleNative":"Using the Copernicus Marine Data Stream for Ocean Applications - Online phase","startDate":1508716800000,"endDate":1509062400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"","contactPerson":"Copernicus Training Team","contactEmail":"copernicus.training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"https://www.eumetsat.int/website/home/TechnicalBulletins/Training/DAT_3460360.html","description":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for oceanographic applications.\r\nWe will focus on the application of data from Sentinel-3.\r\nThe online phase will be followed by a classroom training, held in Accra, Ghana, from 6 to 10 November 2017.\r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"After the course participants will be able to: \r\n- name data/products provided in the CMDS with relevance to their work (variables, timeliness, resolution, data format)\r\n- be able to access / download data and products provided in the Copernicus Marine Data Stream (CODA, EUMETSAT Data archive, EumetCAST)\r\n- be able to know how to work with CMDS data in SNAP, GIS, and / or a scripting language\r\n- be able to use data / products from the CMDS for their purposes.\r\n","summary":"The purpose of the event is to develop skills in using data from EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine Data Stream for oceanographic applications.\r\nWe will focus on the application of data ","content":"The course covers: \r\n- Overview and practice on EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine products with relevance to applications in oceanography","targetAudience":"The workshop is dedicated to (early carrier) scientists: Master / PhD students, Post-Docs, and also experienced scientists with an interest in working with satellite based ocean observation data. Participants should have some working experience in either SNAP, a scripting language such as R or similar, or GIS tools.","registrationHowto":"The applications are closed.","registrationEndDate":1501804800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1606,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Training on GOES-16 for Operational Meteorological Services","titleNative":"Treinamento em GOES-16 para Meteorologia Operacional","startDate":1508518800000,"endDate":1509390000000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Cachoeira Paulista","host":"INPE","contactPerson":"Daniel Vila","contactEmail":"daniel.vila@inpe.br","contactUrl":"","description":"This course is intended to train operational meteorologists to use GOES-16 imagery for weather forecasting and monitoring.","country":{"id":"BR","name":"BRAZIL","region":"RA-III","type":"Rest of the World"},"learningOutcome":"By the end of the course the meteorologists should be able to (i) describe the temporal, spatial and spectral resolutions of the ABI/GOES-16; (ii) associate each spectral channel to potential applications focused on weather monitoring; (iii) recognize and differentiate surface features over land (including vegetation, bare ground and snow/ice) and water (including sun glint) on ABI visible and near infrared (NIR) images; (iv) recognize cloud top structures and micro-physical properties (phase and particle size distribution) and level (high and low) using visible and NIR ABI images; (v) recognize cloud top properties (brightness temperature and associated microphysical properties) and levels, using the infrared channels; (vi) identify high, mid and low level water vapour content with each of the corresponding channels; (vii) identify air mass (polar and tropical), lower level humidity, high level dust and ash, fog and low clouds and cloud microphysics at day and night, using multichannel products with RGB composites; and (viii) identify synoptic and mesoscale meteorological phenomenon over Brazil and South America and interpret the features relevant for weather monitoring services using ABI channels and RGBs.        ","summary":null,"content":"The course is divided in 4 modules (~1h30 each): 1. Introduction to GOES-16, and the benefits of the next generation environmental satellites for weather monitoring. 2. ABI/GOES-16 spectral channels: radiative processes, characteristics and applications. 3. Multichannel products: RGBs, 4. Case studies for Brazil and South America: exploring the new capabilities.  ","targetAudience":"Operational Meteorologists of National and Regional Weather Services","registrationHowto":"By invitation only.","registrationEndDate":1508518800000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2842,"name":"Natalia Rudorff","email":"natalia.rudorff@inpe.br","agency":"INPE","country":"BR","programme":"VLab","trainingPartner":{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":23,"value":"INPE","visible":false},{"id":4,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Brazil","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":5,"value":"Portuguese","iso639":"pt"}],"regions":[{"id":3,"value":"III South America"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1604,"created":null,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","titleNative":"EUMeTrain Weather Briefing","startDate":1507809600000,"endDate":1507813200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"Marko Blaskovic","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"https://met-learning.webex.com/met-learning/k2/j.php?MTID=t1f4972ec02de41539169d119f7bae2fe","description":"Online weather discussion about the phenomena that occurred in the last month, after the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations. Every month an