nd Caribbean"}],"qualification":[{"id":17,"value":"Satellite Skills and Knowledge"}],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1584,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Advanced Webinar: Remote Sensing of Drought","titleNative":"Advanced Webinar: Remote Sensing of Drought","startDate":1499817600000,"endDate":1500422400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"NASA Applied Remote Sensing Training Program (ARSET)","contactPerson":"Brock Blevins","contactEmail":"brockbl1@umbc.edu","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/water/webinars/drought17","description":"Prolonged drought can result in economic, environmental, and health-related impacts. In this webinar, participants will learn how to monitor drought conditions and assess impacts on the ecosystem using precipitation, soil moisture, and vegetation data. The training will provide an overview of drought classification, as well as an introduction to web-based tools for drought monitoring and visualization. Lectures will be followed by hands-on demonstrations of data access and visualization.\r\n\r\n","country":null,"learningOutcome":"In this webinar, participants will learn how remote sensing can be used for drought monitoring, how to acquire remotely-sensed imagery and products for drought and analyze drought data and calculate anomalies within a geospatial software. ","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"Regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in using remote sensing to monitor drought.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free and open but you must register. Instructions to register are available at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/water/webinars/drought17","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5861,"name":"Brock Blevins","email":"brock.blevins@nasa.gov","agency":"","country":"US","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":25,"value":"NASA"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":nul