ited to nominate up to two candidates for this online course. Candidates should either be instructors in satellite meteorology, operational forecasters or experienced satellite data users, with the ability to pass on skills acquired at the course to other operational staff.","registrationHowto":"The nominated candidates are requested to apply to the online course by 28 April 2017 by completing an online questionnaire. Link for application: http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 \r\nThe applications are closed!","registrationEndDate":1493341200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":11,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence South Africa","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1534,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Basic Satellite Meteorology course for South Eastern European countries (SEEMET) ","titleNative":"Basic Satellite Meteorology course for South Eastern European countries (SEEMET) ","startDate":1494201600000,"endDate":1494547200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Bar","host":"Institute of Hydrometeorology and Seismology of Montenegro (ZHMS)","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":"Course on basic Satellite Meteorology for South Eastern European countries, covering basics of satellite meteorology and satellite image interpretation and their application in operational weather forecasting.","country":{"id":"ME","name":"MONTENEGRO","region":"RA-VI","type":"RA-VI"},"learningOutcome":"The course is expected to improve the skills of operational meteorologists in interpretation of satellite images and products, leading to improved competencies in short-term weather forecasting. The identified learning needs are: RGB interpretation, conceptual models, application to convection/thunderstorm and fog, marine forecasting, orography induced phenomena (like orographic precipitation), wild fires detection, air quality / pollution monitoring. The course should increase the skills of forecasters in identifying cloud features and weather phenomena with the support of satellite imagery.","summary":"Course on basic Satellite Meteorology for South Eastern European countries, covering basics of satellite meteorology and satellite image interpretation and their application in ope","content":"This event covers: \r\n\r\n- basics of satellite meteorology (remote sensing)  orbits, missions, resolutions, EM spectrum, instruments, products applications overview\r\n- satellite channels and their characteristics \r\n- conceptual models with single channels\r\n- practical work on RGB interpretation (fog, low level clouds, convection, pollution, fires, dust, cloud properties)\r\n- frontal analysis over Balkan regions, including sub-structure and embedded convection (practical work).","targetAudience":"The course is addressed to weather forecasters working in national hydro-meteorological institutes of South Eastern European countries. Primary countries: Montenegro, Albania, Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina, Republic of Srpska, FYROM, Kosovo, Serbia. Secondary countries: Slovenia, Croatia, Bulgaria, Romania, Hungary and Greece\r\n\r\nTotal about 21-23 students.","registrationHowto":"Only by invitation. Registration on EUMETCAL page https://www.webropolsurveys.com/S/965455EA7CF8C353.par . EUMETSAT will support a limited number of participants from SE European countries.","registrationEndDate":1489104000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":25,"name":"Jochen Kerkmann","email":"jochen.kerkmann@web.de","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":2,"value":"By invitation only"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true},{"id":30,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":true},{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":70,"value":"NHMS","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":16,"value":"Eumetcal","visible":false},{"id":17,"value":"EuMeTrain","visible":false},{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":101,"value":"Serbo-Croatian","iso639":"sh"},{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1558,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Course on the Use of Satellite Products for drought monitoring and Agro-Meteorological Applications","titleNative":"Course on the Use of Satellite Products for drought monitoring and Agro-Meteorological Applications","startDate":1492992000000,"endDate":1493337600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Budapest","host":"OSMZ","contactPerson":"EUMETSAT Training Team","contactEmail":"training@eumetsat.int","contactUrl":"","description":" Expand the use of Land-SAF and Hydrology SAF products and other agencies related products among the  European agrometeorologists and water managers to enhance the benefits derived and to collect and exchange experience from that use; \r\n Development of capacity building at the NMHS and Ministries of Agriculture in Central and Eastern Europe in relation with vegetation status monitoring, soil moisture, rainfall estimations, sand and dust warnings, radiative balance and land use;\r\n Institutional cooperation reinforcement between EUMETSAT, WMO, FAO  and the National Institutions of the region in terms of satellite product utilization and reception stations optimization for drought management and agriculture production; \r\n Development of the cooperation between the Drought Management Centre for South Eastern Europe and other WMO and FAO partners at the Region. To benefit from their experience and methods in drought monitoring and institutional agreements. \r\n Development of effective partnership and work among Hungarian national institutions.    \r\n","country":{"id":"HU","name":"HUNGARY","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"A better use of satellite products on vegetation evolution monitoring, soil moisture evaluation, radiative balance and rainfall estimations. It is expected an improvement into the agrometeorological bulletins by including relevant products based in satellite information as vegetation status changes or mixed satellite and ground based rainfall estimations at every participant country. A sound technical approach to drought monitoring by remote sensing carrying development of drought indexes as a first step towards development of drought indicators based on associated and confirmed impacts. ","summary":null,"content":"","targetAudience":"This course is devoted in non-exclusive basis to experts in agrometeorology in the NMHS and 