orological Services and from research institutions in the use of CM SAF products for operational climate monitoring and climate research.\r\nThe workshop will focus on the project work with supporting presentations and group work on the application of satellite data to climate monitoring.","country":{"id":"PL","name":"POLAND","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as climate data operators (cdo) and R (see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/  for further information) and QGIS) and know how to use CM SAF data in their daily work.","summary":"The key objective of this Workshop is to instruct active and future users from National Meteorological Services and from research institutions in the use of CM SAF products for ope","content":"Participants will learn how to handle CM SAF data using free software tools (such as climate data operators (cdo) and R (see http://www.cmsaf.eu/tools/  for further information) and QGIS) and explore the opportunities to use CM SAF data in their daily work.","targetAudience":"Climatologists at all levels of experience in the use of satellite data for climate applications from NMHSs, universities and other institutions applying climate data. A profound knowledge of the English language is mandatory for participation","registrationHowto":"To attend the event, confirmation is required and must be made through http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 , until 20 January 2017.","registrationEndDate":1484953200000,"fees":"","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5847,"name":"Christine Traeger Chatterjee","email":"christine.traeger@eumetsat.int","agency":"","country":"EM","programme":"","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1544,"created":null,"updated":1693586463000,"title":"Weather Briefing Online, 16th of March at 12 UTC","titleNative":"Weather Briefing Online, 16th of March at 12 UTC","startDate":1489665600000,"endDate":1489669200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"","host":"EUMeTrain","contactPerson":"Marko Blaskovic","contactEmail":"blaskovic@cirus.dhz.hr","contactUrl":"https://met-learning.webex.com/met-learning/k2/j.php?MTID=t6ba537f7ed23a63dc84801c6f22de91f","description":"Online weather discussion about the weather phenomena that occurred in the last month, after the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations. Every month another country, another presenter presents the weather events. The Weather Briefing is hosted by EUMeTrain. Any additional questions can be asked with the provided email.","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Gaining additional knowledge about analyzing weather situations using satellite data.","summary":"Online weather discussion about the weather phenomena that occurred in the last month, after the last weather briefing. Satellite imagery is used to discuss interesting situations.","content":"Every weather briefing has some new events that occurred in the last month.","targetAudience":"Anyone who is interested in learning or hearing something new about describing the weather situation using satellite imagery.","registrationHowto":"Click on the link above.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5837,"name":"Mark Higgins","email":"mark.higgins@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"EM","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT"},"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":40,"value":"EUMeTrain","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1540,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Satellite Derived Annual PM2.5 Data Sets in Support of United Nations Sustainable Development Goals","titleNative":"Satellite Derived Annual PM2.5 Data Sets in Support of United Nations Sustainable Development Goals","startDate":1489536000000,"endDate":1490745600000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NASA/ARSET","contactPerson":"ARSET","contactEmail":"nasa.arset@gmail.com","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/airquality/webinars/AQ-SDG-17","description":"Recently, annual mean PM2.5 maps have been developed using MODIS, MISR, and SeaWiFS observations from 1998-2015 and have been used by organizations, such as the World Health Organization (WHO) and Greenpeace, to assess global air quality and health impacts. In this webinar, participants will learn how to use this database to analyze PM2.5 over cities using satellite observations. This training will cover accessing the data, analyzing long-term trends, and combining PM2.5 and population data sets to understand long-term exposure.\r\nThere will be three online sessions in this course, 15, 22 and 29 March. Sessions will be broadcast twice per day to allow for international participation. Times will be as follows:  11:00-12:00 p.m. and  8:00-9:00 p.m. EDT (UTC-4).\r\nA certificate of completion will be provided to participants that attend the live webinars and complete all prerequisites and homework assignments.","country":null,"learningOutcome":"Attendees will: \r\n- Become familiar with the UN Sustainable Development Goals, as well as the satellite observations of air quality that are used to calculate indicators 3.9.1 and 11.6.2;\r\n- Learn about PM2.5 estimates made using satellite, surface, and model data sets;\r\n- Understand how to use the 2014 WHO data set and access the indicator data for a city or country.","summary":null,"content":"Prerequisites: \r\n- Complete Sessions 1 Fundamentals of Remote Sensing, or equivalent experience;\r\n- Complete Sessions 1, 2, and 4 of Satellite Remote Sensing of Particulate Matter Air Quality.\r\n*Links to the above prerequisites can be found in the course information page at https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/airquality/webinars/AQ-SDG-17\r\nAgenda:\r\n- Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and Relevant Air Quality Observations - March 15, 2017.\r\nThe goals, targets, and indicators of the UN sustainable development goals; the satellite observations of air quality that are used to calculate indicators 3.9.1 and 11.6.2; how satellite observations can fill in the gaps; and methodology and applications.\r\n- World Health Organization (WHO) PM2.5 Data Set - March 22, 2017.\r\nPM2.5 estimates using satellite, surface, and model data sets for 2014, released by the WHO; how the data applies to indicators 3.9.1 and 11.6.2; and methodology, limitations, and data access. \r\n- Case Study Analysis - March 29, 2017.\r\nUsing the 2014 WHO data set, read and convert the data for a region of interest, complete a mapping exercise, perform a case study analysis on spatial pattern comparisons for different cities, and learn to apply all the skills learned to create a time series once more data becomes available. ","targetAudience":"Agencies involved in addressing and reporting on United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), as well as, local, regional, state, federal, and international organizations interested in assessing PM2.5 air quality.","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free, but you must register by following link provided. Space is limited, and preference will be given to organizations in the public and private sectors involved in environmental management and monitoring over organizations focused primarily on research. You will be notified by email if your registration has been approved on or before March 8, 2017. Please only register for the session times that work best for your time zone. ","registrationEndDate":1488931200000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5852,"name":"Luciane Veeck","email":"lveeck@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central America and Caribbean"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1520,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Baltic+ 2017 - Classroom Phase","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2017 - Classroom Phase","startDate":1489449600000,"endDate":1489622400000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Vilnius","host":"Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service (LHMS)","contactPerson":"Izolda Marcinoniene","contactEmail":"contact@meteo.lt","contactUrl":"","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\n\r\n","country":{"id":"LT","name":"LITHUANIA","region":"RA-VI","type":"Member State"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to: \r\n- Select the most appropriate channels or combinations of channels for monitoring deep convection;\r\n- Interpret satellite data within the context of all other observations, guidance and situational awareness;\r\n- Understand the structure and evaluation of various clouds and convective systems; \r\n- Use satellite images to issue more precise forecasts and warnings; Use different SAF products for situation analysis; \r\n- Could take into account the main factors affecting satellite data quality and characteristics.\r\n","summary":null,"content":"This event covers: \r\n- Identification of convective cloud types, features and characteristics;\r\n- Understanding the atmospheric conditions favorable for deep convection. \r\n","targetAudience":"The course is primarily aimed at weather forecasters working in shifts with at least six months professional experience.","registrationHowto":"Please use email contact@meteo.lt for further information on how to apply for this course. Deadline for applications is 28 November 2016.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana B