s Group - 02:00 UTC","startDate":1488247200000,"endDate":1488250800000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"BMTC","contactPerson":"Bodo Zeschke","contactEmail":"B.Zeschke@bom.gov.au","contactUrl":"https://attendee.gotowebinar.com/register/872714645619448066","description":"The Regional Focus Group meeting will be coordinated by Bodo Zeschke. You are welcome to attend.\r\nThe GoToWebinar web conferencing software will be used and you can attend the session by using the link provided.","country":null,"learningOutcome":"","summary":null,"content":"This Regional Focus Group meeting will feature a contribution from Mr. Joe Courtney, BMTC/Perth pertaining to Cyclogenesis.\r\n\r\nBodo Zeschke may also add a short topic of interest during the session.","targetAudience":"","registrationHowto":"There is no need to register in advance to attend the meeting.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5852,"name":"Luciane Veeck","email":"lveeck@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":104,"value":"Discussion"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":90,"value":"VLab","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":5,"value":"VLab Centre of Excellence Australia","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1528,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Overview of the Global Disaster Alert and Coordination System (GDACS)","titleNative":"Overview of the Global Disaster Alert and Coordination System (GDACS)","startDate":1487635200000,"endDate":1487635200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"NASA/ARSET","contactPerson":"ARSET","contactEmail":"nasa.arset@gmail.com","contactUrl":"https://arset.gsfc.nasa.gov/disasters/webinars/GDACS17","description":"Up-to-date and accessible information is essential to providing an effective, coordinated response to disasters, such as earthquakes, floods, and tropical storms. The Global Disaster Alert and Coordination System (GDACS) provides near real-time data, alerts, and impact assessments that can be accessed online. The interactive website integrates coordination tools with maps and satellite imagery relevant to an event, including NASA satellite imagery and MODIS-based flood mapping from the Dartmouth Flood Observatory. In this two-hour webinar, participants will learn how they can use GDACS to monitor real-time disasters, assess the impacts of an event, and develop response strategies for both national and international events. The training will include a presentation, followed by a demonstration of GDACS features and a case study with step-by-step instructions for obtaining satellite images, alerts, and crisis management information using GDACS.\r\nSessions are broadcast twice per day to allow for international participation. They will be held on Thursday, February 21,  8:00-10:00 a.m. and  5:00-7:00 p.m. EST (UTC-5).\r\nA certificate of completion will be provided to participants that attend the live webinar\r\n","country":null,"learningOutcome":"By the end of this training, participants will be able to:\r\nMonitor real-time disasters using satellite images and maps\r\nUse GIS-based and in situ information to inform impact assessments and response strategies","summary":null,"content":"Agenda:\r\nGlobal Disaster Alert and Coordination System Background\r\n8:00-8:30 a.m. EST, 5:00-5:30 p.m. EST\r\nDemonstration of GDACS Features\r\n8:30-9:00 a.m. EST, 5:30-6:00 p.m. EST\r\nDisaster Monitoring and Impact Assessments\r\n9:00-9:50 a.m. EST, 6:00-6:50 p.m. EST\r\n(Includes a demonstration of applying the data with a historical and a near real-time event)\r\nQuestion & Answer Session\r\n9:50-10:00 a.m. EST, 6:50-7:00 p.m. EST","targetAudience":"Disaster managers, emergency and relief organizations, and NGOs operating on local to international levels. Professional organizations in the public and private sectors engaged in disaster management and relief will be given preference over organizations focused primarily on research. ","registrationHowto":"This webinar is free, but you must register by following link provided. Space is limited, and preference will be given to organizations listed above over organizations focused primarily on research. You will be notified by email if your registration has been approved on or before February 20. Please only register for the session that works best for your time zone.","registrationEndDate":null,"fees":"No fees apply","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":5852,"name":"Luciane Veeck","email":"lveeck@wmo.int","agency":"","country":"CH","programme":"","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":120,"value":"NASA-ARSET","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":2,"value":"II Asia"},{"id":3,"value":"III South America"},{"id":6,"value":"V South-West Pacific"},{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"},{"id":1,"value":"I Africa"},{"id":4,"value":"IV North America, Central 