ce on EUMETSAT's Copernicus Marine products with relevance to marine forecasting; \r\n- Waves from Space (Altimeters);\r\n- Winds from Space (Scatterometers).","targetAudience":"Experts from operational centers with responsibilities to monitor Baltic Sea, with all levels of experience in the use of satellite data for marine analysis propose. ","registrationHowto":"To attend the event, an application is required and must be made through http://training.eumetsat.int/course/view.php?id=158 , until 13 February 2017.","registrationEndDate":1486944000000,"fees":"No","awardGranted":null,"creator":{"id":2829,"name":"Joana Betencourt ","email":"Joana.Betencourt@eumetsat.int","agency":"EUMETSAT","country":"DE","programme":"EUMETSAT","trainingPartner":null,"userIdentifier":null,"blocked":null,"lastAccess":null,"webGroup":null,"profile":null,"aclRoleIds":null,"aclGroupIds":null},"approver":null,"leadTrainer":null,"aclGroup":{"id":2,"name":"EUMETSAT"},"statusUpdate":null,"eventType":{"id":101,"value":"Course"},"attendance":{"id":1,"value":"Open"},"status":{"id":2,"value":"Confirmed"},"condition":"DEFINITE","format":null,"attendeeCount":0,"external":false,"previouslyConfirmed":true,"initiative":[{"id":50,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":true},{"id":180,"value":"Copernicus","visible":true}],"trainingPartner":[{"id":15,"value":"EUMETSAT","visible":false}],"programmes":[],"language":[{"id":3,"value":"English","iso639":"en"}],"regions":[{"id":7,"value":"VI Europe"}],"qualification":[],"eumDataApplications":[],"eumDataAccessTypes":[],"eumSatelliteMissions":[],"eumSensors":[]},{"id":1531,"created":null,"updated":null,"title":"Baltic+ 2017 - Online Phase ","titleNative":"Baltic+ 2017 - Online Phase ","startDate":1486944000000,"endDate":1488499200000,"tbdDate":null,"city":"Online","host":"Lithuanian Hydrometeorological Service (LHMS)","contactPerson":"Izolda Marcinoniene","contactEmail":"izolda.marcinoniene@meteo.lt","contactUrl":"","description":"The Baltic+ course is a joint initiative of the National Meteorological Services of Latvia, Lithuania, Estonia and Poland, who join the forces in order to increase the knowledge in skills in the use of satellite observation data and to create a platform for exchanging ideas, applications and knowledge. \r\n\r\nThe course in 2017 will focus on improving the skills in monitoring the  summertime convection. \r\n","country":{"id":"--","name":"ONLINE","region":null,"type":"Other"},"learningOutcome":"Participants will be able to: \r\n\r\n- Select the most appropriate channels or combinations of channels for monitoring deep convection;\r\n- Interpret satellite data within the context of all other observations, guidance and situational awareness;\r\n- Understand the structure and evaluation of various clouds and convective systems; \r\n- Use satellite images to issue more precise forecasts and warnings; Use different SAF products for situation analysis; \r\n- Could take into account the main factors affecting satellite data quality and characteristics;\r\n\r\n","summary":null,"content":"This event covers: \r\n\r\n- Identification of convective cloud types, features and characteristics;\r\n- Understanding the atmospheric conditions favorable for deep convection. \r\nThis course will have two phases, an online (asynchronous) component with reading materials, exercises and collaborative case study preparatory work. This will take three weeks (13 February  3 March), including approximately 4 hours of individual work per week. The course will finish with a three-day-classroom course 14-16 March. The classroom course will consist of lab exercises, presentations, group work and finalization of case studies started during the online phase. \r\n\r\n","targetAudience":"The course is primarily aimed at weather forecasters working in shifts with at least six months professional experience.","registrationHowto":"Please use email contact@meteo.lt for further information on how to apply for this course. \r\nFor the classroom phase